<node id="Cesare Pugni">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Cesare Pugni was an Italian composer of ballet music, a pianist and a violinist.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Cesare Pugni (Russian: Цезарь Пуни ) (] ; 31 May 1802–26 January\r\n[O.S. 14 January]\r\n1870 ) born in Genoa, was an Italian composer of ballet music, a pianist and a violinist.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Genoa">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Genoa is the birthplace of Cesare Pugni.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Cesare Pugni (Russian: Цезарь Пуни ) (] ; 31 May 1802–26 January\r\n[O.S. 14 January]\r\n1870 ) born in Genoa, was an Italian composer of ballet music, a pianist and a violinist.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Her Majesty's Theatre">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Her Majesty's Theatre is a theatre in London where Cesare Pugni composed ballets.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Pugni is most noted for the ballets he composed for Her Majesty's Theatre in London (1843–1850), and for the Imperial Theatres in St. Petersburg, Russia (1850–1870).", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="London">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "London is a city where Her Majesty's Theatre is located and where Cesare Pugni composed ballets.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}, {"text": "London is a city where Peacefrog Records is based.", "chunk_id": "1c1d19351df2d318", "doc_id": "hp_28fb4ee88cd9de85"}, {"text": "London is a location where Ninja Tune is based.", "chunk_id": "86dbbff6a0d26c75", "doc_id": "hp_417d28d6df2c046e"}, {"text": "London is a city where Wembley Stadium is located.", "chunk_id": "1606e1aa9cfc722b", "doc_id": "hp_631a38475ad4383e"}, {"text": "The city where the band Florence and the Machine was formed.", "chunk_id": "a0e37e5744f28418", "doc_id": "hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e"}, {"text": "London is a city where Downing Street is located.", "chunk_id": "9f673348a0fb7a1f", "doc_id": "hp_75fe9fb18dc6c720"}, {"text": "Domino Recording Company, generally known as Domino, is a British independent record label based in London.", "chunk_id": "ce488a80e2770168", "doc_id": "hp_928492f8f11b78de"}, {"text": "The city where the society was founded.", "chunk_id": "33a9a750a0cbc7b4", "doc_id": "hp_a4dd7ae51691935c"}, {"text": "A city where the tour was performed.", "chunk_id": "da03dc4aa612a116", "doc_id": "hp_b1fcfbca9c340147"}, {"text": "London is the current residence of Marco Fu.", "chunk_id": "40bdefa8eb4df2fe", "doc_id": "hp_d05fd69dc2a1479f"}, {"text": "The Langham, London is one of the largest and best known traditional style grand hotels in London.", "chunk_id": "386e04a7f968f9b6", "doc_id": "hp_e9091880eafc6658"}, {"text": "A city where 'The Sound of Change Live' concert took place.", "chunk_id": "4a9a4f6f83f32605", "doc_id": "hp_ef31a7b23736d77e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Pugni is most noted for the ballets he composed for Her Majesty's Theatre in London (1843–1850), and for the Imperial Theatres in St. Petersburg, Russia (1850–1870).", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}, {"text": "Peacefrog Records is an independent record label based in London, United Kingdom.", "chunk_id": "1c1d19351df2d318", "doc_id": "hp_28fb4ee88cd9de85"}, {"text": "Ninja Tune is an English independent record label based in London.", "chunk_id": "86dbbff6a0d26c75", "doc_id": "hp_417d28d6df2c046e"}, {"text": "It was the first of a record 26 times that London's Wembley Stadium would host the World Final with the last being in 1981.", "chunk_id": "1606e1aa9cfc722b", "doc_id": "hp_631a38475ad4383e"}, {"text": "Florence and the Machine (stylised as Florence + the Machine) are an English indie rock band that formed in London in 2007, consisting of lead singer Florence Welch, keyboardist Isabella Summers, and a collaboration of other artists.", "chunk_id": "a0e37e5744f28418", "doc_id": "hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e"}, {"text": "The residence, in Downing Street in London, was built alongside the official residence of the Prime Minister at Number 10 in 1682.", "chunk_id": "9f673348a0fb7a1f", "doc_id": "hp_75fe9fb18dc6c720"}, {"text": "Domino Recording Company, generally known as Domino, is a British independent record label based in London.", "chunk_id": "ce488a80e2770168", "doc_id": "hp_928492f8f11b78de"}, {"text": "It was founded in London, England in 1853 as The Photographic Society of London with the objective of promoting the art and science of photography, and in 1854 received Royal patronage from Queen Victoria and Prince Albert.", "chunk_id": "33a9a750a0cbc7b4", "doc_id": "hp_a4dd7ae51691935c"}, {"text": "They performed in the UK in February - May in 2008 and were at Drury Lane, London for a month.", "chunk_id": "da03dc4aa612a116", "doc_id": "hp_b1fcfbca9c340147"}, {"text": "He currently resides in London.", "chunk_id": "40bdefa8eb4df2fe", "doc_id": "hp_d05fd69dc2a1479f"}, {"text": "The Langham, London is one of the largest and best known traditional style grand hotels in London.", "chunk_id": "386e04a7f968f9b6", "doc_id": "hp_e9091880eafc6658"}, {"text": "On 25 February 2013 it was announced that Florence and the Machine would be playing at the Coke Live Music Festival in Poland on 10 August 2013, and on 26 March 2013 it was announced that the band would be playing at Chime for Change's \"The Sound of Change Live\" concert at London's Twickenham Stadium alongside Beyoncé, Ellie Goulding and Haim, amongst others.", "chunk_id": "4a9a4f6f83f32605", "doc_id": "hp_ef31a7b23736d77e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "hp_28fb4ee88cd9de85", "hp_417d28d6df2c046e", "hp_631a38475ad4383e", "hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e", "hp_75fe9fb18dc6c720", "hp_928492f8f11b78de", "hp_a4dd7ae51691935c", "hp_b1fcfbca9c340147", "hp_d05fd69dc2a1479f", "hp_e9091880eafc6658", "hp_ef31a7b23736d77e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Imperial Theatres">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Imperial Theatres are theatres in St. Petersburg, Russia, where Cesare Pugni composed ballets.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Pugni is most noted for the ballets he composed for Her Majesty's Theatre in London (1843–1850), and for the Imperial Theatres in St. Petersburg, Russia (1850–1870).", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Jules Perrot">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Jules Perrot was a ballet master whose works were often set to scores by Cesare Pugni.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The majority of his ballet music was composed for the works of the ballet master Jules Perrot, who mounted nearly every one of his ballets to scores by Pugni.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="ballet music">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Ballet music is a genre of music composed for ballets.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The majority of his ballet music was composed for the works of the ballet master Jules Perrot, who mounted nearly every one of his ballets to scores by Pugni.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Premier maître de ballet">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Premier maître de ballet is a position at the St. Petersburg Imperial Theatres.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In 1850 Perrot departed London for Russia, having accepted the position of \"Premier maître de ballet\" of the St. Petersburg Imperial Theatres at the behest of Carlotta Grisi, who was engaged as \"Prima ballerina\".", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Carlotta Grisi">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Carlotta Grisi was engaged as 'Prima ballerina' at the St. Petersburg Imperial Theatres.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In 1850 Perrot departed London for Russia, having accepted the position of \"Premier maître de ballet\" of the St. Petersburg Imperial Theatres at the behest of Carlotta Grisi, who was engaged as \"Prima ballerina\".", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Prima ballerina">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Prima ballerina is a title for a leading female dancer.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In 1850 Perrot departed London for Russia, having accepted the position of \"Premier maître de ballet\" of the St. Petersburg Imperial Theatres at the behest of Carlotta Grisi, who was engaged as \"Prima ballerina\".", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Arthur Saint-Léon">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Arthur Saint-Léon was a successor to Jules Perrot at the Imperial Theatres.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Pugni went on the compose for Perrot's successors Arthur Saint-Léon and Marius Petipa, serving as the Imperial Theatre's official composer of ballet music until his death in 1870.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Rockstar Vienna">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Rockstar Vienna was an Austrian video game developer based in Vienna, Austria, and a subsidiary of Rockstar Games.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Rockstar Productions GmbH (formerly Neo Software Produktions GmbH), doing business as Rockstar Vienna, was an Austrian Video game developer based in Vienna, Austria, and a subsidiary of Rockstar Games.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_034d7f4890c999d2"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Rockstar Productions GmbH">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
