<node id="Neo Deutschland">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Neo Deutschland was a video game publishing subsidiary of Neo Software that operated between 1995 and 1996.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Between 1995 and 1996, Neo Software also operated a video game publishing subsidiary, Neo Deutschland, in Paderborn, Germany.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_034d7f4890c999d2"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Paderborn">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Paderborn, Germany was the location of Neo Deutschland.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Between 1995 and 1996, Neo Software also operated a video game publishing subsidiary, Neo Deutschland, in Paderborn, Germany.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_034d7f4890c999d2"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Germany">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Germany is a country where Neo Deutschland was located.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}, {"text": "The country where Catan was first published in 1995.", "chunk_id": "492ee6567ec9e1c7", "doc_id": "hp_27d7c27c384bbb29"}, {"text": "Germany is a country where Cologne is located.", "chunk_id": "cf3ed09c1d2f8654", "doc_id": "hp_5d7964cd7edd106e"}, {"text": "Germany is a country where the Kiehnmoor nature reserve is located.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}, {"text": "Germany is the country where Bastei-Verlag is located and where Celal Kandemiroglu offered his comics.", "chunk_id": "9ced057e330685fe", "doc_id": "hp_88b4fa8c4b3d726e"}, {"text": "Germany is a country where the Hoch Conservatory is located and is the seventh oldest music conservatory.", "chunk_id": "43c8b1224e31b404", "doc_id": "hp_a82ec9e667a313c7"}, {"text": "Germany is a location where Alma Moodie established an excellent reputation in the 1920s and 1930s.", "chunk_id": "5978fb5d2c7a87fb", "doc_id": "hp_ac759163e3bcf4aa"}, {"text": "A country where Würzburg is located and where the record label No Man's Land was based.", "chunk_id": "2eafd94ce17135d2", "doc_id": "hp_b72d424527397087"}, {"text": "The country where Kosmos publishes Catan Dice Game.", "chunk_id": "d146a6f0cb5047a2", "doc_id": "hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Between 1995 and 1996, Neo Software also operated a video game publishing subsidiary, Neo Deutschland, in Paderborn, Germany.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}, {"text": "The Settlers of Catan, sometimes shortened to Catan or Settlers, is a multiplayer board game designed by Klaus Teuber and first published in 1995 in Germany by Franckh-Kosmos Verlag (Kosmos) as Die Siedler von Catan.", "chunk_id": "492ee6567ec9e1c7", "doc_id": "hp_27d7c27c384bbb29"}, {"text": "The Dom-Hotel is a five-star hotel in Cologne, Germany, located on Roncalliplatz in Innenstadt.", "chunk_id": "cf3ed09c1d2f8654", "doc_id": "hp_5d7964cd7edd106e"}, {"text": "The Kiehnmoor is a nature reserve in Germany.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}, {"text": "After graduating at the fine arts academy in Istanbul he started to offer his comics to the Bastei-Verlag in Germany around 1978.", "chunk_id": "9ced057e330685fe", "doc_id": "hp_88b4fa8c4b3d726e"}, {"text": "It is, after Leipzig and Berlin, the seventh oldest music conservatory in Germany.", "chunk_id": "43c8b1224e31b404", "doc_id": "hp_a82ec9e667a313c7"}, {"text": "Alma Templeton Moodie (12 September 18987 March 1943) was an Australian violinist who established an excellent reputation in Germany in the 1920s and 1930s.", "chunk_id": "5978fb5d2c7a87fb", "doc_id": "hp_ac759163e3bcf4aa"}, {"text": "No Man's Land was a German record label based in Würzburg, Germany.", "chunk_id": "2eafd94ce17135d2", "doc_id": "hp_b72d424527397087"}, {"text": "Catan Dice Game is a German-style board game, developed by Klaus Teuber and published in 2007 by Catan GmbH and its licensors, Kosmos in Germany and Mayfair Games in English-speaking countries.", "chunk_id": "d146a6f0cb5047a2", "doc_id": "hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_034d7f4890c999d2", "hp_27d7c27c384bbb29", "hp_5d7964cd7edd106e", "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880", "hp_88b4fa8c4b3d726e", "hp_a82ec9e667a313c7", "hp_ac759163e3bcf4aa", "hp_b72d424527397087", "hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Vienna">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Vienna, Austria is the base location of Rockstar Vienna.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Rockstar Productions GmbH (formerly Neo Software Produktions GmbH), doing business as Rockstar Vienna, was an Austrian Video game developer based in Vienna, Austria, and a subsidiary of Rockstar Games.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_034d7f4890c999d2"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Austria">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Austria is the country where Rockstar Vienna was based.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}, {"text": "A country allied with Russia against the First French Empire.", "chunk_id": "0c7dbfb126626c8b", "doc_id": "hp_1fde0cb754789706"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Rockstar Productions GmbH (formerly Neo Software Produktions GmbH), doing business as Rockstar Vienna, was an Austrian Video game developer based in Vienna, Austria, and a subsidiary of Rockstar Games.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}, {"text": "The Battle of Amstetten was a minor engagement during the War of the Third Coalition between the First French Empire and the alliance of Austria and Russia.", "chunk_id": "0c7dbfb126626c8b", "doc_id": "hp_1fde0cb754789706"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_034d7f4890c999d2", "hp_1fde0cb754789706"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Games That Matter Productions">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Games That Matter Productions is a successor company founded by former Rockstar Vienna employees.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "A successor to the company, Games That Matter Productions, was founded by former Rockstar Vienna employees Hannes Seifert, Niki Laber and Jürgen Goeldner.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_034d7f4890c999d2"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Jürgen Goeldner">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Jürgen Goeldner is a former Rockstar Vienna employee and a founder of Games That Matter Productions.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "A successor to the company, Games That Matter Productions, was founded by former Rockstar Vienna employees Hannes Seifert, Niki Laber and Jürgen Goeldner.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_034d7f4890c999d2"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="video game developer">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A video game developer is a company that creates video games.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Rockstar Productions GmbH (formerly Neo Software Produktions GmbH), doing business as Rockstar Vienna, was an Austrian Video game developer based in Vienna, Austria, and a subsidiary of Rockstar Games.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_034d7f4890c999d2"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="video game publishing subsidiary">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A video game publishing subsidiary is a company that publishes video games and is owned by a larger entity.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Between 1995 and 1996, Neo Software also operated a video game publishing subsidiary, Neo Deutschland, in Paderborn, Germany.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_034d7f4890c999d2"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="company's tenth anniversary">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The company's tenth anniversary was celebrated in January 2003.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In January 2003, during the company's tenth anniversary, the company was rebranded Rockstar Vienna and became part of the Rockstar Games umbrella.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_034d7f4890c999d2"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Rockstar Games umbrella">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Rockstar Games umbrella refers to the group of companies under Rockstar Games.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In January 2003, during the company's tenth anniversary, the company was rebranded Rockstar Vienna and became part of the Rockstar Games umbrella.", "chunk_id": "0cc52c6f4ba06192", "doc_id": "hp_034d7f4890c999d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_034d7f4890c999d2"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Dregea sinensis">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Dregea sinensis is a species of plant.", "chunk_id": "220246b8aa2958db", "doc_id": "hp_03f51aa918aeaa02"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Dregea sinensis is a species of plant in the Apocynaceae family that is native to China.", "chunk_id": "220246b8aa2958db", "doc_id": "hp_03f51aa918aeaa02"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_03f51aa918aeaa02"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Apocynaceae">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Apocynaceae is a family of plants.", "chunk_id": "220246b8aa2958db", "doc_id": "hp_03f51aa918aeaa02"}, {"text": "Apocynaceae is a family of flowering plants.", "chunk_id": "b434d13cc8863180", "doc_id": "hp_2b52b5ab8c2b4e73"}, {"text": "Apocynaceae is a family of flowering plants.", "chunk_id": "578db93c2087665a", "doc_id": "hp_65e5dd7a12e038cc"}, {"text": "Apocynaceae is the dogbane family to which Pachypodium belongs.", "chunk_id": "c65de02bc9af4260", "doc_id": "hp_a9669326c71f5122"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Dregea sinensis is a species of plant in the Apocynaceae family that is native to China.", "chunk_id": "220246b8aa2958db", "doc_id": "hp_03f51aa918aeaa02"}, {"text": "Dregea is a genus of vines in the Apocynaceae, first described as a genus with this name in 1838.", "chunk_id": "b434d13cc8863180", "doc_id": "hp_2b52b5ab8c2b4e73"}, {"text": "Dregea volubilis is a species of plant in the Apocynaceae family that is native to India.", "chunk_id": "578db93c2087665a", "doc_id": "hp_65e5dd7a12e038cc"}, {"text": "It belongs to the dogbane family, Apocynaceae.", "chunk_id": "c65de02bc9af4260", "doc_id": "hp_a9669326c71f5122"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_03f51aa918aeaa02", "hp_2b52b5ab8c2b4e73", "hp_65e5dd7a12e038cc", "hp_a9669326c71f5122"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="China">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "China is a country.", "chunk_id": "220246b8aa2958db", "doc_id": "hp_03f51aa918aeaa02"}, {"text": "China is a country where Hunan Province is located.", "chunk_id": "e5fc7c6607c7f74d", "doc_id": "hp_0cadb19ab7b7f673"}, {"text": "China is a country in East Asia.", "chunk_id": "1900876eb0183fa0", "doc_id": "hp_0d2b9749009e4dd9"}, {"text": "A country in East Asia.", "chunk_id": "f6e0ca7c3e63f550", "doc_id": "hp_0e1b00a3eeabb9ce"}, {"text": "China is a country where Liaoning Province is located.", "chunk_id": "14a2260d346f6ea1", "doc_id": "hp_109016e70ed6685b"}, {"text": "China is a country where the Kunlun Mountain Range is located.", "chunk_id": "b1b282e5386423ab", "doc_id": "hp_1091daa9d1a0830a"}, {"text": "China is a native region for Pterostyrax hispidus.", "chunk_id": "5a4b1080849ca551", "doc_id": "hp_10ed6dd74595a5bc"}, {"text": "China is a country where Andatee China Marine Fuel Service Corporation is based and where it sells its products.", "chunk_id": "0ae16a4e4e4c0144", "doc_id": "hp_1e1ee8b3317b2831"}, {"text": "China is a country.", "chunk_id": "e4b8cfa2e82ef0c0", "doc_id": "hp_3918c7f9f1efe04d"}, {"text": "A country where Sanya, the host city of the 2013 World's Strongest Man, is located.", "chunk_id": "241806d0ee3666dd", "doc_id": "hp_45c17b9e08342c16"}, {"text": "China is a country.", "chunk_id": "ff0f3f2e384a3a68", "doc_id": "hp_49bb33ee8514f5e2"}, {"text": "China is the native region for Philadelphus incanus.", "chunk_id": "ce5fc90c4d57decb", "doc_id": "hp_5ebd609393339d53"}, {"text": "A country in East Asia.", "chunk_id": "0cb99287d9c2da80", "doc_id": "hp_81f5a8696daf3dee"}, {"text": "China is the country where Dongtai is located.", "chunk_id": "551f221f922de162", "doc_id": "hp_8cfa6859d9227577"}, {"text": "China is a country.", "chunk_id": "6cbf95d958c94cd7", "doc_id": "hp_8f217e15be3875b3"}, {"text": "A country in East Asia.", "chunk_id": "9432ffb2818fa833", "doc_id": "hp_9c94d1d46a54f88d"}, {"text": "China is a location where GeIL has branches.", "chunk_id": "94d646829c3ad5f6", "doc_id": "hp_a08e17bf87e824f4"}, {"text": "China is a country in eastern Asia where Pterostyrax is native.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917"}, {"text": "A country.", "chunk_id": "6acf624f54ca7f79", "doc_id": "hp_a2f0f467a0548d2b"}, {"text": "A country where Mount Jizu is located.", "chunk_id": "d12957e9bb1b45a2", "doc_id": "hp_b7298b1cd3170cc8"}, {"text": "China is located to the north of Mingli Sar.", "chunk_id": "49deece00239c9e4", "doc_id": "hp_d1711a52f98a3a6d"}, {"text": "The country where the Hangzhou–Ruili Expressway is located.", "chunk_id": "b445d8e4dd3011b8", "doc_id": "hp_f8f508f7fcc4bad6"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Dregea sinensis is a species of plant in the Apocynaceae family that is native to China.", "chunk_id": "220246b8aa2958db", "doc_id": "hp_03f51aa918aeaa02"}, {"text": "Ningxiang High-tech Industrial Park () is a High tech industrial park at province level in Ningxiang City, Hunan Province, China.", "chunk_id": "e5fc7c6607c7f74d", "doc_id": "hp_0cadb19ab7b7f673"}, {"text": "According to one blogger, Gollum provides a way to bypass censorship of Wikipedia in China.", "chunk_id": "1900876eb0183fa0", "doc_id": "hp_0d2b9749009e4dd9"}, {"text": "Wanding Border Economic Cooperation Zone (WTBECZ) is a Chinese State Council-approved Industrial Park based in Wanding Town, Ruili City, Dehong Prefecture, Yunnan, China, founded in 1992 and was established to promote trade between China and Myanmar.", "chunk_id": "f6e0ca7c3e63f550", "doc_id": "hp_0e1b00a3eeabb9ce"}, {"text": "Fenghuang Mountain () is a mountain located in Fengcheng, Dandong City, Liaoning Province, China.", "chunk_id": "14a2260d346f6ea1", "doc_id": "hp_109016e70ed6685b"}, {"text": "Liushi Shan, also commonly called Kunlun Goddess, is a mountain in the Kunlun Mountain Range in China.", "chunk_id": "b1b282e5386423ab", "doc_id": "hp_1091daa9d1a0830a"}, {"text": "Pterostyrax hispidus, the epaulette tree or fragrant epaulette tree, is a species of flowering plant in the family Styracaceae, native to China and Japan.", "chunk_id": "5a4b1080849ca551", "doc_id": "hp_10ed6dd74595a5bc"}, {"text": "Andatee China Marine Fuel Service Corporation (\"Andatee\") (NASDAQ: AMCF ) is a marine fuel wholesale and retail company that is based in Dalian, China.", "chunk_id": "0ae16a4e4e4c0144", "doc_id": "hp_1e1ee8b3317b2831"}, {"text": "Kangpenqing (also Gang Benchhen) is a mountain in the Baiku Himalayas of Tibet, China.", "chunk_id": "e4b8cfa2e82ef0c0", "doc_id": "hp_3918c7f9f1efe04d"}, {"text": "The event was held in Haitang Bay, Sanya, China, the same host city as the 2006 World's Strongest Man contest.", "chunk_id": "241806d0ee3666dd", "doc_id": "hp_45c17b9e08342c16"}, {"text": "The Jiangxia Tidal Power Station (江厦潮汐电站) is the fourth largest tidal power station in the world, located in Wuyantou, Wenling City, Zhejiang Province, China.", "chunk_id": "ff0f3f2e384a3a68", "doc_id": "hp_49bb33ee8514f5e2"}, {"text": "Native to China, it is a medium to large shrub characterised by its hairy leaves and later flowering than other members of the genus.", "chunk_id": "ce5fc90c4d57decb", "doc_id": "hp_5ebd609393339d53"}, {"text": "Ruili Border Economic Cooperation Zone (RLBECZ) is a Chinese State Council-approved Industrial Park based in Ruili City, Dehong Prefecture, Yunnan, China, founded in 1992 and was established to promote trade between China and Myanmar.", "chunk_id": "0cb99287d9c2da80", "doc_id": "hp_81f5a8696daf3dee"}, {"text": "Dongtai () is a coastal county-level city under the administration of Yancheng, Jiangsu province, China.", "chunk_id": "551f221f922de162", "doc_id": "hp_8cfa6859d9227577"}, {"text": "Wenling (Wenling dialect: Uen-lin Zy ] ; ) is a coastal county-level city in the municipal region of Taizhou, in southeastern Zhejiang province, China.", "chunk_id": "6cbf95d958c94cd7", "doc_id": "hp_8f217e15be3875b3"}, {"text": "Kunming Changshui International Airport (IATA: KMG, ICAO: ZPPP) is the primary airport serving Kunming, the capital of Yunnan Province, China.", "chunk_id": "9432ffb2818fa833", "doc_id": "hp_9c94d1d46a54f88d"}, {"text": "GeIL’s headquarters is located in Taipei, Taiwan, with branches in Hong Kong and China.", "chunk_id": "94d646829c3ad5f6", "doc_id": "hp_a08e17bf87e824f4"}, {"text": "Pterostyrax, the epaulette tree, is a small genus of four species of deciduous large shrubs or small trees in the family Styracaceae, native to eastern Asia in China and Japan.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917"}, {"text": "Liuyang Two-oriented Industrial Park () is an agricultural products processing industrial park at province level in Liuyang City, Hunan Province, China.", "chunk_id": "6acf624f54ca7f79", "doc_id": "hp_a2f0f467a0548d2b"}, {"text": "Mount Jizu () is situated Dali Prefecture, Yunnan Province, China.", "chunk_id": "d12957e9bb1b45a2", "doc_id": "hp_b7298b1cd3170cc8"}, {"text": "China is located to the north, while to the left is the Hindukush mountain range.", "chunk_id": "49deece00239c9e4", "doc_id": "hp_d1711a52f98a3a6d"}, {"text": "The Hangzhou–Ruili Expressway (), commonly referred to as the \"Hangrui Expressway\" () is an expressway in China that connects the cities of Hangzhou, Zhejiang, and Ruili, Yunnan, a city on the border with Burma.", "chunk_id": "b445d8e4dd3011b8", "doc_id": "hp_f8f508f7fcc4bad6"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_03f51aa918aeaa02", "hp_0cadb19ab7b7f673", "hp_0d2b9749009e4dd9", "hp_0e1b00a3eeabb9ce", "hp_109016e70ed6685b", "hp_1091daa9d1a0830a", "hp_10ed6dd74595a5bc", "hp_1e1ee8b3317b2831", "hp_3918c7f9f1efe04d", "hp_45c17b9e08342c16", "hp_49bb33ee8514f5e2", "hp_5ebd609393339d53", "hp_81f5a8696daf3dee", "hp_8cfa6859d9227577", "hp_8f217e15be3875b3", "hp_9c94d1d46a54f88d", "hp_a08e17bf87e824f4", "hp_a0fb254153ed3917", "hp_a2f0f467a0548d2b", "hp_b7298b1cd3170cc8", "hp_d1711a52f98a3a6d", "hp_f8f508f7fcc4bad6"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Enamorada (film)">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A 1946 Mexican drama film.", "chunk_id": "fd7329c42fd6e651", "doc_id": "hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Enamorada (\"Enamoured\") is a 1946 Mexican drama film directed by Emilio Fernández and starring María Félix and Pedro Armendáriz.", "chunk_id": "fd7329c42fd6e651", "doc_id": "hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Emilio Fernández">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The director of the 1946 Mexican drama film Enamorada.", "chunk_id": "fd7329c42fd6e651", "doc_id": "hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6"}, {"text": "The famous film director and brother of Fernando Fernández.", "chunk_id": "f22987b0a2a07a86", "doc_id": "hp_0a82eabb231d743f"}, {"text": "Emilio Fernández was a film director and one of the muses of Columba Domínguez.", "chunk_id": "c5b56d3da2c4d74b", "doc_id": "hp_2cf3a3820e736dce"}, {"text": "Emilio Fernández is the director of the Mexican film Las Abandonadas.", "chunk_id": "4cb081bc0e3295ae", "doc_id": "hp_52300967f6c3f951"}, {"text": "Emilio Fernández is one of the most influential directors and actors of the Golden Age of Mexican cinema.", "chunk_id": "15bc36547e2dd368", "doc_id": "hp_729cba8a7fa727ec"}, {"text": "The director of the 1948 Mexican drama film Río Escondido.", "chunk_id": "5e0b47f6aaf060d0", "doc_id": "hp_98722d3018fb7583"}, {"text": "The director of the Mexican movie Bugambilia.", "chunk_id": "3626aa418e38ab94", "doc_id": "hp_b7f3e092b32229f7"}, {"text": "Emilio Fernández was a Mexican film director, actor, and screenwriter.", "chunk_id": "e2bd3c61103e4d8b", "doc_id": "hp_e6718a97d51ea825"}, {"text": "The older brother of Jaime Fernández, who was also an actor and director.", "chunk_id": "5caaa82e915cbb20", "doc_id": "hp_f4a1d9afa0828a54"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Enamorada (\"Enamoured\") is a 1946 Mexican drama film directed by Emilio Fernández and starring María Félix and Pedro Armendáriz.", "chunk_id": "fd7329c42fd6e651", "doc_id": "hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6"}, {"text": "He was brother of the famous film director Emilio Fernández and actor Jaime Fernández.", "chunk_id": "f22987b0a2a07a86", "doc_id": "hp_0a82eabb231d743f"}, {"text": "Considered a crucial figure in the Golden Age of Mexican cinema, she was one of the muses of the film director Emilio Fernández, with whom she was romantically linked for several years.", "chunk_id": "c5b56d3da2c4d74b", "doc_id": "hp_2cf3a3820e736dce"}, {"text": "Las Abandonadas (The Abandoned) is a Mexican film of 1945, directed by Emilio Fernández, starring Dolores del Río and Pedro Armendáriz.", "chunk_id": "4cb081bc0e3295ae", "doc_id": "hp_52300967f6c3f951"}, {"text": "Some of the most influential directors and actors are Emilio Fernández, Raul De Anda, Roberto B. Cervenna, Cantinflas, Vitola, Tin Tan, etc.", "chunk_id": "15bc36547e2dd368", "doc_id": "hp_729cba8a7fa727ec"}, {"text": "Río Escondido is a 1948 Mexican drama film directed by Emilio Fernández and starring María Félix.", "chunk_id": "5e0b47f6aaf060d0", "doc_id": "hp_98722d3018fb7583"}, {"text": "Bugambilia (\"Bougainvillea\") is a Mexican movie of 1945 directed by Emilio Fernández and starring Dolores del Río and Pedro Armendáriz.", "chunk_id": "3626aa418e38ab94", "doc_id": "hp_b7f3e092b32229f7"}, {"text": "Emilio \"El Indio\" Fernández (born Emilio Fernández Romo, ] ; March 26, 1904 – August 6, 1986) was a Mexican film director, actor and screenwriter.", "chunk_id": "e2bd3c61103e4d8b", "doc_id": "hp_e6718a97d51ea825"}, {"text": "His older brother was actor/director Emilio Fernández.", "chunk_id": "5caaa82e915cbb20", "doc_id": "hp_f4a1d9afa0828a54"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6", "hp_0a82eabb231d743f", "hp_2cf3a3820e736dce", "hp_52300967f6c3f951", "hp_729cba8a7fa727ec", "hp_98722d3018fb7583", "hp_b7f3e092b32229f7", "hp_e6718a97d51ea825", "hp_f4a1d9afa0828a54"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="María Félix">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An actress who starred in the 1946 Mexican drama film Enamorada.", "chunk_id": "fd7329c42fd6e651", "doc_id": "hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6"}, {"text": "A star of the 1948 Mexican drama film Río Escondido.", "chunk_id": "5e0b47f6aaf060d0", "doc_id": "hp_98722d3018fb7583"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Enamorada (\"Enamoured\") is a 1946 Mexican drama film directed by Emilio Fernández and starring María Félix and Pedro Armendáriz.", "chunk_id": "fd7329c42fd6e651", "doc_id": "hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6"}, {"text": "Río Escondido is a 1948 Mexican drama film directed by Emilio Fernández and starring María Félix.", "chunk_id": "5e0b47f6aaf060d0", "doc_id": "hp_98722d3018fb7583"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6", "hp_98722d3018fb7583"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Pedro Armendáriz">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An actor who starred in the 1946 Mexican drama film Enamorada and reprised his role in its 1950 remake.", "chunk_id": "fd7329c42fd6e651", "doc_id": "hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6"}, {"text": "Pedro Armendáriz is a star of the Mexican film Las Abandonadas.", "chunk_id": "4cb081bc0e3295ae", "doc_id": "hp_52300967f6c3f951"}, {"text": "A star of the Mexican movie Bugambilia.", "chunk_id": "3626aa418e38ab94", "doc_id": "hp_b7f3e092b32229f7"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Enamorada (\"Enamoured\") is a 1946 Mexican drama film directed by Emilio Fernández and starring María Félix and Pedro Armendáriz.", "chunk_id": "fd7329c42fd6e651", "doc_id": "hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6"}, {"text": "Las Abandonadas (The Abandoned) is a Mexican film of 1945, directed by Emilio Fernández, starring Dolores del Río and Pedro Armendáriz.", "chunk_id": "4cb081bc0e3295ae", "doc_id": "hp_52300967f6c3f951"}, {"text": "Bugambilia (\"Bougainvillea\") is a Mexican movie of 1945 directed by Emilio Fernández and starring Dolores del Río and Pedro Armendáriz.", "chunk_id": "3626aa418e38ab94", "doc_id": "hp_b7f3e092b32229f7"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6", "hp_52300967f6c3f951", "hp_b7f3e092b32229f7"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="The Torch">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A 1950 remake of the film Enamorada.", "chunk_id": "fd7329c42fd6e651", "doc_id": "hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The film was remade in 1950 as \"The Torch\" with Armendáriz repeating his role alongside Paulette Goddard who was credited as an associate producer on the film.", "chunk_id": "fd7329c42fd6e651", "doc_id": "hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Paulette Goddard">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An actress and associate producer on the 1950 film \"The Torch\".", "chunk_id": "fd7329c42fd6e651", "doc_id": "hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The film was remade in 1950 as \"The Torch\" with Armendáriz repeating his role alongside Paulette Goddard who was credited as an associate producer on the film.", "chunk_id": "fd7329c42fd6e651", "doc_id": "hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_03f8108a4be7c5d6"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="The Kids of Catan">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Kids of Catan is a German board game designed for children using the theme from \"The Settlers of Catan\".", "chunk_id": "e7373ffc29a63cc4", "doc_id": "hp_03f848248ac84a82"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The Kids of Catan is a German board game designed for children using the theme from \"The Settlers of Catan\".", "chunk_id": "e7373ffc29a63cc4", "doc_id": "hp_03f848248ac84a82"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_03f848248ac84a82"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="The Settlers of Catan">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Settlers of Catan is a board game that serves as the theme for The Kids of Catan.", "chunk_id": "e7373ffc29a63cc4", "doc_id": "hp_03f848248ac84a82"}, {"text": "The Settlers of Catan is a hit game by Klaus Teuber.", "chunk_id": "9a8b53c7a1a0a0b3", "doc_id": "hp_0f73ecd4f9162b2c"}, {"text": "A multiplayer board game designed by Klaus Teuber.", "chunk_id": "492ee6567ec9e1c7", "doc_id": "hp_27d7c27c384bbb29"}, {"text": "The original board game on which The Rivals for Catan and its adaptations are based.", "chunk_id": "155359f8ca0aea2f", "doc_id": "hp_5f6bdf06a278e8d8"}, {"text": "The original game that the Catan Card Game is based on.", "chunk_id": "dbfe350afe445342", "doc_id": "hp_a2aabfc161961b2c"}, {"text": "A board game for which Catan: Cities &amp; Knights is an expansion.", "chunk_id": "42769d289195cfc3", "doc_id": "hp_c20f6b270e53f1ff"}, {"text": "A board game for which Catan: Seafarers is an expansion.", "chunk_id": "4604dd9ff3227806", "doc_id": "hp_f44b12ff517dfad8"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The Kids of Catan is a German board game designed for children using the theme from \"The Settlers of Catan\".", "chunk_id": "e7373ffc29a63cc4", "doc_id": "hp_03f848248ac84a82"}, {"text": "It is the second game in the \"Catan Adventures\" series (the first being \"\", a series of spinoff games based on the theme from Teuber's hit game \"The Settlers of Catan\" as well as its German-language novelization by Rebecca Gablé.", "chunk_id": "9a8b53c7a1a0a0b3", "doc_id": "hp_0f73ecd4f9162b2c"}, {"text": "The Settlers of Catan, sometimes shortened to Catan or Settlers, is a multiplayer board game designed by Klaus Teuber and first published in 1995 in Germany by Franckh-Kosmos Verlag (Kosmos) as Die Siedler von Catan.", "chunk_id": "492ee6567ec9e1c7", "doc_id": "hp_27d7c27c384bbb29"}, {"text": "The Rivals for Catan (German: \"Die Fürsten von Catan\" ) is an updated revision of the \"Catan Card Game\", a card game adaptation of \"The Settlers of Catan\".", "chunk_id": "155359f8ca0aea2f", "doc_id": "hp_5f6bdf06a278e8d8"}, {"text": "The Catan Card Game, originally named The Settlers of Catan: The Card Game, is a card game adaptation of \"The Settlers of Catan\".", "chunk_id": "dbfe350afe445342", "doc_id": "hp_a2aabfc161961b2c"}, {"text": "Catan: Cities &amp; Knights (German: \"Städte und Ritter\" ), formerly \"The Cities and Knights of Catan\" is an expansion to the board game \"The Settlers of Catan\" for three to four players (five to six player play is also possible with the \"Settlers\" and \"Cities &amp; Knights\" five to six player extensions; two-player play is possible with the \"\" expansion).", "chunk_id": "42769d289195cfc3", "doc_id": "hp_c20f6b270e53f1ff"}, {"text": "Catan: Seafarers, or Seafarers of Catan in older editions, (German: \"Die Seefahrer von Catan\" ) is an expansion of the board game \"The Settlers of Catan\" for three to four players (five-to-six-player play is also possible with both of the respective five-to-six-player extensions).", "chunk_id": "4604dd9ff3227806", "doc_id": "hp_f44b12ff517dfad8"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_03f848248ac84a82", "hp_0f73ecd4f9162b2c", "hp_27d7c27c384bbb29", "hp_5f6bdf06a278e8d8", "hp_a2aabfc161961b2c", "hp_c20f6b270e53f1ff", "hp_f44b12ff517dfad8"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Klaus Teuber">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Klaus Teuber is the creator of the game The Kids of Catan.", "chunk_id": "e7373ffc29a63cc4", "doc_id": "hp_03f848248ac84a82"}, {"text": "Klaus Teuber is the designer of the board game Elasund.", "chunk_id": "9a8b53c7a1a0a0b3", "doc_id": "hp_0f73ecd4f9162b2c"}, {"text": "The creator of \"Settlers of Catan\" and the creator of Catan Histories: Struggle for Rome.", "chunk_id": "03c733f6cd0d7d56", "doc_id": "hp_14e68ec60eba2e91"}, {"text": "The designer of the board game Catan.", "chunk_id": "492ee6567ec9e1c7", "doc_id": "hp_27d7c27c384bbb29"}, {"text": "The developer of the Catan Dice Game.", "chunk_id": "d146a6f0cb5047a2", "doc_id": "hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Like other Catan titles, the game is created by Klaus Teuber and published by Kosmos in German and Mayfair Games in English.", "chunk_id": "e7373ffc29a63cc4", "doc_id": "hp_03f848248ac84a82"}, {"text": "Elasund: The First City (German: \"Elasund - Die erste Stadt\" ; ] ) is a German-style board game designed by Klaus Teuber.", "chunk_id": "9a8b53c7a1a0a0b3", "doc_id": "hp_0f73ecd4f9162b2c"}, {"text": "The game is created by Klaus Teuber, the creator of \"Settlers\", and is published under license from Catan GmbH by Kosmos in German and Mayfair Games in English.", "chunk_id": "03c733f6cd0d7d56", "doc_id": "hp_14e68ec60eba2e91"}, {"text": "The Settlers of Catan, sometimes shortened to Catan or Settlers, is a multiplayer board game designed by Klaus Teuber and first published in 1995 in Germany by Franckh-Kosmos Verlag (Kosmos) as Die Siedler von Catan.", "chunk_id": "492ee6567ec9e1c7", "doc_id": "hp_27d7c27c384bbb29"}, {"text": "Catan Dice Game is a German-style board game, developed by Klaus Teuber and published in 2007 by Catan GmbH and its licensors, Kosmos in Germany and Mayfair Games in English-speaking countries.", "chunk_id": "d146a6f0cb5047a2", "doc_id": "hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_03f848248ac84a82", "hp_0f73ecd4f9162b2c", "hp_14e68ec60eba2e91", "hp_27d7c27c384bbb29", "hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Kosmos">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Kosmos is a publisher of the game The Kids of Catan in German.", "chunk_id": "e7373ffc29a63cc4", "doc_id": "hp_03f848248ac84a82"}, {"text": "Kosmos is a publisher of the game Elasund in German.", "chunk_id": "9a8b53c7a1a0a0b3", "doc_id": "hp_0f73ecd4f9162b2c"}, {"text": "A publisher of the German version of Catan Histories: Struggle for Rome.", "chunk_id": "03c733f6cd0d7d56", "doc_id": "hp_14e68ec60eba2e91"}, {"text": "An alternative name for Franckh-Kosmos Verlag, the publisher of Catan in Germany in 1995.", "chunk_id": "492ee6567ec9e1c7", "doc_id": "hp_27d7c27c384bbb29"}, {"text": "A publisher of games, specifically publishing The Rivals for Catan in German.", "chunk_id": "155359f8ca0aea2f", "doc_id": "hp_5f6bdf06a278e8d8"}, {"text": "A publisher of the Catan Card Game in German.", "chunk_id": "dbfe350afe445342", "doc_id": "hp_a2aabfc161961b2c"}, {"text": "A licensor and publisher of Catan Dice Game in Germany.", "chunk_id": "d146a6f0cb5047a2", "doc_id": "hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Like other Catan titles, the game is created by Klaus Teuber and published by Kosmos in German and Mayfair Games in English.", "chunk_id": "e7373ffc29a63cc4", "doc_id": "hp_03f848248ac84a82"}, {"text": "As a game in the \"Catan\" series, it is published by Kosmos in German and Mayfair Games in English.", "chunk_id": "9a8b53c7a1a0a0b3", "doc_id": "hp_0f73ecd4f9162b2c"}, {"text": "The game is created by Klaus Teuber, the creator of \"Settlers\", and is published under license from Catan GmbH by Kosmos in German and Mayfair Games in English.", "chunk_id": "03c733f6cd0d7d56", "doc_id": "hp_14e68ec60eba2e91"}, {"text": "The Settlers of Catan, sometimes shortened to Catan or Settlers, is a multiplayer board game designed by Klaus Teuber and first published in 1995 in Germany by Franckh-Kosmos Verlag (Kosmos) as Die Siedler von Catan.", "chunk_id": "492ee6567ec9e1c7", "doc_id": "hp_27d7c27c384bbb29"}, {"text": "It is a member of the \"Catan\" series of games, and is published by Kosmos in German and Mayfair Games in English.", "chunk_id": "155359f8ca0aea2f", "doc_id": "hp_5f6bdf06a278e8d8"}, {"text": "It is a member of the \"Catan\" series of games, and is published by Kosmos in German, and Mayfair Games in English.", "chunk_id": "dbfe350afe445342", "doc_id": "hp_a2aabfc161961b2c"}, {"text": "Catan Dice Game is a German-style board game, developed by Klaus Teuber and published in 2007 by Catan GmbH and its licensors, Kosmos in Germany and Mayfair Games in English-speaking countries.", "chunk_id": "d146a6f0cb5047a2", "doc_id": "hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_03f848248ac84a82", "hp_0f73ecd4f9162b2c", "hp_14e68ec60eba2e91", "hp_27d7c27c384bbb29", "hp_5f6bdf06a278e8d8", "hp_a2aabfc161961b2c", "hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Mayfair Games">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Mayfair Games is a publisher of the game The Kids of Catan in English.", "chunk_id": "e7373ffc29a63cc4", "doc_id": "hp_03f848248ac84a82"}, {"text": "Mayfair Games is a publisher of the game Elasund in English.", "chunk_id": "9a8b53c7a1a0a0b3", "doc_id": "hp_0f73ecd4f9162b2c"}, {"text": "A publisher of the English version of Catan Histories: Struggle for Rome.", "chunk_id": "03c733f6cd0d7d56", "doc_id": "hp_14e68ec60eba2e91"}, {"text": "A publisher of Catan and its expansions.", "chunk_id": "492ee6567ec9e1c7", "doc_id": "hp_27d7c27c384bbb29"}, {"text": "A publisher of games, specifically publishing The Rivals for Catan in English.", "chunk_id": "155359f8ca0aea2f", "doc_id": "hp_5f6bdf06a278e8d8"}, {"text": "A publisher of the Catan Card Game in English.", "chunk_id": "dbfe350afe445342", "doc_id": "hp_a2aabfc161961b2c"}, {"text": "A licensor and publisher of Catan Dice Game in English-speaking countries.", "chunk_id": "d146a6f0cb5047a2", "doc_id": "hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Like other Catan titles, the game is created by Klaus Teuber and published by Kosmos in German and Mayfair Games in English.", "chunk_id": "e7373ffc29a63cc4", "doc_id": "hp_03f848248ac84a82"}, {"text": "As a game in the \"Catan\" series, it is published by Kosmos in German and Mayfair Games in English.", "chunk_id": "9a8b53c7a1a0a0b3", "doc_id": "hp_0f73ecd4f9162b2c"}, {"text": "The game is created by Klaus Teuber, the creator of \"Settlers\", and is published under license from Catan GmbH by Kosmos in German and Mayfair Games in English.", "chunk_id": "03c733f6cd0d7d56", "doc_id": "hp_14e68ec60eba2e91"}, {"text": "The game and its many expansions are also published by Mayfair Games, Filosofia, Capcom, 999 Games, Κάισσα, and Devir.", "chunk_id": "492ee6567ec9e1c7", "doc_id": "hp_27d7c27c384bbb29"}, {"text": "It is a member of the \"Catan\" series of games, and is published by Kosmos in German and Mayfair Games in English.", "chunk_id": "155359f8ca0aea2f", "doc_id": "hp_5f6bdf06a278e8d8"}, {"text": "It is a member of the \"Catan\" series of games, and is published by Kosmos in German, and Mayfair Games in English.", "chunk_id": "dbfe350afe445342", "doc_id": "hp_a2aabfc161961b2c"}, {"text": "Catan Dice Game is a German-style board game, developed by Klaus Teuber and published in 2007 by Catan GmbH and its licensors, Kosmos in Germany and Mayfair Games in English-speaking countries.", "chunk_id": "d146a6f0cb5047a2", "doc_id": "hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_03f848248ac84a82", "hp_0f73ecd4f9162b2c", "hp_14e68ec60eba2e91", "hp_27d7c27c384bbb29", "hp_5f6bdf06a278e8d8", "hp_a2aabfc161961b2c", "hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Istanbul Şehir University">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A private, non-profit university located in Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "c4ae848456d08dbd", "doc_id": "hp_0470400943ee62eb"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Istanbul Şehir University (Turkish: \"İstanbul Şehir Üniversitesi\" , literally City University of Istanbul) is a private, non-profit university located in Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "c4ae848456d08dbd", "doc_id": "hp_0470400943ee62eb"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0470400943ee62eb"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="İstanbul Şehir Üniversitesi">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Turkish name for Istanbul Şehir University.", "chunk_id": "c4ae848456d08dbd", "doc_id": "hp_0470400943ee62eb"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Istanbul Şehir University (Turkish: \"İstanbul Şehir Üniversitesi\" , literally City University of Istanbul) is a private, non-profit university located in Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "c4ae848456d08dbd", "doc_id": "hp_0470400943ee62eb"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0470400943ee62eb"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="City University of Istanbul">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The literal English translation of \"İstanbul Şehir Üniversitesi\".", "chunk_id": "c4ae848456d08dbd", "doc_id": "hp_0470400943ee62eb"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Istanbul Şehir University (Turkish: \"İstanbul Şehir Üniversitesi\" , literally City University of Istanbul) is a private, non-profit university located in Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "c4ae848456d08dbd", "doc_id": "hp_0470400943ee62eb"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0470400943ee62eb"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Istanbul">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The city in Turkey where Istanbul Şehir University is located.", "chunk_id": "c4ae848456d08dbd", "doc_id": "hp_0470400943ee62eb"}, {"text": "Istanbul is a major city in Turkey where Ayakapı is located.", "chunk_id": "6e81cc2224f69a7f", "doc_id": "hp_1e26d1b1943ab6e1"}, {"text": "A city in Turkey where the Gül Mosque is located.", "chunk_id": "8567d31eef2db61e", "doc_id": "hp_7afc03b2a09c3287"}, {"text": "Istanbul is the city where the fine arts academy is located, from which Celal Kandemiroglu graduated.", "chunk_id": "9ced057e330685fe", "doc_id": "hp_88b4fa8c4b3d726e"}, {"text": "A major city in Turkey where the Gazi Atik Ali Pasha Mosque is located.", "chunk_id": "8f5d1ed038b51df1", "doc_id": "hp_90153a2ea74b8250"}, {"text": "Istanbul is a city in Turkey where the Mihrimah Sultan Mosque is located.", "chunk_id": "2b745e897c8565f6", "doc_id": "hp_a52cead96a6e20c2"}, {"text": "The city in Turkey where the Firuz Agha Mosque is located.", "chunk_id": "f4b3646a27921496", "doc_id": "hp_ac4c6b296e4e7b01"}, {"text": "A major city in Turkey, formerly known as Constantinople.", "chunk_id": "dffd0908b3e87179", "doc_id": "hp_c9f9cf36b314fa0a"}, {"text": "Istanbul is a city in Turkey where the Süleymaniye Mosque is located.", "chunk_id": "3996f0dbbfdc0462", "doc_id": "hp_f0503f227612f6c6"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Istanbul Şehir University (Turkish: \"İstanbul Şehir Üniversitesi\" , literally City University of Istanbul) is a private, non-profit university located in Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "c4ae848456d08dbd", "doc_id": "hp_0470400943ee62eb"}, {"text": "Ayakapı (Turkish: \"The Gate of the Saint\", \"The holy gate\" ) (the toponym comes from the Turkish word \"Aya\", derived from pronunciation of the Greek word ἁγἰα, mean. \"female Saint\" and the Turkish word \"kapı\", mean. \"gate\") is a quarter of Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "6e81cc2224f69a7f", "doc_id": "hp_1e26d1b1943ab6e1"}, {"text": "Gül Mosque (Turkish: \"Gül Camii\" , meaning: \"The Mosque of the Rose\" in English) is a former Eastern Orthodox church in Istanbul, Turkey, converted into a mosque by the Ottomans.", "chunk_id": "8567d31eef2db61e", "doc_id": "hp_7afc03b2a09c3287"}, {"text": "After graduating at the fine arts academy in Istanbul he started to offer his comics to the Bastei-Verlag in Germany around 1978.", "chunk_id": "9ced057e330685fe", "doc_id": "hp_88b4fa8c4b3d726e"}, {"text": "The Gazi Atik Ali Pasha Mosque (Turkish: \"Gazi Atik Ali Paşa Camii\" ) is an old Ottoman mosque located in the Çemberlitaş neighbourhood of the Fatih district in Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "8f5d1ed038b51df1", "doc_id": "hp_90153a2ea74b8250"}, {"text": "The Mihrimah Sultan Mosque (Turkish: 'Mihrimah Sultan Camii' ) is an Ottoman mosque located in the Edirnekapı neighborhood near the Byzantine land walls of Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "2b745e897c8565f6", "doc_id": "hp_a52cead96a6e20c2"}, {"text": "The Firuz Ağa Mosque (Turkish: \"Firuz Ağa Camii\" ) is an old Ottoman mosque in the Fatih district of Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "f4b3646a27921496", "doc_id": "hp_ac4c6b296e4e7b01"}, {"text": "It stands in what is now Gülhane Park, Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "dffd0908b3e87179", "doc_id": "hp_c9f9cf36b314fa0a"}, {"text": "The Süleymaniye Mosque (Turkish: \"Süleymaniye Camii\" , ] ) is an Ottoman imperial mosque located on the Third Hill of Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "3996f0dbbfdc0462", "doc_id": "hp_f0503f227612f6c6"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0470400943ee62eb", "hp_1e26d1b1943ab6e1", "hp_7afc03b2a09c3287", "hp_88b4fa8c4b3d726e", "hp_90153a2ea74b8250", "hp_a52cead96a6e20c2", "hp_ac4c6b296e4e7b01", "hp_c9f9cf36b314fa0a", "hp_f0503f227612f6c6"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Turkey">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The country where Istanbul Şehir University is located.", "chunk_id": "c4ae848456d08dbd", "doc_id": "hp_0470400943ee62eb"}, {"text": "Turkey is the country where Istanbul and Ayakapı are located.", "chunk_id": "6e81cc2224f69a7f", "doc_id": "hp_1e26d1b1943ab6e1"}, {"text": "A country where Istanbul is located.", "chunk_id": "8567d31eef2db61e", "doc_id": "hp_7afc03b2a09c3287"}, {"text": "Turkey is the birthplace of Celal Kandemiroglu.", "chunk_id": "9ced057e330685fe", "doc_id": "hp_88b4fa8c4b3d726e"}, {"text": "A country where Istanbul is located.", "chunk_id": "8f5d1ed038b51df1", "doc_id": "hp_90153a2ea74b8250"}, {"text": "Turkey is a country where Istanbul is located.", "chunk_id": "2b745e897c8565f6", "doc_id": "hp_a52cead96a6e20c2"}, {"text": "The country where Istanbul is located.", "chunk_id": "f4b3646a27921496", "doc_id": "hp_ac4c6b296e4e7b01"}, {"text": "A transcontinental country located mainly on the Anatolian Peninsula in Western Asia, with a smaller portion on the Balkan Peninsula in Southeast Europe.", "chunk_id": "dffd0908b3e87179", "doc_id": "hp_c9f9cf36b314fa0a"}, {"text": "Turkey is a country where Istanbul is located.", "chunk_id": "3996f0dbbfdc0462", "doc_id": "hp_f0503f227612f6c6"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Istanbul Şehir University (Turkish: \"İstanbul Şehir Üniversitesi\" , literally City University of Istanbul) is a private, non-profit university located in Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "c4ae848456d08dbd", "doc_id": "hp_0470400943ee62eb"}, {"text": "Ayakapı (Turkish: \"The Gate of the Saint\", \"The holy gate\" ) (the toponym comes from the Turkish word \"Aya\", derived from pronunciation of the Greek word ἁγἰα, mean. \"female Saint\" and the Turkish word \"kapı\", mean. \"gate\") is a quarter of Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "6e81cc2224f69a7f", "doc_id": "hp_1e26d1b1943ab6e1"}, {"text": "Gül Mosque (Turkish: \"Gül Camii\" , meaning: \"The Mosque of the Rose\" in English) is a former Eastern Orthodox church in Istanbul, Turkey, converted into a mosque by the Ottomans.", "chunk_id": "8567d31eef2db61e", "doc_id": "hp_7afc03b2a09c3287"}, {"text": "He was born in 1953 in Turkey and made his first comic when he was five years old.", "chunk_id": "9ced057e330685fe", "doc_id": "hp_88b4fa8c4b3d726e"}, {"text": "The Gazi Atik Ali Pasha Mosque (Turkish: \"Gazi Atik Ali Paşa Camii\" ) is an old Ottoman mosque located in the Çemberlitaş neighbourhood of the Fatih district in Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "8f5d1ed038b51df1", "doc_id": "hp_90153a2ea74b8250"}, {"text": "The Mihrimah Sultan Mosque (Turkish: 'Mihrimah Sultan Camii' ) is an Ottoman mosque located in the Edirnekapı neighborhood near the Byzantine land walls of Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "2b745e897c8565f6", "doc_id": "hp_a52cead96a6e20c2"}, {"text": "The Firuz Ağa Mosque (Turkish: \"Firuz Ağa Camii\" ) is an old Ottoman mosque in the Fatih district of Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "f4b3646a27921496", "doc_id": "hp_ac4c6b296e4e7b01"}, {"text": "It stands in what is now Gülhane Park, Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "dffd0908b3e87179", "doc_id": "hp_c9f9cf36b314fa0a"}, {"text": "The Süleymaniye Mosque (Turkish: \"Süleymaniye Camii\" , ] ) is an Ottoman imperial mosque located on the Third Hill of Istanbul, Turkey.", "chunk_id": "3996f0dbbfdc0462", "doc_id": "hp_f0503f227612f6c6"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0470400943ee62eb", "hp_1e26d1b1943ab6e1", "hp_7afc03b2a09c3287", "hp_88b4fa8c4b3d726e", "hp_90153a2ea74b8250", "hp_a52cead96a6e20c2", "hp_ac4c6b296e4e7b01", "hp_c9f9cf36b314fa0a", "hp_f0503f227612f6c6"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="2008">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The year Istanbul Şehir University was established.", "chunk_id": "c4ae848456d08dbd", "doc_id": "hp_0470400943ee62eb"}, {"text": "The year Amanda Dameron joined Dwell.", "chunk_id": "e3034f5ee568e837", "doc_id": "hp_d20dd81b0b3d11dc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was established in 2008 by the Bilim ve Sanat Vakfı (BiSaV or BSV, English: Foundation for Science and Arts ).", "chunk_id": "c4ae848456d08dbd", "doc_id": "hp_0470400943ee62eb"}, {"text": "Current Editor-in-Chief and EVP Content Amanda Dameron joined Dwell in 2008.", "chunk_id": "e3034f5ee568e837", "doc_id": "hp_d20dd81b0b3d11dc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0470400943ee62eb", "hp_d20dd81b0b3d11dc"]</data>
