<node id="Queensland">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A state in Australia.", "chunk_id": "2dd066198b3cb968", "doc_id": "hp_079ae3daf7c24649"}, {"text": "Queensland, Australia is a native location for Oenanthe javanica.", "chunk_id": "ec6a06d2240b9f28", "doc_id": "hp_5af6f615361404c2"}, {"text": "A state in Australia where Chermside is located.", "chunk_id": "ba730c4e66833a5a", "doc_id": "hp_5e729b3de393ded8"}, {"text": "Queensland is a state in Australia.", "chunk_id": "fbf61adc749de348", "doc_id": "hp_c5ef67346cb356c5"}, {"text": "A state in Australia.", "chunk_id": "e46c2a621963ae57", "doc_id": "hp_d9c16ac1a14c473e"}, {"text": "A state in Australia where Capalaba is located.", "chunk_id": "73348332beb37e73", "doc_id": "hp_f5380a35f3a97562"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Indooroopilly Shopping Centre (formerly Indooroopilly Shoppingtown) is a major regional shopping centre in the western suburb of Indooroopilly in the City of Brisbane, Queensland, Australia.", "chunk_id": "2dd066198b3cb968", "doc_id": "hp_079ae3daf7c24649"}, {"text": "It has a widespread native distribution in temperate Asia and tropical Asia, and is also native to Queensland, Australia.", "chunk_id": "ec6a06d2240b9f28", "doc_id": "hp_5af6f615361404c2"}, {"text": "The Chermside bus station, at Chermside, Queensland, is serviced by TransLink bus routes.", "chunk_id": "ba730c4e66833a5a", "doc_id": "hp_5e729b3de393ded8"}, {"text": "The Aspley Bus Station, at Aspley, Queensland, Australia, is served by TransLink bus routes.", "chunk_id": "fbf61adc749de348", "doc_id": "hp_c5ef67346cb356c5"}, {"text": "The Victoria Point Bus Station, at Victoria Point Queensland, is serviced by TransLink bus routes.", "chunk_id": "e46c2a621963ae57", "doc_id": "hp_d9c16ac1a14c473e"}, {"text": "The Capalaba Bus Station, at Capalaba, Queensland, is serviced by TransLink bus routes.", "chunk_id": "73348332beb37e73", "doc_id": "hp_f5380a35f3a97562"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_079ae3daf7c24649", "hp_5af6f615361404c2", "hp_5e729b3de393ded8", "hp_c5ef67346cb356c5", "hp_d9c16ac1a14c473e", "hp_f5380a35f3a97562"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Australia">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A country and continent.", "chunk_id": "2dd066198b3cb968", "doc_id": "hp_079ae3daf7c24649"}, {"text": "A country where the album Evermore was released.", "chunk_id": "e5ddd6707aee70ac", "doc_id": "hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a"}, {"text": "Australia is a country.", "chunk_id": "1908956e32efc2d1", "doc_id": "hp_1414681ce139d8b0"}, {"text": "An epic historical romantic drama film directed by Baz Luhrmann, released in 2008.", "chunk_id": "6e2520e76c300111", "doc_id": "hp_2f6efd859dd967a9"}, {"text": "Australia is the nationality of the tennis player John Frawley.", "chunk_id": "f15e52cd4eed7a68", "doc_id": "hp_36218807b21ee7a5"}, {"text": "Australia is a country with which Mark Philippoussis won two Davis Cup titles.", "chunk_id": "4d09236de753d49e", "doc_id": "hp_3a454527b720381c"}, {"text": "A country and continent.", "chunk_id": "539ff347cbaa67c2", "doc_id": "hp_4ff036de49247657"}, {"text": "A country where the song was also released as a single.", "chunk_id": "159b19643bce98d8", "doc_id": "hp_593b07de5fa84d4e"}, {"text": "A country where Evermore is based and where the ARIA Singles Chart is located.", "chunk_id": "bf8df350b104fc54", "doc_id": "hp_5a1e23a825efe5cb"}, {"text": "Australia is a country where Queensland, a native location for Oenanthe javanica, is situated.", "chunk_id": "ec6a06d2240b9f28", "doc_id": "hp_5af6f615361404c2"}, {"text": "Australia is the country Lionel Van Praag is from.", "chunk_id": "1606e1aa9cfc722b", "doc_id": "hp_631a38475ad4383e"}, {"text": "A country where Thomas Welton Stanford lived most of his adult life.", "chunk_id": "232d1486ef3116d2", "doc_id": "hp_69dbe4380588b108"}, {"text": "The country of origin for the rider Jack Young.", "chunk_id": "3f37f1d57cb3f639", "doc_id": "hp_71501f4cf0223b43"}, {"text": "A country where all three series of 'Richard Hammond's Engineering Connections' are available on DVD.", "chunk_id": "ec87e3591d7acc99", "doc_id": "hp_8429039f0ec9c01d"}, {"text": "Andrea Perego worked as a broadcaster for SBS Radio in Australia.", "chunk_id": "a005ee5e6658f2c6", "doc_id": "hp_8dc0bafcecb1ab98"}, {"text": "Australia is a country and continent.", "chunk_id": "2b4451cce149d95e", "doc_id": "hp_97a390a9fc775a07"}, {"text": "A country where Tasmania is located.", "chunk_id": "c759b172d9ba0764", "doc_id": "hp_992323b5620cfbfd"}, {"text": "Australia is a country.", "chunk_id": "17ec0b20721cd11e", "doc_id": "hp_9be184228ee1e48d"}, {"text": "Australia is the nationality of Ross Case.", "chunk_id": "9f06e9e836369a70", "doc_id": "hp_9e113091020e9e0d"}, {"text": "Australia is the country Ken Rosewall is from.", "chunk_id": "430b814f8abe3ad2", "doc_id": "hp_a8d43feead8ab699"}, {"text": "A location where the tour continued.", "chunk_id": "da03dc4aa612a116", "doc_id": "hp_b1fcfbca9c340147"}, {"text": "Australia is a country where the ARIA Singles Chart is located.", "chunk_id": "d4c212cc890b725d", "doc_id": "hp_b314ee58b364424a"}, {"text": "Australia is a country.", "chunk_id": "fbf61adc749de348", "doc_id": "hp_c5ef67346cb356c5"}, {"text": "A country where Dancing on Ice was titled 'Torvill and Dean's Dancing on Ice' and was axed after one series.", "chunk_id": "11198ab313088443", "doc_id": "hp_d35c5fabe367cde8"}, {"text": "Australia is a country where Atherosperma moschatum is native.", "chunk_id": "e1044c549e97de7c", "doc_id": "hp_dce12d59ef968ea1"}, {"text": "It is located on the Mid North Coast of New South Wales, Australia, about 390 km north of Sydney, and 570 km south of Brisbane.", "chunk_id": "6223f89935ee9cfe", "doc_id": "hp_de00d7ebc47399cc"}, {"text": "Australia is a country where Fuscospora gunnii is endemic to Tasmania.", "chunk_id": "cc7d1eb73c73bea4", "doc_id": "hp_f4fcfac633a5b005"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Indooroopilly Shopping Centre (formerly Indooroopilly Shoppingtown) is a major regional shopping centre in the western suburb of Indooroopilly in the City of Brisbane, Queensland, Australia.", "chunk_id": "2dd066198b3cb968", "doc_id": "hp_079ae3daf7c24649"}, {"text": "Evermore is the self-titled international debut album by New Zealand rock band Evermore, which was also released in Australia and New Zealand on 12 March 2010.", "chunk_id": "e5ddd6707aee70ac", "doc_id": "hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a"}, {"text": "Port Macquarie Airport (IATA: PQQ, ICAO: YPMQ) is an airport in Port Macquarie, New South Wales, Australia.", "chunk_id": "1908956e32efc2d1", "doc_id": "hp_1414681ce139d8b0"}, {"text": "His 2008 film \"Australia\" is an epic historical romantic drama film starring Hugh Jackman and Nicole Kidman.", "chunk_id": "6e2520e76c300111", "doc_id": "hp_2f6efd859dd967a9"}, {"text": "John Frawley (born 4 July 1965 in Redcliffe) is an Australian retired tennis player.", "chunk_id": "f15e52cd4eed7a68", "doc_id": "hp_36218807b21ee7a5"}, {"text": "His greatest achievements are winning two Davis Cup titles with Australia in 1999 and 2003, winning the deciding rubber in the final of each.", "chunk_id": "4d09236de753d49e", "doc_id": "hp_3a454527b720381c"}, {"text": "From 1975 onwards Australia and New Zealand held their own World Individual Speedway championship qualifying rounds.", "chunk_id": "539ff347cbaa67c2", "doc_id": "hp_4ff036de49247657"}, {"text": "The song was also released as a single in Australia under the name \"By Your Side\", due to the Australian bush fires which were happening at the time.", "chunk_id": "159b19643bce98d8", "doc_id": "hp_593b07de5fa84d4e"}, {"text": "It peaked at No. 4 on their native RIANZ Singles Chart in New Zealand and No. 5 on their adopted country of Australia's ARIA Singles Chart.", "chunk_id": "bf8df350b104fc54", "doc_id": "hp_5a1e23a825efe5cb"}, {"text": "It has a widespread native distribution in temperate Asia and tropical Asia, and is also native to Queensland, Australia.", "chunk_id": "ec6a06d2240b9f28", "doc_id": "hp_5af6f615361404c2"}, {"text": "The 1936 Individual Speedway World Championship was the first ever Speedway World Championship and was won by Lionel Van Praag of Australia.", "chunk_id": "1606e1aa9cfc722b", "doc_id": "hp_631a38475ad4383e"}, {"text": "Although living most of his adult life in Australia, he kept his American citizenship and served intermittently as honorary American vice consul-general in Melbourne.", "chunk_id": "232d1486ef3116d2", "doc_id": "hp_69dbe4380588b108"}, {"text": "Australian rider Jack Young became the first ever dual winner (and the first to win two in a row) when he won his second straight World Championship after scoring 14 points.", "chunk_id": "3f37f1d57cb3f639", "doc_id": "hp_71501f4cf0223b43"}, {"text": "In Australia, all three series are available on DVD, either separately or as a box-set.", "chunk_id": "ec87e3591d7acc99", "doc_id": "hp_8429039f0ec9c01d"}, {"text": "In Australia he worked as a broadcaster for SBS Radio, doing reports that had wide resonance, such as the one about the murder of two Swiss Guards in the Vatican.", "chunk_id": "a005ee5e6658f2c6", "doc_id": "hp_8dc0bafcecb1ab98"}, {"text": "Macquarie County is one of the 141 Cadastral divisions of New South Wales, Australia.", "chunk_id": "2b4451cce149d95e", "doc_id": "hp_97a390a9fc775a07"}, {"text": "The Hotel Grand Chancellor is a twelve-storey hotel located on the waterfront of Hobart, Tasmania, Australia", "chunk_id": "c759b172d9ba0764", "doc_id": "hp_992323b5620cfbfd"}, {"text": "Bonny Hills is a town in New South Wales, Australia about 30 minutes drive south of Port Macquarie.", "chunk_id": "17ec0b20721cd11e", "doc_id": "hp_9be184228ee1e48d"}, {"text": "Ross Case (born 1 November 1951) is an Australian former tennis player.", "chunk_id": "9f06e9e836369a70", "doc_id": "hp_9e113091020e9e0d"}, {"text": "Ken Rosewall Kenneth Robert Rosewall {'1': \", '2': \", '3': 'AM, MBE', '4': \"} (born 2 November 1934) is a former world top-ranking amateur and professional tennis player from Australia.", "chunk_id": "430b814f8abe3ad2", "doc_id": "hp_a8d43feead8ab699"}, {"text": "The tour continued to Australia in mid-2009.", "chunk_id": "da03dc4aa612a116", "doc_id": "hp_b1fcfbca9c340147"}, {"text": "The song was released in October 2006 and peaked at No. 15 on the RIANZ Singles Chart in New Zealand and number one on the ARIA Singles Chart, making it Evermore's most successful single in Australia.", "chunk_id": "d4c212cc890b725d", "doc_id": "hp_b314ee58b364424a"}, {"text": "The Aspley Bus Station, at Aspley, Queensland, Australia, is served by TransLink bus routes.", "chunk_id": "fbf61adc749de348", "doc_id": "hp_c5ef67346cb356c5"}, {"text": "In Australia, where it was titled \"Torvill and Dean's Dancing on Ice\", it was axed after just one series owing to production costs.", "chunk_id": "11198ab313088443", "doc_id": "hp_d35c5fabe367cde8"}, {"text": "Atherosperma moschatum, the southern sassafras or blackheart sassafras, is an evergreen tree native to the cool temperate rainforests of Tasmania, Victoria, and New South Wales in Australia.", "chunk_id": "e1044c549e97de7c", "doc_id": "hp_dce12d59ef968ea1"}, {"text": "It is located on the Mid North Coast of New South Wales, Australia, about 390 km north of Sydney, and 570 km south of Brisbane.", "chunk_id": "6223f89935ee9cfe", "doc_id": "hp_de00d7ebc47399cc"}, {"text": "Fuscospora gunnii, the tanglefoot- or deciduous beech, or fagus, is a deciduous shrub endemic to the highlands of Tasmania, Australia.", "chunk_id": "cc7d1eb73c73bea4", "doc_id": "hp_f4fcfac633a5b005"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_079ae3daf7c24649", "hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a", "hp_1414681ce139d8b0", "hp_2f6efd859dd967a9", "hp_36218807b21ee7a5", "hp_3a454527b720381c", "hp_4ff036de49247657", "hp_593b07de5fa84d4e", "hp_5a1e23a825efe5cb", "hp_5af6f615361404c2", "hp_631a38475ad4383e", "hp_69dbe4380588b108", "hp_71501f4cf0223b43", "hp_8429039f0ec9c01d", "hp_8dc0bafcecb1ab98", "hp_97a390a9fc775a07", "hp_992323b5620cfbfd", "hp_9be184228ee1e48d", "hp_9e113091020e9e0d", "hp_a8d43feead8ab699", "hp_b1fcfbca9c340147", "hp_b314ee58b364424a", "hp_c5ef67346cb356c5", "hp_d35c5fabe367cde8", "hp_dce12d59ef968ea1", "hp_de00d7ebc47399cc", "hp_f4fcfac633a5b005"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Myer">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A department store chain in Australia.", "chunk_id": "2dd066198b3cb968", "doc_id": "hp_079ae3daf7c24649"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It hosts over 360 specialty stores and is the largest shopping centre in the western suburbs of Brisbane, by gross lettable area, and contains the only Myer store in that region.", "chunk_id": "2dd066198b3cb968", "doc_id": "hp_079ae3daf7c24649"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_079ae3daf7c24649"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Danny Elfman">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Daniel Robert Elfman is an American composer, singer, songwriter, and record producer.", "chunk_id": "1870b32e305bfb77", "doc_id": "hp_0812dc58375d3542"}, {"text": "The composer of the score album for the 1989 film \"Batman\".", "chunk_id": "8c1c86c18a223728", "doc_id": "hp_f90b8fdeee8924ac"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Daniel Robert Elfman (born May 29, 1953) is an American composer, singer, songwriter, and record producer.", "chunk_id": "1870b32e305bfb77", "doc_id": "hp_0812dc58375d3542"}, {"text": "Batman: Original Motion Picture Score is the score album for the 1989 film \"Batman\" by Danny Elfman.", "chunk_id": "8c1c86c18a223728", "doc_id": "hp_f90b8fdeee8924ac"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0812dc58375d3542", "hp_f90b8fdeee8924ac"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Oingo Boingo">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Oingo Boingo was a band from 1974 to 1995, for which Danny Elfman was the lead singer and songwriter.", "chunk_id": "1870b32e305bfb77", "doc_id": "hp_0812dc58375d3542"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "and for being the lead singer and songwriter for the band Oingo Boingo from 1974 to 1995.", "chunk_id": "1870b32e305bfb77", "doc_id": "hp_0812dc58375d3542"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0812dc58375d3542"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Tim Burton">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Tim Burton is a director with whom Danny Elfman has had frequent collaborations.", "chunk_id": "1870b32e305bfb77", "doc_id": "hp_0812dc58375d3542"}, {"text": "The director of the film \"Miss Peregrine's Home for Peculiar Children\".", "chunk_id": "1e3c115665e783ed", "doc_id": "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8"}, {"text": "Tim Burton is a director associated with the film \"Edward Scissorhands\".", "chunk_id": "cd3dc8041fe2ba4b", "doc_id": "hp_23773bc65d0154a3"}, {"text": "The director who influenced Jon Peters' decision regarding Danny Elfman as the composer for the film \"Batman\".", "chunk_id": "8c1c86c18a223728", "doc_id": "hp_f90b8fdeee8924ac"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "in particular his frequent collaborations with director Tim Burton, and for being the lead singer and songwriter for the band Oingo Boingo from 1974 to 1995.", "chunk_id": "1870b32e305bfb77", "doc_id": "hp_0812dc58375d3542"}, {"text": "The song was made available via digital download, and is featured on the soundtrack of the film \"Miss Peregrine's Home for Peculiar Children\" which was directed by Tim Burton.", "chunk_id": "1e3c115665e783ed", "doc_id": "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8"}, {"text": "He is also known as Kevin, Winona Ryder's little brother, in Tim Burton's \"Edward Scissorhands\".", "chunk_id": "cd3dc8041fe2ba4b", "doc_id": "hp_23773bc65d0154a3"}, {"text": "According to the \"Batman\" DVD Special Edition, Elfman said that producer Jon Peters was not sure about him as a composer until Tim Burton made him play the main titles.", "chunk_id": "8c1c86c18a223728", "doc_id": "hp_f90b8fdeee8924ac"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0812dc58375d3542", "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8", "hp_23773bc65d0154a3", "hp_f90b8fdeee8924ac"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Evermore (Evermore album)">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The self-titled international debut album by the New Zealand rock band Evermore.", "chunk_id": "e5ddd6707aee70ac", "doc_id": "hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Evermore is the self-titled international debut album by New Zealand rock band Evermore, which was also released in Australia and New Zealand on 12 March 2010.", "chunk_id": "e5ddd6707aee70ac", "doc_id": "hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Evermore">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A New Zealand rock band.", "chunk_id": "e5ddd6707aee70ac", "doc_id": "hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a"}, {"text": "Evermore is an alternative rock band formed in 1999.", "chunk_id": "d4587b7df6346e8b", "doc_id": "hp_43e4303474c939c5"}, {"text": "An alternative rock band.", "chunk_id": "bf8df350b104fc54", "doc_id": "hp_5a1e23a825efe5cb"}, {"text": "Evermore is an alternative rock band.", "chunk_id": "d4c212cc890b725d", "doc_id": "hp_b314ee58b364424a"}, {"text": "A band that released the song \"Between the Lines\".", "chunk_id": "5a7629ff0f885755", "doc_id": "hp_b33b91420ae271b4"}, {"text": "Evermore is a New Zealand band.", "chunk_id": "502a922827b4a3a3", "doc_id": "hp_fdf3095075ada67d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Evermore is the self-titled international debut album by New Zealand rock band Evermore, which was also released in Australia and New Zealand on 12 March 2010.", "chunk_id": "e5ddd6707aee70ac", "doc_id": "hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a"}, {"text": "Hume is the youngest of three brothers (with Peter Hume and Jon Hume) who make up the alternative rock band, Evermore since 1999.", "chunk_id": "d4587b7df6346e8b", "doc_id": "hp_43e4303474c939c5"}, {"text": "\"Running\" is the lead single by alternative rock band Evermore, taken from their second studio album, \"Real Life\" (July 2006).", "chunk_id": "bf8df350b104fc54", "doc_id": "hp_5a1e23a825efe5cb"}, {"text": "\"Light Surrounding You\" is the second single by alternative rock band, Evermore, taken from their second studio album, \"Real Life\" (June 2006).", "chunk_id": "d4c212cc890b725d", "doc_id": "hp_b314ee58b364424a"}, {"text": "\"Between the Lines\" is the first single by Evermore, taken from their third studio album \"\".", "chunk_id": "5a7629ff0f885755", "doc_id": "hp_b33b91420ae271b4"}, {"text": "Jon Hume (born 6 November 1983) is the lead singer of Evermore.", "chunk_id": "502a922827b4a3a3", "doc_id": "hp_fdf3095075ada67d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a", "hp_43e4303474c939c5", "hp_5a1e23a825efe5cb", "hp_b314ee58b364424a", "hp_b33b91420ae271b4", "hp_fdf3095075ada67d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="New Zealand">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A country where the album Evermore was released.", "chunk_id": "e5ddd6707aee70ac", "doc_id": "hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a"}, {"text": "New Zealand is a country native to Coprosma repens.", "chunk_id": "3dcbe023e23fe94c", "doc_id": "hp_31165984928ebb87"}, {"text": "New Zealand is a country where Dann Hume was born.", "chunk_id": "d4587b7df6346e8b", "doc_id": "hp_43e4303474c939c5"}, {"text": "A country in the southwestern Pacific Ocean.", "chunk_id": "539ff347cbaa67c2", "doc_id": "hp_4ff036de49247657"}, {"text": "A country where Evermore is from and where the RIANZ Singles Chart is located.", "chunk_id": "bf8df350b104fc54", "doc_id": "hp_5a1e23a825efe5cb"}, {"text": "New Zealand is a location where an infection on Pinus radiata in 1950 was caused by P. kernoviae.", "chunk_id": "f0f758ffcef041f7", "doc_id": "hp_7b90b80a57936da9"}, {"text": "New Zealand is a country where the RIANZ Singles Chart is located.", "chunk_id": "d4c212cc890b725d", "doc_id": "hp_b314ee58b364424a"}, {"text": "A country where the song \"When It's Over\" reached number 6 on the charts.", "chunk_id": "ea9f0bb2bf44b926", "doc_id": "hp_f61e6f2275345f39"}, {"text": "New Zealand is the country where the band Evermore is from.", "chunk_id": "502a922827b4a3a3", "doc_id": "hp_fdf3095075ada67d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Evermore is the self-titled international debut album by New Zealand rock band Evermore, which was also released in Australia and New Zealand on 12 March 2010.", "chunk_id": "e5ddd6707aee70ac", "doc_id": "hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a"}, {"text": "Coprosma repens is a species of flowering shrub or small tree of the genus \"Coprosma\", in the family Rubiaceae, native to New Zealand.", "chunk_id": "3dcbe023e23fe94c", "doc_id": "hp_31165984928ebb87"}, {"text": "Dann Hume (born Daniel Benjamin Cobbe, 1 September 1987, Whangaparaoa, New Zealand) is a singer-songwriter and record producer.", "chunk_id": "d4587b7df6346e8b", "doc_id": "hp_43e4303474c939c5"}, {"text": "It has been open in the past to riders from British dominions and was dominated in its early years by riders from New Zealand such as Barry Briggs and Ivan Mauger this was due to the fact that the British Final formed part of the World Individual Speedway championship qualifying rounds.", "chunk_id": "539ff347cbaa67c2", "doc_id": "hp_4ff036de49247657"}, {"text": "It peaked at No. 4 on their native RIANZ Singles Chart in New Zealand and No. 5 on their adopted country of Australia's ARIA Singles Chart.", "chunk_id": "bf8df350b104fc54", "doc_id": "hp_5a1e23a825efe5cb"}, {"text": "Molecular analysis has revealed that an infection on \"Pinus radiata\", recorded in New Zealand in 1950, was caused by \"P. kernoviae\".", "chunk_id": "f0f758ffcef041f7", "doc_id": "hp_7b90b80a57936da9"}, {"text": "The song was released in October 2006 and peaked at No. 15 on the RIANZ Singles Chart in New Zealand and number one on the ARIA Singles Chart, making it Evermore's most successful single in Australia.", "chunk_id": "d4c212cc890b725d", "doc_id": "hp_b314ee58b364424a"}, {"text": "The song reached number 6 in New Zealand, number 13 on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 and number 32 on the UK Singles Chart.", "chunk_id": "ea9f0bb2bf44b926", "doc_id": "hp_f61e6f2275345f39"}, {"text": "Jon is the eldest of the three brothers who make up the New Zealand band Evermore.", "chunk_id": "502a922827b4a3a3", "doc_id": "hp_fdf3095075ada67d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a", "hp_31165984928ebb87", "hp_43e4303474c939c5", "hp_4ff036de49247657", "hp_5a1e23a825efe5cb", "hp_7b90b80a57936da9", "hp_b314ee58b364424a", "hp_f61e6f2275345f39", "hp_fdf3095075ada67d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="12 March 2010">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The release date of the album Evermore in Australia and New Zealand.", "chunk_id": "e5ddd6707aee70ac", "doc_id": "hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Evermore is the self-titled international debut album by New Zealand rock band Evermore, which was also released in Australia and New Zealand on 12 March 2010.", "chunk_id": "e5ddd6707aee70ac", "doc_id": "hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Underground">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A single from the album Evermore.", "chunk_id": "e5ddd6707aee70ac", "doc_id": "hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The album is a collection of songs from the band's entire history, as well as three new songs including the single \"Underground\".", "chunk_id": "e5ddd6707aee70ac", "doc_id": "hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0813bbee3b26ad1a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Edward Dmytryk">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Edward Dmytryk was a Canadian-born American film director.", "chunk_id": "082328cae5bc4e3a", "doc_id": "hp_085295b872c152bd"}, {"text": "Edward Dmytryk was the director of the film The Human Factor.", "chunk_id": "aa8c9ddffbfcfbbf", "doc_id": "hp_68a51af21818248e"}, {"text": "Edward Dmytryk was the director of the 1935 film The Hawk.", "chunk_id": "468a7c3fd34321f3", "doc_id": "hp_af70c5218eca2efc"}, {"text": "Edward Dmytryk was a Polish-American film director.", "chunk_id": "f4d99f18a4f175d5", "doc_id": "hp_cda28e9f1cb25d71"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Edward Dmytryk (September 4, 1908 – July 1, 1999) was a Canadian-born American film director.", "chunk_id": "082328cae5bc4e3a", "doc_id": "hp_085295b872c152bd"}, {"text": "The Human Factor is a 1975 drama film directed by Edward Dmytryk and starring George Kennedy and John Mills.", "chunk_id": "aa8c9ddffbfcfbbf", "doc_id": "hp_68a51af21818248e"}, {"text": "The Hawk is a 1935 American Western film directed by Edward Dmytryk.", "chunk_id": "468a7c3fd34321f3", "doc_id": "hp_af70c5218eca2efc"}, {"text": "Cornered is a 1945 film noir starring Dick Powell and directed by Edward Dmytryk.", "chunk_id": "f4d99f18a4f175d5", "doc_id": "hp_cda28e9f1cb25d71"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_085295b872c152bd", "hp_68a51af21818248e", "hp_af70c5218eca2efc", "hp_cda28e9f1cb25d71"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="films noir">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Films noir refers to a style of filmmaking that Edward Dmytryk was known for in the 1940s.", "chunk_id": "082328cae5bc4e3a", "doc_id": "hp_085295b872c152bd"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He was known for his 1940s \"films noir\" and received an Oscar nomination for Best Director for \"Crossfire\" (1947).", "chunk_id": "082328cae5bc4e3a", "doc_id": "hp_085295b872c152bd"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_085295b872c152bd"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Crossfire">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Crossfire is a film for which Edward Dmytryk received an Oscar nomination for Best Director.", "chunk_id": "082328cae5bc4e3a", "doc_id": "hp_085295b872c152bd"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He was known for his 1940s \"films noir\" and received an Oscar nomination for Best Director for \"Crossfire\" (1947).", "chunk_id": "082328cae5bc4e3a", "doc_id": "hp_085295b872c152bd"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_085295b872c152bd"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Governor of Santiago del Estero">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Governor of Santiago del Estero is a citizen of the Santiago del Estero Province, in Argentina, holding the office of governor for the corresponding period.", "chunk_id": "e5aa7223c4fd8868", "doc_id": "hp_0936e1baff654759"}, {"text": "Governor of Santiago del Estero is a political office.", "chunk_id": "edd44b1129c36be6", "doc_id": "hp_f59efa62f9d38b97"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The Governor of Santiago del Estero is a citizen of the Santiago del Estero Province, in Argentina, holding the office of governor for the corresponding period.", "chunk_id": "e5aa7223c4fd8868", "doc_id": "hp_0936e1baff654759"}, {"text": "Governor of Santiago del Estero since 2005, he is a member of the centrist Radical Civic Union (UCR).", "chunk_id": "edd44b1129c36be6", "doc_id": "hp_f59efa62f9d38b97"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0936e1baff654759", "hp_f59efa62f9d38b97"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Santiago del Estero Province">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Santiago del Estero Province is a province in Argentina.", "chunk_id": "e5aa7223c4fd8868", "doc_id": "hp_0936e1baff654759"}, {"text": "A province in northern Argentina.", "chunk_id": "eee0658a37ea7481", "doc_id": "hp_5d6ed7a42a524dc4"}, {"text": "Santiago del Estero Province is a province in Argentina.", "chunk_id": "1c837566de6c327a", "doc_id": "hp_63f113b7dfd806d3"}, {"text": "A province in Argentina.", "chunk_id": "4023165b97b30d1b", "doc_id": "hp_9b9ee7139af0e1c5"}, {"text": "A province in Argentina.", "chunk_id": "248c25f8e90d936e", "doc_id": "hp_c2b1e3eedbd2cd43"}, {"text": "A province in Argentina.", "chunk_id": "c4c74d93654d6651", "doc_id": "hp_d82c744304c9486a"}, {"text": "A province located in the north of Argentina.", "chunk_id": "2d1b699909d5d732", "doc_id": "hp_ef86af7ae75bd3a2"}, {"text": "Santiago del Estero Province is a location in Argentina.", "chunk_id": "edd44b1129c36be6", "doc_id": "hp_f59efa62f9d38b97"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The Governor of Santiago del Estero is a citizen of the Santiago del Estero Province, in Argentina, holding the office of governor for the corresponding period.", "chunk_id": "e5aa7223c4fd8868", "doc_id": "hp_0936e1baff654759"}, {"text": "Santiago del Estero (] , Spanish for \"Saint-James-Upon-The-Lagoon\") is the capital of Santiago del Estero Province in northern Argentina.", "chunk_id": "eee0658a37ea7481", "doc_id": "hp_5d6ed7a42a524dc4"}, {"text": "Sixto Doroteo Palavecino (March 31, 1915, Barrancas, Salavina, Santiago del Estero Province, Argentina – April 24, 2009, Santiago del Estero, same province) was a poet, musician and singer of Argentine folk music, who started playing the violin when he was 10 years old.", "chunk_id": "1c837566de6c327a", "doc_id": "hp_63f113b7dfd806d3"}, {"text": "Río Hondo Department (Spanish: \"Departamento Río Hondo\" ) is a department of Argentina in Santiago del Estero Province.", "chunk_id": "4023165b97b30d1b", "doc_id": "hp_9b9ee7139af0e1c5"}, {"text": "The National University of Santiago del Estero (Spanish: \"Universidad Nacional de Santiago del Estero\" ) is an Argentine national university located in the capital of Santiago del Estero Province.", "chunk_id": "248c25f8e90d936e", "doc_id": "hp_c2b1e3eedbd2cd43"}, {"text": "Vicecomodoro Ángel de la Paz Aragonés Airport (Spanish: \"Aeropuerto de Santiago del Estero – Ángel de la Paz Aragonés\" ) (IATA: SDE, ICAO: SANE) is located 6 km north-northwest of the center of Santiago del Estero, a city in the Santiago del Estero Province of Argentina.", "chunk_id": "c4c74d93654d6651", "doc_id": "hp_d82c744304c9486a"}, {"text": "Santiago del Estero Province", "chunk_id": "2d1b699909d5d732", "doc_id": "hp_ef86af7ae75bd3a2"}, {"text": "Gerardo Zamora (born January 6, 1964) is an Argentine politician from Santiago del Estero Province.", "chunk_id": "edd44b1129c36be6", "doc_id": "hp_f59efa62f9d38b97"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0936e1baff654759", "hp_5d6ed7a42a524dc4", "hp_63f113b7dfd806d3", "hp_9b9ee7139af0e1c5", "hp_c2b1e3eedbd2cd43", "hp_d82c744304c9486a", "hp_ef86af7ae75bd3a2", "hp_f59efa62f9d38b97"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Argentina">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Argentina is a country where the Santiago del Estero Province is located.", "chunk_id": "e5aa7223c4fd8868", "doc_id": "hp_0936e1baff654759"}, {"text": "The country of origin for Claudia Albertario Rodríguez.", "chunk_id": "17bdebd96802cd57", "doc_id": "hp_130e948bad92c9a5"}, {"text": "Argentina is the country where Árraga is located.", "chunk_id": "1169ed720e69619f", "doc_id": "hp_20739c2399543481"}, {"text": "A country in South America.", "chunk_id": "eee0658a37ea7481", "doc_id": "hp_5d6ed7a42a524dc4"}, {"text": "Argentina is a country.", "chunk_id": "1c837566de6c327a", "doc_id": "hp_63f113b7dfd806d3"}, {"text": "Argentina is a country.", "chunk_id": "3e623f78834fd3ec", "doc_id": "hp_7151fb458fd16091"}, {"text": "The country where the film Así es el tango was made and where Argentine tango was a popular genre.", "chunk_id": "21b8d3828adf14e8", "doc_id": "hp_795e409d70a760a7"}, {"text": "A country in South America.", "chunk_id": "4023165b97b30d1b", "doc_id": "hp_9b9ee7139af0e1c5"}, {"text": "A country where Santiago del Estero Province is located.", "chunk_id": "c4c74d93654d6651", "doc_id": "hp_d82c744304c9486a"}, {"text": "A country in the north of which Santiago del Estero Province is located.", "chunk_id": "2d1b699909d5d732", "doc_id": "hp_ef86af7ae75bd3a2"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The Governor of Santiago del Estero is a citizen of the Santiago del Estero Province, in Argentina, holding the office of governor for the corresponding period.", "chunk_id": "e5aa7223c4fd8868", "doc_id": "hp_0936e1baff654759"}, {"text": "Claudia Albertario Rodríguez (] ; born May 16, 1977) is an Argentine model, vedette and actress of theatre, television and film.", "chunk_id": "17bdebd96802cd57", "doc_id": "hp_130e948bad92c9a5"}, {"text": "Árraga is a municipality and village in Santiago del Estero in Argentina.", "chunk_id": "1169ed720e69619f", "doc_id": "hp_20739c2399543481"}, {"text": "Santiago del Estero (] , Spanish for \"Saint-James-Upon-The-Lagoon\") is the capital of Santiago del Estero Province in northern Argentina.", "chunk_id": "eee0658a37ea7481", "doc_id": "hp_5d6ed7a42a524dc4"}, {"text": "Sixto Doroteo Palavecino (March 31, 1915, Barrancas, Salavina, Santiago del Estero Province, Argentina – April 24, 2009, Santiago del Estero, same province) was a poet, musician and singer of Argentine folk music, who started playing the violin when he was 10 years old.", "chunk_id": "1c837566de6c327a", "doc_id": "hp_63f113b7dfd806d3"}, {"text": "Añatuya is a city in the province of Santiago del Estero, Argentina.", "chunk_id": "3e623f78834fd3ec", "doc_id": "hp_7151fb458fd16091"}, {"text": "The film is an Argentine tango film a hugely popular genre of the period and Argentine culture.", "chunk_id": "21b8d3828adf14e8", "doc_id": "hp_795e409d70a760a7"}, {"text": "Río Hondo Department (Spanish: \"Departamento Río Hondo\" ) is a department of Argentina in Santiago del Estero Province.", "chunk_id": "4023165b97b30d1b", "doc_id": "hp_9b9ee7139af0e1c5"}, {"text": "Vicecomodoro Ángel de la Paz Aragonés Airport (Spanish: \"Aeropuerto de Santiago del Estero – Ángel de la Paz Aragonés\" ) (IATA: SDE, ICAO: SANE) is located 6 km north-northwest of the center of Santiago del Estero, a city in the Santiago del Estero Province of Argentina.", "chunk_id": "c4c74d93654d6651", "doc_id": "hp_d82c744304c9486a"}, {"text": "Santiago del Estero (] ), also called \"Santiago\", is a province in the north of Argentina.", "chunk_id": "2d1b699909d5d732", "doc_id": "hp_ef86af7ae75bd3a2"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0936e1baff654759", "hp_130e948bad92c9a5", "hp_20739c2399543481", "hp_5d6ed7a42a524dc4", "hp_63f113b7dfd806d3", "hp_7151fb458fd16091", "hp_795e409d70a760a7", "hp_9b9ee7139af0e1c5", "hp_d82c744304c9486a", "hp_ef86af7ae75bd3a2"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
