<node id="Magnoliaceae">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Magnoliaceae is the magnolia family.", "chunk_id": "0b6a1717369be2d5", "doc_id": "hp_09965476daf9cc57"}, {"text": "Magnoliaceae is the family to which Liriodendron belongs.", "chunk_id": "3a3894b0c2506647", "doc_id": "hp_96ca685873d892fc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Magnolia virginiana, most commonly known as sweetbay magnolia, or merely sweetbay (also laurel magnolia, swampbay, swamp magnolia, whitebay, or beaver tree), is a member of the magnolia family, Magnoliaceae.", "chunk_id": "0b6a1717369be2d5", "doc_id": "hp_09965476daf9cc57"}, {"text": "Liriodendron is a genus of two species of characteristically large deciduous trees in the magnolia family (Magnoliaceae).", "chunk_id": "3a3894b0c2506647", "doc_id": "hp_96ca685873d892fc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_09965476daf9cc57", "hp_96ca685873d892fc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Magnolia">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Magnolia is a genus of flowering plants.", "chunk_id": "0b6a1717369be2d5", "doc_id": "hp_09965476daf9cc57"}, {"text": "Magnolia is a genus of plants that the original paper describing Phytophthora kernoviae stated it can infect.", "chunk_id": "f0f758ffcef041f7", "doc_id": "hp_7b90b80a57936da9"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was the first magnolia to be scientifically described under modern rules of botanical nomenclature, and is the type species of the genus \"Magnolia\"; as \"Magnolia\" is also the type genus of all flowering plants (magnoliophytes), this species in a sense typifies all flowering plants.", "chunk_id": "0b6a1717369be2d5", "doc_id": "hp_09965476daf9cc57"}, {"text": "The original paper describing the species, stated it can infect \"Magnolia\" and \"Camellia\" species, \"Pieris formosa\", \"Gevuina avellana\", \"Michelia doltsopa\" and \"Quercus ilex\".", "chunk_id": "f0f758ffcef041f7", "doc_id": "hp_7b90b80a57936da9"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_09965476daf9cc57", "hp_7b90b80a57936da9"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="magnoliophytes">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Magnoliophytes are flowering plants.", "chunk_id": "0b6a1717369be2d5", "doc_id": "hp_09965476daf9cc57"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was the first magnolia to be scientifically described under modern rules of botanical nomenclature, and is the type species of the genus \"Magnolia\"; as \"Magnolia\" is also the type genus of all flowering plants (magnoliophytes), this species in a sense typifies all flowering plants.", "chunk_id": "0b6a1717369be2d5", "doc_id": "hp_09965476daf9cc57"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_09965476daf9cc57"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="No Light, No Light">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A song by English indie rock band Florence and the Machine.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "No Light, No Light is a song by English indie rock band Florence and the Machine from their second studio album, \"Ceremonials\" (2011).", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Florence and the Machine">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An English indie rock band.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}, {"text": "An English indie rock band.", "chunk_id": "1e3c115665e783ed", "doc_id": "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8"}, {"text": "Florence and the Machine is a band whose singer is Florence Welch.", "chunk_id": "95980d0e5191cb2e", "doc_id": "hp_15126f7df8c067b8"}, {"text": "Florence and the Machine is an indie rock band.", "chunk_id": "0238c6f4d8a2d243", "doc_id": "hp_281a1709942e2d2a"}, {"text": "Florence and the Machine is an English indie rock band.", "chunk_id": "2055480b7468cc45", "doc_id": "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f"}, {"text": "An English indie rock band formed in London in 2007.", "chunk_id": "a0e37e5744f28418", "doc_id": "hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e"}, {"text": "An English indie rock band.", "chunk_id": "4a33b3fb6c1ee1fa", "doc_id": "hp_7804b34667739a36"}, {"text": "An English indie rock band.", "chunk_id": "4a9a4f6f83f32605", "doc_id": "hp_ef31a7b23736d77e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "No Light, No Light is a song by English indie rock band Florence and the Machine from their second studio album, \"Ceremonials\" (2011).", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}, {"text": "\"Wish That You Were Here\" is a song by the English indie rock band Florence and the Machine, written by Florence Welch, Andrew Wyatt, and Emilie Haynie, and was released on Island Records on 26 August 2016.", "chunk_id": "1e3c115665e783ed", "doc_id": "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8"}, {"text": "It features vocals from Florence and the Machine singer Florence Welch.", "chunk_id": "95980d0e5191cb2e", "doc_id": "hp_15126f7df8c067b8"}, {"text": "Florence Leontine Mary Welch (born 28 August 1986) is an English musician, singer and songwriter, best known as the vocalist of indie rock band Florence and the Machine.", "chunk_id": "0238c6f4d8a2d243", "doc_id": "hp_281a1709942e2d2a"}, {"text": "Lungs is the debut studio album by English indie rock band Florence and the Machine, released on 3 July 2009 on Island Records.", "chunk_id": "2055480b7468cc45", "doc_id": "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f"}, {"text": "Florence and the Machine (stylised as Florence + the Machine) are an English indie rock band that formed in London in 2007, consisting of lead singer Florence Welch, keyboardist Isabella Summers, and a collaboration of other artists.", "chunk_id": "a0e37e5744f28418", "doc_id": "hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e"}, {"text": "\"What the Water Gave Me\" is a song by English indie rock band Florence and the Machine from their second studio album \"Ceremonials\" (2011).", "chunk_id": "4a33b3fb6c1ee1fa", "doc_id": "hp_7804b34667739a36"}, {"text": "The Ceremonials Tour was the second concert tour by English indie rock band Florence and the Machine.", "chunk_id": "4a9a4f6f83f32605", "doc_id": "hp_ef31a7b23736d77e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f", "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8", "hp_15126f7df8c067b8", "hp_281a1709942e2d2a", "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f", "hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e", "hp_7804b34667739a36", "hp_ef31a7b23736d77e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Ceremonials">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The second studio album by Florence and the Machine.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}, {"text": "The second studio album by Florence and the Machine.", "chunk_id": "4a33b3fb6c1ee1fa", "doc_id": "hp_7804b34667739a36"}, {"text": "A previous tour by Florence and the Machine.", "chunk_id": "4a9a4f6f83f32605", "doc_id": "hp_ef31a7b23736d77e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "No Light, No Light is a song by English indie rock band Florence and the Machine from their second studio album, \"Ceremonials\" (2011).", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}, {"text": "\"What the Water Gave Me\" is a song by English indie rock band Florence and the Machine from their second studio album \"Ceremonials\" (2011).", "chunk_id": "4a33b3fb6c1ee1fa", "doc_id": "hp_7804b34667739a36"}, {"text": "Welch had originally planned to spend over one year touring for \"Ceremonials\" (their previous tour lasted almost three and a half years) before announcing that the December 2012 dates would be the final performances of the tour.", "chunk_id": "4a9a4f6f83f32605", "doc_id": "hp_ef31a7b23736d77e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f", "hp_7804b34667739a36", "hp_ef31a7b23736d77e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Florence Welch">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A band member of Florence and the Machine who co-wrote the song 'No Light, No Light'.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}, {"text": "A songwriter for the song \"Wish That You Were Here\".", "chunk_id": "1e3c115665e783ed", "doc_id": "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8"}, {"text": "Florence Welch is the singer for the band Florence and the Machine.", "chunk_id": "95980d0e5191cb2e", "doc_id": "hp_15126f7df8c067b8"}, {"text": "Florence Welch is an English musician, singer, and songwriter.", "chunk_id": "0238c6f4d8a2d243", "doc_id": "hp_281a1709942e2d2a"}, {"text": "Florence Welch is the frontwoman of Florence and the Machine.", "chunk_id": "2055480b7468cc45", "doc_id": "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f"}, {"text": "The lead singer of the band Florence and the Machine.", "chunk_id": "a0e37e5744f28418", "doc_id": "hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e"}, {"text": "Lead singer of Florence and the Machine.", "chunk_id": "4a33b3fb6c1ee1fa", "doc_id": "hp_7804b34667739a36"}, {"text": "The lead singer of Florence and the Machine.", "chunk_id": "4a9a4f6f83f32605", "doc_id": "hp_ef31a7b23736d77e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The song was written by band members Florence Welch and Isabella Summers while the production was handled by Paul Epworth.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}, {"text": "\"Wish That You Were Here\" is a song by the English indie rock band Florence and the Machine, written by Florence Welch, Andrew Wyatt, and Emilie Haynie, and was released on Island Records on 26 August 2016.", "chunk_id": "1e3c115665e783ed", "doc_id": "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8"}, {"text": "It features vocals from Florence and the Machine singer Florence Welch.", "chunk_id": "95980d0e5191cb2e", "doc_id": "hp_15126f7df8c067b8"}, {"text": "Florence Leontine Mary Welch (born 28 August 1986) is an English musician, singer and songwriter, best known as the vocalist of indie rock band Florence and the Machine.", "chunk_id": "0238c6f4d8a2d243", "doc_id": "hp_281a1709942e2d2a"}, {"text": "Frontwoman Florence Welch experimented with and honed the album's sound with bandmate Isabella Summers, while also collaborating with five record producers including James Ford, Paul Epworth, Steve Mackey.", "chunk_id": "2055480b7468cc45", "doc_id": "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f"}, {"text": "Florence and the Machine (stylised as Florence + the Machine) are an English indie rock band that formed in London in 2007, consisting of lead singer Florence Welch, keyboardist Isabella Summers, and a collaboration of other artists.", "chunk_id": "a0e37e5744f28418", "doc_id": "hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e"}, {"text": "The song was written by lead singer Florence Welch and Francis \"Eg\" White, and produced by Paul Epworth.", "chunk_id": "4a33b3fb6c1ee1fa", "doc_id": "hp_7804b34667739a36"}, {"text": "The tour included performances at Music festivals because it is lead singer Florence Welch's favourite way to perform live.", "chunk_id": "4a9a4f6f83f32605", "doc_id": "hp_ef31a7b23736d77e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f", "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8", "hp_15126f7df8c067b8", "hp_281a1709942e2d2a", "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f", "hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e", "hp_7804b34667739a36", "hp_ef31a7b23736d77e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Isabella Summers">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A band member of Florence and the Machine who co-wrote the song 'No Light, No Light'.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}, {"text": "Isabella Summers is a bandmate of Florence Welch.", "chunk_id": "2055480b7468cc45", "doc_id": "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f"}, {"text": "The keyboardist of the band Florence and the Machine.", "chunk_id": "a0e37e5744f28418", "doc_id": "hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The song was written by band members Florence Welch and Isabella Summers while the production was handled by Paul Epworth.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}, {"text": "Frontwoman Florence Welch experimented with and honed the album's sound with bandmate Isabella Summers, while also collaborating with five record producers including James Ford, Paul Epworth, Steve Mackey.", "chunk_id": "2055480b7468cc45", "doc_id": "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f"}, {"text": "Florence and the Machine (stylised as Florence + the Machine) are an English indie rock band that formed in London in 2007, consisting of lead singer Florence Welch, keyboardist Isabella Summers, and a collaboration of other artists.", "chunk_id": "a0e37e5744f28418", "doc_id": "hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f", "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f", "hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Paul Epworth">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The producer of the song 'No Light, No Light'.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}, {"text": "Paul Epworth is a record producer who collaborated on the album Lungs.", "chunk_id": "2055480b7468cc45", "doc_id": "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f"}, {"text": "The producer of the song \"What the Water Gave Me\".", "chunk_id": "4a33b3fb6c1ee1fa", "doc_id": "hp_7804b34667739a36"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The song was written by band members Florence Welch and Isabella Summers while the production was handled by Paul Epworth.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}, {"text": "Frontwoman Florence Welch experimented with and honed the album's sound with bandmate Isabella Summers, while also collaborating with five record producers including James Ford, Paul Epworth, Steve Mackey.", "chunk_id": "2055480b7468cc45", "doc_id": "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f"}, {"text": "The song was written by lead singer Florence Welch and Francis \"Eg\" White, and produced by Paul Epworth.", "chunk_id": "4a33b3fb6c1ee1fa", "doc_id": "hp_7804b34667739a36"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f", "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f", "hp_7804b34667739a36"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Island Records">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The record label that released the song 'No Light, No Light' as a single.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}, {"text": "The record label that released the song \"Wish That You Were Here\".", "chunk_id": "1e3c115665e783ed", "doc_id": "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8"}, {"text": "Island Records is a record label.", "chunk_id": "2055480b7468cc45", "doc_id": "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Island Records released the song as the second single from the album on 16 January 2012.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}, {"text": "\"Wish That You Were Here\" is a song by the English indie rock band Florence and the Machine, written by Florence Welch, Andrew Wyatt, and Emilie Haynie, and was released on Island Records on 26 August 2016.", "chunk_id": "1e3c115665e783ed", "doc_id": "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8"}, {"text": "Lungs is the debut studio album by English indie rock band Florence and the Machine, released on 3 July 2009 on Island Records.", "chunk_id": "2055480b7468cc45", "doc_id": "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f", "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8", "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Amsterdam">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The city where the song 'No Light, No Light' was first written.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}, {"text": "The city where 'The Next Web conference' was held.", "chunk_id": "903bcebb130bdbec", "doc_id": "hp_c9583d290063614a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The song was the first one written for the album in the band's tour bus in Amsterdam.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}, {"text": "It was screened at The Next Web conference in Amsterdam on 4 April 2008 and broadcast by the Dutch documentary series \"Backlight\" (Dutch: \"Tegenlicht\" ) on Nederland 2 on 7 April 2008.", "chunk_id": "903bcebb130bdbec", "doc_id": "hp_c9583d290063614a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f", "hp_c9583d290063614a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="UK Singles Chart">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A music chart in the United Kingdom.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}, {"text": "A music chart that the song \"Wish That You Were Here\" reached number 128 on.", "chunk_id": "1e3c115665e783ed", "doc_id": "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8"}, {"text": "The UK Singles Chart is a weekly record chart based on record sales in the United Kingdom.", "chunk_id": "992a86ff20688553", "doc_id": "hp_1440798ad8faf801"}, {"text": "A music chart where the song \"When It's Over\" reached number 32.", "chunk_id": "ea9f0bb2bf44b926", "doc_id": "hp_f61e6f2275345f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The song peaked at number fifty on the UK Singles Chart, the Irish Singles Chart and number thirty nine on the US \"Billboard\" Alternative Songs chart.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}, {"text": "Upon release, the composition was positively received by music critics and reached number 128 on the UK Singles Chart.", "chunk_id": "1e3c115665e783ed", "doc_id": "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8"}, {"text": "The single peaked at #48 on the UK Singles Chart, becoming their worst performing single to date.", "chunk_id": "992a86ff20688553", "doc_id": "hp_1440798ad8faf801"}, {"text": "The song reached number 6 in New Zealand, number 13 on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 and number 32 on the UK Singles Chart.", "chunk_id": "ea9f0bb2bf44b926", "doc_id": "hp_f61e6f2275345f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f", "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8", "hp_1440798ad8faf801", "hp_f61e6f2275345f39"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Irish Singles Chart">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A music chart in Ireland.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The song peaked at number fifty on the UK Singles Chart, the Irish Singles Chart and number thirty nine on the US \"Billboard\" Alternative Songs chart.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="US &quot;Billboard&quot; Alternative Songs chart">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A music chart in the United States for alternative songs.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The song peaked at number fifty on the UK Singles Chart, the Irish Singles Chart and number thirty nine on the US \"Billboard\" Alternative Songs chart.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Fallen Angel">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A 1945 black-and-white film noir.", "chunk_id": "a4bf6fd9b2b898ee", "doc_id": "hp_09bbc1d69c7ef40f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Fallen Angel is a 1945 black-and-white film noir directed by Otto Preminger, with cinematography by Joseph LaShelle, who had also worked with Preminger on \"Laura\" a year before.", "chunk_id": "a4bf6fd9b2b898ee", "doc_id": "hp_09bbc1d69c7ef40f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_09bbc1d69c7ef40f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Otto Preminger">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The director of the film Fallen Angel.", "chunk_id": "a4bf6fd9b2b898ee", "doc_id": "hp_09bbc1d69c7ef40f"}, {"text": "An actor-director-producer and brother of Ingo Preminger.", "chunk_id": "11399d9e6ed9e2a4", "doc_id": "hp_2f3cd8d24b5f56f1"}, {"text": "Otto Preminger was an American theatre and film director.", "chunk_id": "82bcd4a397a999ac", "doc_id": "hp_80a324515dfb8756"}, {"text": "The producer and director of the film 'The Moon Is Blue'.", "chunk_id": "5d85c27446c62606", "doc_id": "hp_eadec239ee6584cf"}, {"text": "Otto Preminger is the director of the 1975 film Rosebud.", "chunk_id": "dcfaee24c767d698", "doc_id": "hp_f83ff5aa5b31fa7a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Fallen Angel is a 1945 black-and-white film noir directed by Otto Preminger, with cinematography by Joseph LaShelle, who had also worked with Preminger on \"Laura\" a year before.", "chunk_id": "a4bf6fd9b2b898ee", "doc_id": "hp_09bbc1d69c7ef40f"}, {"text": "He was brother of actor-director-producer Otto Preminger.", "chunk_id": "11399d9e6ed9e2a4", "doc_id": "hp_2f3cd8d24b5f56f1"}, {"text": "Otto Ludwig Preminger ( , ] ; 5 December 1905 – 23 April 1986) was an American theatre and film director, originally from Austria-Hungary.", "chunk_id": "82bcd4a397a999ac", "doc_id": "hp_80a324515dfb8756"}, {"text": "The Moon Is Blue is a 1953 American romantic comedy film produced and directed by Otto Preminger and starring William Holden, David Niven, and Maggie McNamara.", "chunk_id": "5d85c27446c62606", "doc_id": "hp_eadec239ee6584cf"}, {"text": "Rosebud is a 1975 film directed by Otto Preminger, and starring Peter O'Toole, Richard Attenborough, and Peter Lawford.", "chunk_id": "dcfaee24c767d698", "doc_id": "hp_f83ff5aa5b31fa7a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_09bbc1d69c7ef40f", "hp_2f3cd8d24b5f56f1", "hp_80a324515dfb8756", "hp_eadec239ee6584cf", "hp_f83ff5aa5b31fa7a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Joseph LaShelle">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The cinematographer of the film Fallen Angel.", "chunk_id": "a4bf6fd9b2b898ee", "doc_id": "hp_09bbc1d69c7ef40f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Fallen Angel is a 1945 black-and-white film noir directed by Otto Preminger, with cinematography by Joseph LaShelle, who had also worked with Preminger on \"Laura\" a year before.", "chunk_id": "a4bf6fd9b2b898ee", "doc_id": "hp_09bbc1d69c7ef40f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_09bbc1d69c7ef40f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Laura">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A film that Otto Preminger and Joseph LaShelle worked on.", "chunk_id": "a4bf6fd9b2b898ee", "doc_id": "hp_09bbc1d69c7ef40f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Fallen Angel is a 1945 black-and-white film noir directed by Otto Preminger, with cinematography by Joseph LaShelle, who had also worked with Preminger on \"Laura\" a year before.", "chunk_id": "a4bf6fd9b2b898ee", "doc_id": "hp_09bbc1d69c7ef40f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_09bbc1d69c7ef40f"]</data>
