<node id="chanson de geste">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A chanson de geste is a type of epic poem that first appeared in Old French literature.", "chunk_id": "707fa67e1952a89d", "doc_id": "hp_0ab939b45e2f3fdb"}, {"text": "A literary genre of Old French epic poetry.", "chunk_id": "850408ca66a7d9e6", "doc_id": "hp_3fac05a2ac9ec6d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Ogier the Dane (French: \"Ogier le Danois\" or archaically \"Ogier de Danemarche\", Danish: \"Holger Danske\") is a legendary character who first appears in an Old French \"chanson de geste\", in the cycle of poems \"Geste de Doon de Mayence\".", "chunk_id": "707fa67e1952a89d", "doc_id": "hp_0ab939b45e2f3fdb"}, {"text": "Galiens li Restorés, or Galien le Restoré or Galien rhétoré (in English, \"Galien the Restored\"), is an Old French \"chanson de geste\" which borrows heavily from chivalric romance.", "chunk_id": "850408ca66a7d9e6", "doc_id": "hp_3fac05a2ac9ec6d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0ab939b45e2f3fdb", "hp_3fac05a2ac9ec6d2"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Geste de Doon de Mayence">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Geste de Doon de Mayence is a cycle of poems in which the legendary character Ogier the Dane first appears.", "chunk_id": "707fa67e1952a89d", "doc_id": "hp_0ab939b45e2f3fdb"}, {"text": "A collection of chansons de geste that includes the poem Gormond et Isembart.", "chunk_id": "54cbfcfe8378cde7", "doc_id": "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Ogier the Dane (French: \"Ogier le Danois\" or archaically \"Ogier de Danemarche\", Danish: \"Holger Danske\") is a legendary character who first appears in an Old French \"chanson de geste\", in the cycle of poems \"Geste de Doon de Mayence\".", "chunk_id": "707fa67e1952a89d", "doc_id": "hp_0ab939b45e2f3fdb"}, {"text": "The poem is sometimes grouped with the \"Geste de Doon de Mayence\" or \"rebellious vassal cycle\" of \"chansons de geste\".", "chunk_id": "54cbfcfe8378cde7", "doc_id": "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_0ab939b45e2f3fdb", "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
