<node id="Lauraceae">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Lauraceae is a family of flowering plants.", "chunk_id": "f0fe680fe359fc0b", "doc_id": "hp_10b3b9822146cc1a"}, {"text": "The Laurel family.", "chunk_id": "1680d6be464bcfe6", "doc_id": "hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a"}, {"text": "Lauraceae is the Laurel family, to which the genus Laurus belongs.", "chunk_id": "02e85a764b598b43", "doc_id": "hp_d246ca7d297d3c28"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Mezilaurus is a genus of plant in the family Lauraceae.", "chunk_id": "f0fe680fe359fc0b", "doc_id": "hp_10b3b9822146cc1a"}, {"text": "belonging to \"Laurus\" genus of evergreen trees belonging to the Laurel family, Lauraceae.", "chunk_id": "1680d6be464bcfe6", "doc_id": "hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a"}, {"text": "Laurus is a genus of evergreen trees belonging to the Laurel family, Lauraceae.", "chunk_id": "02e85a764b598b43", "doc_id": "hp_d246ca7d297d3c28"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_10b3b9822146cc1a", "hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a", "hp_d246ca7d297d3c28"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Costa Rica">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Costa Rica is a country in Central America.", "chunk_id": "f0fe680fe359fc0b", "doc_id": "hp_10b3b9822146cc1a"}, {"text": "Costa Rica is a country where Megalorhipida dulcis is known from.", "chunk_id": "1d65390cf7063363", "doc_id": "hp_36690b48d45f1e4b"}, {"text": "A country in Central America.", "chunk_id": "cfcc8f8ff86d83c3", "doc_id": "hp_dbf42d0cc7b618be"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is a neotropical genus consisting of 18-27 species, mostly hardwood evergreen trees, occurring from Costa Rica to the southeast of Brazil (Werff 1987).", "chunk_id": "f0fe680fe359fc0b", "doc_id": "hp_10b3b9822146cc1a"}, {"text": "Megalorhipida dulcis is a species of moth in the genus \"Megalorhipida\", known from Belize, Costa Rica, and Mexico.", "chunk_id": "1d65390cf7063363", "doc_id": "hp_36690b48d45f1e4b"}, {"text": "Stenocereus (Gk. stenos, narrow, L. cereus, candle) is a genus of columnar or tree-like cacti from the Baja California Peninsula and other parts of Mexico, Arizona in the United States, Colombia, Costa Rica, Guatemala, Venezuela and the ABC islands of the Dutch Caribbean.", "chunk_id": "cfcc8f8ff86d83c3", "doc_id": "hp_dbf42d0cc7b618be"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_10b3b9822146cc1a", "hp_36690b48d45f1e4b", "hp_dbf42d0cc7b618be"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Brazil">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Brazil is a country in South America.", "chunk_id": "f0fe680fe359fc0b", "doc_id": "hp_10b3b9822146cc1a"}, {"text": "A country in South America, home to the Bahia state and the setting for the novel The Violent Land.", "chunk_id": "5b9d731909fa866e", "doc_id": "hp_3182b9b6096ed733"}, {"text": "The country where São Paulo is located, and where the Native Tour finished.", "chunk_id": "fbf2e81187688813", "doc_id": "hp_bf77c9d36b5389d5"}, {"text": "Brazil is a country where Cerrado vegetation is found.", "chunk_id": "954299a74c533cc7", "doc_id": "hp_e7f8a5633759d23e"}, {"text": "A country where Ilhéus and Itabuna are located.", "chunk_id": "9f782a49a277f215", "doc_id": "hp_fdfe034a285a0db7"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is a neotropical genus consisting of 18-27 species, mostly hardwood evergreen trees, occurring from Costa Rica to the southeast of Brazil (Werff 1987).", "chunk_id": "f0fe680fe359fc0b", "doc_id": "hp_10b3b9822146cc1a"}, {"text": "It describes the battles to develop cacao plantations in the forests of the Bahia state of Brazil.", "chunk_id": "5b9d731909fa866e", "doc_id": "hp_3182b9b6096ed733"}, {"text": "The tour began on April 2, 2013, in Milan, Italy and finished on September 20, 2015, in São Paulo, Brazil.", "chunk_id": "fbf2e81187688813", "doc_id": "hp_bf77c9d36b5389d5"}, {"text": "In addition, this plant grows either in Cerrado vegetation of Brazil.", "chunk_id": "954299a74c533cc7", "doc_id": "hp_e7f8a5633759d23e"}, {"text": "Ilhéus/Bahia-Jorge Amado Airport (IATA: IOS, ICAO: SBIL) , is the airport serving Ilhéus, Brazil.", "chunk_id": "9f782a49a277f215", "doc_id": "hp_fdfe034a285a0db7"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_10b3b9822146cc1a", "hp_3182b9b6096ed733", "hp_bf77c9d36b5389d5", "hp_e7f8a5633759d23e", "hp_fdfe034a285a0db7"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="M. navalium">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "M. navalium is a species recorded in Rio de Janeiro state.", "chunk_id": "f0fe680fe359fc0b", "doc_id": "hp_10b3b9822146cc1a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In Rio de Janeiro state only \"M. navalium\" (Allemão) Taub. ex Mez has been recorded.", "chunk_id": "f0fe680fe359fc0b", "doc_id": "hp_10b3b9822146cc1a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_10b3b9822146cc1a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Rio de Janeiro">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Rio de Janeiro is a state in Brazil.", "chunk_id": "f0fe680fe359fc0b", "doc_id": "hp_10b3b9822146cc1a"}, {"text": "Rio de Janeiro is a state in Brazil where Mendoncia velloziana grows.", "chunk_id": "954299a74c533cc7", "doc_id": "hp_e7f8a5633759d23e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In Rio de Janeiro state only \"M. navalium\" (Allemão) Taub. ex Mez has been recorded.", "chunk_id": "f0fe680fe359fc0b", "doc_id": "hp_10b3b9822146cc1a"}, {"text": "This plant grows in following states of Brazil: Bahia, Ceará Minas Gerais Rio de Janeiro, São Paulo, Paraná and Santa Catarina, and it is usually visited by the hummingbirds.", "chunk_id": "954299a74c533cc7", "doc_id": "hp_e7f8a5633759d23e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_10b3b9822146cc1a", "hp_e7f8a5633759d23e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Cerrado">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Cerrado is a vast tropical savanna ecoregion of Brazil.", "chunk_id": "f0fe680fe359fc0b", "doc_id": "hp_10b3b9822146cc1a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Some species have been reported within the Cerrado and in semideciduous forest surrounding the Pantanal Matogrossense.", "chunk_id": "f0fe680fe359fc0b", "doc_id": "hp_10b3b9822146cc1a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_10b3b9822146cc1a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
