<node id="Japan">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Japan is a native region for Pterostyrax hispidus.", "chunk_id": "5a4b1080849ca551", "doc_id": "hp_10ed6dd74595a5bc"}, {"text": "Japan is a native region of Lonicera morrowii.", "chunk_id": "f7b345f78dfedaf4", "doc_id": "hp_2dbc22a588912449"}, {"text": "The country Saori Obata is from.", "chunk_id": "12c382642ec2c72f", "doc_id": "hp_4e13c8c5b154ee99"}, {"text": "Japan is a country where Koshi Inaba was born.", "chunk_id": "fa89540a3b417420", "doc_id": "hp_54bdec92cbf4fd9c"}, {"text": "Japan is a country in eastern Asia where Pterostyrax is native.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917"}, {"text": "Japan is a country in East Asia.", "chunk_id": "bd018a45665dcb2e", "doc_id": "hp_a6decab6ae6a1912"}, {"text": "The country where the novel sold more than one million copies.", "chunk_id": "fd13834eff44cf9c", "doc_id": "hp_b39f0237511ae07e"}, {"text": "A country in East Asia.", "chunk_id": "7fcbe97a0e441ab4", "doc_id": "hp_d534800743a3d491"}, {"text": "Japan is the country where the album Singing Bird was released and charted.", "chunk_id": "ca46c02b980db182", "doc_id": "hp_e2dc91ec138a82f9"}, {"text": "A country where Xóchitl Hamada makes occasional appearances.", "chunk_id": "beab562ef9fe8887", "doc_id": "hp_e53c480ef8a45aab"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Pterostyrax hispidus, the epaulette tree or fragrant epaulette tree, is a species of flowering plant in the family Styracaceae, native to China and Japan.", "chunk_id": "5a4b1080849ca551", "doc_id": "hp_10ed6dd74595a5bc"}, {"text": "Lonicera morrowii, the Morrow's honeysuckle, is a deciduous honeysuckle in the family Caprifoliaceae, native to Japan, Korea, and Northeast China.", "chunk_id": "f7b345f78dfedaf4", "doc_id": "hp_2dbc22a588912449"}, {"text": "Saori Obata (Obata Saori , born 23 April 1978 ) is a retired tennis player from Japan.", "chunk_id": "12c382642ec2c72f", "doc_id": "hp_4e13c8c5b154ee99"}, {"text": "Koshi Inaba (稲葉浩志 , Inaba Kōshi ) , born Hiroshi Inaba (稲葉浩志 , Inaba Hiroshi ) on September 23, 1964 in Tsuyama, Okayama, is a Japanese vocalist, multi-instrumentalist and songwriter.", "chunk_id": "fa89540a3b417420", "doc_id": "hp_54bdec92cbf4fd9c"}, {"text": "Pterostyrax, the epaulette tree, is a small genus of four species of deciduous large shrubs or small trees in the family Styracaceae, native to eastern Asia in China and Japan.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917"}, {"text": "Bokuzen Hidari (左 卜全 , Hidari Bokuzen , 20 February 1894 - 26 May 1971) was a Japanese actor and comedian born in Kotesashi Village (now part of Tokorozawa), Iruma District, Saitama Prefecture, Japan.", "chunk_id": "bd018a45665dcb2e", "doc_id": "hp_a6decab6ae6a1912"}, {"text": "The film, about an ordinary young couple named Kosuke and Mao, is based on a novel by Osamu Koshigaya of the same name that ranked first among novels which Japanese girls wanted boys to read in the year 2011, and has sold more than one million copies in Japan.", "chunk_id": "fd13834eff44cf9c", "doc_id": "hp_b39f0237511ae07e"}, {"text": "Pizza of Death is a Japanese record label based in Tokyo, Japan, and was founded by Hi-Standard front man Ken Yokoyama.", "chunk_id": "7fcbe97a0e441ab4", "doc_id": "hp_d534800743a3d491"}, {"text": "It was released by Vermillion Records on May 21, 2014 in Japan.", "chunk_id": "ca46c02b980db182", "doc_id": "hp_e2dc91ec138a82f9"}, {"text": "Hamada has worked for most of her professional wrestling career in Mexico, making occasional appearances in her father's home country of Japan.", "chunk_id": "beab562ef9fe8887", "doc_id": "hp_e53c480ef8a45aab"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_10ed6dd74595a5bc", "hp_2dbc22a588912449", "hp_4e13c8c5b154ee99", "hp_54bdec92cbf4fd9c", "hp_a0fb254153ed3917", "hp_a6decab6ae6a1912", "hp_b39f0237511ae07e", "hp_d534800743a3d491", "hp_e2dc91ec138a82f9", "hp_e53c480ef8a45aab"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="deciduous shrub">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Pterostyrax hispidus is described as a substantial, spreading, deciduous shrub.", "chunk_id": "5a4b1080849ca551", "doc_id": "hp_10ed6dd74595a5bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Growing to 15 m tall by 12 m broad, it is a substantial, spreading, deciduous shrub with oval leaves up to 20 cm long, and clusters of pure white, fragrant, pendent flowers in summer.", "chunk_id": "5a4b1080849ca551", "doc_id": "hp_10ed6dd74595a5bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_10ed6dd74595a5bc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="oval leaves">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The deciduous shrub has oval leaves.", "chunk_id": "5a4b1080849ca551", "doc_id": "hp_10ed6dd74595a5bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Growing to 15 m tall by 12 m broad, it is a substantial, spreading, deciduous shrub with oval leaves up to 20 cm long, and clusters of pure white, fragrant, pendent flowers in summer.", "chunk_id": "5a4b1080849ca551", "doc_id": "hp_10ed6dd74595a5bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_10ed6dd74595a5bc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Lantana">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Lantana is a genus of about 150 species of perennial flowering plants in the verbena family, Verbenaceae.", "chunk_id": "e4f91f3cba1a9e61", "doc_id": "hp_112a39087a5960d5"}, {"text": "Lantanas are common names for Lantana.", "chunk_id": "e4f91f3cba1a9e61", "doc_id": "hp_112a39087a5960d5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Lantana is a genus of about 150 species of perennial flowering plants in the verbena family, Verbenaceae.", "chunk_id": "e4f91f3cba1a9e61", "doc_id": "hp_112a39087a5960d5"}, {"text": "Their common names are shrub verbenas or lantanas.", "chunk_id": "e4f91f3cba1a9e61", "doc_id": "hp_112a39087a5960d5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_112a39087a5960d5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
