<node id="Africa">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Africa is a tropical region where Lantana is native.", "chunk_id": "e4f91f3cba1a9e61", "doc_id": "hp_112a39087a5960d5"}, {"text": "Africa is a continent.", "chunk_id": "b434d13cc8863180", "doc_id": "hp_2b52b5ab8c2b4e73"}, {"text": "Africa is a location where Pachypodium is native to.", "chunk_id": "c65de02bc9af4260", "doc_id": "hp_a9669326c71f5122"}, {"text": "A continent across which the Native Tour traveled.", "chunk_id": "fbf2e81187688813", "doc_id": "hp_bf77c9d36b5389d5"}, {"text": "Africa is a continent where Bothriochloa ischaemum var. ischaemum is native.", "chunk_id": "d4e8ac5bda630039", "doc_id": "hp_f7e1751d7e276925"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "They are native to tropical regions of the Americas and Africa but exist as an introduced species in numerous areas, especially in the Australian-Pacific region.", "chunk_id": "e4f91f3cba1a9e61", "doc_id": "hp_112a39087a5960d5"}, {"text": "It is native to Africa and southern Asia.", "chunk_id": "b434d13cc8863180", "doc_id": "hp_2b52b5ab8c2b4e73"}, {"text": "Pachypodium is a genus of succulent spine-bearing trees and shrubs, native to Madagascar and Africa.", "chunk_id": "c65de02bc9af4260", "doc_id": "hp_a9669326c71f5122"}, {"text": "The tour has traveled across five continents; Asia, Europe, Oceania, North America, and Africa.", "chunk_id": "fbf2e81187688813", "doc_id": "hp_bf77c9d36b5389d5"}, {"text": "Two varieties are recognized, of which \"Bothriochloa ischaemum\" var. \"ischaemum\" is native to Europe, Asia, and Africa and naturalized elsewhere, and var. \"songarica\" is native to Asia and naturalized elsewhere.", "chunk_id": "d4e8ac5bda630039", "doc_id": "hp_f7e1751d7e276925"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_112a39087a5960d5", "hp_2b52b5ab8c2b4e73", "hp_a9669326c71f5122", "hp_bf77c9d36b5389d5", "hp_f7e1751d7e276925"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Australian-Pacific region">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Australian-Pacific region is an area where Lantana exists as an introduced species.", "chunk_id": "e4f91f3cba1a9e61", "doc_id": "hp_112a39087a5960d5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "They are native to tropical regions of the Americas and Africa but exist as an introduced species in numerous areas, especially in the Australian-Pacific region.", "chunk_id": "e4f91f3cba1a9e61", "doc_id": "hp_112a39087a5960d5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_112a39087a5960d5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="shrub verbenas">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Shrub verbenas are common names for Lantana.", "chunk_id": "e4f91f3cba1a9e61", "doc_id": "hp_112a39087a5960d5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Their common names are shrub verbenas or lantanas.", "chunk_id": "e4f91f3cba1a9e61", "doc_id": "hp_112a39087a5960d5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_112a39087a5960d5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Late Latin">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Late Latin is the origin of the generic name Lantana.", "chunk_id": "e4f91f3cba1a9e61", "doc_id": "hp_112a39087a5960d5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The generic name originated in Late Latin, where it refers to the unrelated \"Viburnum lantana\".", "chunk_id": "e4f91f3cba1a9e61", "doc_id": "hp_112a39087a5960d5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_112a39087a5960d5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Viburnum lantana">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Viburnum lantana is an unrelated plant referred to by the generic name Lantana in Late Latin.", "chunk_id": "e4f91f3cba1a9e61", "doc_id": "hp_112a39087a5960d5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The generic name originated in Late Latin, where it refers to the unrelated \"Viburnum lantana\".", "chunk_id": "e4f91f3cba1a9e61", "doc_id": "hp_112a39087a5960d5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_112a39087a5960d5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Tan Kai">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Tan Kai is a mainland Chinese computer technician and an environmental activist from Zhejiang province.", "chunk_id": "f068118f617846f8", "doc_id": "hp_115f1b9bb83783a8"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Tan Kai (Chinese: 谭凯; born 1973) is a mainland Chinese computer technician and an environmental activist from Zhejiang province.", "chunk_id": "f068118f617846f8", "doc_id": "hp_115f1b9bb83783a8"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_115f1b9bb83783a8"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Lanyi Computer Repair">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Lanyi Computer Repair was a company operated by Tan Kai.", "chunk_id": "f068118f617846f8", "doc_id": "hp_115f1b9bb83783a8"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He operated his own company, called Lanyi Computer Repair, and co-founded an environmental advocacy and monitoring NGO called Green Watch (绿色观察).", "chunk_id": "f068118f617846f8", "doc_id": "hp_115f1b9bb83783a8"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_115f1b9bb83783a8"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Green Watch">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Green Watch is an environmental advocacy and monitoring NGO co-founded by Tan Kai.", "chunk_id": "f068118f617846f8", "doc_id": "hp_115f1b9bb83783a8"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He operated his own company, called Lanyi Computer Repair, and co-founded an environmental advocacy and monitoring NGO called Green Watch (绿色观察).", "chunk_id": "f068118f617846f8", "doc_id": "hp_115f1b9bb83783a8"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_115f1b9bb83783a8"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Zhejiang province">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Zhejiang province is a location in mainland China from which Tan Kai originates.", "chunk_id": "f068118f617846f8", "doc_id": "hp_115f1b9bb83783a8"}, {"text": "Zhejiang Province is a province in China.", "chunk_id": "ff0f3f2e384a3a68", "doc_id": "hp_49bb33ee8514f5e2"}, {"text": "A province in eastern China where the Yandang Mountains are located.", "chunk_id": "696929108fab1bcf", "doc_id": "hp_a71b119b261e3b26"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Tan Kai (Chinese: 谭凯; born 1973) is a mainland Chinese computer technician and an environmental activist from Zhejiang province.", "chunk_id": "f068118f617846f8", "doc_id": "hp_115f1b9bb83783a8"}, {"text": "The Jiangxia Tidal Power Station (江厦潮汐电站) is the fourth largest tidal power station in the world, located in Wuyantou, Wenling City, Zhejiang Province, China.", "chunk_id": "ff0f3f2e384a3a68", "doc_id": "hp_49bb33ee8514f5e2"}, {"text": "Yandang Mountains or Yandangshan (Chinese:  雁蕩山 ,  雁荡山 ,  \"Yàndàng Shān\",  \"Wild Goose Pond Mountain(s)\") refers, in the broad sense, to a coastal mountain range in southeastern Zhejiang province in eastern China, covering much of the prefecture-level city of Wenzhou (from Pingyang County in the south to Yueqing County in the northeast) and extending to the county-level city of Wenling in Taizhou prefecture.", "chunk_id": "696929108fab1bcf", "doc_id": "hp_a71b119b261e3b26"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_115f1b9bb83783a8", "hp_49bb33ee8514f5e2", "hp_a71b119b261e3b26"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="illegally obtaining state secrets">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Illegally obtaining state secrets was the charge for which Tan Kai was convicted in May 2006.", "chunk_id": "f068118f617846f8", "doc_id": "hp_115f1b9bb83783a8"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He was convicted in May 2006 \"illegally obtaining state secrets.\"", "chunk_id": "f068118f617846f8", "doc_id": "hp_115f1b9bb83783a8"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_115f1b9bb83783a8"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="East Windsor Hill Historic District">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A historic district located in the northwestern corner of the town of South Windsor, Connecticut.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "East Windsor Hill Historic District is a historic district located in the northwestern corner of the town of South Windsor, Connecticut.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_11772f6fd63db74e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="South Windsor">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A town in Connecticut where the East Windsor Hill Historic District is located.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "East Windsor Hill Historic District is a historic district located in the northwestern corner of the town of South Windsor, Connecticut.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_11772f6fd63db74e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Connecticut">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A state in the United States where South Windsor is located.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "East Windsor Hill Historic District is a historic district located in the northwestern corner of the town of South Windsor, Connecticut.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_11772f6fd63db74e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Main Street">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A street along which the East Windsor Hill Historic District runs.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The district runs along both sides of Main Street from the Scantic River south to the Edwards Cemetery.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_11772f6fd63db74e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Scantic River">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A river that forms a southern boundary for a portion of the East Windsor Hill Historic District.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The district runs along both sides of Main Street from the Scantic River south to the Edwards Cemetery.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_11772f6fd63db74e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Edwards Cemetery">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A cemetery that forms a southern boundary for a portion of the East Windsor Hill Historic District.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The district runs along both sides of Main Street from the Scantic River south to the Edwards Cemetery.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_11772f6fd63db74e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Connecticut River">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A river that forms a western boundary for a portion of the East Windsor Hill Historic District.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The district also includes areas west of Main Street to the Connecticut River, including properties along Ferry Lane.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_11772f6fd63db74e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Ferry Lane">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A lane with properties included in the East Windsor Hill Historic District.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The district also includes areas west of Main Street to the Connecticut River, including properties along Ferry Lane.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_11772f6fd63db74e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Windsor Farms Historic District">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Another historic district located directly south of the East Windsor Hill Historic District.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The district is located directly north of another historic district, Windsor Farms Historic District.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_11772f6fd63db74e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="folk vernacular buildings">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A style of buildings erected between about 1700 and 1860 within the East Windsor Hill Historic District.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The district encompasses a neighborhood of well-preserved largely folk vernacular buildings erected between about 1700 and 1860.", "chunk_id": "7bfcc18e594af3bb", "doc_id": "hp_11772f6fd63db74e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_11772f6fd63db74e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="All-American Strongman Challenge">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A leading competition in strength athletics.", "chunk_id": "fb43fe49d9c01907", "doc_id": "hp_1183c20fecf2a891"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The All-American Strongman Challenge is a leading competition in strength athletics that takes place within the annual Californian FitExpo.", "chunk_id": "fb43fe49d9c01907", "doc_id": "hp_1183c20fecf2a891"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1183c20fecf2a891"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
