<node id="Port Macquarie">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Port Macquarie is a city in New South Wales, Australia.", "chunk_id": "1908956e32efc2d1", "doc_id": "hp_1414681ce139d8b0"}, {"text": "Port Macquarie is a location where Eli James Harrison was born.", "chunk_id": "53f3bbd1c43e3155", "doc_id": "hp_7820faef8a00d610"}, {"text": "Port Macquarie is a town included within Macquarie County.", "chunk_id": "2b4451cce149d95e", "doc_id": "hp_97a390a9fc775a07"}, {"text": "Port Macquarie is a city in New South Wales, Australia.", "chunk_id": "17ec0b20721cd11e", "doc_id": "hp_9be184228ee1e48d"}, {"text": "A town in New South Wales, Australia, serving as a depot for the 41st Battalion, Royal New South Wales Regiment.", "chunk_id": "18cfadbc25fe419e", "doc_id": "hp_cf67bd08ea76563b"}, {"text": "A coastal town in New South Wales.", "chunk_id": "203bcd26d9746ba7", "doc_id": "hp_d399c5634a0f3001"}, {"text": "Port Macquarie is a location in New South Wales, west of which Mount Grundy is situated.", "chunk_id": "e1044c549e97de7c", "doc_id": "hp_dce12d59ef968ea1"}, {"text": "Port Macquarie is a coastal town in the local government area of Port Macquarie-Hastings.", "chunk_id": "6223f89935ee9cfe", "doc_id": "hp_de00d7ebc47399cc"}, {"text": "A place represented by Leslie Williams in the New South Wales Legislative Assembly.", "chunk_id": "de697cb94cf1954b", "doc_id": "hp_e13c0cde045c0455"}, {"text": "A location in New South Wales where a female factory was established.", "chunk_id": "4149c8ff0afe3241", "doc_id": "hp_e4df916ac39f713d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Port Macquarie Airport (IATA: PQQ, ICAO: YPMQ) is an airport in Port Macquarie, New South Wales, Australia.", "chunk_id": "1908956e32efc2d1", "doc_id": "hp_1414681ce139d8b0"}, {"text": "Born in Port Macquarie, New South Wales to farmer William Binney and Sophia Selina Turnbull, he was educated at state schools.", "chunk_id": "53f3bbd1c43e3155", "doc_id": "hp_7820faef8a00d610"}, {"text": "It includes Port Macquarie and the area around it.", "chunk_id": "2b4451cce149d95e", "doc_id": "hp_97a390a9fc775a07"}, {"text": "Bonny Hills is a town in New South Wales, Australia about 30 minutes drive south of Port Macquarie.", "chunk_id": "17ec0b20721cd11e", "doc_id": "hp_9be184228ee1e48d"}, {"text": "It is based in northern New South Wales, with its headquarters in Lismore and depots in a number of locations including Tweed Heads, Taree, Grafton, Kempsey, Port Macquarie and Coffs Harbour.", "chunk_id": "18cfadbc25fe419e", "doc_id": "hp_cf67bd08ea76563b"}, {"text": "The dismissal of the Port Macquarie-Hastings Council on 27 February 2008 marked the end of a series of events involving a project which was initiated in 2001 in the New South Wales coastal town of Port Macquarie to build a cultural and entertainment centre, known to locals as the Glasshouse.", "chunk_id": "203bcd26d9746ba7", "doc_id": "hp_d399c5634a0f3001"}, {"text": "The northernmost area is at Mount Grundy, west of Port Macquarie.", "chunk_id": "e1044c549e97de7c", "doc_id": "hp_dce12d59ef968ea1"}, {"text": "Port Macquarie is a coastal town in the local government area of Port Macquarie-Hastings.", "chunk_id": "6223f89935ee9cfe", "doc_id": "hp_de00d7ebc47399cc"}, {"text": "Leslie Gladys Williams (born on Kangaroo Island, South Australia), an Australian politician and a member of the New South Wales Legislative Assembly representing Port Macquarie since 2011 for the Nationals.", "chunk_id": "de697cb94cf1954b", "doc_id": "hp_e13c0cde045c0455"}, {"text": "In New South Wales, female factories were also established in Bathurst, Newcastle, Port Macquarie and Moreton Bay (2 factories).", "chunk_id": "4149c8ff0afe3241", "doc_id": "hp_e4df916ac39f713d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1414681ce139d8b0", "hp_7820faef8a00d610", "hp_97a390a9fc775a07", "hp_9be184228ee1e48d", "hp_cf67bd08ea76563b", "hp_d399c5634a0f3001", "hp_dce12d59ef968ea1", "hp_de00d7ebc47399cc", "hp_e13c0cde045c0455", "hp_e4df916ac39f713d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="New South Wales">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "New South Wales is a state in Australia.", "chunk_id": "1908956e32efc2d1", "doc_id": "hp_1414681ce139d8b0"}, {"text": "New South Wales is a location where Euryops chrysanthemoides is a ruderal weed.", "chunk_id": "402abfe881c67ee7", "doc_id": "hp_2c7ea4fcf64b2cee"}, {"text": "New South Wales is a location in Australia where Eli James Harrison was born and where he was educated at state schools.", "chunk_id": "53f3bbd1c43e3155", "doc_id": "hp_7820faef8a00d610"}, {"text": "New South Wales is a state in Australia.", "chunk_id": "2b4451cce149d95e", "doc_id": "hp_97a390a9fc775a07"}, {"text": "New South Wales is a state in Australia.", "chunk_id": "17ec0b20721cd11e", "doc_id": "hp_9be184228ee1e48d"}, {"text": "A state in Australia.", "chunk_id": "18cfadbc25fe419e", "doc_id": "hp_cf67bd08ea76563b"}, {"text": "A state in Australia.", "chunk_id": "203bcd26d9746ba7", "doc_id": "hp_d399c5634a0f3001"}, {"text": "New South Wales is a location in Australia where Atherosperma moschatum is native.", "chunk_id": "e1044c549e97de7c", "doc_id": "hp_dce12d59ef968ea1"}, {"text": "It is located on the Mid North Coast of New South Wales, Australia, about 390 km north of Sydney, and 570 km south of Brisbane.", "chunk_id": "6223f89935ee9cfe", "doc_id": "hp_de00d7ebc47399cc"}, {"text": "A former penal colony and current location of several female factories.", "chunk_id": "4149c8ff0afe3241", "doc_id": "hp_e4df916ac39f713d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Port Macquarie Airport (IATA: PQQ, ICAO: YPMQ) is an airport in Port Macquarie, New South Wales, Australia.", "chunk_id": "1908956e32efc2d1", "doc_id": "hp_1414681ce139d8b0"}, {"text": "It is a ruderal weed in New South Wales, although it is not weedy in all places where it is cultivated or has naturalized.", "chunk_id": "402abfe881c67ee7", "doc_id": "hp_2c7ea4fcf64b2cee"}, {"text": "Born in Port Macquarie, New South Wales to farmer William Binney and Sophia Selina Turnbull, he was educated at state schools.", "chunk_id": "53f3bbd1c43e3155", "doc_id": "hp_7820faef8a00d610"}, {"text": "Macquarie County is one of the 141 Cadastral divisions of New South Wales, Australia.", "chunk_id": "2b4451cce149d95e", "doc_id": "hp_97a390a9fc775a07"}, {"text": "Bonny Hills is a town in New South Wales, Australia about 30 minutes drive south of Port Macquarie.", "chunk_id": "17ec0b20721cd11e", "doc_id": "hp_9be184228ee1e48d"}, {"text": "It is based in northern New South Wales, with its headquarters in Lismore and depots in a number of locations including Tweed Heads, Taree, Grafton, Kempsey, Port Macquarie and Coffs Harbour.", "chunk_id": "18cfadbc25fe419e", "doc_id": "hp_cf67bd08ea76563b"}, {"text": "The dismissal of the Port Macquarie-Hastings Council on 27 February 2008 marked the end of a series of events involving a project which was initiated in 2001 in the New South Wales coastal town of Port Macquarie to build a cultural and entertainment centre, known to locals as the Glasshouse.", "chunk_id": "203bcd26d9746ba7", "doc_id": "hp_d399c5634a0f3001"}, {"text": "Atherosperma moschatum, the southern sassafras or blackheart sassafras, is an evergreen tree native to the cool temperate rainforests of Tasmania, Victoria, and New South Wales in Australia.", "chunk_id": "e1044c549e97de7c", "doc_id": "hp_dce12d59ef968ea1"}, {"text": "It is located on the Mid North Coast of New South Wales, Australia, about 390 km north of Sydney, and 570 km south of Brisbane.", "chunk_id": "6223f89935ee9cfe", "doc_id": "hp_de00d7ebc47399cc"}, {"text": "The Parramatta Female Factory, in the former penal colony of New South Wales, is located in the grounds of Cumberland Hospital, North Parramatta, New South Wales.", "chunk_id": "4149c8ff0afe3241", "doc_id": "hp_e4df916ac39f713d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1414681ce139d8b0", "hp_2c7ea4fcf64b2cee", "hp_7820faef8a00d610", "hp_97a390a9fc775a07", "hp_9be184228ee1e48d", "hp_cf67bd08ea76563b", "hp_d399c5634a0f3001", "hp_dce12d59ef968ea1", "hp_de00d7ebc47399cc", "hp_e4df916ac39f713d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Port Macquarie-Hastings Council">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Port Macquarie-Hastings Council is the owner and manager of Port Macquarie Airport.", "chunk_id": "1908956e32efc2d1", "doc_id": "hp_1414681ce139d8b0"}, {"text": "The local government authority for the Port Macquarie-Hastings region.", "chunk_id": "203bcd26d9746ba7", "doc_id": "hp_d399c5634a0f3001"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The airport is 2.25 NM west of the city center and is owned and managed by the Port Macquarie-Hastings Council (ABN 11 236 901 601) on behalf of its owners - the constituents of the Hastings.", "chunk_id": "1908956e32efc2d1", "doc_id": "hp_1414681ce139d8b0"}, {"text": "The dismissal of the Port Macquarie-Hastings Council on 27 February 2008 marked the end of a series of events involving a project which was initiated in 2001 in the New South Wales coastal town of Port Macquarie to build a cultural and entertainment centre, known to locals as the Glasshouse.", "chunk_id": "203bcd26d9746ba7", "doc_id": "hp_d399c5634a0f3001"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1414681ce139d8b0", "hp_d399c5634a0f3001"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Port Macquarie Airport Proprietary Limited">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Port Macquarie Airport Proprietary Limited is an entity whose ownership is not to be confused with the management of Port Macquarie Airport.", "chunk_id": "1908956e32efc2d1", "doc_id": "hp_1414681ce139d8b0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The ownership is not to be confused with the Port Macquarie Airport Proprietary Limited (ABN 88 002 323 122).", "chunk_id": "1908956e32efc2d1", "doc_id": "hp_1414681ce139d8b0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1414681ce139d8b0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="The Beautiful Occupation">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Beautiful Occupation is the second single from Travis' fourth studio album, 12 Memories.", "chunk_id": "992a86ff20688553", "doc_id": "hp_1440798ad8faf801"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"The Beautiful Occupation\" is the second single from Scottish indie rock band Travis' fourth studio album, \"12 Memories\".", "chunk_id": "992a86ff20688553", "doc_id": "hp_1440798ad8faf801"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1440798ad8faf801"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Travis">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Travis is a Scottish indie rock band.", "chunk_id": "992a86ff20688553", "doc_id": "hp_1440798ad8faf801"}, {"text": "Travis is an alternative rock band from Glasgow, Scotland.", "chunk_id": "8043cae2ef7b7fae", "doc_id": "hp_5e36dcc4c1a872ca"}, {"text": "Travis is a band associated with Fran Healy.", "chunk_id": "161799124afdf1e1", "doc_id": "hp_6a39ea6d8c8a05f8"}, {"text": "A band that Fran Healy is a part of.", "chunk_id": "f0e4892b3b37bba4", "doc_id": "hp_7cc233817d9e07c7"}, {"text": "Travis is a band for which Fran Healy is the lead singer and main songwriter.", "chunk_id": "b495da896345a856", "doc_id": "hp_8e3f3120ae8497a2"}, {"text": "A band of which Fran Healy is the frontman.", "chunk_id": "02e94c52db8f837e", "doc_id": "hp_d73d23b34d64cf3a"}, {"text": "An alternative rock band.", "chunk_id": "f4459cecee69896e", "doc_id": "hp_ede5d2c03eeb3cf1"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"The Beautiful Occupation\" is the second single from Scottish indie rock band Travis' fourth studio album, \"12 Memories\".", "chunk_id": "992a86ff20688553", "doc_id": "hp_1440798ad8faf801"}, {"text": "Travis is an alternative rock band from Glasgow, Scotland, comprising Fran Healy (lead vocals, guitar, piano, banjo), Dougie Payne (bass guitar, backing vocals), Andy Dunlop (lead guitar, banjo, keyboards, backing vocals) and Neil Primrose (drums, percussion).", "chunk_id": "8043cae2ef7b7fae", "doc_id": "hp_5e36dcc4c1a872ca"}, {"text": "BNQT (pronounced banquet ( ) is an indie super-group featuring Fran Healy (Travis), Alex Kapranos (Franz Ferdinand), Eric Pulido (Midlake), Ben Bridwell (Band of Horses) and Jason Lytle (Grandaddy), backed by other members of Midlake; Jesse Chandler, Joey McClellan and McKenzie Smith.", "chunk_id": "161799124afdf1e1", "doc_id": "hp_6a39ea6d8c8a05f8"}, {"text": "Volume 1 is the debut studio album by indie super-group BNQT, lead by Eric Pulido (Midlake) with Ben Bridwell (Band of Horses), Alex Kapranos (Franz Ferdinand), Fran Healy (Travis) and Jason Lytle (Grandaddy), backed by the other members of Midlake.", "chunk_id": "f0e4892b3b37bba4", "doc_id": "hp_7cc233817d9e07c7"}, {"text": "He is the lead singer and main songwriter of the band Travis, having written nearly all of the songs on their first six studio albums, with the 8th being more of a co-written work.", "chunk_id": "b495da896345a856", "doc_id": "hp_8e3f3120ae8497a2"}, {"text": "Wreckorder is the debut solo album from Travis frontman, Fran Healy.", "chunk_id": "02e94c52db8f837e", "doc_id": "hp_d73d23b34d64cf3a"}, {"text": "\"Where You Stand\" is a song by alternative rock band Travis, written by Dougie Payne, Holly Partridge and Fran Healy.", "chunk_id": "f4459cecee69896e", "doc_id": "hp_ede5d2c03eeb3cf1"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1440798ad8faf801", "hp_5e36dcc4c1a872ca", "hp_6a39ea6d8c8a05f8", "hp_7cc233817d9e07c7", "hp_8e3f3120ae8497a2", "hp_d73d23b34d64cf3a", "hp_ede5d2c03eeb3cf1"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="12 Memories">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "12 Memories is the fourth studio album by the Scottish indie rock band Travis.", "chunk_id": "992a86ff20688553", "doc_id": "hp_1440798ad8faf801"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"The Beautiful Occupation\" is the second single from Scottish indie rock band Travis' fourth studio album, \"12 Memories\".", "chunk_id": "992a86ff20688553", "doc_id": "hp_1440798ad8faf801"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1440798ad8faf801"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Fran Healy">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Fran Healy is the frontman of the band Travis and wrote the song \"The Beautiful Occupation\".", "chunk_id": "992a86ff20688553", "doc_id": "hp_1440798ad8faf801"}, {"text": "Fran Healy is a member of the band Travis, playing lead vocals, guitar, piano, and banjo.", "chunk_id": "8043cae2ef7b7fae", "doc_id": "hp_5e36dcc4c1a872ca"}, {"text": "Fran Healy is a member of the indie super-group BNQT and is associated with Travis.", "chunk_id": "161799124afdf1e1", "doc_id": "hp_6a39ea6d8c8a05f8"}, {"text": "A member of the indie super-group BNQT.", "chunk_id": "f0e4892b3b37bba4", "doc_id": "hp_7cc233817d9e07c7"}, {"text": "Fran Healy is a Scottish musician, lead singer, and main songwriter of the band Travis.", "chunk_id": "b495da896345a856", "doc_id": "hp_8e3f3120ae8497a2"}, {"text": "Frontman of the band Travis and the artist behind the solo album Wreckorder.", "chunk_id": "02e94c52db8f837e", "doc_id": "hp_d73d23b34d64cf3a"}, {"text": "A writer of the song \"Where You Stand\".", "chunk_id": "f4459cecee69896e", "doc_id": "hp_ede5d2c03eeb3cf1"}, {"text": "A songwriter who co-wrote the song \"Here with Me\".", "chunk_id": "ea618fdd901514b3", "doc_id": "hp_f6f4e0beb9d8d251"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The song was written by frontman Fran Healy and is a reflection of the anti-war sentiments of the War on Iraq, also carrying serious criticism to the invasion itself.", "chunk_id": "992a86ff20688553", "doc_id": "hp_1440798ad8faf801"}, {"text": "Travis is an alternative rock band from Glasgow, Scotland, comprising Fran Healy (lead vocals, guitar, piano, banjo), Dougie Payne (bass guitar, backing vocals), Andy Dunlop (lead guitar, banjo, keyboards, backing vocals) and Neil Primrose (drums, percussion).", "chunk_id": "8043cae2ef7b7fae", "doc_id": "hp_5e36dcc4c1a872ca"}, {"text": "BNQT (pronounced banquet ( ) is an indie super-group featuring Fran Healy (Travis), Alex Kapranos (Franz Ferdinand), Eric Pulido (Midlake), Ben Bridwell (Band of Horses) and Jason Lytle (Grandaddy), backed by other members of Midlake; Jesse Chandler, Joey McClellan and McKenzie Smith.", "chunk_id": "161799124afdf1e1", "doc_id": "hp_6a39ea6d8c8a05f8"}, {"text": "Volume 1 is the debut studio album by indie super-group BNQT, lead by Eric Pulido (Midlake) with Ben Bridwell (Band of Horses), Alex Kapranos (Franz Ferdinand), Fran Healy (Travis) and Jason Lytle (Grandaddy), backed by the other members of Midlake.", "chunk_id": "f0e4892b3b37bba4", "doc_id": "hp_7cc233817d9e07c7"}, {"text": "Francis \"Fran\" Healy (born 23 July 1973) is a Scottish musician.", "chunk_id": "b495da896345a856", "doc_id": "hp_8e3f3120ae8497a2"}, {"text": "Wreckorder is the debut solo album from Travis frontman, Fran Healy.", "chunk_id": "02e94c52db8f837e", "doc_id": "hp_d73d23b34d64cf3a"}, {"text": "\"Where You Stand\" is a song by alternative rock band Travis, written by Dougie Payne, Holly Partridge and Fran Healy.", "chunk_id": "f4459cecee69896e", "doc_id": "hp_ede5d2c03eeb3cf1"}, {"text": "It was released as the third single from the album on December 16, 2012, and was written by Brandon Flowers and Fran Healy.", "chunk_id": "ea618fdd901514b3", "doc_id": "hp_f6f4e0beb9d8d251"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1440798ad8faf801", "hp_5e36dcc4c1a872ca", "hp_6a39ea6d8c8a05f8", "hp_7cc233817d9e07c7", "hp_8e3f3120ae8497a2", "hp_d73d23b34d64cf3a", "hp_ede5d2c03eeb3cf1", "hp_f6f4e0beb9d8d251"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="War on Iraq">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The War on Iraq refers to the conflict that began in 2003 with the invasion of Iraq by coalition forces.", "chunk_id": "992a86ff20688553", "doc_id": "hp_1440798ad8faf801"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The song was written by frontman Fran Healy and is a reflection of the anti-war sentiments of the War on Iraq, also carrying serious criticism to the invasion itself.", "chunk_id": "992a86ff20688553", "doc_id": "hp_1440798ad8faf801"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1440798ad8faf801"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Mera Naam Joker">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A 1970 Indian Hindi drama film directed by Raj Kapoor.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Mera Naam Joker (translation: \"My Name is Joker\") is a 1970 Indian Hindi drama film directed by Raj Kapoor.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_147900705f372e86"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="My Name is Joker">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The English translation of the film title \"Mera Naam Joker\".", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Mera Naam Joker (translation: \"My Name is Joker\") is a 1970 Indian Hindi drama film directed by Raj Kapoor.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_147900705f372e86"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Khwaja Ahmad Abbas">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The writer of the screenplay for \"Mera Naam Joker\".", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}, {"text": "Writer of the 1955 Hindi film Shree 420.", "chunk_id": "0a8e3d3f676d8b89", "doc_id": "hp_8c200a803fef76a7"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The screenplay was written by Khwaja Ahmad Abbas.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}, {"text": "Shree 420 (\"Hindi\" श्री ४२०, translation: \"Sir 420\", also transliterated as Shri 420) is a 1955 Hindi film, directed and produced by Raj Kapoor, written by Khwaja Ahmad Abbas, and starring Raj Kapoor and Nargis.", "chunk_id": "0a8e3d3f676d8b89", "doc_id": "hp_8c200a803fef76a7"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_147900705f372e86", "hp_8c200a803fef76a7"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Rishi Kapoor">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The film \"Mera Naam Joker\" was his debut.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "This film was the debut of Rishi Kapoor.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_147900705f372e86"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Indian cinema">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The film industry in India.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}, {"text": "The film industry in India.", "chunk_id": "656937d22d978bfd", "doc_id": "hp_e3306a4963e6e08c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The film is considered to be one of the lengthiest films of Indian cinema.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}, {"text": "Ranbir Raj Kapoor (14 December 1924 – 2 June 1988), also known as \"the greatest showman of Indian cinema\", was a noted Indian film actor, producer and director of Hindi cinema.", "chunk_id": "656937d22d978bfd", "doc_id": "hp_e3306a4963e6e08c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_147900705f372e86", "hp_e3306a4963e6e08c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Sangam">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A film that became a blockbuster.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "After \"Sangam\" became a blockbuster, \"Mera Naam Joker\" was highly anticipated as it was under production for six years and was heavily publicized to be loosely based on Raj Kapoor's own life.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_147900705f372e86"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="financial crisis">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A state of severe financial difficulty.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Upon release the film turned out to be a critical and commercial disaster putting Kapoor into a financial crisis.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_147900705f372e86"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="cult status">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A status achieved by a work that has a dedicated following.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "However, over the years, the film has gained a cult status and is regarded as a classic today.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_147900705f372e86"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="classic">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A work of art of the highest quality, standing the test of time.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "However, over the years, the film has gained a cult status and is regarded as a classic today.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_147900705f372e86"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="abridged version">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A shortened version of the film \"Mera Naam Joker\".", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "An abridged version was released in the 1980s and had a highly successful run at the box office.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_147900705f372e86"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="box office">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The place where tickets are sold for a film.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "An abridged version was released in the 1980s and had a highly successful run at the box office.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_147900705f372e86"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="misunderstood masterpiece">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A label given to a work that is not initially appreciated but is later recognized for its quality.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The film is regarded as one of Kapoor's finest works today with film experts labeling it as a 'misunderstood masterpiece'.", "chunk_id": "a1abbeeae15652d0", "doc_id": "hp_147900705f372e86"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_147900705f372e86"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Jonathan Davis">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An American musician best known as the leading vocalist and frontman of the nu metal band Korn.", "chunk_id": "426fc5ed27199faa", "doc_id": "hp_149d7704ca37e2bd"}, {"text": "The frontman of the band Korn.", "chunk_id": "86a10bb482fcd4be", "doc_id": "hp_39c2c8083595c753"}, {"text": "The lead vocalist of the band Korn.", "chunk_id": "013ecef0e3cecfa1", "doc_id": "hp_90c61d43b4ea3d45"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Jonathan Howsmon Davis (born January 18, 1971), also known as JD and JDevil (or J Devil), is an American musician best known as the leading vocalist and frontman of the nu metal band Korn.", "chunk_id": "426fc5ed27199faa", "doc_id": "hp_149d7704ca37e2bd"}, {"text": "Jonathan Davis and the SFA (Simply Fucking Amazings) is the solo band of Korn frontman Jonathan Davis.", "chunk_id": "86a10bb482fcd4be", "doc_id": "hp_39c2c8083595c753"}, {"text": "The song is about how Korn's lead vocalist Jonathan Davis was bullied in high school for being into arts, wearing eyeliner, being into new wave music (for example, Duran Duran), and wearing frilly shirts.", "chunk_id": "013ecef0e3cecfa1", "doc_id": "hp_90c61d43b4ea3d45"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_149d7704ca37e2bd", "hp_39c2c8083595c753", "hp_90c61d43b4ea3d45"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="JD">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An alternative name for Jonathan Davis.", "chunk_id": "426fc5ed27199faa", "doc_id": "hp_149d7704ca37e2bd"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Jonathan Howsmon Davis (born January 18, 1971), also known as JD and JDevil (or J Devil), is an American musician best known as the leading vocalist and frontman of the nu metal band Korn.", "chunk_id": "426fc5ed27199faa", "doc_id": "hp_149d7704ca37e2bd"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_149d7704ca37e2bd"]</data>
