<node id="Falls Apart">
  <data key="d0">SONG</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A song by American rock band Sugar Ray.", "chunk_id": "c2fab40cef72276e", "doc_id": "hp_1826a58de10298d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Falls Apart\" is a song by American rock band Sugar Ray from their album \"\".", "chunk_id": "c2fab40cef72276e", "doc_id": "hp_1826a58de10298d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1826a58de10298d3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Billboard Hot 100">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A music chart that ranks songs.", "chunk_id": "c2fab40cef72276e", "doc_id": "hp_1826a58de10298d3"}, {"text": "A music chart for popular songs.", "chunk_id": "79f2e927bc5b3f09", "doc_id": "hp_3b9acbbdcc47f797"}, {"text": "A music chart that \"Someday\" reached #7 on.", "chunk_id": "d2de0918bf1b22b8", "doc_id": "hp_482e2d8f73f605ee"}, {"text": "A music chart.", "chunk_id": "1c9e0b6104c2f63d", "doc_id": "hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"}, {"text": "A music chart that ranks the top songs in the U.S.", "chunk_id": "4b7512b6f1c5cb80", "doc_id": "hp_c1b2bbdafbcaad90"}, {"text": "A music chart that ranks songs based on popularity.", "chunk_id": "b4d3f874cde3d202", "doc_id": "hp_d679581e3707876c"}, {"text": "A music chart where the song \"When It's Over\" reached number 13.", "chunk_id": "ea9f0bb2bf44b926", "doc_id": "hp_f61e6f2275345f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The song reached number 29 on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 and number 5 on the Hot Modern Rock Tracks.", "chunk_id": "c2fab40cef72276e", "doc_id": "hp_1826a58de10298d3"}, {"text": "It topped the country songs chart, reached number two on the Billboard Hot 100, and became an international hit.", "chunk_id": "79f2e927bc5b3f09", "doc_id": "hp_3b9acbbdcc47f797"}, {"text": "The song reached #7 on both the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 and the Hot Modern Rock Tracks, as well as #4 on the Hot 100 Airplay and #4 on Canada's \"RPM\" singles chart.", "chunk_id": "d2de0918bf1b22b8", "doc_id": "hp_482e2d8f73f605ee"}, {"text": "The song was composed by Robbin Crosby, Stephen Pearcy, and Joey Cristofanilli (who was briefly filling in for full-time Ratt bassist Juan Croucier), and it was the second biggest hit on the album (note: \"Back for more\" did not qualify for a chart position since it was not an actual single release), reaching number 87 on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 and 38 on the \"Billboard\" Mainstream Rock Tracks chart.", "chunk_id": "1c9e0b6104c2f63d", "doc_id": "hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"}, {"text": "It is the group's second most successful single, peaking at number 18 on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 and number nine on the Hot R&amp;B/Hip-Hop Singles &amp; Tracks in the U.S. in January 2002.", "chunk_id": "4b7512b6f1c5cb80", "doc_id": "hp_c1b2bbdafbcaad90"}, {"text": "It first became a popular \"Billboard\" Hot 100 number one hit for the American Motown group The Supremes in late 1966.", "chunk_id": "b4d3f874cde3d202", "doc_id": "hp_d679581e3707876c"}, {"text": "The song reached number 6 in New Zealand, number 13 on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 and number 32 on the UK Singles Chart.", "chunk_id": "ea9f0bb2bf44b926", "doc_id": "hp_f61e6f2275345f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1826a58de10298d3", "hp_3b9acbbdcc47f797", "hp_482e2d8f73f605ee", "hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32", "hp_c1b2bbdafbcaad90", "hp_d679581e3707876c", "hp_f61e6f2275345f39"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Hot Modern Rock Tracks">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A music chart that ranks modern rock songs.", "chunk_id": "c2fab40cef72276e", "doc_id": "hp_1826a58de10298d3"}, {"text": "A music chart that \"Someday\" reached #7 on.", "chunk_id": "d2de0918bf1b22b8", "doc_id": "hp_482e2d8f73f605ee"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The song reached number 29 on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 and number 5 on the Hot Modern Rock Tracks.", "chunk_id": "c2fab40cef72276e", "doc_id": "hp_1826a58de10298d3"}, {"text": "The song reached #7 on both the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 and the Hot Modern Rock Tracks, as well as #4 on the Hot 100 Airplay and #4 on Canada's \"RPM\" singles chart.", "chunk_id": "d2de0918bf1b22b8", "doc_id": "hp_482e2d8f73f605ee"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1826a58de10298d3", "hp_482e2d8f73f605ee"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Dale Minami">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A San Francisco-based lawyer best known for heading the legal team that overturned the conviction of Fred Korematsu.", "chunk_id": "63f34134976a8d32", "doc_id": "hp_18a6d077ab278415"}, {"text": "Lead litigator of the \"Korematsu v. United States\" civil rights case and an alumnus of Berkeley Law.", "chunk_id": "0ba5a45b986c419a", "doc_id": "hp_5dddd5f952802e7e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Dale Minami (born October 13, 1946) is a San Francisco-based lawyer best known for heading the legal team that overturned the conviction of Fred Korematsu, whose defiance of the World War II Japanese American internment order lead to Korematsu v. United States, one of the most controversial United States Supreme Court decisions of the 20th century.", "chunk_id": "63f34134976a8d32", "doc_id": "hp_18a6d077ab278415"}, {"text": "The law school has produced leaders in law, government, and society, including Chief Justice of the United States Earl Warren, Secretary of State of the United States Dean Rusk, Attorney General of the United States Edwin Meese, United States Secretary of the Treasury and Chairman of the Federal Reserve G. William Miller, Solicitor General of the United States Theodore Olson, and lead litigator of the \"Korematsu v. United States\" civil rights case, Dale Minami.", "chunk_id": "0ba5a45b986c419a", "doc_id": "hp_5dddd5f952802e7e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_18a6d077ab278415", "hp_5dddd5f952802e7e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="World War II">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A global conflict during which the Japanese American internment order was issued.", "chunk_id": "63f34134976a8d32", "doc_id": "hp_18a6d077ab278415"}, {"text": "A global conflict during which the Holocaust occurred, involving Nazi Germany and its collaborators.", "chunk_id": "0b6495ca8fb3c7ab", "doc_id": "hp_58dc44606385cdf1"}, {"text": "World War II was a global war that lasted from 1939 to 1945.", "chunk_id": "7ed2f23b7d77b089", "doc_id": "hp_6eb8e4170df0651b"}, {"text": "World War II was a conflict during which Walter Walsh served in the Pacific theatre with the Marine Corps.", "chunk_id": "3fc5da1aa653543a", "doc_id": "hp_95e3e85178f2cc76"}, {"text": "A global war that occurred from 1939 to 1945, during which Japanese Americans were interned.", "chunk_id": "c923a57087201126", "doc_id": "hp_ad41e3555a82bb26"}, {"text": "World War II is a global conflict during which Lawrence Haskell served in the United States Navy.", "chunk_id": "bf6beb2e41c2adee", "doc_id": "hp_ae365671bb34f99c"}, {"text": "A global war that lasted from 1939 to 1945.", "chunk_id": "615cdfa10474d8b6", "doc_id": "hp_c36e9406d9e10267"}, {"text": "World War II is an event during which The Cadet ceased production for three years.", "chunk_id": "ef24deb7580a2b51", "doc_id": "hp_d44bdbb955a3799c"}, {"text": "A global war that lasted from 1939 to 1945, involving the vast majority of the world's countries.", "chunk_id": "b24df285a9cc0262", "doc_id": "hp_ea0eba1a0f59fdf8"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Dale Minami (born October 13, 1946) is a San Francisco-based lawyer best known for heading the legal team that overturned the conviction of Fred Korematsu, whose defiance of the World War II Japanese American internment order lead to Korematsu v. United States, one of the most controversial United States Supreme Court decisions of the 20th century.", "chunk_id": "63f34134976a8d32", "doc_id": "hp_18a6d077ab278415"}, {"text": "The Holocaust, also referred to as the Shoah, was a genocide in which Adolf Hitler's Nazi Germany and its World War II collaborators killed some six million European Jews.", "chunk_id": "0b6495ca8fb3c7ab", "doc_id": "hp_58dc44606385cdf1"}, {"text": "Frederick Regional Airport, which includes restored World War II hangars which house the World War II Airborne Demonstration Team.", "chunk_id": "7ed2f23b7d77b089", "doc_id": "hp_6eb8e4170df0651b"}, {"text": "He served in the Pacific theatre during World War II with the Marine Corps and, after a brief return to the FBI, served as a shooting instructor with the Marine Corps until his retirement in the 1970s.", "chunk_id": "3fc5da1aa653543a", "doc_id": "hp_95e3e85178f2cc76"}, {"text": "Korematsu v. United States, 323 U.S. 214 (1944), was a landmark United States Supreme Court case concerning the constitutionality of Executive Order 9066, which ordered Japanese Americans into internment camps during World War II regardless of citizenship.", "chunk_id": "c923a57087201126", "doc_id": "hp_ad41e3555a82bb26"}, {"text": "In the military, Haskell was a Lieutenant Commander in the United States Navy during World War II.", "chunk_id": "bf6beb2e41c2adee", "doc_id": "hp_ae365671bb34f99c"}, {"text": "Although the Court did not touch on the constitutionality of the exclusion of people of Japanese ancestry from the West Coast—which they had found not to violate citizen rights in their \"Korematsu v. United States\" decision on the same date—the Endo ruling nonetheless led to the reopening of the West Coast to Japanese Americans after their incarceration in camps across the U.S. interior during World War II.", "chunk_id": "615cdfa10474d8b6", "doc_id": "hp_c36e9406d9e10267"}, {"text": "\"The Cadet\" did cease production for three years during World War II, however, it has been continuously published since then.", "chunk_id": "ef24deb7580a2b51", "doc_id": "hp_d44bdbb955a3799c"}, {"text": "Also referred to as the Shoah (in Hebrew), the Holocaust was a genocide in which some six million European Jews were killed by Nazi Germany and its World War II collaborators.", "chunk_id": "b24df285a9cc0262", "doc_id": "hp_ea0eba1a0f59fdf8"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_18a6d077ab278415", "hp_58dc44606385cdf1", "hp_6eb8e4170df0651b", "hp_95e3e85178f2cc76", "hp_ad41e3555a82bb26", "hp_ae365671bb34f99c", "hp_c36e9406d9e10267", "hp_d44bdbb955a3799c", "hp_ea0eba1a0f59fdf8"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Japanese American internment order">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An order related to the internment of Japanese Americans, defied by Fred Korematsu.", "chunk_id": "63f34134976a8d32", "doc_id": "hp_18a6d077ab278415"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Dale Minami (born October 13, 1946) is a San Francisco-based lawyer best known for heading the legal team that overturned the conviction of Fred Korematsu, whose defiance of the World War II Japanese American internment order lead to Korematsu v. United States, one of the most controversial United States Supreme Court decisions of the 20th century.", "chunk_id": "63f34134976a8d32", "doc_id": "hp_18a6d077ab278415"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_18a6d077ab278415"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="United States Supreme Court">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The highest court in the United States, which made the controversial decision in Korematsu v. United States.", "chunk_id": "63f34134976a8d32", "doc_id": "hp_18a6d077ab278415"}, {"text": "The highest court in the federal judiciary of the United States.", "chunk_id": "2d33ed84f83873de", "doc_id": "hp_2c019fb6db7dcbec"}, {"text": "The highest federal court of the United States.", "chunk_id": "e32ee493ed809ece", "doc_id": "hp_3811e4729d75dd3c"}, {"text": "The highest federal court of the United States.", "chunk_id": "c1e246687344e804", "doc_id": "hp_38ad5fccbbab039a"}, {"text": "The highest court of the United States, which heard the Korematsu v. United States case.", "chunk_id": "c923a57087201126", "doc_id": "hp_ad41e3555a82bb26"}, {"text": "The highest court of the United States, which heard the Ex parte Endo case.", "chunk_id": "615cdfa10474d8b6", "doc_id": "hp_c36e9406d9e10267"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Dale Minami (born October 13, 1946) is a San Francisco-based lawyer best known for heading the legal team that overturned the conviction of Fred Korematsu, whose defiance of the World War II Japanese American internment order lead to Korematsu v. United States, one of the most controversial United States Supreme Court decisions of the 20th century.", "chunk_id": "63f34134976a8d32", "doc_id": "hp_18a6d077ab278415"}, {"text": "United States v. Nixon, 418 U.S. 683 (1974), was a landmark United States Supreme Court decision which resulted in a unanimous 8–0 ruling against President Richard Nixon, ordering him to deliver presidential tape recordings and other subpoenaed materials to the District Court.", "chunk_id": "2d33ed84f83873de", "doc_id": "hp_2c019fb6db7dcbec"}, {"text": "Chaplinsky v. New Hampshire, 315 U.S. 568 (1942) , is a United States Supreme Court case in which the Court articulated the fighting words doctrine, a limitation of the First Amendment's guarantee of freedom of speech.", "chunk_id": "e32ee493ed809ece", "doc_id": "hp_3811e4729d75dd3c"}, {"text": "Duncan v. Kahanamoku, 327 U.S. 304 (1946), was a decision by the United States Supreme Court.", "chunk_id": "c1e246687344e804", "doc_id": "hp_38ad5fccbbab039a"}, {"text": "Korematsu v. United States, 323 U.S. 214 (1944), was a landmark United States Supreme Court case concerning the constitutionality of Executive Order 9066, which ordered Japanese Americans into internment camps during World War II regardless of citizenship.", "chunk_id": "c923a57087201126", "doc_id": "hp_ad41e3555a82bb26"}, {"text": "Ex parte Endo, or Ex parte Mitsuye Endo, 323 U.S. 283 (1944), was a United States Supreme Court ex parte decision handed down on December 18, 1944, in which the Justices unanimously ruled that the U.S. government could not continue to detain a citizen who was \"concededly loyal\" to the United States.", "chunk_id": "615cdfa10474d8b6", "doc_id": "hp_c36e9406d9e10267"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_18a6d077ab278415", "hp_2c019fb6db7dcbec", "hp_3811e4729d75dd3c", "hp_38ad5fccbbab039a", "hp_ad41e3555a82bb26", "hp_c36e9406d9e10267"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="San Francisco">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The city where Dale Minami is based.", "chunk_id": "63f34134976a8d32", "doc_id": "hp_18a6d077ab278415"}, {"text": "San Francisco is a city in California where the Occidental Hotel was located.", "chunk_id": "fbd09bf5bc7b0c64", "doc_id": "hp_350233375cc7c884"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Dale Minami (born October 13, 1946) is a San Francisco-based lawyer best known for heading the legal team that overturned the conviction of Fred Korematsu, whose defiance of the World War II Japanese American internment order lead to Korematsu v. United States, one of the most controversial United States Supreme Court decisions of the 20th century.", "chunk_id": "63f34134976a8d32", "doc_id": "hp_18a6d077ab278415"}, {"text": "The Occidental Hotel opened in 1861 in San Francisco, California.", "chunk_id": "fbd09bf5bc7b0c64", "doc_id": "hp_350233375cc7c884"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_18a6d077ab278415", "hp_350233375cc7c884"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Thomas James">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An American billionaire businessman who is the chairman of Raymond James Financial.", "chunk_id": "b6874d56d2fdd648", "doc_id": "hp_18fbcd7469354b78"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Thomas James (born 1942/43) is an American billionaire businessman, the chairman of Raymond James Financial, founded by his father Robert James, for 30 years.", "chunk_id": "b6874d56d2fdd648", "doc_id": "hp_18fbcd7469354b78"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_18fbcd7469354b78"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Laurus novocanariensis">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An evergreen large shrub or tree with aromatic, shiny dark-green foliage.", "chunk_id": "1680d6be464bcfe6", "doc_id": "hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Laurus novocanariensis is an evergreen large shrub or tree with aromatic, shiny dark-green foliage.", "chunk_id": "1680d6be464bcfe6", "doc_id": "hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Canary islands">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Islands where Laurus novocanariensis is native.", "chunk_id": "1680d6be464bcfe6", "doc_id": "hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a"}, {"text": "The Canary Islands are a Spanish archipelago and the southernmost autonomous community of Spain located in the Atlantic Ocean, 100 kilometres west of Morocco.", "chunk_id": "e5eca2e6dd8b8b88", "doc_id": "hp_7e8473e41faea381"}, {"text": "An archipelago and Spanish autonomous community off the coast of northwestern Africa.", "chunk_id": "f80e060f5f51afc7", "doc_id": "hp_a7eae4981b3aeb7c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is native of rich soils in the cloud zone of always moist spots in subtropical climate with a high air-humidity, on the Canary and Madeira islands.", "chunk_id": "1680d6be464bcfe6", "doc_id": "hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a"}, {"text": "Semele is a genus of flowering plants native to the Canary Islands and Madeira.", "chunk_id": "e5eca2e6dd8b8b88", "doc_id": "hp_7e8473e41faea381"}, {"text": "Podenco Canario (In English: \"Canary Islands Hound\", \"Canarian Warren Hound\") is a breed of dog originally from the Canary Islands.", "chunk_id": "f80e060f5f51afc7", "doc_id": "hp_a7eae4981b3aeb7c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a", "hp_7e8473e41faea381", "hp_a7eae4981b3aeb7c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Madeira islands">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Islands where Laurus novocanariensis is native.", "chunk_id": "1680d6be464bcfe6", "doc_id": "hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is native of rich soils in the cloud zone of always moist spots in subtropical climate with a high air-humidity, on the Canary and Madeira islands.", "chunk_id": "1680d6be464bcfe6", "doc_id": "hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Michael Jackson's This Is It (album)">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A posthumous two-disc soundtrack album by American singer Michael Jackson.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Michael Jackson's This Is It (album)", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Michael Jackson">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An American singer.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}, {"text": "The subject of the documentary-concert film Michael Jackson's This Is It, who was preparing for a concert series that was cancelled due to his death.", "chunk_id": "e8f7b78282274913", "doc_id": "hp_7df09ceedd2a307f"}, {"text": "An American recording artist.", "chunk_id": "4386b9386a9184fc", "doc_id": "hp_93fcd5b2eb13932b"}, {"text": "The subject of the documentary film, known as the 'King of Pop'.", "chunk_id": "824fceecb23d14cd", "doc_id": "hp_a2704beb739d6738"}, {"text": "An American pop star and musician.", "chunk_id": "8fc2541873625ab9", "doc_id": "hp_aba1d192473010be"}, {"text": "A musician whose choreographer Travis Payne worked with him.", "chunk_id": "6f28f99354276835", "doc_id": "hp_c98c5f35b4927af5"}, {"text": "A solo entertainer being celebrated for his 30th anniversary.", "chunk_id": "27c840a9f2ae6d8f", "doc_id": "hp_e324150cd91f309d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Michael Jackson's This Is It (or simply This Is It) is a posthumous two-disc soundtrack album by American singer Michael Jackson.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}, {"text": "Michael Jackson's This Is It is a 2009 American documentary–concert film directed by Kenny Ortega that documents Michael Jackson's rehearsals and preparation for his concert series of the same name that was originally scheduled to start on July 13, 2009, but was cancelled due to his death eighteen days prior on June 25.", "chunk_id": "e8f7b78282274913", "doc_id": "hp_7df09ceedd2a307f"}, {"text": "Michael Jackson's Vision is a deluxe DVD box set by American recording artist Michael Jackson.", "chunk_id": "4386b9386a9184fc", "doc_id": "hp_93fcd5b2eb13932b"}, {"text": "This historical documentary about Michael Jackson's last magazine cover-shoots in 2007.", "chunk_id": "824fceecb23d14cd", "doc_id": "hp_a2704beb739d6738"}, {"text": "\"This Is It\" is a song co-written by American pop star and musician Michael Jackson and Canadian singer-songwriter Paul Anka.", "chunk_id": "8fc2541873625ab9", "doc_id": "hp_aba1d192473010be"}, {"text": "Judging alongside Abdul were Kimberly Wyatt, the former member of Pussycat Dolls, and Michael Jackson's long-time choreographer Travis Payne.", "chunk_id": "6f28f99354276835", "doc_id": "hp_c98c5f35b4927af5"}, {"text": "The Michael Jackson: 30th Anniversary Celebration was a 2001 New York City revue show by Michael Jackson.", "chunk_id": "27c840a9f2ae6d8f", "doc_id": "hp_e324150cd91f309d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6", "hp_7df09ceedd2a307f", "hp_93fcd5b2eb13932b", "hp_a2704beb739d6738", "hp_aba1d192473010be", "hp_c98c5f35b4927af5", "hp_e324150cd91f309d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="This Is It">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A posthumous two-disc soundtrack album by American singer Michael Jackson.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Michael Jackson's This Is It (or simply This Is It) is a posthumous two-disc soundtrack album by American singer Michael Jackson.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="MJJ Music">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The record label that released the album \"This Is It\".", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Released by MJJ Music on October 26, 2009, \"This Is It\" features previously released music, as well as six previously unreleased recordings by Michael Jackson.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Michael Jackson's This Is It">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A concert film documenting Michael Jackson's rehearsals for the This Is It concert series.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}, {"text": "A 2009 American documentary–concert film directed by Kenny Ortega that documents Michael Jackson's rehearsals and preparation for his concert series of the same name.", "chunk_id": "e8f7b78282274913", "doc_id": "hp_7df09ceedd2a307f"}, {"text": "A 2009 concert documentary.", "chunk_id": "8fc2541873625ab9", "doc_id": "hp_aba1d192473010be"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"This Is It\" was released to coincide with the theatrical release of \"Michael Jackson's This Is It\", a concert film documenting Michael Jackson's rehearsals for the This Is It concert series at London's O2 Arena.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}, {"text": "Michael Jackson's This Is It is a 2009 American documentary–concert film directed by Kenny Ortega that documents Michael Jackson's rehearsals and preparation for his concert series of the same name that was originally scheduled to start on July 13, 2009, but was cancelled due to his death eighteen days prior on June 25.", "chunk_id": "e8f7b78282274913", "doc_id": "hp_7df09ceedd2a307f"}, {"text": "The song was recorded by the former and featured as a track on the album, \"This Is It\" (2009), which accompanies the 2009 concert documentary \"Michael Jackson's This Is It\".", "chunk_id": "8fc2541873625ab9", "doc_id": "hp_aba1d192473010be"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6", "hp_7df09ceedd2a307f", "hp_aba1d192473010be"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="This Is It concert series">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A concert series for which Michael Jackson was rehearsing.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"This Is It\" was released to coincide with the theatrical release of \"Michael Jackson's This Is It\", a concert film documenting Michael Jackson's rehearsals for the This Is It concert series at London's O2 Arena.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="London's O2 Arena">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The venue where Michael Jackson was rehearsing for the This Is It concert series.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"This Is It\" was released to coincide with the theatrical release of \"Michael Jackson's This Is It\", a concert film documenting Michael Jackson's rehearsals for the This Is It concert series at London's O2 Arena.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Sony">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A company that has released albums by Michael Jackson since his death.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"This Is It\" is the sixth album to be released by Sony and Motown/Universal since Michael Jackson's death in June 2009.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Motown/Universal">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A company that has released albums by Michael Jackson since his death.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"This Is It\" is the sixth album to be released by Sony and Motown/Universal since Michael Jackson's death in June 2009.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Convoy TM 1">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Convoy TM 1 was the code name for an Allied convoy during the Second World War.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Convoy TM 1 was the code name for an Allied convoy during the Second World War.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1ac7b848b0417759"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Second World War">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The historical period during which Convoy TM 1 took place.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}, {"text": "The Second World War was a period during which William de Ropp was involved in dealings with Nazi Germany.", "chunk_id": "c718da7aed95bfa4", "doc_id": "hp_6693cb8c76cc99b6"}, {"text": "A major global conflict that began twenty-one years after the end of World War I, partly due to unresolved rivalries from the earlier conflict.", "chunk_id": "b344f42adf99d038", "doc_id": "hp_831bc66834df032a"}, {"text": "The Second World War is the historical period after which Boulevard Solitude is set in Paris.", "chunk_id": "8dbccb5758e54e3f", "doc_id": "hp_ce10cea1030952d1"}, {"text": "A global conflict whose combatants were later included in the eligibility for the Escapees' Medal.", "chunk_id": "cd19157192f4048d", "doc_id": "hp_e60b5baaa105aa72"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Convoy TM 1 was the code name for an Allied convoy during the Second World War.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}, {"text": "Baron William Sylvester de Ropp, originally Sylvester Wilhelm Gotthard von der Ropp (12 December 1886 - 1973 ) was a British agent involved in dealings with Nazi Germany before and during the Second World War.", "chunk_id": "c718da7aed95bfa4", "doc_id": "hp_6693cb8c76cc99b6"}, {"text": "Unresolved rivalries still extant at the end of the conflict contributed to the start of the Second World War only twenty-one years later.", "chunk_id": "b344f42adf99d038", "doc_id": "hp_831bc66834df032a"}, {"text": "The piece is a reworking of the Manon Lescaut story, already adapted operatically by Auber, Massenet and Puccini, and here relocated to Paris after the Second World War where, as is noted in Grove, the focus of the story moves away from Manon and towards Armand des Grieux.", "chunk_id": "8dbccb5758e54e3f", "doc_id": "hp_ce10cea1030952d1"}, {"text": "Its statute was later amended to include combatants of the Second World War and later conflicts.", "chunk_id": "cd19157192f4048d", "doc_id": "hp_e60b5baaa105aa72"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1ac7b848b0417759", "hp_6693cb8c76cc99b6", "hp_831bc66834df032a", "hp_ce10cea1030952d1", "hp_e60b5baaa105aa72"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Allied convoy">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A convoy organized by the Allies during wartime.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Convoy TM 1 was the code name for an Allied convoy during the Second World War.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1ac7b848b0417759"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Royal Navy">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The United Kingdom's naval warfare force.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}, {"text": "The United Kingdom's naval warfare force.", "chunk_id": "fc8924b200c0f580", "doc_id": "hp_5129e4fb643a43c0"}, {"text": "The United Kingdom's naval warfare force.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Nine tankers, escorted by Royal Navy warships, attempted to reach Gibraltar from Trinidad.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}, {"text": "HMS \"Clonmel\" was a Hunt class minesweeper of the Royal Navy from World War I.", "chunk_id": "fc8924b200c0f580", "doc_id": "hp_5129e4fb643a43c0"}, {"text": "Rear Admiral George Heneage Lawrence Dundas CB (8 September 1778 – 7 October 1834) was a senior officer in the Royal Navy.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1ac7b848b0417759", "hp_5129e4fb643a43c0", "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Gibraltar">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A British Overseas Territory located on the southern tip of the Iberian Peninsula.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Nine tankers, escorted by Royal Navy warships, attempted to reach Gibraltar from Trinidad.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1ac7b848b0417759"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Trinidad">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An island country in the southern Caribbean.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Nine tankers, escorted by Royal Navy warships, attempted to reach Gibraltar from Trinidad.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1ac7b848b0417759"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="U-boat wolf pack">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A group of German submarines operating together.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The convoy was attacked by a U-boat wolf pack in the central Atlantic Ocean, and most of the merchant vessels were sunk.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1ac7b848b0417759"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="central Atlantic Ocean">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The central region of the Atlantic Ocean.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The convoy was attacked by a U-boat wolf pack in the central Atlantic Ocean, and most of the merchant vessels were sunk.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1ac7b848b0417759"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="merchant vessels">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Ships used for commerce, in this context, tankers carrying supplies.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The convoy was attacked by a U-boat wolf pack in the central Atlantic Ocean, and most of the merchant vessels were sunk.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1ac7b848b0417759"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Allied supply convoys">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Convoys organized by the Allies to transport supplies during wartime.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "This was one of the most successful attacks on Allied supply convoys throughout the entire war.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1ac7b848b0417759"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="HMS &quot;Havelock&quot;">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A destroyer that defended Convoy TM 1.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The convoy was defended by the destroyer HMS \"Havelock\", and three Flower class corvettes, HMS \"Godetia\" , HMS \"Pimpernel\" and HMS \"Saxifrage\".", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1ac7b848b0417759"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Flower class corvettes">
  <data key="d0">TECHNOLOGY</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A class of small warships built for the Royal Navy during World War II.", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The convoy was defended by the destroyer HMS \"Havelock\", and three Flower class corvettes, HMS \"Godetia\" , HMS \"Pimpernel\" and HMS \"Saxifrage\".", "chunk_id": "c88e8c3532f53397", "doc_id": "hp_1ac7b848b0417759"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_1ac7b848b0417759"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
