<node id="Scotland">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Scotland is a country where Leith is located.", "chunk_id": "fed038ae0c566b69", "doc_id": "hp_26004159736d7249"}, {"text": "A country in the United Kingdom where Glasgow is located.", "chunk_id": "e7083278f65fe2f0", "doc_id": "hp_4b9fa482e8ceec5a"}, {"text": "Scotland is a country where the band Travis is from.", "chunk_id": "8043cae2ef7b7fae", "doc_id": "hp_5e36dcc4c1a872ca"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The Siege of Leith ended a twelve-year encampment of French troops at Leith, the port near Edinburgh, Scotland.", "chunk_id": "fed038ae0c566b69", "doc_id": "hp_26004159736d7249"}, {"text": "Notre Dame High School is a comprehensive state school for girls located on Observatory Road in Glasgow, Scotland, and founded in 1897.", "chunk_id": "e7083278f65fe2f0", "doc_id": "hp_4b9fa482e8ceec5a"}, {"text": "Travis is an alternative rock band from Glasgow, Scotland, comprising Fran Healy (lead vocals, guitar, piano, banjo), Dougie Payne (bass guitar, backing vocals), Andy Dunlop (lead guitar, banjo, keyboards, backing vocals) and Neil Primrose (drums, percussion).", "chunk_id": "8043cae2ef7b7fae", "doc_id": "hp_5e36dcc4c1a872ca"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_26004159736d7249", "hp_4b9fa482e8ceec5a", "hp_5e36dcc4c1a872ca"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="1548">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The year 1548 when French troops arrived by invitation.", "chunk_id": "fed038ae0c566b69", "doc_id": "hp_26004159736d7249"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The French troops arrived by invitation in 1548 and left in 1560 after an English force arrived to attempt to assist in removing them from Scotland.", "chunk_id": "fed038ae0c566b69", "doc_id": "hp_26004159736d7249"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_26004159736d7249"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="1560">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The year 1560 when French troops left.", "chunk_id": "fed038ae0c566b69", "doc_id": "hp_26004159736d7249"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The French troops arrived by invitation in 1548 and left in 1560 after an English force arrived to attempt to assist in removing them from Scotland.", "chunk_id": "fed038ae0c566b69", "doc_id": "hp_26004159736d7249"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_26004159736d7249"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="English force">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An English force arrived to assist in removing French troops from Scotland.", "chunk_id": "fed038ae0c566b69", "doc_id": "hp_26004159736d7249"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The French troops arrived by invitation in 1548 and left in 1560 after an English force arrived to attempt to assist in removing them from Scotland.", "chunk_id": "fed038ae0c566b69", "doc_id": "hp_26004159736d7249"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_26004159736d7249"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="France">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "France is a country that signed a treaty regarding the French troops.", "chunk_id": "fed038ae0c566b69", "doc_id": "hp_26004159736d7249"}, {"text": "The country of origin for the Chien Français Tricolore breed of dog.", "chunk_id": "434a4988e0d48510", "doc_id": "hp_551a94d4b6ae14c7"}, {"text": "The country of origin for the Chien Français Blanc et Orange dog breed.", "chunk_id": "c2eabaef2329cb08", "doc_id": "hp_6fcdf37bec724a84"}, {"text": "The country of origin for the Chien Français Blanc et Noir dog breed.", "chunk_id": "de5a56171a2e0728", "doc_id": "hp_7ed6a2b681322402"}, {"text": "A country where the Champagne region is located.", "chunk_id": "528eebe85217e215", "doc_id": "hp_8aed4603836974ec"}, {"text": "A country where the poet studied and can still hear the tree's lament.", "chunk_id": "4311709e1a9f0b6d", "doc_id": "hp_8cb6340f34038734"}, {"text": "France is a country where Braque français are popular hunting dogs.", "chunk_id": "27ab68d978f43c6c", "doc_id": "hp_cdc7b0cc951d083b"}, {"text": "A country that bestows the Escapees' Medal.", "chunk_id": "cd19157192f4048d", "doc_id": "hp_e60b5baaa105aa72"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The town was not taken by force and the French troops finally left peacefully under the terms of a treaty signed by Scotland, England and France.", "chunk_id": "fed038ae0c566b69", "doc_id": "hp_26004159736d7249"}, {"text": "The Chien Français Tricolore (FCI No.219) translated into English as the French Tricolour Hound, is a breed of dog of the scenthound type, originating in France.", "chunk_id": "434a4988e0d48510", "doc_id": "hp_551a94d4b6ae14c7"}, {"text": "The Chien Français Blanc et Orange (FCI No.316) is a breed of dog of the scenthound type, originating in France.", "chunk_id": "c2eabaef2329cb08", "doc_id": "hp_6fcdf37bec724a84"}, {"text": "The Chien Français Blanc et Noir (FCI No.220) translated into English as the French White and Black Hound, is a breed of dog of the scenthound type, originating in France.", "chunk_id": "de5a56171a2e0728", "doc_id": "hp_7ed6a2b681322402"}, {"text": "Bertrand de Bar- Bar-sur-Aube (i.e. Bertrand from Bar-sur-Aube) (end of the 12th century – early 13th century) was an Old French poet from the Champagne region of France who wrote a number of \"chansons de geste\".", "chunk_id": "528eebe85217e215", "doc_id": "hp_8aed4603836974ec"}, {"text": "Even in France and Italy (where the poet studied), she can hear the tree's lament.", "chunk_id": "4311709e1a9f0b6d", "doc_id": "hp_8cb6340f34038734"}, {"text": "They are popular hunting dogs in France, but are seldom seen elsewhere.", "chunk_id": "27ab68d978f43c6c", "doc_id": "hp_cdc7b0cc951d083b"}, {"text": "The Escapees' Medal (French: \"Médaille des Évadés\" ) is a military award bestowed by the government of France to individuals who were prisoners of war and who successfully escaped internment or died as a result of their escape attempt.", "chunk_id": "cd19157192f4048d", "doc_id": "hp_e60b5baaa105aa72"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_26004159736d7249", "hp_551a94d4b6ae14c7", "hp_6fcdf37bec724a84", "hp_7ed6a2b681322402", "hp_8aed4603836974ec", "hp_8cb6340f34038734", "hp_cdc7b0cc951d083b", "hp_e60b5baaa105aa72"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="James Bernard Machen">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An American university professor and administrator.", "chunk_id": "af74dae8d5aba822", "doc_id": "hp_278033422b0dac1b"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "James Bernard Machen ( ; born March 26, 1944) is an American university professor and administrator.", "chunk_id": "af74dae8d5aba822", "doc_id": "hp_278033422b0dac1b"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_278033422b0dac1b"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
