<node id="Liriodendron">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Liriodendron is a genus of two species, with Liriodendron tulipifera being the Western Hemisphere representative.", "chunk_id": "976ede3d58522907", "doc_id": "hp_2c1beb2f73cca8d4"}, {"text": "Liriodendron is a genus of two species of large deciduous trees.", "chunk_id": "3a3894b0c2506647", "doc_id": "hp_96ca685873d892fc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Liriodendron tulipifera—known as the tulip tree, American tulip tree, tuliptree, tulip poplar, whitewood, fiddletree, and yellow-poplar—is the Western Hemisphere representative of the two-species genus \"Liriodendron,\" and the tallest eastern hardwood.", "chunk_id": "976ede3d58522907", "doc_id": "hp_2c1beb2f73cca8d4"}, {"text": "Liriodendron is a genus of two species of characteristically large deciduous trees in the magnolia family (Magnoliaceae).", "chunk_id": "3a3894b0c2506647", "doc_id": "hp_96ca685873d892fc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_2c1beb2f73cca8d4", "hp_96ca685873d892fc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="eastern hardwood">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Eastern hardwood refers to the tallest hardwood species found in the eastern regions.", "chunk_id": "976ede3d58522907", "doc_id": "hp_2c1beb2f73cca8d4"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Liriodendron tulipifera—known as the tulip tree, American tulip tree, tuliptree, tulip poplar, whitewood, fiddletree, and yellow-poplar—is the Western Hemisphere representative of the two-species genus \"Liriodendron,\" and the tallest eastern hardwood.", "chunk_id": "976ede3d58522907", "doc_id": "hp_2c1beb2f73cca8d4"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_2c1beb2f73cca8d4"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Southern Ontario">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Southern Ontario is a region in Canada where Liriodendron tulipifera is native.", "chunk_id": "976ede3d58522907", "doc_id": "hp_2c1beb2f73cca8d4"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is native to eastern North America from Southern Ontario and Illinois eastward to southeastern Massachusetts and Rhode Island, and south to central Florida and Louisiana.", "chunk_id": "976ede3d58522907", "doc_id": "hp_2c1beb2f73cca8d4"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_2c1beb2f73cca8d4"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Illinois">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Illinois is a state in the United States where Liriodendron tulipifera is native.", "chunk_id": "976ede3d58522907", "doc_id": "hp_2c1beb2f73cca8d4"}, {"text": "Illinois is a state in the United States where Chicago is located.", "chunk_id": "e1f93f4fdb5e61f5", "doc_id": "hp_db88fb2791fae586"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is native to eastern North America from Southern Ontario and Illinois eastward to southeastern Massachusetts and Rhode Island, and south to central Florida and Louisiana.", "chunk_id": "976ede3d58522907", "doc_id": "hp_2c1beb2f73cca8d4"}, {"text": "Notre Dame High School for Girls was a private, Roman Catholic, all-girls college prep high school in Chicago, Illinois.", "chunk_id": "e1f93f4fdb5e61f5", "doc_id": "hp_db88fb2791fae586"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_2c1beb2f73cca8d4", "hp_db88fb2791fae586"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
