<node id="fynbos">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Fynbos is a type of vegetation found in South Africa, which Phylica species form part of.", "chunk_id": "6b62f66ee7182ec5", "doc_id": "hp_2ca4198c5242553c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It contains about 150 species, the majority of which are restricted to South Africa, where they form part of the \"fynbos \".", "chunk_id": "6b62f66ee7182ec5", "doc_id": "hp_2ca4198c5242553c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_2ca4198c5242553c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Madagascar">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Madagascar is an island where a few species of Phylica occur.", "chunk_id": "6b62f66ee7182ec5", "doc_id": "hp_2ca4198c5242553c"}, {"text": "Madagascar is a location where Pachypodium is native to.", "chunk_id": "c65de02bc9af4260", "doc_id": "hp_a9669326c71f5122"}, {"text": "Madagascar is an island country in the Indian Ocean.", "chunk_id": "328b606d106a5a36", "doc_id": "hp_ebe09fc434bfa448"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "A few species occur in other parts of southern Africa, and on islands including Madagascar, the Mascarene Islands, Île Amsterdam, Saint Helena, Tristan da Cunha, and Gough Island.", "chunk_id": "6b62f66ee7182ec5", "doc_id": "hp_2ca4198c5242553c"}, {"text": "Pachypodium is a genus of succulent spine-bearing trees and shrubs, native to Madagascar and Africa.", "chunk_id": "c65de02bc9af4260", "doc_id": "hp_a9669326c71f5122"}, {"text": "They are woody or weakly woody plants occurring in Southeast Asia, the Pacific, Madagascar, Central and South America, and the West Indies.", "chunk_id": "328b606d106a5a36", "doc_id": "hp_ebe09fc434bfa448"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_2ca4198c5242553c", "hp_a9669326c71f5122", "hp_ebe09fc434bfa448"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
