<node id="BBC One">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A British television channel.", "chunk_id": "2d1cd752b15a14fe", "doc_id": "hp_323aaf8fc4b0ff2c"}, {"text": "A British television channel that aired the sitcom 'Let Them Eat Cake'.", "chunk_id": "3fa71aaae5f778d3", "doc_id": "hp_66c764ac56267d4d"}, {"text": "A British television channel that aired the sitcom Jam &amp; Jerusalem.", "chunk_id": "0a9ce939e4324315", "doc_id": "hp_e874da810d9b0fb1"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The fourth series of British sitcom \"Absolutely Fabulous\" premiered on BBC One on 31 August 2001.", "chunk_id": "2d1cd752b15a14fe", "doc_id": "hp_323aaf8fc4b0ff2c"}, {"text": "Let Them Eat Cake is a British sitcom that aired on BBC One in 1999.", "chunk_id": "3fa71aaae5f778d3", "doc_id": "hp_66c764ac56267d4d"}, {"text": "Jam &amp; Jerusalem is a British sitcom that aired on BBC One from 2006 to 2009.", "chunk_id": "0a9ce939e4324315", "doc_id": "hp_e874da810d9b0fb1"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_323aaf8fc4b0ff2c", "hp_66c764ac56267d4d", "hp_e874da810d9b0fb1"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="The Last Shout">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Two specials created to serve as an official finale to the series Absolutely Fabulous.", "chunk_id": "2d1cd752b15a14fe", "doc_id": "hp_323aaf8fc4b0ff2c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "then the final episodes, titled 'The Last Shout', consisting of two specials were created to serve as an official finale to the series.", "chunk_id": "2d1cd752b15a14fe", "doc_id": "hp_323aaf8fc4b0ff2c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_323aaf8fc4b0ff2c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Mirrorball">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A proposed upcoming new series for which Jennifer Saunders created and wrote a television pilot.", "chunk_id": "2d1cd752b15a14fe", "doc_id": "hp_323aaf8fc4b0ff2c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "However, in 2000, Jennifer Saunders had created and written a television pilot for a proposed upcoming new series, \"Mirrorball\" in which she intended to reunite the cast of \"Ab Fab\" in new character roles and a different plot.", "chunk_id": "2d1cd752b15a14fe", "doc_id": "hp_323aaf8fc4b0ff2c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_323aaf8fc4b0ff2c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Jennifer Saunders">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Creator and writer of the television pilot for \"Mirrorball\" and writer for \"Absolutely Fabulous\".", "chunk_id": "2d1cd752b15a14fe", "doc_id": "hp_323aaf8fc4b0ff2c"}, {"text": "An English comedian, actor, and writer who co-created and starred in Absolutely Fabulous.", "chunk_id": "f54971948ab8acd8", "doc_id": "hp_327a998a822bc9e6"}, {"text": "Jennifer Saunders is a comedian and a member of the spoof group Lananeeneenoonoo.", "chunk_id": "c11c9287534c04db", "doc_id": "hp_57f0c97f7881985b"}, {"text": "An actress who starred in the British sitcom 'Let Them Eat Cake'.", "chunk_id": "3fa71aaae5f778d3", "doc_id": "hp_66c764ac56267d4d"}, {"text": "A comic who is part of the duo French and Saunders.", "chunk_id": "0cba2f1e48972df0", "doc_id": "hp_a43a1b7d6bf4ac88"}, {"text": "Jennifer Saunders is a comedy partner of Dawn French.", "chunk_id": "8f5e1ed518366291", "doc_id": "hp_b150127ee448fafd"}, {"text": "A member of the comedy duo French and Saunders.", "chunk_id": "da03dc4aa612a116", "doc_id": "hp_b1fcfbca9c340147"}, {"text": "Jennifer Saunders is a Canadian racquetball player who has won multiple titles with Josée Grand'Maître.", "chunk_id": "55ab038a3c41aeea", "doc_id": "hp_d2b1b9b8bce24c9a"}, {"text": "A writer and star of the sitcom Jam &amp; Jerusalem.", "chunk_id": "0a9ce939e4324315", "doc_id": "hp_e874da810d9b0fb1"}, {"text": "Jennifer Saunders is an actress who starred in the film The Supergrass.", "chunk_id": "3490da9f777ecd88", "doc_id": "hp_f962c6bd05ae98f7"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "However, in 2000, Jennifer Saunders had created and written a television pilot for a proposed upcoming new series, \"Mirrorball\" in which she intended to reunite the cast of \"Ab Fab\" in new character roles and a different plot.", "chunk_id": "2d1cd752b15a14fe", "doc_id": "hp_323aaf8fc4b0ff2c"}, {"text": "Absolutely Fabulous, also known as Ab Fab, is a BBC television sitcom created by, written by and starring Jennifer Saunders.", "chunk_id": "f54971948ab8acd8", "doc_id": "hp_327a998a822bc9e6"}, {"text": "Lananeeneenoonoo was a British spoof all-girl group consisting of comedians Dawn French, Jennifer Saunders and Kathy Burke.", "chunk_id": "c11c9287534c04db", "doc_id": "hp_57f0c97f7881985b"}, {"text": "Starring Dawn French and Jennifer Saunders, it is one of the few programmes in which French and Saunders have appeared which they did not create themselves.", "chunk_id": "3fa71aaae5f778d3", "doc_id": "hp_66c764ac56267d4d"}, {"text": "French and Saunders is a British sketch comedy television series written by and starring comic duo Dawn French and Jennifer Saunders.", "chunk_id": "0cba2f1e48972df0", "doc_id": "hp_a43a1b7d6bf4ac88"}, {"text": "She is best known for starring in and writing for the comedy sketch show \"French and Saunders\" with comedy partner Jennifer Saunders and for playing the lead role as Geraldine Granger in the sitcom \"The Vicar of Dibley\".", "chunk_id": "8f5e1ed518366291", "doc_id": "hp_b150127ee448fafd"}, {"text": "French and Saunders: Still Alive! is a 2008 tour by comedy duo Dawn French and Jennifer Saunders.", "chunk_id": "da03dc4aa612a116", "doc_id": "hp_b1fcfbca9c340147"}, {"text": "Grand'Maître is the current Canadian Women's Doubles Champion, winning her 14th doubles title in Langley, British Columbia with Jennifer Saunders in May 2013.", "chunk_id": "55ab038a3c41aeea", "doc_id": "hp_d2b1b9b8bce24c9a"}, {"text": "Written by Jennifer Saunders and Abigail Wilson, it starred Sue Johnston, Jennifer Saunders, Pauline McLynn, Dawn French, Maggie Steed, David Mitchell, and Sally Phillips.", "chunk_id": "0a9ce939e4324315", "doc_id": "hp_e874da810d9b0fb1"}, {"text": "The film starred Richardson, Adrian Edmondson, Jennifer Saunders, Dawn French, Keith Allen, Nigel Planer, Alexei Sayle, Ronald Allen and Robbie Coltrane.", "chunk_id": "3490da9f777ecd88", "doc_id": "hp_f962c6bd05ae98f7"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_323aaf8fc4b0ff2c", "hp_327a998a822bc9e6", "hp_57f0c97f7881985b", "hp_66c764ac56267d4d", "hp_a43a1b7d6bf4ac88", "hp_b150127ee448fafd", "hp_b1fcfbca9c340147", "hp_d2b1b9b8bce24c9a", "hp_e874da810d9b0fb1", "hp_f962c6bd05ae98f7"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Ab Fab">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An alternative name for the British sitcom Absolutely Fabulous.", "chunk_id": "2d1cd752b15a14fe", "doc_id": "hp_323aaf8fc4b0ff2c"}, {"text": "An alternative name for the BBC television sitcom Absolutely Fabulous.", "chunk_id": "f54971948ab8acd8", "doc_id": "hp_327a998a822bc9e6"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "However, in 2000, Jennifer Saunders had created and written a television pilot for a proposed upcoming new series, \"Mirrorball\" in which she intended to reunite the cast of \"Ab Fab\" in new character roles and a different plot.", "chunk_id": "2d1cd752b15a14fe", "doc_id": "hp_323aaf8fc4b0ff2c"}, {"text": "Absolutely Fabulous, also known as Ab Fab, is a BBC television sitcom created by, written by and starring Jennifer Saunders.", "chunk_id": "f54971948ab8acd8", "doc_id": "hp_327a998a822bc9e6"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_323aaf8fc4b0ff2c", "hp_327a998a822bc9e6"]</data>
