<node id="Gormond et Isembart">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An Old French chanson de geste from the second half of the eleventh or first half of the twelfth century.", "chunk_id": "54cbfcfe8378cde7", "doc_id": "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Gormond et Isembart (English: \"Gormond and Isembart\") is an Old French \"chanson de geste\" from the second half of the eleventh or first half of the twelfth century.", "chunk_id": "54cbfcfe8378cde7", "doc_id": "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="The Song of Roland">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A chanson de geste whose composition incontestably dates from before 1150.", "chunk_id": "54cbfcfe8378cde7", "doc_id": "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"}, {"text": "An earlier \"chanson de geste\" closely linked to Galiens li Restorés.", "chunk_id": "850408ca66a7d9e6", "doc_id": "hp_3fac05a2ac9ec6d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Along with \"The Song of Roland\" and the \"Chanson de Guillaume\", it is one of the three \"chansons de geste\" whose composition incontestably dates from before 1150; it may be slightly younger than \"The Song of Roland\" and, according to one expert, may date from as early as 1068.", "chunk_id": "54cbfcfe8378cde7", "doc_id": "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"}, {"text": "The story—which is closely linked to the earlier \"chansons de geste\" \"Pèlerinage de Charlemagne\" and \"The Song of Roland\" (especially in the latter's rhymed version)—tells of the adventures of Galien, son of the hero Olivier and of Jacqueline, the daughter of the (fictional) emperor Hugon (Hue the Strong) of Constantinople.", "chunk_id": "850408ca66a7d9e6", "doc_id": "hp_3fac05a2ac9ec6d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_348f259ed8ae2d75", "hp_3fac05a2ac9ec6d2"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Chanson de Guillaume">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A chanson de geste whose composition incontestably dates from before 1150.", "chunk_id": "54cbfcfe8378cde7", "doc_id": "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Along with \"The Song of Roland\" and the \"Chanson de Guillaume\", it is one of the three \"chansons de geste\" whose composition incontestably dates from before 1150; it may be slightly younger than \"The Song of Roland\" and, according to one expert, may date from as early as 1068.", "chunk_id": "54cbfcfe8378cde7", "doc_id": "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Isembart">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A rebellious young French lord who allies himself with a Saracen king, Gormond, renounces his Christianity, and battles the French king.", "chunk_id": "54cbfcfe8378cde7", "doc_id": "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The poem tells the story of a rebellious young French lord, Isembart, who allies himself with a Saracen king, Gormond, renounces his Christianity, and battles the French king.", "chunk_id": "54cbfcfe8378cde7", "doc_id": "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Gormond">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A Saracen king with whom Isembart allies himself.", "chunk_id": "54cbfcfe8378cde7", "doc_id": "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The poem tells the story of a rebellious young French lord, Isembart, who allies himself with a Saracen king, Gormond, renounces his Christianity, and battles the French king.", "chunk_id": "54cbfcfe8378cde7", "doc_id": "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_348f259ed8ae2d75"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
