<node id="Moment (mathematics)">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A moment in mathematics is a quantitative measure of the shape of a set of points, used in mechanics and statistics.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In mathematics, a moment is a specific quantitative measure, used in both mechanics and statistics, of the shape of a set of points.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_377365afd31f980a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="mechanics">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Mechanics is a field where moments are used as a quantitative measure of the shape of a set of points.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In mathematics, a moment is a specific quantitative measure, used in both mechanics and statistics, of the shape of a set of points.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_377365afd31f980a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="statistics">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Statistics is a field where moments are used as a quantitative measure of the shape of a set of points.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In mathematics, a moment is a specific quantitative measure, used in both mechanics and statistics, of the shape of a set of points.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_377365afd31f980a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="total mass">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The zeroth moment, when points represent mass, is the total mass.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "If the points represent mass, then the zeroth moment is the total mass, the first moment divided by the total mass is the center of mass, and the second moment is the rotational inertia.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_377365afd31f980a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="center of mass">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The first moment divided by the total mass, when points represent mass, is the center of mass.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "If the points represent mass, then the zeroth moment is the total mass, the first moment divided by the total mass is the center of mass, and the second moment is the rotational inertia.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_377365afd31f980a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="rotational inertia">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The second moment, when points represent mass, is the rotational inertia.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "If the points represent mass, then the zeroth moment is the total mass, the first moment divided by the total mass is the center of mass, and the second moment is the rotational inertia.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_377365afd31f980a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="probability density">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Probability density is a concept where moments are used to describe its properties.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "If the points represent probability density, then the zeroth moment is the total probability (i.e. one), the first moment is the mean, the second central moment is the variance, the third central moment is the skewness, and the fourth central moment (with normalization and shift) is the kurtosis.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_377365afd31f980a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="total probability">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The zeroth moment, when points represent probability density, is the total probability.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "If the points represent probability density, then the zeroth moment is the total probability (i.e. one), the first moment is the mean, the second central moment is the variance, the third central moment is the skewness, and the fourth central moment (with normalization and shift) is the kurtosis.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_377365afd31f980a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="mean">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The first moment, when points represent probability density, is the mean.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "If the points represent probability density, then the zeroth moment is the total probability (i.e. one), the first moment is the mean, the second central moment is the variance, the third central moment is the skewness, and the fourth central moment (with normalization and shift) is the kurtosis.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_377365afd31f980a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="variance">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The second central moment, when points represent probability density, is the variance.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "If the points represent probability density, then the zeroth moment is the total probability (i.e. one), the first moment is the mean, the second central moment is the variance, the third central moment is the skewness, and the fourth central moment (with normalization and shift) is the kurtosis.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_377365afd31f980a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="skewness">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The third central moment, when points represent probability density, is the skewness.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "If the points represent probability density, then the zeroth moment is the total probability (i.e. one), the first moment is the mean, the second central moment is the variance, the third central moment is the skewness, and the fourth central moment (with normalization and shift) is the kurtosis.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_377365afd31f980a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="kurtosis">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The fourth central moment (with normalization and shift), when points represent probability density, is the kurtosis.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "If the points represent probability density, then the zeroth moment is the total probability (i.e. one), the first moment is the mean, the second central moment is the variance, the third central moment is the skewness, and the fourth central moment (with normalization and shift) is the kurtosis.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_377365afd31f980a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="moment in physics">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A concept in physics that is closely related to the mathematical concept of a moment.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The mathematical concept is closely related to the concept of moment in physics.", "chunk_id": "d05fccba660922a2", "doc_id": "hp_377365afd31f980a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_377365afd31f980a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Chaplinsky v. New Hampshire">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A United States Supreme Court case that articulated the fighting words doctrine.", "chunk_id": "e32ee493ed809ece", "doc_id": "hp_3811e4729d75dd3c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Chaplinsky v. New Hampshire, 315 U.S. 568 (1942) , is a United States Supreme Court case in which the Court articulated the fighting words doctrine, a limitation of the First Amendment's guarantee of freedom of speech.", "chunk_id": "e32ee493ed809ece", "doc_id": "hp_3811e4729d75dd3c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3811e4729d75dd3c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="fighting words doctrine">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A limitation of the First Amendment's guarantee of freedom of speech.", "chunk_id": "e32ee493ed809ece", "doc_id": "hp_3811e4729d75dd3c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Chaplinsky v. New Hampshire, 315 U.S. 568 (1942) , is a United States Supreme Court case in which the Court articulated the fighting words doctrine, a limitation of the First Amendment's guarantee of freedom of speech.", "chunk_id": "e32ee493ed809ece", "doc_id": "hp_3811e4729d75dd3c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3811e4729d75dd3c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="First Amendment">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The First Amendment to the United States Constitution protects freedom of speech.", "chunk_id": "e32ee493ed809ece", "doc_id": "hp_3811e4729d75dd3c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Chaplinsky v. New Hampshire, 315 U.S. 568 (1942) , is a United States Supreme Court case in which the Court articulated the fighting words doctrine, a limitation of the First Amendment's guarantee of freedom of speech.", "chunk_id": "e32ee493ed809ece", "doc_id": "hp_3811e4729d75dd3c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3811e4729d75dd3c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="freedom of speech">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The right to express any opinions without censorship or restraint.", "chunk_id": "e32ee493ed809ece", "doc_id": "hp_3811e4729d75dd3c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Chaplinsky v. New Hampshire, 315 U.S. 568 (1942) , is a United States Supreme Court case in which the Court articulated the fighting words doctrine, a limitation of the First Amendment's guarantee of freedom of speech.", "chunk_id": "e32ee493ed809ece", "doc_id": "hp_3811e4729d75dd3c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3811e4729d75dd3c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
