<node id="Mark Philippoussis">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Mark Philippoussis is an Australian retired tennis player.", "chunk_id": "4d09236de753d49e", "doc_id": "hp_3a454527b720381c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Mark Anthony Philippoussis ( ; born 7 November 1976) is an Australian retired tennis player of Greek and Italian descent.", "chunk_id": "4d09236de753d49e", "doc_id": "hp_3a454527b720381c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3a454527b720381c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="1999">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "1999 is a year in which Mark Philippoussis won a Davis Cup title with Australia.", "chunk_id": "4d09236de753d49e", "doc_id": "hp_3a454527b720381c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "His greatest achievements are winning two Davis Cup titles with Australia in 1999 and 2003, winning the deciding rubber in the final of each.", "chunk_id": "4d09236de753d49e", "doc_id": "hp_3a454527b720381c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3a454527b720381c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="2003">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "2003 is a year in which Mark Philippoussis won a Davis Cup title with Australia and reached the finals of a Wimbledon tournament.", "chunk_id": "4d09236de753d49e", "doc_id": "hp_3a454527b720381c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "His greatest achievements are winning two Davis Cup titles with Australia in 1999 and 2003, winning the deciding rubber in the final of each.", "chunk_id": "4d09236de753d49e", "doc_id": "hp_3a454527b720381c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3a454527b720381c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="US Open">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The US Open is a tennis tournament where Mark Philippoussis reached the finals in 1998.", "chunk_id": "4d09236de753d49e", "doc_id": "hp_3a454527b720381c"}, {"text": "The US Open is one of the four Grand Slam tennis tournaments, held in August and September.", "chunk_id": "9d09b0720a059b02", "doc_id": "hp_3b064c68e72a4e49"}, {"text": "A major tennis tournament where Pam Teeguarden played and was voted \"Most Watchable Player\".", "chunk_id": "b07f6a48318ea8c0", "doc_id": "hp_8e9d4247e8ae3a7a"}, {"text": "The US Open is one of the Grand Slam mixed doubles titles won by Jim Pugh.", "chunk_id": "7b5e0db5ada508ba", "doc_id": "hp_8ec8cd0791ca8bff"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He also reached the finals of the 1998 US Open and the 2003 Wimbledon tournaments, losing to countryman Pat Rafter and Swiss Roger Federer respectively.", "chunk_id": "4d09236de753d49e", "doc_id": "hp_3a454527b720381c"}, {"text": "The Grand Slam itinerary consists of the Australian Open in mid January, the French Open in May and June, Wimbledon in July, and the US Open in August and September.", "chunk_id": "9d09b0720a059b02", "doc_id": "hp_3b064c68e72a4e49"}, {"text": "Teeguarden was voted the \"Most Watchable Player\" based on play and appearance by a group of Madison Avenue advertising executives or \"Mad Men\" while playing at the US Open.", "chunk_id": "b07f6a48318ea8c0", "doc_id": "hp_8e9d4247e8ae3a7a"}, {"text": "A doubles specialist, he won three Grand Slam men's doubles titles (two Australian Open, one Wimbledon) and five Grand Slam mixed doubles titles (three Australian Open, one Wimbledon, one US Open).", "chunk_id": "7b5e0db5ada508ba", "doc_id": "hp_8ec8cd0791ca8bff"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3a454527b720381c", "hp_3b064c68e72a4e49", "hp_8e9d4247e8ae3a7a", "hp_8ec8cd0791ca8bff"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="1998">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "1998 is a year in which Mark Philippoussis reached the finals of the US Open.", "chunk_id": "4d09236de753d49e", "doc_id": "hp_3a454527b720381c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He also reached the finals of the 1998 US Open and the 2003 Wimbledon tournaments, losing to countryman Pat Rafter and Swiss Roger Federer respectively.", "chunk_id": "4d09236de753d49e", "doc_id": "hp_3a454527b720381c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3a454527b720381c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Wimbledon">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Wimbledon is a tennis tournament where Mark Philippoussis reached the finals in 2003.", "chunk_id": "4d09236de753d49e", "doc_id": "hp_3a454527b720381c"}, {"text": "Wimbledon is one of the four Grand Slam tennis tournaments, held in July.", "chunk_id": "9d09b0720a059b02", "doc_id": "hp_3b064c68e72a4e49"}, {"text": "A major tennis tournament where Virginia Wade achieved a triumph in 1977.", "chunk_id": "b07f6a48318ea8c0", "doc_id": "hp_8e9d4247e8ae3a7a"}, {"text": "Wimbledon is one of the Grand Slam men's doubles titles won by Jim Pugh.", "chunk_id": "7b5e0db5ada508ba", "doc_id": "hp_8ec8cd0791ca8bff"}, {"text": "A tennis tournament where Daniel C. Goldie reached the quarterfinals in 1989.", "chunk_id": "f3bc6bdeb3b7f477", "doc_id": "hp_ce1cd3eb59940b9f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He also reached the finals of the 1998 US Open and the 2003 Wimbledon tournaments, losing to countryman Pat Rafter and Swiss Roger Federer respectively.", "chunk_id": "4d09236de753d49e", "doc_id": "hp_3a454527b720381c"}, {"text": "The Grand Slam itinerary consists of the Australian Open in mid January, the French Open in May and June, Wimbledon in July, and the US Open in August and September.", "chunk_id": "9d09b0720a059b02", "doc_id": "hp_3b064c68e72a4e49"}, {"text": "Her father Jerry, a well known coach, helped Margaret Court win the coveted Grand Slam (all four Grand Slam titles in one year) in 1970 and Virginia Wade to her 1977 Wimbledon triumph.", "chunk_id": "b07f6a48318ea8c0", "doc_id": "hp_8e9d4247e8ae3a7a"}, {"text": "A doubles specialist, he won three Grand Slam men's doubles titles (two Australian Open, one Wimbledon) and five Grand Slam mixed doubles titles (three Australian Open, one Wimbledon, one US Open).", "chunk_id": "7b5e0db5ada508ba", "doc_id": "hp_8ec8cd0791ca8bff"}, {"text": "The right-hander reached the quarterfinals of Wimbledon in 1989 where he beat Kelly Evernden, Jimmy Connors, Wally Masur and Slobodan Živojinović before losing to Ivan Lendl.", "chunk_id": "f3bc6bdeb3b7f477", "doc_id": "hp_ce1cd3eb59940b9f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3a454527b720381c", "hp_3b064c68e72a4e49", "hp_8e9d4247e8ae3a7a", "hp_8ec8cd0791ca8bff", "hp_ce1cd3eb59940b9f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Pat Rafter">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Pat Rafter is a countryman of Mark Philippoussis to whom he lost in the 1998 US Open finals.", "chunk_id": "4d09236de753d49e", "doc_id": "hp_3a454527b720381c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He also reached the finals of the 1998 US Open and the 2003 Wimbledon tournaments, losing to countryman Pat Rafter and Swiss Roger Federer respectively.", "chunk_id": "4d09236de753d49e", "doc_id": "hp_3a454527b720381c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3a454527b720381c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Gene Kiniski">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A Canadian athlete who played football and was a professional wrestler.", "chunk_id": "0118cdaa518de864", "doc_id": "hp_3a771f493056a90e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Eugene Nicholas Kiniski (November 23, 1928 – April 14, 2010) was a Canadian athlete who played football for the Edmonton Eskimos and later was a successful professional wrestler recognized as a multiple-time World Heavyweight Champion.", "chunk_id": "0118cdaa518de864", "doc_id": "hp_3a771f493056a90e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3a771f493056a90e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Eugene Nicholas Kiniski">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A Canadian athlete who played football and was a professional wrestler.", "chunk_id": "0118cdaa518de864", "doc_id": "hp_3a771f493056a90e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Eugene Nicholas Kiniski (November 23, 1928 – April 14, 2010) was a Canadian athlete who played football for the Edmonton Eskimos and later was a successful professional wrestler recognized as a multiple-time World Heavyweight Champion.", "chunk_id": "0118cdaa518de864", "doc_id": "hp_3a771f493056a90e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3a771f493056a90e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
