<node id="Dublin">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Dublin is a city in Ireland where Alexander Amini is from.", "chunk_id": "fd7d14febf5321c2", "doc_id": "hp_3b72e36a921b4635"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Alexander Amini (born April 29, 1995) is an American scientist from Dublin, Ireland, currently studying at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) in America.", "chunk_id": "fd7d14febf5321c2", "doc_id": "hp_3b72e36a921b4635"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3b72e36a921b4635"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="America">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "America is a country where Alexander Amini is studying at MIT.", "chunk_id": "fd7d14febf5321c2", "doc_id": "hp_3b72e36a921b4635"}, {"text": "A country from which students of the Conservatory originated.", "chunk_id": "8866c9256d91177d", "doc_id": "hp_530d45fd86f01aa0"}, {"text": "The Americas are tropical regions where Lantana is native.", "chunk_id": "e4f91f3cba1a9e61", "doc_id": "hp_112a39087a5960d5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Alexander Amini (born April 29, 1995) is an American scientist from Dublin, Ireland, currently studying at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) in America.", "chunk_id": "fd7d14febf5321c2", "doc_id": "hp_3b72e36a921b4635"}, {"text": "In the 1890s about 25% of the students were from other countries: 46 were from England and 23 from America.", "chunk_id": "8866c9256d91177d", "doc_id": "hp_530d45fd86f01aa0"}, {"text": "They are native to tropical regions of the Americas and Africa but exist as an introduced species in numerous areas, especially in the Australian-Pacific region.", "chunk_id": "e4f91f3cba1a9e61", "doc_id": "hp_112a39087a5960d5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_112a39087a5960d5", "hp_3b72e36a921b4635", "hp_530d45fd86f01aa0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Fly">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A song by the American rock band Sugar Ray.", "chunk_id": "8bcb056d4d4cad5f", "doc_id": "hp_3b83bf76ed88c6b4"}, {"text": "Fly is a hit song included on the album Floored.", "chunk_id": "8cd652904b229d0e", "doc_id": "hp_4ed856daf788c853"}, {"text": "A song released by Sugar Ray in 1997 that brought them mainstream fame.", "chunk_id": "ca10670f4e9a955b", "doc_id": "hp_5682f3a022ba8ac2"}, {"text": "A single by Sugar Ray from their prior album, \"Floored\".", "chunk_id": "a83c783458cb120f", "doc_id": "hp_767039256bd5743c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Fly\" is a song by American rock band Sugar Ray.", "chunk_id": "8bcb056d4d4cad5f", "doc_id": "hp_3b83bf76ed88c6b4"}, {"text": "It includes the hit song \"Fly\", and another moderately successful single, \"RPM\".", "chunk_id": "8cd652904b229d0e", "doc_id": "hp_4ed856daf788c853"}, {"text": "The band, starting off more as a funk metal band, gained mainstream fame in 1997 with their release of the song \"Fly\".", "chunk_id": "ca10670f4e9a955b", "doc_id": "hp_5682f3a022ba8ac2"}, {"text": "The album shows the band moving into a more mainstream pop rock sound, away from their earlier funk metal and nu metal sound, due to the success of their single \"Fly\" off their prior album, \"Floored\".", "chunk_id": "a83c783458cb120f", "doc_id": "hp_767039256bd5743c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3b83bf76ed88c6b4", "hp_4ed856daf788c853", "hp_5682f3a022ba8ac2", "hp_767039256bd5743c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Floored">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The 1997 album by Sugar Ray on which the song \"Fly\" appears.", "chunk_id": "8bcb056d4d4cad5f", "doc_id": "hp_3b83bf76ed88c6b4"}, {"text": "Floored is the second studio album by American rock band Sugar Ray.", "chunk_id": "8cd652904b229d0e", "doc_id": "hp_4ed856daf788c853"}, {"text": "The prior album by Sugar Ray, from which the single \"Fly\" was released.", "chunk_id": "a83c783458cb120f", "doc_id": "hp_767039256bd5743c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It appears on their 1997 album \"Floored\" twice: one version with reggae artist Super Cat (Track 4) and the other without (Track 13).", "chunk_id": "8bcb056d4d4cad5f", "doc_id": "hp_3b83bf76ed88c6b4"}, {"text": "Floored is the second studio album by American rock band Sugar Ray, released on June 24, 1997.", "chunk_id": "8cd652904b229d0e", "doc_id": "hp_4ed856daf788c853"}, {"text": "The album shows the band moving into a more mainstream pop rock sound, away from their earlier funk metal and nu metal sound, due to the success of their single \"Fly\" off their prior album, \"Floored\".", "chunk_id": "a83c783458cb120f", "doc_id": "hp_767039256bd5743c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3b83bf76ed88c6b4", "hp_4ed856daf788c853", "hp_767039256bd5743c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Super Cat">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A reggae artist featured on one version of the song \"Fly\".", "chunk_id": "8bcb056d4d4cad5f", "doc_id": "hp_3b83bf76ed88c6b4"}, {"text": "Super Cat is a reggae artist featured on one version of the song \"Fly\".", "chunk_id": "8cd652904b229d0e", "doc_id": "hp_4ed856daf788c853"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It appears on their 1997 album \"Floored\" twice: one version with reggae artist Super Cat (Track 4) and the other without (Track 13).", "chunk_id": "8bcb056d4d4cad5f", "doc_id": "hp_3b83bf76ed88c6b4"}, {"text": "Two versions of \"Fly\" are found on the album, one of them featuring reggae artist Super Cat.", "chunk_id": "8cd652904b229d0e", "doc_id": "hp_4ed856daf788c853"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3b83bf76ed88c6b4", "hp_4ed856daf788c853"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Crystal Gayle">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An American country artist.", "chunk_id": "79f2e927bc5b3f09", "doc_id": "hp_3b9acbbdcc47f797"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "American country artist Crystal Gayle has released fifteen music videos and sixty-eight singles.", "chunk_id": "79f2e927bc5b3f09", "doc_id": "hp_3b9acbbdcc47f797"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3b9acbbdcc47f797"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="music videos">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Visual content accompanying music.", "chunk_id": "79f2e927bc5b3f09", "doc_id": "hp_3b9acbbdcc47f797"}, {"text": "A short film integrating a song and imagery, produced for promotional purposes.", "chunk_id": "4386b9386a9184fc", "doc_id": "hp_93fcd5b2eb13932b"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "American country artist Crystal Gayle has released fifteen music videos and sixty-eight singles.", "chunk_id": "79f2e927bc5b3f09", "doc_id": "hp_3b9acbbdcc47f797"}, {"text": "It includes three DVDs, featuring 4.5 hours of content of 42 music videos with newly restored color and remastered audio.", "chunk_id": "4386b9386a9184fc", "doc_id": "hp_93fcd5b2eb13932b"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3b9acbbdcc47f797", "hp_93fcd5b2eb13932b"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="singles">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Musical recordings released individually.", "chunk_id": "79f2e927bc5b3f09", "doc_id": "hp_3b9acbbdcc47f797"}, {"text": "Singles is a tennis format where one player competes against another.", "chunk_id": "cc00d89bd0ab005a", "doc_id": "hp_80a1699490fb30e6"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "American country artist Crystal Gayle has released fifteen music videos and sixty-eight singles.", "chunk_id": "79f2e927bc5b3f09", "doc_id": "hp_3b9acbbdcc47f797"}, {"text": "She achieved a career Grand Slam in singles, doubles, and mixed doubles.", "chunk_id": "cc00d89bd0ab005a", "doc_id": "hp_80a1699490fb30e6"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3b9acbbdcc47f797", "hp_80a1699490fb30e6"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="promotional singles">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Singles released for promotional purposes.", "chunk_id": "79f2e927bc5b3f09", "doc_id": "hp_3b9acbbdcc47f797"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The latter includes six promotional singles, three singles as a collaborative artist, and five singles as a featured artist.", "chunk_id": "79f2e927bc5b3f09", "doc_id": "hp_3b9acbbdcc47f797"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3b9acbbdcc47f797"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
