<node id="Carrier Dome">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Carrier Dome is a venue that opened in 1980.", "chunk_id": "f2b57f4a59e6b366", "doc_id": "hp_3e92bdc5489290ce"}, {"text": "The Carrier Dome is the current site of Archbold Stadium.", "chunk_id": "9a89f86e35e64ab2", "doc_id": "hp_b8ec94a3c00016f8"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was home to the Syracuse Orange men's and women's basketball teams, the indoor track team, and the women's volleyball team before the Carrier Dome opened in 1980.", "chunk_id": "f2b57f4a59e6b366", "doc_id": "hp_3e92bdc5489290ce"}, {"text": "It was built in 1908 with money donated by John Dustin Archbold, a major benefactor of the university, who also funded the building of Archbold Stadium, just to the west of the gymnasium (now the site of the Carrier Dome).", "chunk_id": "9a89f86e35e64ab2", "doc_id": "hp_b8ec94a3c00016f8"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3e92bdc5489290ce", "hp_b8ec94a3c00016f8"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Dr. George L. Manley">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Dr. George L. Manley was a University trustee and graduate of the College of Medicine, and the benefactor of Manley Field House.", "chunk_id": "f2b57f4a59e6b366", "doc_id": "hp_3e92bdc5489290ce"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is named for Dr. George L. Manley, a University trustee and graduate of the College of Medicine, who was the benefactor of the building.", "chunk_id": "f2b57f4a59e6b366", "doc_id": "hp_3e92bdc5489290ce"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3e92bdc5489290ce"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Archbold Gymnasium">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Archbold Gymnasium was an old gymnasium that Manley Field House was built to replace.", "chunk_id": "f2b57f4a59e6b366", "doc_id": "hp_3e92bdc5489290ce"}, {"text": "Archbold Gymnasium is a gymnasium located on the campus of Syracuse University in Syracuse, New York.", "chunk_id": "9a89f86e35e64ab2", "doc_id": "hp_b8ec94a3c00016f8"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was built to replace the old Archbold Gymnasium, which had served for almost 60 years prior.", "chunk_id": "f2b57f4a59e6b366", "doc_id": "hp_3e92bdc5489290ce"}, {"text": "Archbold Gymnasium is a gymnasium located on the campus of Syracuse University in Syracuse, New York.", "chunk_id": "9a89f86e35e64ab2", "doc_id": "hp_b8ec94a3c00016f8"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3e92bdc5489290ce", "hp_b8ec94a3c00016f8"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Gnetophyta">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Gnetophyta is a division of plants, grouped within the gymnosperms.", "chunk_id": "e8e7eb907eb94958", "doc_id": "hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Gnetophyta is a division of plants, grouped within the gymnosperms (which also includes conifers, cycads, and ginkgos), that consists of some 70 species across the three relict genera: \"Gnetum\" (family Gnetaceae), \"Welwitschia\" (family Welwitschiaceae), and \"Ephedra\" (family Ephedraceae).", "chunk_id": "e8e7eb907eb94958", "doc_id": "hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="gymnosperms">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Gymnosperms are a group of plants that includes conifers, cycads, ginkgos, and Gnetophyta.", "chunk_id": "e8e7eb907eb94958", "doc_id": "hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Gnetophyta is a division of plants, grouped within the gymnosperms (which also includes conifers, cycads, and ginkgos), that consists of some 70 species across the three relict genera: \"Gnetum\" (family Gnetaceae), \"Welwitschia\" (family Welwitschiaceae), and \"Ephedra\" (family Ephedraceae).", "chunk_id": "e8e7eb907eb94958", "doc_id": "hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
