  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Gnetophyta is a division of plants, grouped within the gymnosperms (which also includes conifers, cycads, and ginkgos), that consists of some 70 species across the three relict genera: \"Gnetum\" (family Gnetaceae), \"Welwitschia\" (family Welwitschiaceae), and \"Ephedra\" (family Ephedraceae).", "chunk_id": "e8e7eb907eb94958", "doc_id": "hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Fossilized pollen">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Fossilized pollen attributed to a close relative of \"Ephedra\" has been dated as far back as the Early Cretaceous.", "chunk_id": "e8e7eb907eb94958", "doc_id": "hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Fossilized pollen attributed to a close relative of \"Ephedra\" has been dated as far back as the Early Cretaceous.", "chunk_id": "e8e7eb907eb94958", "doc_id": "hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Early Cretaceous">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Early Cretaceous is a geological period mentioned in relation to the dating of fossilized pollen.", "chunk_id": "e8e7eb907eb94958", "doc_id": "hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Fossilized pollen attributed to a close relative of \"Ephedra\" has been dated as far back as the Early Cretaceous.", "chunk_id": "e8e7eb907eb94958", "doc_id": "hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Tertiary">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Tertiary is a geological period when gnetophytes were diverse and dominant.", "chunk_id": "e8e7eb907eb94958", "doc_id": "hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Though diverse and dominant in the Tertiary, only three families, each containing a single genus, are still alive today.", "chunk_id": "e8e7eb907eb94958", "doc_id": "hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="vessel elements">
  <data key="d0">TECHNOLOGY</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Vessel elements are a system of conduits that transport water within the plant, and their presence is a primary difference between gnetophytes and other gymnosperms.", "chunk_id": "e8e7eb907eb94958", "doc_id": "hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The primary difference between gnetophytes and other gymnosperms is the presence of vessel elements, a system of conduits that transport water within the plant, similar to those found in flowering plants.", "chunk_id": "e8e7eb907eb94958", "doc_id": "hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="flowering plants">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Flowering plants are mentioned as having vessel elements similar to those found in gnetophytes.", "chunk_id": "e8e7eb907eb94958", "doc_id": "hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"}, {"text": "Flowering plants are plants that produce flowers.", "chunk_id": "1f632d1e16d718cb", "doc_id": "hp_75b4474ae1461a10"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The primary difference between gnetophytes and other gymnosperms is the presence of vessel elements, a system of conduits that transport water within the plant, similar to those found in flowering plants.", "chunk_id": "e8e7eb907eb94958", "doc_id": "hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33"}, {"text": "Psychotria is a genus of flowering plants in the Rubiaceae family.", "chunk_id": "1f632d1e16d718cb", "doc_id": "hp_75b4474ae1461a10"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_3ea3f73701bd3b33", "hp_75b4474ae1461a10"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
