<node id="The Umbrellas of Cherbourg">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A musical directed by Jacques Demy in 1964.", "chunk_id": "27dd0cc4171a09f6", "doc_id": "hp_4627d420baa4b1fd"}, {"text": "A film by Jacques Demy that achieved international success.", "chunk_id": "3488ae8198c6ceab", "doc_id": "hp_654ac6630b014afb"}, {"text": "A famous film by Jacques Demy, mentioned for comparison to Une chambre en ville.", "chunk_id": "79ecca5757e35f6c", "doc_id": "hp_a7f67f1b79caebb6"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He is best known for the two musicals he directed in the mid-1960s: \"The Umbrellas of Cherbourg\" (1964) and \"The Young Girls of Rochefort\" (1967).", "chunk_id": "27dd0cc4171a09f6", "doc_id": "hp_4627d420baa4b1fd"}, {"text": "Demy made \"Model Shop\", which was his first English-language film, following the international success of his film, \"The Umbrellas of Cherbourg\".", "chunk_id": "3488ae8198c6ceab", "doc_id": "hp_654ac6630b014afb"}, {"text": "Like Demy's most famous film, \"The Umbrellas of Cherbourg\", it is an operetta-musical in which every line of dialogue is sung.", "chunk_id": "79ecca5757e35f6c", "doc_id": "hp_a7f67f1b79caebb6"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4627d420baa4b1fd", "hp_654ac6630b014afb", "hp_a7f67f1b79caebb6"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="The Young Girls of Rochefort">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A musical directed by Jacques Demy in 1967.", "chunk_id": "27dd0cc4171a09f6", "doc_id": "hp_4627d420baa4b1fd"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He is best known for the two musicals he directed in the mid-1960s: \"The Umbrellas of Cherbourg\" (1964) and \"The Young Girls of Rochefort\" (1967).", "chunk_id": "27dd0cc4171a09f6", "doc_id": "hp_4627d420baa4b1fd"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4627d420baa4b1fd"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Michel Legrand">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The composer of the lush musical scores in Jacques Demy's films.", "chunk_id": "27dd0cc4171a09f6", "doc_id": "hp_4627d420baa4b1fd"}, {"text": "The composer of the music for the film Donkey Skin.", "chunk_id": "8d587d634a322b19", "doc_id": "hp_f52c762de35c34e7"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "His films contain overlapping continuity (i.e., characters cross over from film to film), lush musical scores (typically composed by Michel Legrand) and motifs like teenaged love, labor rights, incest, and the intersection between dreams and reality.", "chunk_id": "27dd0cc4171a09f6", "doc_id": "hp_4627d420baa4b1fd"}, {"text": "It stars Catherine Deneuve and Jean Marais, with music by Michel Legrand.", "chunk_id": "8d587d634a322b19", "doc_id": "hp_f52c762de35c34e7"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4627d420baa4b1fd", "hp_f52c762de35c34e7"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
