<node id="Ballet">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Ballet is a formalized form of dance.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Ballet is a formalized form of dance with its origins in the Italian Renaissance courts of the 15th and 16th centuries.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Italian Renaissance">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Italian Renaissance was a period in European history marking the transition from the Middle Ages to modernity and covering the 15th and 16th centuries.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Ballet is a formalized form of dance with its origins in the Italian Renaissance courts of the 15th and 16th centuries.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Catherine de' Medici">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Catherine de' Medici was a prominent figure in the spread and development of ballet.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Ballet spread from Italy to France with the help of Catherine de' Medici, where ballet developed even further under her aristocratic influence.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Le Paradis d' Amour">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Le Paradis d' Amour is an early example of Catherine de' Medici's development of ballet.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "An early example of Catherine's development of ballet is through 'Le Paradis d' Amour', a piece of work presented at her daughter's wedding, Marguerite de Valois to Henry of Navarre.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Marguerite de Valois">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Marguerite de Valois is the daughter of Catherine de' Medici, and her wedding was the occasion for the presentation of 'Le Paradis d' Amour'.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "An early example of Catherine's development of ballet is through 'Le Paradis d' Amour', a piece of work presented at her daughter's wedding, Marguerite de Valois to Henry of Navarre.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Henry of Navarre">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Henry of Navarre was married to Marguerite de Valois.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "An early example of Catherine's development of ballet is through 'Le Paradis d' Amour', a piece of work presented at her daughter''s wedding, Marguerite de Valois to Henry of Navarre.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="court ballet">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Court ballet was an early form of ballet that was developed with aristocratic and royal funding and influence.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Aristocratic money was responsible for the initial stages of development in 'court ballet', as it was royal money that dictated the ideas, literature and music used in ballets that were created to primarily entertain the aristocrats of the time.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Ballet des Polonais">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Ballet des Polonais was the first formal 'court ballet' ever recognized, staged in 1573.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The first formal 'court ballet' ever recognized was staged in 1573, 'Ballet des Polonais'.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Henry of Anjou">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Henry of Anjou ascended to the throne of Poland, an event honored by 'Ballet des Polonais'.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In true form of royal entertainment, 'Ballet des Polonais' was commissioned by Catherine de' Medici to honor the Polish ambassadors who were visiting Paris upon the accession of Henry of Anjou to the throne of Poland.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Ballet Comique de la Reine">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Ballet Comique de la Reine is a court ballet commissioned by Catherine de' Medici in 1581.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In 1581, Catherine de' Medici commissioned another court ballet, \"Ballet Comique de la Reine\", however it was her compatriot, Balthasar de Beaujoyeulx, who organized the ballet.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Balthasar de Beaujoyeulx">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Balthasar de Beaujoyeulx was a compatriot of Catherine de' Medici and organized 'Ballet Comique de la Reine'.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In 1581, Catherine de' Medici commissioned another court ballet, \"Ballet Comique de la Reine\", however it was her compatriot, Balthasar de Beaujoyeulx, who organized the ballet.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Baif's Academie">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Baif's Academie was an institution whose principles were applied to 'court ballet' by Catherine de' Medici and Balthasar de Beaujoyeulx.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Catherine de' Medici and Balthasar de Beaujoyeulx were responsible for presenting the first court ballet ever to apply the principles of Baif's Academie, by integrating poetry, dance, music and set design to convey a unified dramatic storyline.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4c5083f96f89fa77"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Gracie Mansion">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Gracie Mansion is the official residence of the Mayor of the City of New York.", "chunk_id": "3d263a06d589ae09", "doc_id": "hp_4c7c0e0e98b5650e"}, {"text": "Gracie Mansion is a location in New York where Stokely Webster's paintings can be found.", "chunk_id": "1207dedf3633b579", "doc_id": "hp_e2ee24b441181783"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Archibald Gracie Mansion (commonly called Gracie Mansion) is the official residence of the Mayor of the City of New York.", "chunk_id": "3d263a06d589ae09", "doc_id": "hp_4c7c0e0e98b5650e"}, {"text": "His paintings can be found in the permanent collections of many museums, including the Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York, the National Museum of American Art, the Smithsonian Institution, the White House, Gracie Mansion in New York, the Senate Office Building, and the Museum of the City of New York.", "chunk_id": "1207dedf3633b579", "doc_id": "hp_e2ee24b441181783"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4c7c0e0e98b5650e", "hp_e2ee24b441181783"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Mayor of the City of New York">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Mayor of the City of New York is the head of the executive branch of the New York City government.", "chunk_id": "3d263a06d589ae09", "doc_id": "hp_4c7c0e0e98b5650e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Archibald Gracie Mansion (commonly called Gracie Mansion) is the official residence of the Mayor of the City of New York.", "chunk_id": "3d263a06d589ae09", "doc_id": "hp_4c7c0e0e98b5650e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4c7c0e0e98b5650e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="City of New York">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The City of New York is a major global center for finance, culture, and fashion.", "chunk_id": "3d263a06d589ae09", "doc_id": "hp_4c7c0e0e98b5650e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Archibald Gracie Mansion (commonly called Gracie Mansion) is the official residence of the Mayor of the City of New York.", "chunk_id": "3d263a06d589ae09", "doc_id": "hp_4c7c0e0e98b5650e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_4c7c0e0e98b5650e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Carl Schurz Park">
