<node id="hatchet man">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "In politics, a trusted subordinate tasked with destroying a political opponent by any means necessary.", "chunk_id": "d0b1e443837cd70f", "doc_id": "hp_5042be17d44308ee"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In the context of the Watergate scandal, the term hatchet man was used to refer to a trusted and particularly orthodox subordinate tasked by his employer with destroying a political opponent by any means necessary.", "chunk_id": "d0b1e443837cd70f", "doc_id": "hp_5042be17d44308ee"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5042be17d44308ee"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Charles Colson">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A person known as a hatchet man for President Richard Nixon.", "chunk_id": "d0b1e443837cd70f", "doc_id": "hp_5042be17d44308ee"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Charles Colson was known as a hatchet man for President Richard Nixon, as was H.R. Haldeman, who proudly described himself as \"Richard Nixon's 'son of a bitch'\".", "chunk_id": "d0b1e443837cd70f", "doc_id": "hp_5042be17d44308ee"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5042be17d44308ee"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="H.R. Haldeman">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A person who was known as a hatchet man for President Richard Nixon and described himself as 'Richard Nixon's son of a bitch'.", "chunk_id": "d0b1e443837cd70f", "doc_id": "hp_5042be17d44308ee"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Charles Colson was known as a hatchet man for President Richard Nixon, as was H.R. Haldeman, who proudly described himself as \"Richard Nixon's 'son of a bitch'\".", "chunk_id": "d0b1e443837cd70f", "doc_id": "hp_5042be17d44308ee"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5042be17d44308ee"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Ferdinando Provesi">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Ferdinando Angelo Maria Provesi was an Italian opera composer.", "chunk_id": "6f1f0a0b8ceacebf", "doc_id": "hp_504f3a1745c4e938"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Ferdinando Angelo Maria Provesi (1770 – 1833) was a native of Parma, Italy.", "chunk_id": "6f1f0a0b8ceacebf", "doc_id": "hp_504f3a1745c4e938"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_504f3a1745c4e938"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Parma">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Parma is a city in Italy where Ferdinando Provesi was a native of.", "chunk_id": "6f1f0a0b8ceacebf", "doc_id": "hp_504f3a1745c4e938"}, {"text": "Parma is a city in the Emilia-Romagna region of Italy.", "chunk_id": "90aa0e3b675f8e93", "doc_id": "hp_e9d687a7dd49fca0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Ferdinando Angelo Maria Provesi (1770 – 1833) was a native of Parma, Italy.", "chunk_id": "6f1f0a0b8ceacebf", "doc_id": "hp_504f3a1745c4e938"}, {"text": "Parma Airport (Italian: \"Aeroporto di Parma\" , IATA: PMF, ICAO: LIMP ) is located 1.3 NM northwest of Parma, a city in the Emilia-Romagna region of Italy.", "chunk_id": "90aa0e3b675f8e93", "doc_id": "hp_e9d687a7dd49fca0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_504f3a1745c4e938", "hp_e9d687a7dd49fca0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Maestro di cappella">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Maestro di cappella is a title meaning master of music.", "chunk_id": "6f1f0a0b8ceacebf", "doc_id": "hp_504f3a1745c4e938"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Provesi is best known as being an early tutor of Giuseppe Verdi when he was the \"Maestro di cappella\" (master of music) at the St. Bartolomeo cathedral in Busseto (the town very close to Le Roncole, the village where Verdi was born.)", "chunk_id": "6f1f0a0b8ceacebf", "doc_id": "hp_504f3a1745c4e938"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_504f3a1745c4e938"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="St. Bartolomeo cathedral">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "St. Bartolomeo cathedral is a cathedral in Busseto where Ferdinando Provesi served as Maestro di cappella.", "chunk_id": "6f1f0a0b8ceacebf", "doc_id": "hp_504f3a1745c4e938"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Provesi is best known as being an early tutor of Giuseppe Verdi when he was the \"Maestro di cappella\" (master of music) at the St. Bartolomeo cathedral in Busseto (the town very close to Le Roncole, the village where Verdi was born.)", "chunk_id": "6f1f0a0b8ceacebf", "doc_id": "hp_504f3a1745c4e938"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_504f3a1745c4e938"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Le Roncole">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Le Roncole is a village near Busseto where Giuseppe Verdi was born.", "chunk_id": "6f1f0a0b8ceacebf", "doc_id": "hp_504f3a1745c4e938"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Provesi is best known as being an early tutor of Giuseppe Verdi when he was the \"Maestro di cappella\" (master of music) at the St. Bartolomeo cathedral in Busseto (the town very close to Le Roncole, the village where Verdi was born.)", "chunk_id": "6f1f0a0b8ceacebf", "doc_id": "hp_504f3a1745c4e938"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_504f3a1745c4e938"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="municipal music school">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The municipal music school was an institution directed by Ferdinando Provesi.", "chunk_id": "6f1f0a0b8ceacebf", "doc_id": "hp_504f3a1745c4e938"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Provesi was also director of the municipal music school and local Philharmonic Society.", "chunk_id": "6f1f0a0b8ceacebf", "doc_id": "hp_504f3a1745c4e938"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_504f3a1745c4e938"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="local Philharmonic Society">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The local Philharmonic Society was an organization directed by Ferdinando Provesi.", "chunk_id": "6f1f0a0b8ceacebf", "doc_id": "hp_504f3a1745c4e938"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Provesi was also director of the municipal music school and local Philharmonic Society.", "chunk_id": "6f1f0a0b8ceacebf", "doc_id": "hp_504f3a1745c4e938"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_504f3a1745c4e938"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="HMS Clonmel">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A Hunt class minesweeper of the Royal Navy from World War I.", "chunk_id": "fc8924b200c0f580", "doc_id": "hp_5129e4fb643a43c0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "HMS \"Clonmel\" was a Hunt class minesweeper of the Royal Navy from World War I.", "chunk_id": "fc8924b200c0f580", "doc_id": "hp_5129e4fb643a43c0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5129e4fb643a43c0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="World War I">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A major global conflict that involved the Central Powers against the Allied Powers.", "chunk_id": "fc8924b200c0f580", "doc_id": "hp_5129e4fb643a43c0"}, {"text": "A major global conflict that involved numerous countries.", "chunk_id": "45856128b6a22257", "doc_id": "hp_7e06d5c1c2ef0dce"}, {"text": "A global war that originated in Europe and lasted from July 28, 1914, to November 11, 1918.", "chunk_id": "b344f42adf99d038", "doc_id": "hp_831bc66834df032a"}, {"text": "World War I was a global war originating in Europe that lasted from 28 July 1914 to 11 November 1918.", "chunk_id": "3e06e403a963f53b", "doc_id": "hp_ec775ce2037fd502"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "HMS \"Clonmel\" was a Hunt class minesweeper of the Royal Navy from World War I.", "chunk_id": "fc8924b200c0f580", "doc_id": "hp_5129e4fb643a43c0"}, {"text": "The Battle of Saint-Mihiel was a major World War I battle fought from 12–15 September 1918, involving the American Expeditionary Force (AEF) and 110,000 French troops under the command of General John J. Pershing of the United States against German positions.", "chunk_id": "45856128b6a22257", "doc_id": "hp_7e06d5c1c2ef0dce"}, {"text": "World War I (WWI or WW1), also known as the First World War, the Great War, or the War to End All Wars, was a global war originating in Europe that lasted from 28 July 1914 to 11 November 1918.", "chunk_id": "b344f42adf99d038", "doc_id": "hp_831bc66834df032a"}, {"text": "His most famous post was when he served as the commander of the American Expeditionary Force (AEF) on the Western Front in World War I, 1917–18.", "chunk_id": "3e06e403a963f53b", "doc_id": "hp_ec775ce2037fd502"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5129e4fb643a43c0", "hp_7e06d5c1c2ef0dce", "hp_831bc66834df032a", "hp_ec775ce2037fd502"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Stranraer">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The original intended name for HMS Clonmel.", "chunk_id": "fc8924b200c0f580", "doc_id": "hp_5129e4fb643a43c0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "She was originally to be named \"Stranraer\", but was renamed before launch to avoid possible misunderstandings of having vessels named after coastal locations.", "chunk_id": "fc8924b200c0f580", "doc_id": "hp_5129e4fb643a43c0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5129e4fb643a43c0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
