<node id="Salvia">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Salvia is a genus that the species called \"sages\" have no relationship to.", "chunk_id": "d3f92c958cb5561c", "doc_id": "hp_51931a701df55281"}, {"text": "Salvia is another name for Salvia divinorum.", "chunk_id": "b84d18605bb81aec", "doc_id": "hp_5b549ddaeafe9045"}, {"text": "Salvia is the largest genus of plants in the family Lamiaceae.", "chunk_id": "a02f6c09a33fee66", "doc_id": "hp_6e6c3433daecaed3"}, {"text": "A genus of plants that includes cultivars like 'Jean's Purple Passion'.", "chunk_id": "6c8ea648c2d5ed76", "doc_id": "hp_980453e19b052243"}, {"text": "Salvia is a genus of plants known as sages.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}, {"text": "Salvia is the largest genus of plants in the mint family, Lamiaceae.", "chunk_id": "5634c2e12f5049d1", "doc_id": "hp_ea708a0e606fa04d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The dozen-odd species are often called \"sages\", although they have no relationship to the genus \"Salvia\".", "chunk_id": "d3f92c958cb5561c", "doc_id": "hp_51931a701df55281"}, {"text": "Salvia divinorum (also known as sage of the diviners, ska maría pastora, seer's sage, yerba de la pastora and just salvia) is a psychoactive plant which can induce visions and other spiritual experiences.", "chunk_id": "b84d18605bb81aec", "doc_id": "hp_5b549ddaeafe9045"}, {"text": "Salvia is the largest genus of plants in the family Lamiaceae, with the number of species estimated to range from 700 to nearly 1,000.", "chunk_id": "a02f6c09a33fee66", "doc_id": "hp_6e6c3433daecaed3"}, {"text": "Salvia 'Jean's Purple Passion' is a \"Salvia\" cultivar discovered at Cabrillo College in Aptos, California.", "chunk_id": "6c8ea648c2d5ed76", "doc_id": "hp_980453e19b052243"}, {"text": "Salvia chamelaeagnea is a species of flowering plant in genus \"Salvia\", known as sages.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}, {"text": "Salvia is the largest genus of plants in the mint family, Lamiaceae, with nearly 1000 species of shrubs, herbaceous perennials, and annuals.", "chunk_id": "5634c2e12f5049d1", "doc_id": "hp_ea708a0e606fa04d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_51931a701df55281", "hp_5b549ddaeafe9045", "hp_6e6c3433daecaed3", "hp_980453e19b052243", "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e", "hp_ea708a0e606fa04d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Manon Lescaut (Auber)">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An opera or opéra comique in 3 acts by Daniel Auber.", "chunk_id": "62ee8e762a5f8458", "doc_id": "hp_51938f55ccd7098e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Manon Lescaut (Auber)\nManon Lescaut is an opera or opéra comique in 3 acts by Daniel Auber to a libretto by Eugène Scribe, and, like Puccini's \"Manon Lescaut\" and Massenet's \"Manon\", is based on the Abbé Prévost's novel \"Manon Lescaut\".", "chunk_id": "62ee8e762a5f8458", "doc_id": "hp_51938f55ccd7098e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_51938f55ccd7098e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Daniel Auber">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The composer of the opera Manon Lescaut.", "chunk_id": "62ee8e762a5f8458", "doc_id": "hp_51938f55ccd7098e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Manon Lescaut is an opera or opéra comique in 3 acts by Daniel Auber to a libretto by Eugène Scribe, and, like Puccini's \"Manon Lescaut\" and Massenet's \"Manon\", is based on the Abbé Prévost's novel \"Manon Lescaut\".", "chunk_id": "62ee8e762a5f8458", "doc_id": "hp_51938f55ccd7098e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_51938f55ccd7098e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
