<node id="Music for Electric Metronomes">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An avant-garde aleatoric composition written in 1960 by Japanese composer Toshi Ichiyanagi.", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Music for Electric Metronomes is an avant-garde aleatoric composition written in 1960 by Japanese composer Toshi Ichiyanagi for any number of performers between three and eight.", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Toshi Ichiyanagi">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A Japanese composer who wrote the composition 'Music for Electric Metronomes'.", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}, {"text": "Toshi Ichiyanagi is a Japanese composer of avant-garde music.", "chunk_id": "0d8ff17508c0bbc6", "doc_id": "hp_63ccc0ae800eae3c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Music for Electric Metronomes is an avant-garde aleatoric composition written in 1960 by Japanese composer Toshi Ichiyanagi for any number of performers between three and eight.", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}, {"text": "Toshi Ichiyanagi (一柳 慧 , Ichiyanagi Toshi , born 4 February 1933) is a Japanese composer of avant-garde music.", "chunk_id": "0d8ff17508c0bbc6", "doc_id": "hp_63ccc0ae800eae3c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5", "hp_63ccc0ae800eae3c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="electric metronome">
  <data key="d0">TECHNOLOGY</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An instrument used in the composition 'Music for Electric Metronomes'.", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The only true scored \"instrument\" is an electric metronome for each individual player, though the varying sounds and/or actions may involve many different instruments and objects at the discretion of the performer.", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="graphic notation">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A system of musical notation used in 'Music for Electric Metronomes' that is a series of dashes, lines, and numbers in an erratic pattern of connected paths.", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Because the graphic notation of score (which is a series of dashes, lines, and numbers in an erratic pattern of connected paths) leaves a lot of room for personal interpretation and expression, each performance is unique, and almost certainly cannot be reproduced.", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Toshi Ichiyanagi: 1960's &amp; 1990's">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An album on which 'Music for Electric Metronomes' has been recorded.", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It has been recorded on the album \"Toshi Ichiyanagi: 1960's &amp; 1990's\".", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="S.E.M. Ensemble">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An ensemble that performed 'Music for Electric Metronomes' in 1992.", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In a review of a performance by the S.E.M. Ensemble in 1992 at the Paula Cooper Gallery, the music critic of \"The New York Times\", Alex Ross, described the piece as \"merely a timid, spastic prelude to György Ligeti's monumental \"Poème symphonique\" for 100 metronomes\".", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Paula Cooper Gallery">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A gallery where the S.E.M. Ensemble performed 'Music for Electric Metronomes' in 1992.", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In a review of a performance by the S.E.M. Ensemble in 1992 at the Paula Cooper Gallery, the music critic of \"The New York Times\", Alex Ross, described the piece as \"merely a timid, spastic prelude to György Ligeti's monumental \"Poème symphonique\" for 100 metronomes\".", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Alex Ross">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A music critic for 'The New York Times' who reviewed a performance of 'Music for Electric Metronomes'.", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In a review of a performance by the S.E.M. Ensemble in 1992 at the Paula Cooper Gallery, the music critic of \"The New York Times\", Alex Ross, described the piece as \"merely a timid, spastic prelude to György Ligeti's monumental \"Poème symphonique\" for 100 metronomes\".", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="György Ligeti">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A composer whose work 'Poème symphonique' is compared to 'Music for Electric Metronomes'.", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In a review of a performance by the S.E.M. Ensemble in 1992 at the Paula Cooper Gallery, the music critic of \"The New York Times\", Alex Ross, described the piece as \"merely a timid, spastic prelude to György Ligeti's monumental \"Poème symphonique\" for 100 metronomes\".", "chunk_id": "90b05205269973c5", "doc_id": "hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_51b683ecaa90fcc5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
