<node id="Tongyeong">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A coastal city in South Gyeongsang Province, South Korea.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}, {"text": "The meaning of the name Tongyeong, referring to Admiral Yi's principal base.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Tongyeong (] ) is a coastal city in South Gyeongsang Province, South Korea.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}, {"text": "The name Tongyeong means \"command post\" and is itself associated with Admiral Yi, as it refers to his principal base that was located on nearby Hansan Island.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5597a745514f1f39"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="South Gyeongsang Province">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A province in South Korea where Tongyeong is located.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Tongyeong (] ) is a coastal city in South Gyeongsang Province, South Korea.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5597a745514f1f39"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="South Korea">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A country in East Asia where Tongyeong is located.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}, {"text": "A country in East Asia, one of the two Koreas.", "chunk_id": "ab78baf12b2f8b16", "doc_id": "hp_b840ad7146ba28d6"}, {"text": "A country that was invaded by North Korean forces during the Korean War.", "chunk_id": "3b98f4b424fb0646", "doc_id": "hp_c1f8f58c74899fbc"}, {"text": "A country in East Asia, where Seoul and the statue of Admiral Yi Sun-sin are located.", "chunk_id": "14151d0231146059", "doc_id": "hp_dd641696f4729ecc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Tongyeong (] ) is a coastal city in South Gyeongsang Province, South Korea.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}, {"text": "The term \"Cinema of Korea\" (or \"Korean cinema\") encompasses the motion picture industries of North and South Korea.", "chunk_id": "ab78baf12b2f8b16", "doc_id": "hp_b840ad7146ba28d6"}, {"text": "The Battle of Yongju (21–22 October 1950), also known as the Battle of the Apple Orchard, took place as part of the United Nations (UN) offensive towards the Yalu River, against the North Korean forces which had invaded South Korea during the Korean War.", "chunk_id": "3b98f4b424fb0646", "doc_id": "hp_c1f8f58c74899fbc"}, {"text": "The statue of Admiral Yi Sun-sin is located at the Sejongno, Gwanghwamun Plaza in Seoul, South Korea.", "chunk_id": "14151d0231146059", "doc_id": "hp_dd641696f4729ecc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5597a745514f1f39", "hp_b840ad7146ba28d6", "hp_c1f8f58c74899fbc", "hp_dd641696f4729ecc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Chungmu city">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A former administrative division that was reunited with Tongyeong county.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Chungmu city and Tongyeong county were reunited in 1995, creating Tongyeong City as it is known today.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5597a745514f1f39"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Tongyeong county">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A former administrative division that was reunited with Chungmu city.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Chungmu city and Tongyeong county were reunited in 1995, creating Tongyeong City as it is known today.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5597a745514f1f39"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Tongyeong City">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The current administrative division of Tongyeong, created by the reunion of Chungmu city and Tongyeong county.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Chungmu city and Tongyeong county were reunited in 1995, creating Tongyeong City as it is known today.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5597a745514f1f39"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Goseong Peninsula">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A peninsula that is part of Tongyeong City.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It consists of Goseong Peninsula, Hansan Island, Mireuk Island and other islets.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5597a745514f1f39"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Hansan Island">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An island that is part of Tongyeong City and was the location of Admiral Yi's principal base.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It consists of Goseong Peninsula, Hansan Island, Mireuk Island and other islets.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5597a745514f1f39"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Mireuk Island">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An island that is part of Tongyeong City.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It consists of Goseong Peninsula, Hansan Island, Mireuk Island and other islets.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5597a745514f1f39"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Chungmu">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The former name of Tongyeong, named after Admiral Yi Sun-sin.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was formerly known as Chungmu, after the posthumous name of Admiral Yi Sun-sin.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5597a745514f1f39"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Admiral Yi Sun-sin">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A historical figure after whom Tongyeong was formerly known as Chungmu and whose principal base was located on Hansan Island.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}, {"text": "A 16th-century Korean war hero and admiral.", "chunk_id": "14151d0231146059", "doc_id": "hp_dd641696f4729ecc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was formerly known as Chungmu, after the posthumous name of Admiral Yi Sun-sin.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39"}, {"text": "The statue of Admiral Yi Sun-sin is located at the Sejongno, Gwanghwamun Plaza in Seoul, South Korea.", "chunk_id": "14151d0231146059", "doc_id": "hp_dd641696f4729ecc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5597a745514f1f39", "hp_dd641696f4729ecc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Karan Kapoor">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Karan Kapoor is a former Indian film actor and model of British and Indian descent.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Karan Kapoor (born 18 January 1962) is a former Indian film actor and model of British and Indian descent.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Shashi Kapoor">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Shashi Kapoor was an Indian Bollywood International Actor.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}, {"text": "Raj Kapoor's youngest brother, who appeared as a child artist in the film Aag.", "chunk_id": "4df4b5295e67f801", "doc_id": "hp_b8f974e5ce544d7e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He is the son of Indian Bollywood International Actor Shashi Kapoor and his India settled (late) British Actress Jennifer Kendal.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}, {"text": "Raj Kapoor's youngest brother Shashi Kapoor appeared as a child artist in this film playing the younger version of his character (Kewal).", "chunk_id": "4df4b5295e67f801", "doc_id": "hp_b8f974e5ce544d7e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec", "hp_b8f974e5ce544d7e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Jennifer Kendal">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Jennifer Kendal was an India settled (late) British Actress.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He is the son of Indian Bollywood International Actor Shashi Kapoor and his India settled (late) British Actress Jennifer Kendal.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Prithviraj Kapoor">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Prithviraj Kapoor was Karan Kapoor's paternal grandfather.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}, {"text": "A member of the Kapoor family who starred in the film Kal Aaj Aur Kal.", "chunk_id": "16a91e591a40c438", "doc_id": "hp_b3f0efe2307464b8"}, {"text": "An actor and father of Ranbir Raj Kapoor.", "chunk_id": "656937d22d978bfd", "doc_id": "hp_e3306a4963e6e08c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "His paternal grandfather was Prithviraj Kapoor and his paternal uncles are Raj Kapoor and Shammi Kapoor.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}, {"text": "The film's USP is the appearance of three generations of the famous Kapoor family starring Prithviraj Kapoor, his son Raj Kapoor, Raj Kapoor's son Randhir Kapoor (in his acting debut) and Randhir's real-life wife-to-be Babita.", "chunk_id": "16a91e591a40c438", "doc_id": "hp_b3f0efe2307464b8"}, {"text": "Born at Kapoor Haveli in Peshawar to actor Prithviraj Kapoorhe was a prominent member of the Kapoor familythat produced several celebrated Bollywood superstars.", "chunk_id": "656937d22d978bfd", "doc_id": "hp_e3306a4963e6e08c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec", "hp_b3f0efe2307464b8", "hp_e3306a4963e6e08c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Shammi Kapoor">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Shammi Kapoor was Karan Kapoor's paternal uncle.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "His paternal grandfather was Prithviraj Kapoor and his paternal uncles are Raj Kapoor and Shammi Kapoor.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Kunal Kapoor">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Kunal Kapoor is Karan Kapoor's elder brother who has also acted in some films.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "His elder brother Kunal Kapoor and sister Sanjana Kapoor have also acted in some films but like him they were not very successful.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Sanjana Kapoor">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Sanjana Kapoor is Karan Kapoor's sister who has also acted in some films.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "His elder brother Kunal Kapoor and sister Sanjana Kapoor have also acted in some films but like him they were not very successful.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Geoffrey Kendal">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Geoffrey Kendal was Karan Kapoor's maternal grandfather and an actor.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "His maternal grandparents, Geoffrey Kendal and Laura Kendal, were actors who toured India and Asia with their theatre group, Shakespeareana, performing Shakespeare and Shaw.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Laura Kendal">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Laura Kendal was Karan Kapoor's maternal grandmother and an actress.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "His maternal grandparents, Geoffrey Kendal and Laura Kendal, were actors who toured India and Asia with their theatre group, Shakespeareana, performing Shakespeare and Shaw.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Shakespeareana">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Shakespeareana was a theatre group that toured India and Asia, performing Shakespeare and Shaw.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "His maternal grandparents, Geoffrey Kendal and Laura Kendal, were actors who toured India and Asia with their theatre group, Shakespeareana, performing Shakespeare and Shaw.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Shakespeare">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Shakespeare is a playwright whose works were performed by the Shakespeareana theatre group.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}, {"text": "Shakespeare is the author of the play on which Ambroise Thomas's opera 'Hamlet' is based.", "chunk_id": "3facf7eaa59386bf", "doc_id": "hp_75db37c8dc73936b"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "His maternal grandparents, Geoffrey Kendal and Laura Kendal, were actors who toured India and Asia with their theatre group, Shakespeareana, performing Shakespeare and Shaw.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}, {"text": "Charles Louis Ambroise Thomas (5 August 1811 – 12 February 1896) was a French composer, best known for his operas \"Mignon\" (1866) and \"Hamlet\" (1868, after Shakespeare) and as Director of the Conservatoire de Paris from 1871 till his death.", "chunk_id": "3facf7eaa59386bf", "doc_id": "hp_75db37c8dc73936b"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec", "hp_75db37c8dc73936b"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Shaw">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Shaw is a playwright whose works were performed by the Shakespeareana theatre group.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "His maternal grandparents, Geoffrey Kendal and Laura Kendal, were actors who toured India and Asia with their theatre group, Shakespeareana, performing Shakespeare and Shaw.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Shakespeare Wallah">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Shakespeare Wallah is a Merchant Ivory film loosely based on the Kapoor family.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The Merchant Ivory film, \"Shakespeare Wallah\", was loosely based on the family, which starred his father and his aunt, actress Felicity Kendal.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Felicity Kendal">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Felicity Kendal is an actress and Karan Kapoor's aunt.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The Merchant Ivory film, \"Shakespeare Wallah\", was loosely based on the family, which starred his father and his aunt, actress Felicity Kendal.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="photography">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Photography is a profession that Karan Kapoor later moved towards.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}, {"text": "The art and science that the society aims to promote.", "chunk_id": "33a9a750a0cbc7b4", "doc_id": "hp_a4dd7ae51691935c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Karan later moved towards photography and decided to be a part of this profession though he worked as an actor too.", "chunk_id": "9fd31a2bf7019c95", "doc_id": "hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec"}, {"text": "It was founded in London, England in 1853 as The Photographic Society of London with the objective of promoting the art and science of photography, and in 1854 received Royal patronage from Queen Victoria and Prince Albert.", "chunk_id": "33a9a750a0cbc7b4", "doc_id": "hp_a4dd7ae51691935c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_55a86a5d2ce593ec", "hp_a4dd7ae51691935c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Bob Dylan">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Bob Dylan is an artist whose song \"Sweetheart Like You\" was covered on the album.", "chunk_id": "ee3812aae430f03c", "doc_id": "hp_56786c080440345c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The album includes covers of Bob Dylan's \"Sweetheart Like You\" and The Blue Nile's \"The Downtown Lights\".", "chunk_id": "ee3812aae430f03c", "doc_id": "hp_56786c080440345c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_56786c080440345c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
