<node id="Scottish Euro '96 Football Squad">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Scottish Euro '96 Football Squad is a group that featured on the single release of \"Purple Heather\".", "chunk_id": "ee3812aae430f03c", "doc_id": "hp_56786c080440345c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Track 12, later released as a single featuring the Scottish Euro '96 Football Squad, \"Purple Heather\" is a folk song that normally goes by the name \"Wild Mountain Thyme\".", "chunk_id": "ee3812aae430f03c", "doc_id": "hp_56786c080440345c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_56786c080440345c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="The McPeakes">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The McPeakes are credited with writing the folk song \"Purple Heather\" (also known as \"Wild Mountain Thyme\").", "chunk_id": "ee3812aae430f03c", "doc_id": "hp_56786c080440345c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is often credited as traditional, but was written by The McPeakes.", "chunk_id": "ee3812aae430f03c", "doc_id": "hp_56786c080440345c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_56786c080440345c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Tom Petty">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Tom Petty is a songwriter who wrote \"Leave Virginia Alone\" for his album \"Wildflowers\".", "chunk_id": "ee3812aae430f03c", "doc_id": "hp_56786c080440345c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Leave Virginia Alone\" was written by Tom Petty and recorded for his album \"Wildflowers\", but was left off the finished album and given to Stewart instead.", "chunk_id": "ee3812aae430f03c", "doc_id": "hp_56786c080440345c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_56786c080440345c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Wildflowers">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Wildflowers is an album by Tom Petty for which \"Leave Virginia Alone\" was originally recorded.", "chunk_id": "ee3812aae430f03c", "doc_id": "hp_56786c080440345c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Leave Virginia Alone\" was written by Tom Petty and recorded for his album \"Wildflowers\", but was left off the finished album and given to Stewart instead.", "chunk_id": "ee3812aae430f03c", "doc_id": "hp_56786c080440345c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_56786c080440345c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Stewart">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Stewart is an individual who received the song \"Leave Virginia Alone\" after it was left off Tom Petty's album \"Wildflowers\".", "chunk_id": "ee3812aae430f03c", "doc_id": "hp_56786c080440345c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Leave Virginia Alone\" was written by Tom Petty and recorded for his album \"Wildflowers\", but was left off the finished album and given to Stewart instead.", "chunk_id": "ee3812aae430f03c", "doc_id": "hp_56786c080440345c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_56786c080440345c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="funk metal">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A genre of music that the band Sugar Ray started off as.", "chunk_id": "ca10670f4e9a955b", "doc_id": "hp_5682f3a022ba8ac2"}, {"text": "A genre of music that combines elements of funk and metal.", "chunk_id": "a83c783458cb120f", "doc_id": "hp_767039256bd5743c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The band, starting off more as a funk metal band, gained mainstream fame in 1997 with their release of the song \"Fly\".", "chunk_id": "ca10670f4e9a955b", "doc_id": "hp_5682f3a022ba8ac2"}, {"text": "The album shows the band moving into a more mainstream pop rock sound, away from their earlier funk metal and nu metal sound, due to the success of their single \"Fly\" off their prior album, \"Floored\".", "chunk_id": "a83c783458cb120f", "doc_id": "hp_767039256bd5743c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5682f3a022ba8ac2", "hp_767039256bd5743c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="pop rock">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A musical style that Sugar Ray adopted after the success of their song \"Fly\".", "chunk_id": "ca10670f4e9a955b", "doc_id": "hp_5682f3a022ba8ac2"}, {"text": "A genre of music that combines elements of pop and rock.", "chunk_id": "a83c783458cb120f", "doc_id": "hp_767039256bd5743c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "This song's success, coupled with its pop rock sound that was quite different from the rest of their material at the time, led the band to change to a mainstream, pop music style.", "chunk_id": "ca10670f4e9a955b", "doc_id": "hp_5682f3a022ba8ac2"}, {"text": "The album shows the band moving into a more mainstream pop rock sound, away from their earlier funk metal and nu metal sound, due to the success of their single \"Fly\" off their prior album, \"Floored\".", "chunk_id": "a83c783458cb120f", "doc_id": "hp_767039256bd5743c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5682f3a022ba8ac2", "hp_767039256bd5743c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="pop music">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A mainstream music style that Sugar Ray changed to.", "chunk_id": "ca10670f4e9a955b", "doc_id": "hp_5682f3a022ba8ac2"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "This song's success, coupled with its pop rock sound that was quite different from the rest of their material at the time, led the band to change to a mainstream, pop music style.", "chunk_id": "ca10670f4e9a955b", "doc_id": "hp_5682f3a022ba8ac2"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5682f3a022ba8ac2"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Every Morning">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A hit song by Sugar Ray.", "chunk_id": "ca10670f4e9a955b", "doc_id": "hp_5682f3a022ba8ac2"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Subsequent albums shared this style, and the band landed a number of hits with \"Every Morning\" and \"Someday\" from \"\" and \"When It's Over\" from their self-titled album.", "chunk_id": "ca10670f4e9a955b", "doc_id": "hp_5682f3a022ba8ac2"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5682f3a022ba8ac2"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="George Heneage Lawrence Dundas">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A senior officer in the Royal Navy.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Rear Admiral George Heneage Lawrence Dundas CB (8 September 1778 – 7 October 1834) was a senior officer in the Royal Navy.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="HMS &quot;Queen Charlotte&quot;">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A first-rate ship of the line in the Royal Navy.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "As a junior officer he came to prominence due to his brave conduct during a fire on the first-rate HMS \"Queen Charlotte\".", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="HMS &quot;Calpe&quot;">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A sixth-rate ship of the line in the Royal Navy.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "As a result of this he was appointed to the command of the sixth-rate HMS \"Calpe\" in which he took part in the Battle of Algeciras Bay in July 1801 during the French Revolutionary Wars.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Battle of Algeciras Bay">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A naval battle that took place in July 1801 during the French Revolutionary Wars.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "As a result of this he was appointed to the command of the sixth-rate HMS \"Calpe\" in which he took part in the Battle of Algeciras Bay in July 1801 during the French Revolutionary Wars.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="French Revolutionary Wars">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A series of conflicts that pitted the French Republic against various monarchies.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "As a result of this he was appointed to the command of the sixth-rate HMS \"Calpe\" in which he took part in the Battle of Algeciras Bay in July 1801 during the French Revolutionary Wars.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Richmond">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A parliamentary constituency in England.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "After serving for four years as Whig Member of Parliament for Richmond, he was given command of the fifth-rate HMS \"Euryalus\" and took part in the unsuccessful Walcheren Campaign in July 1809 during the Napoleonic Wars.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="HMS &quot;Euryalus&quot;">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A fifth-rate ship of the line in the Royal Navy.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "After serving for four years as Whig Member of Parliament for Richmond, he was given command of the fifth-rate HMS \"Euryalus\" and took part in the unsuccessful Walcheren Campaign in July 1809 during the Napoleonic Wars.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Walcheren Campaign">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An unsuccessful military campaign during the Napoleonic Wars.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "After serving for four years as Whig Member of Parliament for Richmond, he was given command of the fifth-rate HMS \"Euryalus\" and took part in the unsuccessful Walcheren Campaign in July 1809 during the Napoleonic Wars.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_56ae2e2bc0735743"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
