<node id="Kiehnmoor">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Kiehnmoor is a nature reserve in Germany.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The Kiehnmoor is a nature reserve in Germany.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Celle district">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Celle district is a geographical area within Germany that contains a portion of the Kiehnmoor nature reserve.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It has an area of 440 ha of which 100 ha lie in Celle district and 340 ha in Uelzen district.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Uelzen district">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Uelzen district is a geographical area within Germany that contains a portion of the Kiehnmoor nature reserve.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It has an area of 440 ha of which 100 ha lie in Celle district and 340 ha in Uelzen district.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="nature conservation authorities">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Nature conservation authorities are responsible for the management and protection of nature reserves like Kiehnmoor.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The nature conservation authorities of these districts are responsible for the reserve.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Südheide Nature Park">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Südheide Nature Park is a larger heathland area that borders the Kiehnmoor nature reserve.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Its southern perimeter borders immediately on the larger heathland area of the Südheide Nature Park.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Heidschnucken">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Heidschnucken are moorland sheep characteristic of the region where Kiehnmoor is located.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The \"Heidschnucken\", moorland sheep characteristic of the region, are reared here.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Gerdau">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Gerdau is a partially dammed stream located north of the Kiehnmoor.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "North of the Kiehnmoor and immediately adjacent to it is the valley of a partially dammed stream, the \"Gerdau\", and the Brambosteler Moor nature reserve.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Brambosteler Moor nature reserve">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Brambosteler Moor is a nature reserve located north of and adjacent to the Kiehnmoor.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "North of the Kiehnmoor and immediately adjacent to it is the valley of a partially dammed stream, the \"Gerdau\", and the Brambosteler Moor nature reserve.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Unterlüß Firing Range">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Unterlüß Firing Range is an area located to the southeast of the Kiehnmoor reserve.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "To the southeast the reserve borders on the Unterlüß Firing Range (\"Schießplatz Unterlüß\"), belonging to the firm of Rheinmetall, and the \"Große Heide\" (\"Large Heath\") near Unterlüß, that is closed to the public.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Rheinmetall">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Rheinmetall is a firm that owns the Unterlüß Firing Range.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "To the southeast the reserve borders on the Unterlüß Firing Range (\"Schießplatz Unterlüß\"), belonging to the firm of Rheinmetall, and the \"Große Heide\" (\"Large Heath\") near Unterlüß, that is closed to the public.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Große Heide">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Große Heide, also known as Large Heath, is an area near Unterlüß that is closed to the public and borders the Kiehnmoor reserve.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "To the southeast the reserve borders on the Unterlüß Firing Range (\"Schießplatz Unterlüß\"), belonging to the firm of Rheinmetall, and the \"Große Heide\" (\"Large Heath\") near Unterlüß, that is closed to the public.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Unterlüß">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Unterlüß is a place near which the Große Heide is located.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "To the southeast the reserve borders on the Unterlüß Firing Range (\"Schießplatz Unterlüß\"), belonging to the firm of Rheinmetall, and the \"Große Heide\" (\"Large Heath\") near Unterlüß, that is closed to the public.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="crane">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The crane is a type of rare bird that has settled in the Kiehnmoor area.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Rare birds have settled here including the crane and the black stork.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="black stork">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The black stork is a type of rare bird that has settled in the Kiehnmoor area.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Rare birds have settled here including the crane and the black stork.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="otter">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The otter is an animal that may be found in the Kiehnmoor area.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Even the otter may be found here.", "chunk_id": "582723cb6f560140", "doc_id": "hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_5fffbcc1125c9880"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Your Decision">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A song by Alice in Chains.", "chunk_id": "a5827a6383be59e3", "doc_id": "hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7"}, {"text": "A single from the album Black Gives Way to Blue that reached No. 1 on Billboard's Mainstream Rock Tracks.", "chunk_id": "a02521ae2928a8dd", "doc_id": "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Your Decision\" is a song by Alice in Chains, featured on their fourth studio album \"Black Gives Way to Blue\" (2009).", "chunk_id": "a5827a6383be59e3", "doc_id": "hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7"}, {"text": "\"Check My Brain\" and \"Your Decision\" reached No. 1 on Billboard's Mainstream Rock Tracks, while \"Lesson Learned\" reached No. 4.", "chunk_id": "a02521ae2928a8dd", "doc_id": "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7", "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="November 16, 2009">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The release date of the song \"Your Decision\" as a single in the UK.", "chunk_id": "a5827a6383be59e3", "doc_id": "hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was released as the third single and fourth track from the album on November 16, 2009 in the UK, and was released in the US on December 1, 2009.", "chunk_id": "a5827a6383be59e3", "doc_id": "hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="December 1, 2009">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The release date of the song \"Your Decision\" as a single in the US.", "chunk_id": "a5827a6383be59e3", "doc_id": "hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was released as the third single and fourth track from the album on November 16, 2009 in the UK, and was released in the US on December 1, 2009.", "chunk_id": "a5827a6383be59e3", "doc_id": "hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Billboard Rock Songs">
  <data key="d0">CHART</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A music chart where the single \"Your Decision\" reached number one.", "chunk_id": "a5827a6383be59e3", "doc_id": "hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7"}, {"text": "A music chart that tracks rock songs.", "chunk_id": "0ab7d428406248fd", "doc_id": "hp_62d25a1f81638a35"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The single reached number one on the \"Billboard\" Rock Songs and Mainstream Rock charts, and number four on the Alternative Songs chart.", "chunk_id": "a5827a6383be59e3", "doc_id": "hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7"}, {"text": "The single topped the \"Billboard\" Hot Mainstream Rock Tracks and \"Billboard\" Rock Songs charts in September 2009.", "chunk_id": "0ab7d428406248fd", "doc_id": "hp_62d25a1f81638a35"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7", "hp_62d25a1f81638a35"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Mainstream Rock">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A music chart where the single \"Your Decision\" reached number one.", "chunk_id": "a5827a6383be59e3", "doc_id": "hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The single reached number one on the \"Billboard\" Rock Songs and Mainstream Rock charts, and number four on the Alternative Songs chart.", "chunk_id": "a5827a6383be59e3", "doc_id": "hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Alternative Songs">
  <data key="d0">CHART</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A music chart where the single \"Your Decision\" reached number four.", "chunk_id": "a5827a6383be59e3", "doc_id": "hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7"}, {"text": "A music chart that tracks alternative songs.", "chunk_id": "0ab7d428406248fd", "doc_id": "hp_62d25a1f81638a35"}, {"text": "A music chart where \"Check My Brain\" was the band's first #1 song.", "chunk_id": "a02521ae2928a8dd", "doc_id": "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The single reached number one on the \"Billboard\" Rock Songs and Mainstream Rock charts, and number four on the Alternative Songs chart.", "chunk_id": "a5827a6383be59e3", "doc_id": "hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7"}, {"text": "It was also their first #1 on the Alternative Songs chart.", "chunk_id": "0ab7d428406248fd", "doc_id": "hp_62d25a1f81638a35"}, {"text": "\"Check My Brain\" was also the band's first #1 song on the Alternative Songs chart, and on the Hot Rock Songs chart, and it also reached No. 92 on Billboard's Hot 100, becoming the band's first single to appear on the chart.", "chunk_id": "a02521ae2928a8dd", "doc_id": "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_6033a8a5e79f67f7", "hp_62d25a1f81638a35", "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="RT Rail">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "RT Rail was a small British railway spot-hire company.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "RT Rail was a small British railway spot-hire company, a subsidiary of Ealing Community Transport (ECT), that specialised in Class 08 shunting locomotives.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Ealing Community Transport (ECT)">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Ealing Community Transport (ECT) was the parent company of RT Rail.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "RT Rail was a small British railway spot-hire company, a subsidiary of Ealing Community Transport (ECT), that specialised in Class 08 shunting locomotives.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Class 08 shunting locomotives">
  <data key="d0">TECHNOLOGY</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Class 08 shunting locomotives were specialized by RT Rail.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "RT Rail was a small British railway spot-hire company, a subsidiary of Ealing Community Transport (ECT), that specialised in Class 08 shunting locomotives.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="British American Railway Services">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "British American Railway Services acquired RT Rail and other rail assets from Ealing Community Transport (ECT) in 2008.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was sold in 2008 to British American Railway Services along with ECT's other rail assets.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="RMS Locotec Ltd">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "RMS Locotec Ltd is a subsidiary company of British American Railway Services, and RT Rail is now part of its locomotive hire division.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is now part of the locomotive hire division of their subsidiary company, RMS Locotec Ltd.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Bombardier Transportation">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Bombardier Transportation was a customer of RT Rail, utilizing their services at Ilford Works.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Customers included Bombardier Transportation at Ilford Works, Freightliner, First ScotRail at Inverness, and Silverlink.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Ilford Works">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Ilford Works is a location where Bombardier Transportation received services from RT Rail.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Customers included Bombardier Transportation at Ilford Works, Freightliner, First ScotRail at Inverness, and Silverlink.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Freightliner">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Freightliner was a customer of RT Rail.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Customers included Bombardier Transportation at Ilford Works, Freightliner, First ScotRail at Inverness, and Silverlink.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="First ScotRail">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "First ScotRail was a customer of RT Rail at Inverness.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Customers included Bombardier Transportation at Ilford Works, Freightliner, First ScotRail at Inverness, and Silverlink.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Inverness">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Inverness is a location where First ScotRail received services from RT Rail.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Customers included Bombardier Transportation at Ilford Works, Freightliner, First ScotRail at Inverness, and Silverlink.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Silverlink">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Silverlink was a customer of RT Rail.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Customers included Bombardier Transportation at Ilford Works, Freightliner, First ScotRail at Inverness, and Silverlink.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Class 73 locomotives">
  <data key="d0">TECHNOLOGY</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "RT Rail owned two Class 73 locomotives.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The company also owned two Class 73 locomotives, and a single Class 20 locomotive which was placed on loan to the Weardale Railway.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Class 20 locomotive">
  <data key="d0">TECHNOLOGY</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "RT Rail owned a single Class 20 locomotive which was loaned to the Weardale Railway.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The company also owned two Class 73 locomotives, and a single Class 20 locomotive which was placed on loan to the Weardale Railway.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Weardale Railway">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Weardale Railway received a Class 20 locomotive on loan from RT Rail.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The company also owned two Class 73 locomotives, and a single Class 20 locomotive which was placed on loan to the Weardale Railway.", "chunk_id": "0b2d1c38faa33c81", "doc_id": "hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_606b6b7ccce7aff0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Tikkun Chatzot">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A Jewish ritual prayer recited each night after midnight as an expression of mourning and lamentation over the destruction of the Temple in Jerusalem.", "chunk_id": "46b41533532c7444", "doc_id": "hp_60c26856bb2aaa62"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Tikkun Chatzot (Hebrew: תקון חצות‎ , lit. \"Midnight Rectification\"), also spelled Tikkun Chatzos, is a Jewish ritual prayer recited each night after midnight as an expression of mourning and lamentation over the destruction of the Temple in Jerusalem.", "chunk_id": "46b41533532c7444", "doc_id": "hp_60c26856bb2aaa62"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_60c26856bb2aaa62"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Jewish ritual prayer">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A prayer that is part of Jewish religious practice.", "chunk_id": "46b41533532c7444", "doc_id": "hp_60c26856bb2aaa62"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Tikkun Chatzot (Hebrew: תקון חצות‎ , lit. \"Midnight Rectification\"), also spelled Tikkun Chatzos, is a Jewish ritual prayer recited each night after midnight as an expression of mourning and lamentation over the destruction of the Temple in Jerusalem.", "chunk_id": "46b41533532c7444", "doc_id": "hp_60c26856bb2aaa62"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_60c26856bb2aaa62"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Temple in Jerusalem">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A significant religious site in Jerusalem, the destruction of which is mourned in the Tikkun Chatzot prayer.", "chunk_id": "46b41533532c7444", "doc_id": "hp_60c26856bb2aaa62"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Tikkun Chatzot (Hebrew: תקון חצות‎ , lit. \"Midnight Rectification\"), also spelled Tikkun Chatzos, is a Jewish ritual prayer recited each night after midnight as an expression of mourning and lamentation over the destruction of the Temple in Jerusalem.", "chunk_id": "46b41533532c7444", "doc_id": "hp_60c26856bb2aaa62"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_60c26856bb2aaa62"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Sephardi Jews">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A group of Jewish people originating from the Iberian Peninsula.", "chunk_id": "46b41533532c7444", "doc_id": "hp_60c26856bb2aaa62"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is not universally observed, although it is popular among Sephardi and Hasidic Jews.", "chunk_id": "46b41533532c7444", "doc_id": "hp_60c26856bb2aaa62"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_60c26856bb2aaa62"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Hasidic Jews">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A group of Jewish people belonging to the Hasidic movement.", "chunk_id": "46b41533532c7444", "doc_id": "hp_60c26856bb2aaa62"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is not universally observed, although it is popular among Sephardi and Hasidic Jews.", "chunk_id": "46b41533532c7444", "doc_id": "hp_60c26856bb2aaa62"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_60c26856bb2aaa62"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="2010 Major League Soccer season">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The 98th season of FIFA-sanctioned soccer, the 32nd with a national first-division league, in the United States and Canada, and the 15th in MLS history.", "chunk_id": "1221adbf4371c7a0", "doc_id": "hp_60e7d9ac9e049733"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The 2010 Major League Soccer season was the 98th season of FIFA-sanctioned soccer, the 32nd with a national first-division league, in the United States and Canada, and the 15th in MLS history.", "chunk_id": "1221adbf4371c7a0", "doc_id": "hp_60e7d9ac9e049733"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_60e7d9ac9e049733"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="FIFA">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The international governing body of association football, futsal and beach soccer.", "chunk_id": "1221adbf4371c7a0", "doc_id": "hp_60e7d9ac9e049733"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The 2010 Major League Soccer season was the 98th season of FIFA-sanctioned soccer, the 32nd with a national first-division league, in the United States and Canada, and the 15th in MLS history.", "chunk_id": "1221adbf4371c7a0", "doc_id": "hp_60e7d9ac9e049733"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_60e7d9ac9e049733"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Seattle Sounders FC">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A professional soccer club based in Seattle, Washington.", "chunk_id": "1221adbf4371c7a0", "doc_id": "hp_60e7d9ac9e049733"}, {"text": "A professional soccer club that Seattle Sounders FC 2 is the reserve team of and is operated and managed by.", "chunk_id": "0383bd36f57d412b", "doc_id": "hp_c9681d41f79300d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It began on March 25 at Seattle's Qwest Field with Seattle Sounders FC defeating the expansion Philadelphia Union, 2–0.", "chunk_id": "1221adbf4371c7a0", "doc_id": "hp_60e7d9ac9e049733"}, {"text": "Seattle Sounders FC 2 (nicknamed S2) is an American soccer club based in Seattle, Washington that competes in the United Soccer League, the third tier of the United States Soccer Pyramid, as the reserve team of Seattle Sounders FC.", "chunk_id": "0383bd36f57d412b", "doc_id": "hp_c9681d41f79300d2"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_60e7d9ac9e049733", "hp_c9681d41f79300d2"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Philadelphia Union">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A professional soccer club based in Chester, Pennsylvania.", "chunk_id": "1221adbf4371c7a0", "doc_id": "hp_60e7d9ac9e049733"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It began on March 25 at Seattle's Qwest Field with Seattle Sounders FC defeating the expansion Philadelphia Union, 2–0.", "chunk_id": "1221adbf4371c7a0", "doc_id": "hp_60e7d9ac9e049733"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_60e7d9ac9e049733"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="2010 MLS All-Star Game">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An annual exhibition soccer match played by a team of star players from Major League Soccer.", "chunk_id": "1221adbf4371c7a0", "doc_id": "hp_60e7d9ac9e049733"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The 2010 MLS All-Star Game was played at Reliant Stadium, hosted by the Houston Dynamo on July 28 as the MLS XI fell 5–2 to visiting Manchester United.", "chunk_id": "1221adbf4371c7a0", "doc_id": "hp_60e7d9ac9e049733"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_60e7d9ac9e049733"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
