<node id="Western Front">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The main theatre of war during World War I on the Western side of Europe.", "chunk_id": "2eb3f367156872ac", "doc_id": "hp_69a8458a8adc29ab"}, {"text": "A theater of war during World War I.", "chunk_id": "18cfadbc25fe419e", "doc_id": "hp_cf67bd08ea76563b"}, {"text": "The Western Front was the main theatre of war during World War I.", "chunk_id": "3e06e403a963f53b", "doc_id": "hp_ec775ce2037fd502"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The German Attack on Vimy Ridge, 21 May (\"Unternehmen Schleswig-Holstein\"/Operation Schleswig-Holstein) was a local attack on the Western Front during the First World War.", "chunk_id": "2eb3f367156872ac", "doc_id": "hp_69a8458a8adc29ab"}, {"text": "It also perpetuates the battle honours and traditions of a battalion that served on the Western Front during the First World War.", "chunk_id": "18cfadbc25fe419e", "doc_id": "hp_cf67bd08ea76563b"}, {"text": "His most famous post was when he served as the commander of the American Expeditionary Force (AEF) on the Western Front in World War I, 1917–18.", "chunk_id": "3e06e403a963f53b", "doc_id": "hp_ec775ce2037fd502"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_69a8458a8adc29ab", "hp_cf67bd08ea76563b", "hp_ec775ce2037fd502"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Third Battle of Artois">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A battle fought during World War I.", "chunk_id": "2eb3f367156872ac", "doc_id": "hp_69a8458a8adc29ab"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "After the Third Battle of Artois (25 September – 4 November 1915) The French Tenth Army had held positions on the western slope of Vimy Ridge and the German 6th Army (\"Generaloberst\" [Colonel General] Rupprecht, Crown Prince of Bavaria) occupied positions on the steeper eastern slope.", "chunk_id": "2eb3f367156872ac", "doc_id": "hp_69a8458a8adc29ab"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_69a8458a8adc29ab"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
