<node id="Agastachys odorata">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Agastachys odorata, commonly known as the white waratah, is the sole member of the genus Agastachys in the protea family.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Agastachys odorata, commonly known as the white waratah, is the sole member of the genus Agastachys in the protea family.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_753b5832724c81c3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="white waratah">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The white waratah is the common name for Agastachys odorata.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Agastachys odorata, commonly known as the white waratah, is the sole member of the genus Agastachys in the protea family.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_753b5832724c81c3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Agastachys">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Agastachys is a genus in the protea family, with Agastachys odorata being its sole member.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Agastachys odorata, commonly known as the white waratah, is the sole member of the genus Agastachys in the protea family.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_753b5832724c81c3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="protea family">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The protea family is a plant family to which the genus Agastachys belongs.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Agastachys odorata, commonly known as the white waratah, is the sole member of the genus Agastachys in the protea family.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_753b5832724c81c3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="evergreen shrub to small tree">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Agastachys odorata is described as an evergreen shrub to small tree.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is an evergreen shrub to small tree and is endemic to the heaths and button grass sedgelands of western Tasmania.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_753b5832724c81c3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="western Tasmania">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Western Tasmania is a region where Agastachys odorata is endemic.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is an evergreen shrub to small tree and is endemic to the heaths and button grass sedgelands of western Tasmania.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_753b5832724c81c3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="moist heath and scrub">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Agastachys odorata occurs most often in moist heath and scrub.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It occurs most often in moist heath and scrub and occasionally in the alpine regions, but generally prefers well-drained but poor soils.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_753b5832724c81c3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="alpine regions">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Agastachys odorata is occasionally found in alpine regions.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It occurs most often in moist heath and scrub and occasionally in the alpine regions, but generally prefers well-drained but poor soils.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_753b5832724c81c3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="well-drained but poor soils">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Agastachys odorata generally prefers well-drained but poor soils.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It occurs most often in moist heath and scrub and occasionally in the alpine regions, but generally prefers well-drained but poor soils.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_753b5832724c81c3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="rainforests">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Agastachys odorata can grow in some rainforests where it forms a small tree.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It can grow in some rainforests where it forms a small tree but is normally a shrub in all other situations.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_753b5832724c81c3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="small tree">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Agastachys odorata forms a small tree in some rainforests.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It can grow in some rainforests where it forms a small tree but is normally a shrub in all other situations.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_753b5832724c81c3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="the island's south coast">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The heaviest concentrations of Agastachys odorata are along the island's south coast.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The heaviest concentrations are along the island's south coast.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_753b5832724c81c3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="dark green, hairless and almost succulent leaves">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The leaves of Agastachys odorata are dark green, hairless, and almost succulent.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Its leaves are dark green, hairless and almost succulent.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_753b5832724c81c3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="erect spikes">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "White flowers of Agastachys odorata are produced in erect spikes from the ends of the branches.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Masses of white flowers are produced in erect spikes from the ends of the branches.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_753b5832724c81c3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="branches">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The white flowers of Agastachys odorata are produced from the ends of the branches.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Masses of white flowers are produced in erect spikes from the ends of the branches.", "chunk_id": "19175e33feb82407", "doc_id": "hp_753b5832724c81c3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_753b5832724c81c3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Psychotria">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Psychotria is a genus of flowering plants in the Rubiaceae family.", "chunk_id": "1f632d1e16d718cb", "doc_id": "hp_75b4474ae1461a10"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Psychotria is a genus of flowering plants in the Rubiaceae family.", "chunk_id": "1f632d1e16d718cb", "doc_id": "hp_75b4474ae1461a10"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_75b4474ae1461a10"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="species">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Species refers to a group of living organisms that can reproduce with one another.", "chunk_id": "1f632d1e16d718cb", "doc_id": "hp_75b4474ae1461a10"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It contains around 1,850 species and is therefore one of the largest genera of flowering plants.", "chunk_id": "1f632d1e16d718cb", "doc_id": "hp_75b4474ae1461a10"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_75b4474ae1461a10"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="tropical forests">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Tropical forests are forests found in tropical regions.", "chunk_id": "1f632d1e16d718cb", "doc_id": "hp_75b4474ae1461a10"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The genus has a pantropical distribution and members of the genus are small understorey trees in tropical forests.", "chunk_id": "1f632d1e16d718cb", "doc_id": "hp_75b4474ae1461a10"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_75b4474ae1461a10"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="deforestation">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Deforestation is the clearing of forests.", "chunk_id": "1f632d1e16d718cb", "doc_id": "hp_75b4474ae1461a10"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Some species are endangered or facing extinction due to deforestation, especially species of central Africa and the Pacific.", "chunk_id": "1f632d1e16d718cb", "doc_id": "hp_75b4474ae1461a10"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_75b4474ae1461a10"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="central Africa">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Central Africa is a subregion of Africa.", "chunk_id": "1f632d1e16d718cb", "doc_id": "hp_75b4474ae1461a10"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Some species are endangered or facing extinction due to deforestation, especially species of central Africa and the Pacific.", "chunk_id": "1f632d1e16d718cb", "doc_id": "hp_75b4474ae1461a10"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_75b4474ae1461a10"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="the Pacific">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Pacific refers to the Pacific Ocean or regions bordering it.", "chunk_id": "1f632d1e16d718cb", "doc_id": "hp_75b4474ae1461a10"}, {"text": "The Pacific refers to the Pacific Ocean or its surrounding regions.", "chunk_id": "328b606d106a5a36", "doc_id": "hp_ebe09fc434bfa448"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Some species are endangered or facing extinction due to deforestation, especially species of central Africa and the Pacific.", "chunk_id": "1f632d1e16d718cb", "doc_id": "hp_75b4474ae1461a10"}, {"text": "They are woody or weakly woody plants occurring in Southeast Asia, the Pacific, Madagascar, Central and South America, and the West Indies.", "chunk_id": "328b606d106a5a36", "doc_id": "hp_ebe09fc434bfa448"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_75b4474ae1461a10", "hp_ebe09fc434bfa448"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Thom Eberhardt">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Thom Eberhardt is an American film director, producer and screenwriter.", "chunk_id": "83728c058facf91d", "doc_id": "hp_75c1f2306f429a41"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Thom Eberhardt (born March 7, 1947) is an American film director, producer and screenwriter.", "chunk_id": "83728c058facf91d", "doc_id": "hp_75c1f2306f429a41"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_75c1f2306f429a41"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Captain Ron">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Captain Ron is a film directed by Thom Eberhardt.", "chunk_id": "83728c058facf91d", "doc_id": "hp_75c1f2306f429a41"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He is most noted for his work on \"Captain Ron\", \"Honey, I Blew Up the Kid\", and the cult classic \"Night of the Comet\".", "chunk_id": "83728c058facf91d", "doc_id": "hp_75c1f2306f429a41"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_75c1f2306f429a41"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Night of the Comet">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Night of the Comet is a cult classic film directed by Thom Eberhardt.", "chunk_id": "83728c058facf91d", "doc_id": "hp_75c1f2306f429a41"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He is most noted for his work on \"Captain Ron\", \"Honey, I Blew Up the Kid\", and the cult classic \"Night of the Comet\".", "chunk_id": "83728c058facf91d", "doc_id": "hp_75c1f2306f429a41"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_75c1f2306f429a41"]</data>
