<node id="Vietnam War">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A conflict during which the military situation in Laos was discussed in the Zilch memo.", "chunk_id": "51c2cb97c1a1900f", "doc_id": "hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "A memorandum known as the Zilch memo was an American government document sent by National Security Advisor Henry Kissinger to President Richard Nixon on January 3, 1972, about the military situation in Laos during the Vietnam War.", "chunk_id": "51c2cb97c1a1900f", "doc_id": "hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Southeast Asia">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A region where the United States conducted a decade-long bombing campaign.", "chunk_id": "51c2cb97c1a1900f", "doc_id": "hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"}, {"text": "A subregion of Asia.", "chunk_id": "9432ffb2818fa833", "doc_id": "hp_9c94d1d46a54f88d"}, {"text": "A geographical region where Sino-Tibetan languages are spoken.", "chunk_id": "8d2f0f99801ebf15", "doc_id": "hp_b4175e524ae4a823"}, {"text": "Southeast Asia is a subregion of Asia.", "chunk_id": "328b606d106a5a36", "doc_id": "hp_ebe09fc434bfa448"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "On the memo, in his own handwriting, Nixon described the decade-long bombing campaign by the United States in Southeast Asia as a \"failure,\" having achieved \"zilch,\" despite public comments to the contrary.", "chunk_id": "51c2cb97c1a1900f", "doc_id": "hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"}, {"text": "As a gateway to Southeast and South Asia, Changshui Airport is a hub for China Eastern Airlines, Kunming Airlines, Lucky Air, Sichuan Airlines and Ruili Airlines.", "chunk_id": "9432ffb2818fa833", "doc_id": "hp_9c94d1d46a54f88d"}, {"text": "The Sino-Tibetan languages, in a few sources also known as Tibeto-Burman or Trans-Himalayan, are a family of more than 400 languages spoken in East Asia, Southeast Asia and South Asia.", "chunk_id": "8d2f0f99801ebf15", "doc_id": "hp_b4175e524ae4a823"}, {"text": "They are woody or weakly woody plants occurring in Southeast Asia, the Pacific, Madagascar, Central and South America, and the West Indies.", "chunk_id": "328b606d106a5a36", "doc_id": "hp_ebe09fc434bfa448"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50", "hp_9c94d1d46a54f88d", "hp_b4175e524ae4a823", "hp_ebe09fc434bfa448"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Dan Rather">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "CBS News reporter who interviewed President Nixon on January 2, 1972.", "chunk_id": "51c2cb97c1a1900f", "doc_id": "hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Just the day before, January 2, Nixon told CBS News reporter Dan Rather in an interview that the bombing was \"very, very effective.\"", "chunk_id": "51c2cb97c1a1900f", "doc_id": "hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Richard Nixon Library">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A library previously holding the Zilch memo.", "chunk_id": "51c2cb97c1a1900f", "doc_id": "hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Previously missing from the Richard Nixon Library, the memo was discovered in the possession of Alexander Butterfield, who served as the Deputy Assistant to President Nixon from 1969 to 1973, by \"Washington Post\" reporter Bob Woodward, who subsequently published it in his 2015 book \"The Last of the President's Men\".", "chunk_id": "51c2cb97c1a1900f", "doc_id": "hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Alexander Butterfield">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Deputy Assistant to President Nixon from 1969 to 1973, in whose possession the Zilch memo was found.", "chunk_id": "51c2cb97c1a1900f", "doc_id": "hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Previously missing from the Richard Nixon Library, the memo was discovered in the possession of Alexander Butterfield, who served as the Deputy Assistant to President Nixon from 1969 to 1973, by \"Washington Post\" reporter Bob Woodward, who subsequently published it in his 2015 book \"The Last of the President's Men\".", "chunk_id": "51c2cb97c1a1900f", "doc_id": "hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Deputy Assistant to President Nixon">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A role held by Alexander Butterfield from 1969 to 1973.", "chunk_id": "51c2cb97c1a1900f", "doc_id": "hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Previously missing from the Richard Nixon Library, the memo was discovered in the possession of Alexander Butterfield, who served as the Deputy Assistant to President Nixon from 1969 to 1973, by \"Washington Post\" reporter Bob Woodward, who subsequently published it in his 2015 book \"The Last of the President's Men\".", "chunk_id": "51c2cb97c1a1900f", "doc_id": "hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Bob Woodward">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "\"Washington Post\" reporter who discovered the Zilch memo in Alexander Butterfield's possession and published it.", "chunk_id": "51c2cb97c1a1900f", "doc_id": "hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Previously missing from the Richard Nixon Library, the memo was discovered in the possession of Alexander Butterfield, who served as the Deputy Assistant to President Nixon from 1969 to 1973, by \"Washington Post\" reporter Bob Woodward, who subsequently published it in his 2015 book \"The Last of the President's Men\".", "chunk_id": "51c2cb97c1a1900f", "doc_id": "hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Washington Post">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A newspaper that employed Bob Woodward.", "chunk_id": "51c2cb97c1a1900f", "doc_id": "hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Previously missing from the Richard Nixon Library, the memo was discovered in the possession of Alexander Butterfield, who served as the Deputy Assistant to President Nixon from 1969 to 1973, by \"Washington Post\" reporter Bob Woodward, who subsequently published it in his 2015 book \"The Last of the President's Men\".", "chunk_id": "51c2cb97c1a1900f", "doc_id": "hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7681eb8af0f9cd50"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
