</node>
<node id="Quercus ilex">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Quercus ilex is a plant that the original paper describing Phytophthora kernoviae stated it can infect.", "chunk_id": "f0f758ffcef041f7", "doc_id": "hp_7b90b80a57936da9"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The original paper describing the species, stated it can infect \"Magnolia\" and \"Camellia\" species, \"Pieris formosa\", \"Gevuina avellana\", \"Michelia doltsopa\" and \"Quercus ilex\".", "chunk_id": "f0f758ffcef041f7", "doc_id": "hp_7b90b80a57936da9"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7b90b80a57936da9"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Pinus radiata">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Pinus radiata is a plant that was infected by P. kernoviae in New Zealand in 1950.", "chunk_id": "f0f758ffcef041f7", "doc_id": "hp_7b90b80a57936da9"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Molecular analysis has revealed that an infection on \"Pinus radiata\", recorded in New Zealand in 1950, was caused by \"P. kernoviae\".", "chunk_id": "f0f758ffcef041f7", "doc_id": "hp_7b90b80a57936da9"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7b90b80a57936da9"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="National Geographic Explorer">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An American documentary television series that originally premiered on Nickelodeon.", "chunk_id": "f810a5fb38ef5d82", "doc_id": "hp_7baec64414b3f113"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "National Geographic Explorer (or simply Explorer) is an American documentary television series that originally premiered on Nickelodeon on April 7, 1985, after having been produced as a less costly and intensive alternative to PBS's \"National Geographic Specials\" by Pittsburgh station WQED.", "chunk_id": "f810a5fb38ef5d82", "doc_id": "hp_7baec64414b3f113"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7baec64414b3f113"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
