</node>
<node id="Argemone albiflora">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Argemone albiflora is a small erect plant with a decorative white flower with a yellow latex.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Argemone albiflora, the white prickly poppy, also known as the bluestem prickly poppy or the Texas prickly poppy, is a small erect plant with a decorative white flower with a yellow latex.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="white prickly poppy">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The white prickly poppy is another name for Argemone albiflora.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Argemone albiflora, the white prickly poppy, also known as the bluestem prickly poppy or the Texas prickly poppy, is a small erect plant with a decorative white flower with a yellow latex.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="bluestem prickly poppy">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The bluestem prickly poppy is another name for Argemone albiflora.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Argemone albiflora, the white prickly poppy, also known as the bluestem prickly poppy or the Texas prickly poppy, is a small erect plant with a decorative white flower with a yellow latex.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Texas prickly poppy">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Texas prickly poppy is another name for Argemone albiflora.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Argemone albiflora, the white prickly poppy, also known as the bluestem prickly poppy or the Texas prickly poppy, is a small erect plant with a decorative white flower with a yellow latex.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="yellow latex">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Yellow latex is a substance found in Argemone albiflora.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Argemone albiflora, the white prickly poppy, also known as the bluestem prickly poppy or the Texas prickly poppy, is a small erect plant with a decorative white flower with a yellow latex.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="sharp prickles">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Sharp prickles are a characteristic feature on the stem and leaves of Argemone albiflora.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The plant is known for the sharp prickles on its stem and leaves.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="sepals">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Sepals are parts of the flower of Argemone albiflora that fall off as the flower grows bigger.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The sepals fall off as the flower of this plant grows bigger.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="flower">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The flower of Argemone albiflora grows bigger and its sepals fall off.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}, {"text": "The plant produces clusters of pure white, fragrant, pendent flowers in summer.", "chunk_id": "5a4b1080849ca551", "doc_id": "hp_10ed6dd74595a5bc"}, {"text": "Flowers are part of the inflorescence and are about 2 millimeters wide and yellow in color.", "chunk_id": "9c69666274cd8ce7", "doc_id": "hp_42ea38daa77f53b1"}, {"text": "The flowers of Pterostyrax are white and produced in dense panicles.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The sepals fall off as the flower of this plant grows bigger.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}, {"text": "Growing to 15 m tall by 12 m broad, it is a substantial, spreading, deciduous shrub with oval leaves up to 20 cm long, and clusters of pure white, fragrant, pendent flowers in summer.", "chunk_id": "5a4b1080849ca551", "doc_id": "hp_10ed6dd74595a5bc"}, {"text": "The inflorescence is a cluster of flowers surrounded by five hairy greenish bracts tipped with hooked awns.", "chunk_id": "9c69666274cd8ce7", "doc_id": "hp_42ea38daa77f53b1"}, {"text": "The flowers are white, produced in dense panicles 8 - long.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_10ed6dd74595a5bc", "hp_42ea38daa77f53b1", "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a", "hp_a0fb254153ed3917"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="arid regions of the southern Midwest">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The arid regions of the southern Midwest is where Argemone albiflora grows.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It grows in the arid regions of the southern Midwest along roadsides and disturbed pieces of land.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="roadsides">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Roadsides are a type of location where Argemone albiflora grows.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}, {"text": "Roadsides are a habitat where Salvia chamelaeagnea grows in the wild.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It grows in the arid regions of the southern Midwest along roadsides and disturbed pieces of land.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}, {"text": "In the wild, the plant grows in sandy soil in streambeds, open fields, and roadsides.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a", "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="disturbed pieces of land">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Disturbed pieces of land are a type of location where Argemone albiflora grows.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It grows in the arid regions of the southern Midwest along roadsides and disturbed pieces of land.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Native Americans">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Native Americans have long revered Argemone albiflora for its medicinal and other uses.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Native Americans have long revered this plant for its medicinal and other uses.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="medicinal uses">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Medicinal uses are one of the reasons Native Americans revered Argemone albiflora.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Native Americans have long revered this plant for its medicinal and other uses.", "chunk_id": "2e9e2f52b3abdd4f", "doc_id": "hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7c6ab15018cbd75a"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Volume 1">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The debut studio album by indie super-group BNQT.", "chunk_id": "f0e4892b3b37bba4", "doc_id": "hp_7cc233817d9e07c7"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Volume 1 is the debut studio album by indie super-group BNQT, lead by Eric Pulido (Midlake) with Ben Bridwell (Band of Horses), Alex Kapranos (Franz Ferdinand), Fran Healy (Travis) and Jason Lytle (Grandaddy), backed by the other members of Midlake.", "chunk_id": "f0e4892b3b37bba4", "doc_id": "hp_7cc233817d9e07c7"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7cc233817d9e07c7"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Saint Petersburg Conservatory">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Saint Petersburg Conservatory was an institution that Alexander Glazunov served as director of.", "chunk_id": "e64b24cbe66d981f", "doc_id": "hp_7cda087f9f474c1b"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He served as director of the Saint Petersburg Conservatory between 1905 and 1928 and was instrumental in the reorganization of the institute into the Petrograd Conservatory, then the Leningrad Conservatory, following the Bolshevik Revolution.", "chunk_id": "e64b24cbe66d981f", "doc_id": "hp_7cda087f9f474c1b"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7cda087f9f474c1b"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Petrograd Conservatory">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Petrograd Conservatory was a reorganization of the Saint Petersburg Conservatory.", "chunk_id": "e64b24cbe66d981f", "doc_id": "hp_7cda087f9f474c1b"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He served as director of the Saint Petersburg Conservatory between 1905 and 1928 and was instrumental in the reorganization of the institute into the Petrograd Conservatory, then the Leningrad Conservatory, following the Bolshevik Revolution.", "chunk_id": "e64b24cbe66d981f", "doc_id": "hp_7cda087f9f474c1b"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7cda087f9f474c1b"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Leningrad Conservatory">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Leningrad Conservatory was a reorganization of the Petrograd Conservatory.", "chunk_id": "e64b24cbe66d981f", "doc_id": "hp_7cda087f9f474c1b"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He served as director of the Saint Petersburg Conservatory between 1905 and 1928 and was instrumental in the reorganization of the institute into the Petrograd Conservatory, then the Leningrad Conservatory, following the Bolshevik Revolution.", "chunk_id": "e64b24cbe66d981f", "doc_id": "hp_7cda087f9f474c1b"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7cda087f9f474c1b"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Bolshevik Revolution">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Bolshevik Revolution was an event that led to the reorganization of the Saint Petersburg Conservatory.", "chunk_id": "e64b24cbe66d981f", "doc_id": "hp_7cda087f9f474c1b"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He served as director of the Saint Petersburg Conservatory between 1905 and 1928 and was instrumental in the reorganization of the institute into the Petrograd Conservatory, then the Leningrad Conservatory, following the Bolshevik Revolution.", "chunk_id": "e64b24cbe66d981f", "doc_id": "hp_7cda087f9f474c1b"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7cda087f9f474c1b"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Dmitri Shostakovich">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Dmitri Shostakovich was a student under Alexander Glazunov's tenure during the early Soviet years.", "chunk_id": "e64b24cbe66d981f", "doc_id": "hp_7cda087f9f474c1b"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The best-known student under his tenure during the early Soviet years was Dmitri Shostakovich.", "chunk_id": "e64b24cbe66d981f", "doc_id": "hp_7cda087f9f474c1b"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7cda087f9f474c1b"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Wanted Man (Ratt song)">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The first track on Ratt's album \"Out of the Cellar\".", "chunk_id": "1c9e0b6104c2f63d", "doc_id": "hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Wanted Man' is the first track on American heavy metal band Ratt's album \"Out of the Cellar\".", "chunk_id": "1c9e0b6104c2f63d", "doc_id": "hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Out of the Cellar">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An album by the American heavy metal band Ratt.", "chunk_id": "1c9e0b6104c2f63d", "doc_id": "hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"}, {"text": "An album by Ratt on which the song \"Back For More\" appears.", "chunk_id": "69ea2310084e6973", "doc_id": "hp_b786bea89d57e8fa"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Wanted Man' is the first track on American heavy metal band Ratt's album \"Out of the Cellar\".", "chunk_id": "1c9e0b6104c2f63d", "doc_id": "hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"}, {"text": "He co-wrote the song \"Back For More\" with Stephen Pearcy on Ratt's album \"Out of the Cellar\".", "chunk_id": "69ea2310084e6973", "doc_id": "hp_b786bea89d57e8fa"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32", "hp_b786bea89d57e8fa"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Weird Science">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A film released in 1985.", "chunk_id": "1c9e0b6104c2f63d", "doc_id": "hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was also featured on the soundtrack for the 1985 film \"Weird Science\".", "chunk_id": "1c9e0b6104c2f63d", "doc_id": "hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Robbin Crosby">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A composer of the song \"Wanted Man\".", "chunk_id": "1c9e0b6104c2f63d", "doc_id": "hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"}, {"text": "A guitarist and songwriter for the song 'Dance'.", "chunk_id": "73789dfc1fb7d82f", "doc_id": "hp_8e4dbca3117ac40e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The song was composed by Robbin Crosby, Stephen Pearcy, and Joey Cristofanilli (who was briefly filling in for full-time Ratt bassist Juan Croucier), and it was the second biggest hit on the album (note: \"Back for more\" did not qualify for a chart position since it was not an actual single release), reaching number 87 on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 and 38 on the \"Billboard\" Mainstream Rock Tracks chart.", "chunk_id": "1c9e0b6104c2f63d", "doc_id": "hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"}, {"text": "The song was written by Stephen Pearcy, guitarists Robbin Crosby and Warren DeMartini, and album producer Beau Hill.", "chunk_id": "73789dfc1fb7d82f", "doc_id": "hp_8e4dbca3117ac40e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32", "hp_8e4dbca3117ac40e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Joey Cristofanilli">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A composer of the song \"Wanted Man\" and a temporary bassist for Ratt.", "chunk_id": "1c9e0b6104c2f63d", "doc_id": "hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The song was composed by Robbin Crosby, Stephen Pearcy, and Joey Cristofanilli (who was briefly filling in for full-time Ratt bassist Juan Croucier), and it was the second biggest hit on the album (note: \"Back for more\" did not qualify for a chart position since it was not an actual single release), reaching number 87 on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 and 38 on the \"Billboard\" Mainstream Rock Tracks chart.", "chunk_id": "1c9e0b6104c2f63d", "doc_id": "hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Back for more">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A song from the album \"Out of the Cellar\" that did not qualify for a chart position.", "chunk_id": "1c9e0b6104c2f63d", "doc_id": "hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"}, {"text": "A song co-written by Matt Thorr and Stephen Pearcy.", "chunk_id": "69ea2310084e6973", "doc_id": "hp_b786bea89d57e8fa"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The song was composed by Robbin Crosby, Stephen Pearcy, and Joey Cristofanilli (who was briefly filling in for full-time Ratt bassist Juan Croucier), and it was the second biggest hit on the album (note: \"Back for more\" did not qualify for a chart position since it was not an actual single release), reaching number 87 on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 and 38 on the \"Billboard\" Mainstream Rock Tracks chart.", "chunk_id": "1c9e0b6104c2f63d", "doc_id": "hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32"}, {"text": "He co-wrote the song \"Back For More\" with Stephen Pearcy on Ratt's album \"Out of the Cellar\".", "chunk_id": "69ea2310084e6973", "doc_id": "hp_b786bea89d57e8fa"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7dbc7d21f7c51f32", "hp_b786bea89d57e8fa"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
