<node id="Semele">
  <data key="d0">PLANT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Semele is a genus of flowering plants native to the Canary Islands and Madeira.", "chunk_id": "e5eca2e6dd8b8b88", "doc_id": "hp_7e8473e41faea381"}, {"text": "Semele was the mortal mother of Dionysus by Zeus.", "chunk_id": "237c807e83e54ea2", "doc_id": "hp_cac556477f0e3a91"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Semele is a genus of flowering plants native to the Canary Islands and Madeira.", "chunk_id": "e5eca2e6dd8b8b88", "doc_id": "hp_7e8473e41faea381"}, {"text": "Semele ( ; Greek: Σεμέλη \"Semelē\"), in Greek mythology, daughter of the Boeotian hero Cadmus and Harmonia, was the mortal mother of Dionysus by Zeus in one of his many origin myths.", "chunk_id": "237c807e83e54ea2", "doc_id": "hp_cac556477f0e3a91"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7e8473e41faea381", "hp_cac556477f0e3a91"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="APG III classification system">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The APG III classification system is the third version of the Angiosperm Phylogeny Group (APG) system for the classification of flowering plants.", "chunk_id": "e5eca2e6dd8b8b88", "doc_id": "hp_7e8473e41faea381"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In the APG III classification system, it is placed in the family Asparagaceae, subfamily Nolinoideae (formerly the family Ruscaceae).", "chunk_id": "e5eca2e6dd8b8b88", "doc_id": "hp_7e8473e41faea381"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7e8473e41faea381"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Asparagaceae">
  <data key="d0">PLANT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Asparagaceae is a family of flowering plants, encompassing many familiar species.", "chunk_id": "e5eca2e6dd8b8b88", "doc_id": "hp_7e8473e41faea381"}, {"text": "Asparagaceae is a family to which Agave ghiesbreghtii belongs.", "chunk_id": "4b63b68e70b8a72b", "doc_id": "hp_b6c911ef5c542694"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In the APG III classification system, it is placed in the family Asparagaceae, subfamily Nolinoideae (formerly the family Ruscaceae).", "chunk_id": "e5eca2e6dd8b8b88", "doc_id": "hp_7e8473e41faea381"}, {"text": "Agave ghiesbreghtii is an evergreen plant belonging to the family Asparagaceae, subfamily Agavoideae.", "chunk_id": "4b63b68e70b8a72b", "doc_id": "hp_b6c911ef5c542694"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7e8473e41faea381", "hp_b6c911ef5c542694"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Nolinoideae">
  <data key="d0">PLANT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Nolinoideae is a subfamily within the Asparagaceae family, formerly considered a separate family.", "chunk_id": "e5eca2e6dd8b8b88", "doc_id": "hp_7e8473e41faea381"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In the APG III classification system, it is placed in the family Asparagaceae, subfamily Nolinoideae (formerly the family Ruscaceae).", "chunk_id": "e5eca2e6dd8b8b88", "doc_id": "hp_7e8473e41faea381"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7e8473e41faea381"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Ruscaceae">
  <data key="d0">PLANT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Ruscaceae was a family of flowering plants, now largely subsumed into Asparagaceae.", "chunk_id": "e5eca2e6dd8b8b88", "doc_id": "hp_7e8473e41faea381"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In the APG III classification system, it is placed in the family Asparagaceae, subfamily Nolinoideae (formerly the family Ruscaceae).", "chunk_id": "e5eca2e6dd8b8b88", "doc_id": "hp_7e8473e41faea381"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7e8473e41faea381"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Layne Staley">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The former singer of Alice in Chains who died in 2002.", "chunk_id": "a02521ae2928a8dd", "doc_id": "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"}, {"text": "Layne Staley was the original vocalist for the band Alice in Chains.", "chunk_id": "d4b180f1810dfb51", "doc_id": "hp_98b62ec679c7b310"}, {"text": "The original vocalist for Alice in Chains.", "chunk_id": "e152947c3cf74e57", "doc_id": "hp_c79be23e68ef1865"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is their first record without singer Layne Staley, who died in 2002.", "chunk_id": "a02521ae2928a8dd", "doc_id": "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"}, {"text": "William Bradley DuVall (born September 6, 1967) is an American musician, best known as being the current co-vocalist and a rhythm guitarist for the alternative metal band Alice in Chains replacing original vocalist Layne Staley, who died in 2002.", "chunk_id": "d4b180f1810dfb51", "doc_id": "hp_98b62ec679c7b310"}, {"text": "The song was the band's first release with vocalist William DuVall, who replaced the band's original vocalist, Layne Staley.", "chunk_id": "e152947c3cf74e57", "doc_id": "hp_c79be23e68ef1865"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8", "hp_98b62ec679c7b310", "hp_c79be23e68ef1865"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="William DuVall">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The new vocalist and rhythm guitarist for Alice in Chains.", "chunk_id": "a02521ae2928a8dd", "doc_id": "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"}, {"text": "William DuVall is an American musician, best known as being the current co-vocalist and a rhythm guitarist for the alternative metal band Alice in Chains.", "chunk_id": "d4b180f1810dfb51", "doc_id": "hp_98b62ec679c7b310"}, {"text": "Vocalist for Alice in Chains.", "chunk_id": "e152947c3cf74e57", "doc_id": "hp_c79be23e68ef1865"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It instead features new vocalist and rhythm guitarist William DuVall.", "chunk_id": "a02521ae2928a8dd", "doc_id": "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"}, {"text": "William Bradley DuVall (born September 6, 1967) is an American musician, best known as being the current co-vocalist and a rhythm guitarist for the alternative metal band Alice in Chains replacing original vocalist Layne Staley, who died in 2002.", "chunk_id": "d4b180f1810dfb51", "doc_id": "hp_98b62ec679c7b310"}, {"text": "The song was the band's first release with vocalist William DuVall, who replaced the band's original vocalist, Layne Staley.", "chunk_id": "e152947c3cf74e57", "doc_id": "hp_c79be23e68ef1865"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8", "hp_98b62ec679c7b310", "hp_c79be23e68ef1865"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Virgin Records">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A record label that released the album Black Gives Way to Blue.", "chunk_id": "a02521ae2928a8dd", "doc_id": "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is the first Alice in Chains album released on Virgin Records and their first venture away from Columbia, who handled all of their previous releases.", "chunk_id": "a02521ae2928a8dd", "doc_id": "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Lesson Learned">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A single from the album Black Gives Way to Blue that reached No. 4 on Billboard's Mainstream Rock Tracks.", "chunk_id": "a02521ae2928a8dd", "doc_id": "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"}, {"text": "A song by the American rock band Alice in Chains.", "chunk_id": "4943bcc30a38ea88", "doc_id": "hp_b5f26a3c7ae777dc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Check My Brain\" and \"Your Decision\" reached No. 1 on Billboard's Mainstream Rock Tracks, while \"Lesson Learned\" reached No. 4.", "chunk_id": "a02521ae2928a8dd", "doc_id": "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"}, {"text": "\"Lesson Learned\" is a song by the American rock band Alice in Chains, featured on their fourth studio album, \"Black Gives Way to Blue\" (2009).", "chunk_id": "4943bcc30a38ea88", "doc_id": "hp_b5f26a3c7ae777dc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8", "hp_b5f26a3c7ae777dc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Hot Rock Songs">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A music chart where \"Check My Brain\" was the band's first #1 song.", "chunk_id": "a02521ae2928a8dd", "doc_id": "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"}, {"text": "A music chart that tracks rock songs.", "chunk_id": "4943bcc30a38ea88", "doc_id": "hp_b5f26a3c7ae777dc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Check My Brain\" was also the band's first #1 song on the Alternative Songs chart, and on the Hot Rock Songs chart, and it also reached No. 92 on Billboard's Hot 100, becoming the band's first single to appear on the chart.", "chunk_id": "a02521ae2928a8dd", "doc_id": "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"}, {"text": "The song reached No. 4 on Billboard's Mainstream Rock Tracks, and No. 10 on Hot Rock Songs.", "chunk_id": "4943bcc30a38ea88", "doc_id": "hp_b5f26a3c7ae777dc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8", "hp_b5f26a3c7ae777dc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Hot 100">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A music chart where \"Check My Brain\" reached No. 92.", "chunk_id": "a02521ae2928a8dd", "doc_id": "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Check My Brain\" was also the band's first #1 song on the Alternative Songs chart, and on the Hot Rock Songs chart, and it also reached No. 92 on Billboard's Hot 100, becoming the band's first single to appear on the chart.", "chunk_id": "a02521ae2928a8dd", "doc_id": "hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_7e9f73906e63aaa8"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
