</node>
<node id="Shame Shame Shame">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A song by the American heavy metal band Ratt.", "chunk_id": "6320f732c14ef885", "doc_id": "hp_95b0346082b5ad8e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Shame Shame Shame\" is a single by American heavy metal band Ratt, released on their album \"Detonator\".", "chunk_id": "6320f732c14ef885", "doc_id": "hp_95b0346082b5ad8e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_95b0346082b5ad8e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Intro To Shame">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A slow detuned opening guitar solo featured in the song \"Shame Shame Shame\".", "chunk_id": "6320f732c14ef885", "doc_id": "hp_95b0346082b5ad8e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The song features a slow detuned opening guitar solo, titled \"Intro To Shame\", that suddenly speeds up at the 0:55 mark until the drums and the bass come in at 1:01 into the song.", "chunk_id": "6320f732c14ef885", "doc_id": "hp_95b0346082b5ad8e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_95b0346082b5ad8e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Walter Walsh">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Colonel Walter Rudolph Walsh was an FBI agent, USMC shooting instructor and Olympic shooter.", "chunk_id": "3fc5da1aa653543a", "doc_id": "hp_95e3e85178f2cc76"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Colonel Walter Rudolph Walsh (May 4, 1907 – April 29, 2014) was an FBI agent, USMC shooting instructor and Olympic shooter.", "chunk_id": "3fc5da1aa653543a", "doc_id": "hp_95e3e85178f2cc76"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_95e3e85178f2cc76"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="FBI">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The FBI is an organization that Walter Walsh joined in 1934.", "chunk_id": "3fc5da1aa653543a", "doc_id": "hp_95e3e85178f2cc76"}, {"text": "The Federal Bureau of Investigation, where Jack Ryan worked.", "chunk_id": "d4daa9d905f1b0e6", "doc_id": "hp_df0d4a55e8bc0f2f"}, {"text": "A federal law enforcement agency of the United States Department of Justice.", "chunk_id": "e73f7ce666aa44ac", "doc_id": "hp_e188311f102838e1"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Walsh joined the FBI in 1934, serving during the Public enemy era, and was involved in several high-profile FBI cases, including the capture of Arthur Barker and the killing of Al Brady.", "chunk_id": "3fc5da1aa653543a", "doc_id": "hp_95e3e85178f2cc76"}, {"text": "John C. \"Jack\" Ryan (born 19 June 1938) is a former FBI agent and police officer.", "chunk_id": "d4daa9d905f1b0e6", "doc_id": "hp_df0d4a55e8bc0f2f"}, {"text": "Joseph Dominick \"Joe\" Pistone, alias Donnie Brasco, (born September 17, 1939), is a former FBI agent who worked undercover for six years infiltrating the Bonanno crime family and to a lesser extent the Colombo crime family, two of the Five Families of the Mafia in New York City.", "chunk_id": "e73f7ce666aa44ac", "doc_id": "hp_e188311f102838e1"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_95e3e85178f2cc76", "hp_df0d4a55e8bc0f2f", "hp_e188311f102838e1"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="USMC">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The USMC is an organization where Walter Walsh served as a shooting instructor.", "chunk_id": "3fc5da1aa653543a", "doc_id": "hp_95e3e85178f2cc76"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He served in the Pacific theatre during World War II with the Marine Corps and, after a brief return to the FBI, served as a shooting instructor with the Marine Corps until his retirement in the 1970s.", "chunk_id": "3fc5da1aa653543a", "doc_id": "hp_95e3e85178f2cc76"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_95e3e85178f2cc76"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Olympic shooter">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Walter Walsh was an Olympic shooter.", "chunk_id": "3fc5da1aa653543a", "doc_id": "hp_95e3e85178f2cc76"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Colonel Walter Rudolph Walsh (May 4, 1907 – April 29, 2014) was an FBI agent, USMC shooting instructor and Olympic shooter.", "chunk_id": "3fc5da1aa653543a", "doc_id": "hp_95e3e85178f2cc76"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_95e3e85178f2cc76"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Public enemy era">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Public enemy era was a period during which Walter Walsh served in the FBI.", "chunk_id": "3fc5da1aa653543a", "doc_id": "hp_95e3e85178f2cc76"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Walsh joined the FBI in 1934, serving during the Public enemy era, and was involved in several high-profile FBI cases, including the capture of Arthur Barker and the killing of Al Brady.", "chunk_id": "3fc5da1aa653543a", "doc_id": "hp_95e3e85178f2cc76"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_95e3e85178f2cc76"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
