<node id="Pterostyrax">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Pterostyrax is a small genus of four species of deciduous large shrubs or small trees.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Pterostyrax, the epaulette tree, is a small genus of four species of deciduous large shrubs or small trees in the family Styracaceae, native to eastern Asia in China and Japan.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a0fb254153ed3917"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="leaves">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Leaves of Pterostyrax are alternate, simple ovate, and measure 6 - long and 4 - broad.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "They grow 4 - tall, with alternate, simple ovate leaves 6 - long and 4 - broad.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a0fb254153ed3917"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="fruit">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The fruit of Pterostyrax is an oblong dry drupe with longitudinal ribs or narrow wings.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The fruit is an oblong dry drupe, with longitudinal ribs or narrow wings (the wings are absent in the related genus \"Styrax\", whence the name \"Pterostyrax\", \"winged styrax\").", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a0fb254153ed3917"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Styrax">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Styrax is a genus related to Pterostyrax, distinguished by the absence of wings on its fruit.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The fruit is an oblong dry drupe, with longitudinal ribs or narrow wings (the wings are absent in the related genus \"Styrax\", whence the name \"Pterostyrax\", \"winged styrax\").", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a0fb254153ed3917"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Austrobaileyales">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An order of flowering plants consisting of about 100 species of woody plants.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Austrobaileyales is an order of flowering plants, consisting of about 100 species of woody plants growing as trees, shrubs and lianas.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Illicium verum">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A species from which the spice star anise comes.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Perhaps the most familiar species is \"Illicium verum\", from which comes the spice star anise.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="star anise">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A spice that comes from Illicium verum.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Perhaps the most familiar species is \"Illicium verum\", from which comes the spice star anise.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="basal angiosperms">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A group of flowering plants that diverged earlier from the remaining flowering plants.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The order belongs to the group of basal angiosperms, the ANA grade, which diverged earlier from the remaining flowering plants, and, as such, it is the extant group after the Amborellales and Nymphaeales, that is sister to all remaining extant angiosperms outside of the ANA grade.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="ANA grade">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A group of basal angiosperms.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The order belongs to the group of basal angiosperms, the ANA grade, which diverged earlier from the remaining flowering plants, and, as such, it is the extant group after the Amborellales and Nymphaeales, that is sister to all remaining extant angiosperms outside of the ANA grade.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Amborellales">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An extant group of flowering plants.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The order belongs to the group of basal angiosperms, the ANA grade, which diverged earlier from the remaining flowering plants, and, as such, it is the extant group after the Amborellales and Nymphaeales, that is sister to all remaining extant angiosperms outside of the ANA grade.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Nymphaeales">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An extant group of flowering plants.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The order belongs to the group of basal angiosperms, the ANA grade, which diverged earlier from the remaining flowering plants, and, as such, it is the extant group after the Amborellales and Nymphaeales, that is sister to all remaining extant angiosperms outside of the ANA grade.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Austrobaileyaceae">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A monotypic family containing the sole genus, Austrobaileya scandens.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The order includes just three families of flowering plants, the Austrobaileyaceae, a monotypic family containing the sole genus, \"Austrobaileya scandens\", a woody liana, the Schisandraceae, a family of trees, shrubs, or lianas containing essential oils, and the Trimeniaceae, essential oil-bearing trees and lianas.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Austrobaileya scandens">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A woody liana and the sole genus within the Austrobaileyaceae family.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The order includes just three families of flowering plants, the Austrobaileyaceae, a monotypic family containing the sole genus, \"Austrobaileya scandens\", a woody liana, the Schisandraceae, a family of trees, shrubs, or lianas containing essential oils, and the Trimeniaceae, essential oil-bearing trees and lianas.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Schisandraceae">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A family of trees, shrubs, or lianas containing essential oils.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The order includes just three families of flowering plants, the Austrobaileyaceae, a monotypic family containing the sole genus, \"Austrobaileya scandens\", a woody liana, the Schisandraceae, a family of trees, shrubs, or lianas containing essential oils, and the Trimeniaceae, essential oil-bearing trees and lianas.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Trimeniaceae">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A family of essential oil-bearing trees and lianas.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The order includes just three families of flowering plants, the Austrobaileyaceae, a monotypic family containing the sole genus, \"Austrobaileya scandens\", a woody liana, the Schisandraceae, a family of trees, shrubs, or lianas containing essential oils, and the Trimeniaceae, essential oil-bearing trees and lianas.", "chunk_id": "acac422bb08fd6af", "doc_id": "hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1b81ed862b4cf7f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Morchella ulmaria">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A species of fungus in the family Morchellaceae.", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Morchella ulmaria is a species of fungus in the family Morchellaceae.", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Morchellaceae">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The family to which Morchella ulmaria belongs.", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Morchella ulmaria is a species of fungus in the family Morchellaceae.", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Philippe Clowez">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The person who described Morchella ulmaria as new to science in 2012.", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was described as new to science in 2012 by Philippe Clowez.", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Michael Kuo">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A person who, along with colleagues, described Morchella cryptica in 2012.", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Later in the same year, Michael Kuo and colleagues described \"Morchella cryptica\", which is a junior synonym of \"M. ulmaria\".", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Morchella cryptica">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A species described by Michael Kuo and colleagues, which is a junior synonym of M. ulmaria.", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Later in the same year, Michael Kuo and colleagues described \"Morchella cryptica\", which is a junior synonym of \"M. ulmaria\".", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="M. ulmaria">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A junior synonym of Morchella ulmaria.", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Later in the same year, Michael Kuo and colleagues described \"Morchella cryptica\", which is a junior synonym of \"M. ulmaria\".", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Midwestern North America">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The region where the species Morchella ulmaria occurs in forests.", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The species occurs in the forests of Midwestern North America, often associated with white ash (\"Fraxinus americana\"), the American tulip tree (\"Liriodendron tulipifera\") or species of maple or elm.", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Fraxinus americana">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A species of tree, also known as white ash, often associated with Morchella ulmaria.", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The species occurs in the forests of Midwestern North America, often associated with white ash (\"Fraxinus americana\"), the American tulip tree (\"Liriodendron tulipifera\") or species of maple or elm.", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="M. castanea">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A species closely related to Morchella ulmaria.", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is closely related to \"M. castanea\" and 2 unnamed species from Asia.", "chunk_id": "90e3a51e13c6358a", "doc_id": "hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a1c843f7fa58c1d3"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
