<node id="Joss Whedon">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Joss Whedon is an American film director who has worked on a number of projects which never progressed beyond the pre-production stage under his direction.", "chunk_id": "2e07115923b71da0", "doc_id": "hp_a93a2d4c4764f16e"}, {"text": "Creator of the fictional universe for the \"Firefly\" television series and \"Serenity\" film.", "chunk_id": "cd990647fd5220d8", "doc_id": "hp_c4877bdc7a93f3f4"}, {"text": "Joseph Hill Whedon is an American screenwriter, director, producer, comic book writer, and composer.", "chunk_id": "21e926e08f92273a", "doc_id": "hp_e70ef6817d0ab0fa"}, {"text": "A writer and director of the \"Pilot\" episode of \"Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.\".", "chunk_id": "4da76e4d337b9c8c", "doc_id": "hp_e82af13d2d3c78de"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "During his long career, American film director Joss Whedon has worked on a number of projects which never progressed beyond the pre-production stage under his direction.", "chunk_id": "2e07115923b71da0", "doc_id": "hp_a93a2d4c4764f16e"}, {"text": "Several comic book stories have been released under the Serenity title, set in the fictional universe created for Joss Whedon's \"Firefly\" television series and \"Serenity\" film, and which are considered canon.", "chunk_id": "cd990647fd5220d8", "doc_id": "hp_c4877bdc7a93f3f4"}, {"text": "Joseph Hill Whedon ( ; born June 23, 1964) is an American screenwriter, director, producer, comic book writer, and composer.", "chunk_id": "21e926e08f92273a", "doc_id": "hp_e70ef6817d0ab0fa"}, {"text": "The episode was written by series creators Joss Whedon, Jed Whedon, and Maurissa Tancharoen, and was directed by Joss Whedon.", "chunk_id": "4da76e4d337b9c8c", "doc_id": "hp_e82af13d2d3c78de"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a93a2d4c4764f16e", "hp_c4877bdc7a93f3f4", "hp_e70ef6817d0ab0fa", "hp_e82af13d2d3c78de"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="unrealized projects">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Unrealized projects are projects that Joss Whedon has worked on but which never progressed beyond the pre-production stage under his direction.", "chunk_id": "2e07115923b71da0", "doc_id": "hp_a93a2d4c4764f16e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Joss Whedon's unrealized projects", "chunk_id": "2e07115923b71da0", "doc_id": "hp_a93a2d4c4764f16e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a93a2d4c4764f16e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="pre-production stage">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The pre-production stage is a phase in project development where projects do not progress beyond it under Joss Whedon's direction.", "chunk_id": "2e07115923b71da0", "doc_id": "hp_a93a2d4c4764f16e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "During his long career, American film director Joss Whedon has worked on a number of projects which never progressed beyond the pre-production stage under his direction.", "chunk_id": "2e07115923b71da0", "doc_id": "hp_a93a2d4c4764f16e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a93a2d4c4764f16e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="development hell">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Development hell is a state where some of Joss Whedon's projects fell into it.", "chunk_id": "2e07115923b71da0", "doc_id": "hp_a93a2d4c4764f16e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Some of these projects, are officially cancelled or fell in development hell.", "chunk_id": "2e07115923b71da0", "doc_id": "hp_a93a2d4c4764f16e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a93a2d4c4764f16e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Pachypodium">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Pachypodium is a genus of succulent spine-bearing trees and shrubs.", "chunk_id": "c65de02bc9af4260", "doc_id": "hp_a9669326c71f5122"}, {"text": "A genus that includes the species Pachypodium lealii.", "chunk_id": "6be220bfddc2114d", "doc_id": "hp_c0400b095de3dd7b"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Pachypodium is a genus of succulent spine-bearing trees and shrubs, native to Madagascar and Africa.", "chunk_id": "c65de02bc9af4260", "doc_id": "hp_a9669326c71f5122"}, {"text": "The Bottle tree (\"Pachypodium lealii\" Welw.) is a species of plant included in the \"genus\" \"Pachypodium\".", "chunk_id": "6be220bfddc2114d", "doc_id": "hp_c0400b095de3dd7b"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9669326c71f5122", "hp_c0400b095de3dd7b"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="pachus">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Pachus is a Greek word meaning 'thick'.", "chunk_id": "c65de02bc9af4260", "doc_id": "hp_a9669326c71f5122"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Pachypodium\" comes from a Latin form from Greek \"pachus\" (thick) and \"podion\" (foot) (or Gk podos, root form of pous, foot), hence meaning \"thick-footed\".", "chunk_id": "c65de02bc9af4260", "doc_id": "hp_a9669326c71f5122"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9669326c71f5122"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="podion">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Podion is a Greek word meaning 'foot'.", "chunk_id": "c65de02bc9af4260", "doc_id": "hp_a9669326c71f5122"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Pachypodium\" comes from a Latin form from Greek \"pachus\" (thick) and \"podion\" (foot) (or Gk podos, root form of pous, foot), hence meaning \"thick-footed\".", "chunk_id": "c65de02bc9af4260", "doc_id": "hp_a9669326c71f5122"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9669326c71f5122"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="podos">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Podos is the root form of the Greek word pous, meaning 'foot'.", "chunk_id": "c65de02bc9af4260", "doc_id": "hp_a9669326c71f5122"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Pachypodium\" comes from a Latin form from Greek \"pachus\" (thick) and \"podion\" (foot) (or Gk podos, root form of pous, foot), hence meaning \"thick-footed\".", "chunk_id": "c65de02bc9af4260", "doc_id": "hp_a9669326c71f5122"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9669326c71f5122"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="pous">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Pous is a Greek word meaning 'foot'.", "chunk_id": "c65de02bc9af4260", "doc_id": "hp_a9669326c71f5122"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Pachypodium\" comes from a Latin form from Greek \"pachus\" (thick) and \"podion\" (foot) (or Gk podos, root form of pous, foot), hence meaning \"thick-footed\".", "chunk_id": "c65de02bc9af4260", "doc_id": "hp_a9669326c71f5122"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9669326c71f5122"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="G59 – 1st Swiss Horticulture Exhibition">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The first of two Swiss horticulture exhibitions that took place in 1959.", "chunk_id": "a9b5754861a849a2", "doc_id": "hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The G59 – 1st Swiss Horticulture Exhibition was the first of two Swiss horticulture exhibitions up until now.", "chunk_id": "a9b5754861a849a2", "doc_id": "hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Swiss horticulture exhibitions">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Exhibitions focused on horticulture held in Switzerland.", "chunk_id": "a9b5754861a849a2", "doc_id": "hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The G59 – 1st Swiss Horticulture Exhibition was the first of two Swiss horticulture exhibitions up until now.", "chunk_id": "a9b5754861a849a2", "doc_id": "hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Zurich">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The city where the G59 exhibition took place.", "chunk_id": "a9b5754861a849a2", "doc_id": "hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It took place from April 25 to October 11, 1959 in Zurich and covered an area of about 37 acres on the right and left banks of lower Lake Zurich.", "chunk_id": "a9b5754861a849a2", "doc_id": "hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Lake Zurich">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A lake in Switzerland where the G59 exhibition was partially located.", "chunk_id": "a9b5754861a849a2", "doc_id": "hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It took place from April 25 to October 11, 1959 in Zurich and covered an area of about 37 acres on the right and left banks of lower Lake Zurich.", "chunk_id": "a9b5754861a849a2", "doc_id": "hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="commuter ferries">
  <data key="d0">TECHNOLOGY</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Ferries used for commuting between the two halves of the exposition.", "chunk_id": "a9b5754861a849a2", "doc_id": "hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The two separate halves of the exposition were connected by commuter ferries and a specially created cable car.", "chunk_id": "a9b5754861a849a2", "doc_id": "hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="cable car">
  <data key="d0">TECHNOLOGY</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A specially created cable car used to connect the two halves of the exposition.", "chunk_id": "a9b5754861a849a2", "doc_id": "hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The two separate halves of the exposition were connected by commuter ferries and a specially created cable car.", "chunk_id": "a9b5754861a849a2", "doc_id": "hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9d3423ff7479e28"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Vicky Brago-Mitchell">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Vicky Brago-Mitchell is an American fractal artist.", "chunk_id": "b9e66f096d2d52e7", "doc_id": "hp_a9fead16be02ae83"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Vicky Brago-Mitchell is an American fractal artist known in the 1960s as a Stanford University student who, while working as a topless dancer, ran for student body president.", "chunk_id": "b9e66f096d2d52e7", "doc_id": "hp_a9fead16be02ae83"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9fead16be02ae83"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Denis Hayes">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Denis Hayes was the eventual Earth Day national coordinator.", "chunk_id": "b9e66f096d2d52e7", "doc_id": "hp_a9fead16be02ae83"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "She won the preliminary election, but lost to eventual Earth Day national coordinator Denis Hayes in a two-person runoff election.", "chunk_id": "b9e66f096d2d52e7", "doc_id": "hp_a9fead16be02ae83"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9fead16be02ae83"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Earth Day">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Earth Day is an event for which Denis Hayes was the national coordinator.", "chunk_id": "b9e66f096d2d52e7", "doc_id": "hp_a9fead16be02ae83"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "She won the preliminary election, but lost to eventual Earth Day national coordinator Denis Hayes in a two-person runoff election.", "chunk_id": "b9e66f096d2d52e7", "doc_id": "hp_a9fead16be02ae83"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9fead16be02ae83"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Yakima, Washington">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Yakima, Washington is the birthplace of Vicky Brago-Mitchell.", "chunk_id": "b9e66f096d2d52e7", "doc_id": "hp_a9fead16be02ae83"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "She was born on September 30, 1946 in Yakima, Washington.", "chunk_id": "b9e66f096d2d52e7", "doc_id": "hp_a9fead16be02ae83"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9fead16be02ae83"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Victoria Jane Bowles">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Victoria Jane Bowles is the birth name of Vicky Brago-Mitchell.", "chunk_id": "b9e66f096d2d52e7", "doc_id": "hp_a9fead16be02ae83"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Daughter of a Methodist minister, she grew up as Victoria Jane Bowles in small towns in Washington, Oregon and Montana.", "chunk_id": "b9e66f096d2d52e7", "doc_id": "hp_a9fead16be02ae83"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9fead16be02ae83"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Vicky Drake">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Vicky Drake is the stage name used by Vicky Brago-Mitchell when working as a topless dancer.", "chunk_id": "b9e66f096d2d52e7", "doc_id": "hp_a9fead16be02ae83"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In 1968 she began working at night as a topless dancer under the stage name Vicky Drake, and ran for student body president with a campaign poster that was a photo of herself posing nude on the Stanford Mausoleum (\"Stanford Alumni Magazine\", September/October 1994).", "chunk_id": "b9e66f096d2d52e7", "doc_id": "hp_a9fead16be02ae83"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9fead16be02ae83"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Stanford Mausoleum">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Stanford Mausoleum is a location where Vicky Brago-Mitchell posed nude for a campaign poster.", "chunk_id": "b9e66f096d2d52e7", "doc_id": "hp_a9fead16be02ae83"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In 1968 she began working at night as a topless dancer under the stage name Vicky Drake, and ran for student body president with a campaign poster that was a photo of herself posing nude on the Stanford Mausoleum (\"Stanford Alumni Magazine\", September/October 1994).", "chunk_id": "b9e66f096d2d52e7", "doc_id": "hp_a9fead16be02ae83"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9fead16be02ae83"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="San Francisco Chronicle">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The San Francisco Chronicle is a newspaper that first reported the story about Vicky Brago-Mitchell.", "chunk_id": "b9e66f096d2d52e7", "doc_id": "hp_a9fead16be02ae83"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "This story was first reported by the San Francisco Chronicle, May 1, 1968, then carried by wire services Associated Press and United Press International and published in newspapers worldwide.", "chunk_id": "b9e66f096d2d52e7", "doc_id": "hp_a9fead16be02ae83"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_a9fead16be02ae83"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
