<node id="United States vice presidential selection, 1973">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The process by which a vice president was selected in the United States in 1973.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "United States vice presidential selection, 1973", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Spiro Agnew">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Republican Vice President who resigned in 1973 due to a controversy over his personal taxes.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In 1973, Republican Vice President Spiro Agnew was forced to resign following a controversy over his personal taxes.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="25th Amendment">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Constitutional amendment that outlines the process for filling a vice presidential vacancy.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Under the terms of the 25th Amendment, a vice presidential vacancy is filled when the president nominates a candidate who is confirmed by both houses of Congress.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="John Connally">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Former Texas Governor considered by Richard Nixon for the vice presidency.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Nixon considered selecting former Texas Governor John Connally, New York Governor Nelson Rockefeller, and California Governor Ronald Reagan.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Nelson Rockefeller">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "New York Governor considered by Richard Nixon for the vice presidency.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Nixon considered selecting former Texas Governor John Connally, New York Governor Nelson Rockefeller, and California Governor Ronald Reagan.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Ronald Reagan">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "California Governor considered by Richard Nixon for the vice presidency.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Nixon considered selecting former Texas Governor John Connally, New York Governor Nelson Rockefeller, and California Governor Ronald Reagan.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Gerald Ford">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "House Minority Leader from Michigan who was selected as Vice President in 1973 and later became President.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "However, Nixon settled on House Minority Leader Gerald Ford of Michigan, who was popular among the members of Congress and who was good friends with Nixon.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Michigan">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "State in the United States, the home state of Gerald Ford.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "However, Nixon settled on House Minority Leader Gerald Ford of Michigan, who was popular among the members of Congress and who was good friends with Nixon.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Vice President of the United States">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The second-highest executive office in the United States government.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Ford won the approval of both houses by huge margins, and was sworn in as the 40th Vice President of the United States on December 6, 1973.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="President of the United States">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The head of the executive branch of the United States government.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In 1974, Ford ascended to the presidency after the Watergate scandal led to the resignation of President Nixon.", "chunk_id": "54142f25de20997e", "doc_id": "hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_adfdee30bf450e7d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Lawrence Haskell">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Lawrence Haskell was an American university administrator, baseball coach, and football coach.", "chunk_id": "bf6beb2e41c2adee", "doc_id": "hp_ae365671bb34f99c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Lawrence E. \"Jap\" Haskell (c. 1899 – 1964) was an American university administrator, baseball coach, and football coach.", "chunk_id": "bf6beb2e41c2adee", "doc_id": "hp_ae365671bb34f99c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_ae365671bb34f99c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Sooners">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Sooners are a sports team associated with the University of Oklahoma, which won conference championships under Lawrence Haskell's coaching.", "chunk_id": "bf6beb2e41c2adee", "doc_id": "hp_ae365671bb34f99c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "During his tenure, the Sooners won 176 games and eight conference championships.", "chunk_id": "bf6beb2e41c2adee", "doc_id": "hp_ae365671bb34f99c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_ae365671bb34f99c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="United States Navy">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The United States Navy is the branch of the military in which Lawrence Haskell served as a Lieutenant Commander during World War II.", "chunk_id": "bf6beb2e41c2adee", "doc_id": "hp_ae365671bb34f99c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In the military, Haskell was a Lieutenant Commander in the United States Navy during World War II.", "chunk_id": "bf6beb2e41c2adee", "doc_id": "hp_ae365671bb34f99c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_ae365671bb34f99c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="The Hawk">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Hawk is a 1935 American Western film.", "chunk_id": "468a7c3fd34321f3", "doc_id": "hp_af70c5218eca2efc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The Hawk is a 1935 American Western film directed by Edward Dmytryk.", "chunk_id": "468a7c3fd34321f3", "doc_id": "hp_af70c5218eca2efc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_af70c5218eca2efc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="science fiction">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Science fiction is a genre of fiction.", "chunk_id": "a437d927bff0c11c", "doc_id": "hp_af7dab417584284c"}, {"text": "A genre of speculative fiction.", "chunk_id": "c247beb830b15400", "doc_id": "hp_bf2ea5d754ea7865"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Karen Joy Fowler (born February 7, 1950) is an American author of science fiction, fantasy, and literary fiction.", "chunk_id": "a437d927bff0c11c", "doc_id": "hp_af7dab417584284c"}, {"text": "The following is a list of winners and shortlisted works of the James Tiptree Jr. Award, an annual literary prize for works of science fiction or fantasy that expand or explore one's understanding of gender.", "chunk_id": "c247beb830b15400", "doc_id": "hp_bf2ea5d754ea7865"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_af7dab417584284c", "hp_bf2ea5d754ea7865"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="literary fiction">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Literary fiction is a type of fiction.", "chunk_id": "a437d927bff0c11c", "doc_id": "hp_af7dab417584284c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Karen Joy Fowler (born February 7, 1950) is an American author of science fiction, fantasy, and literary fiction.", "chunk_id": "a437d927bff0c11c", "doc_id": "hp_af7dab417584284c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_af7dab417584284c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="nineteenth century">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The nineteenth century is a historical period.", "chunk_id": "a437d927bff0c11c", "doc_id": "hp_af7dab417584284c"}, {"text": "The nineteenth century was a period of time when the Huffman Historic District was formed.", "chunk_id": "bbb6119acb937cda", "doc_id": "hp_c38e964da8a4abbb"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Her work often centers on the nineteenth century, the lives of women, and alienation.", "chunk_id": "a437d927bff0c11c", "doc_id": "hp_af7dab417584284c"}, {"text": "Formed at the end of the nineteenth century primarily by a wealthy businessman, it has long been home to people of many different occupations and numerous places on the social ladder.", "chunk_id": "bbb6119acb937cda", "doc_id": "hp_c38e964da8a4abbb"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_af7dab417584284c", "hp_c38e964da8a4abbb"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="lives of women">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The lives of women refers to the experiences and circumstances of women.", "chunk_id": "a437d927bff0c11c", "doc_id": "hp_af7dab417584284c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Her work often centers on the nineteenth century, the lives of women, and alienation.", "chunk_id": "a437d927bff0c11c", "doc_id": "hp_af7dab417584284c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_af7dab417584284c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="alienation">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Alienation is a state or experience of being isolated from a group or an activity to which one should belong or in which one should be involved.", "chunk_id": "a437d927bff0c11c", "doc_id": "hp_af7dab417584284c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Her work often centers on the nineteenth century, the lives of women, and alienation.", "chunk_id": "a437d927bff0c11c", "doc_id": "hp_af7dab417584284c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_af7dab417584284c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
