  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A variation of Catan Dice Game.", "chunk_id": "d146a6f0cb5047a2", "doc_id": "hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "A variation, known as \"Catan Dice Game Plus\", is freely available from the \"Catan\" website, whose gameplay is closer to its \"Settlers\" origins.", "chunk_id": "d146a6f0cb5047a2", "doc_id": "hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Catan website">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The website from which Catan Dice Game Plus is available.", "chunk_id": "d146a6f0cb5047a2", "doc_id": "hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "A variation, known as \"Catan Dice Game Plus\", is freely available from the \"Catan\" website, whose gameplay is closer to its \"Settlers\" origins.", "chunk_id": "d146a6f0cb5047a2", "doc_id": "hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_ba7adfcb35f11075"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="outrage factor">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "In public policy, outrage factor is public opposition to a policy that is not based on the knowledge of the technical details.", "chunk_id": "0c93ed0262a66f6f", "doc_id": "hp_baa5f6802ceb9caa"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In public policy, outrage factor is public opposition to a policy that is not based on the knowledge of the technical details.", "chunk_id": "0c93ed0262a66f6f", "doc_id": "hp_baa5f6802ceb9caa"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_baa5f6802ceb9caa"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Peter Sandman">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Peter Sandman is associated with the origin of the term \"outrage factor\".", "chunk_id": "0c93ed0262a66f6f", "doc_id": "hp_baa5f6802ceb9caa"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The term \"outrage factor\" originates from Peter Sandman's 1993 book, \"Responding to Community Outrage: Strategies for Effective Risk Communication\".", "chunk_id": "0c93ed0262a66f6f", "doc_id": "hp_baa5f6802ceb9caa"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_baa5f6802ceb9caa"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Responding to Community Outrage: Strategies for Effective Risk Communication">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "This is a book published in 1993 by Peter Sandman, from which the term \"outrage factor\" originates.", "chunk_id": "0c93ed0262a66f6f", "doc_id": "hp_baa5f6802ceb9caa"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The term \"outrage factor\" originates from Peter Sandman's 1993 book, \"Responding to Community Outrage: Strategies for Effective Risk Communication\".", "chunk_id": "0c93ed0262a66f6f", "doc_id": "hp_baa5f6802ceb9caa"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_baa5f6802ceb9caa"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Salvia chamelaeagnea">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Salvia chamelaeagnea is a species of flowering plant in genus \"Salvia\", known as sages.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Salvia chamelaeagnea is a species of flowering plant in genus \"Salvia\", known as sages.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Cape of Good Hope">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Cape of Good Hope is a location in South Africa where Salvia chamelaeagnea grows.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is endemic to South Africa, where it grows on the western coastline of the Cape of Good Hope.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="shrubby perennial herb">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A shrubby perennial herb is a description of the growth habit of Salvia chamelaeagnea.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is a shrubby perennial herb up to 6 ft tall and 4 ft wide.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="light violet-blue flowers">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Light violet-blue flowers are the blooms of the Salvia chamelaeagnea plant.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It bears 3/4 in light violet-blue flowers with pale lower lips and white throats.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="pale lower lips">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Pale lower lips are a feature of the flowers of Salvia chamelaeagnea.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It bears 3/4 in light violet-blue flowers with pale lower lips and white throats.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="white throats">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "White throats are a feature of the flowers of Salvia chamelaeagnea.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It bears 3/4 in light violet-blue flowers with pale lower lips and white throats.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="small, green leaves">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Small, green leaves are a part of the Salvia chamelaeagnea plant.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The small, green leaves release a slight medicinal odor when brushed.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="medicinal odor">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A medicinal odor is released by the leaves of Salvia chamelaeagnea when brushed.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The small, green leaves release a slight medicinal odor when brushed.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="sandy soil">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Sandy soil is the type of soil in which Salvia chamelaeagnea grows in the wild.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In the wild, the plant grows in sandy soil in streambeds, open fields, and roadsides.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="streambeds">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Streambeds are a habitat where Salvia chamelaeagnea grows in the wild.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In the wild, the plant grows in sandy soil in streambeds, open fields, and roadsides.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="open fields">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Open fields are a habitat where Salvia chamelaeagnea grows in the wild.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In the wild, the plant grows in sandy soil in streambeds, open fields, and roadsides.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="gardens">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Gardens are a place where Salvia chamelaeagnea is cultivated.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is cultivated for gardens.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Phil Hill">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A performer, public speaker, \"cult legend\" and \"Don Quixote of the E.T. set\" known for speaking on extraterrestrials and the paranormal.", "chunk_id": "a57b9509e1d93532", "doc_id": "hp_bb2da19e6d96b8c5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Phil Hill (born June 10, 1971) better known as UFO Phil, is a performer, public speaker, \"cult legend\" and \"Don Quixote of the E.T. set\" who has made a name for himself through appearances on national radio programs, television, films, and internet videos speaking on the subject of extraterrestrials and the paranormal.", "chunk_id": "a57b9509e1d93532", "doc_id": "hp_bb2da19e6d96b8c5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bb2da19e6d96b8c5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="UFO Phil">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The stage name of Phil Hill, a performer and public speaker known for his appearances discussing extraterrestrials and the paranormal.", "chunk_id": "a57b9509e1d93532", "doc_id": "hp_bb2da19e6d96b8c5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Phil Hill (born June 10, 1971) better known as UFO Phil, is a performer, public speaker, \"cult legend\" and \"Don Quixote of the E.T. set\" who has made a name for himself through appearances on national radio programs, television, films, and internet videos speaking on the subject of extraterrestrials and the paranormal.", "chunk_id": "a57b9509e1d93532", "doc_id": "hp_bb2da19e6d96b8c5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bb2da19e6d96b8c5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="extraterrestrials">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Beings from outside Earth, a subject on which Phil Hill frequently speaks.", "chunk_id": "a57b9509e1d93532", "doc_id": "hp_bb2da19e6d96b8c5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Phil Hill (born June 10, 1971) better known as UFO Phil, is a performer, public speaker, \"cult legend\" and \"Don Quixote of the E.T. set\" who has made a name for himself through appearances on national radio programs, television, films, and internet videos speaking on the subject of extraterrestrials and the paranormal.", "chunk_id": "a57b9509e1d93532", "doc_id": "hp_bb2da19e6d96b8c5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bb2da19e6d96b8c5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="the paranormal">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Phenomena beyond the scope of normal scientific understanding, a subject on which Phil Hill frequently speaks.", "chunk_id": "a57b9509e1d93532", "doc_id": "hp_bb2da19e6d96b8c5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Phil Hill (born June 10, 1971) better known as UFO Phil, is a performer, public speaker, \"cult legend\" and \"Don Quixote of the E.T. set\" who has made a name for himself through appearances on national radio programs, television, films, and internet videos speaking on the subject of extraterrestrials and the paranormal.", "chunk_id": "a57b9509e1d93532", "doc_id": "hp_bb2da19e6d96b8c5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bb2da19e6d96b8c5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Poe's law">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A principle suggesting that without a clear indicator of the author's intent, it is impossible to create a parody of extremism or fundamentalism that someone won't mistake for the real thing.", "chunk_id": "a57b9509e1d93532", "doc_id": "hp_bb2da19e6d96b8c5"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In this regard, UFO Phil may be an example of Poe's law and has been compared to Andy Kaufman's persona Tony Clifton.", "chunk_id": "a57b9509e1d93532", "doc_id": "hp_bb2da19e6d96b8c5"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bb2da19e6d96b8c5"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="film art">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The artistic expression within North Korean cinema, which official sources claim has created an unprecedented sensation.", "chunk_id": "7cd59a2829630305", "doc_id": "hp_bb98f886833576c8"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In recent years our film art has created an unprecedented sensation in the world's filmdom...", "chunk_id": "7cd59a2829630305", "doc_id": "hp_bb98f886833576c8"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bb98f886833576c8"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="feature film">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A type of film that is praised by revolutionary people worldwide.", "chunk_id": "7cd59a2829630305", "doc_id": "hp_bb98f886833576c8"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The revolutionary people of the world are unstinting in their praise of this feature film and other monumental works, calling them 'the first-class films by international standards', 'the most wonderful movies ever produced' and 'immortal revolutionary and popular films'.", "chunk_id": "7cd59a2829630305", "doc_id": "hp_bb98f886833576c8"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bb98f886833576c8"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Garin de Monglane">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A fictional character created by Conrad von Stöffler.", "chunk_id": "bc44d364b9f11c58", "doc_id": "hp_bd117ea391b64dae"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Garin de Monglane, or Montglane, is a fictional character created by Conrad von Stöffler in 1280.", "chunk_id": "bc44d364b9f11c58", "doc_id": "hp_bd117ea391b64dae"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bd117ea391b64dae"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Montglane">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An alternative name for the fictional character Garin de Monglane.", "chunk_id": "bc44d364b9f11c58", "doc_id": "hp_bd117ea391b64dae"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Garin de Monglane, or Montglane, is a fictional character created by Conrad von Stöffler in 1280.", "chunk_id": "bc44d364b9f11c58", "doc_id": "hp_bd117ea391b64dae"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bd117ea391b64dae"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Conrad von Stöffler">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The creator of the fictional character Garin de Monglane.", "chunk_id": "bc44d364b9f11c58", "doc_id": "hp_bd117ea391b64dae"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Garin de Monglane, or Montglane, is a fictional character created by Conrad von Stöffler in 1280.", "chunk_id": "bc44d364b9f11c58", "doc_id": "hp_bd117ea391b64dae"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bd117ea391b64dae"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="La Geste de Garin de Monglane">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The second cycle of Old French \"chansons de geste\", named after the character Garin de Monglane.", "chunk_id": "bc44d364b9f11c58", "doc_id": "hp_bd117ea391b64dae"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The character gives his name to the second cycle of Old French \"chansons de geste\", \"La Geste de Garin de Monglane\".", "chunk_id": "bc44d364b9f11c58", "doc_id": "hp_bd117ea391b64dae"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bd117ea391b64dae"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Saracens">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A historical term used in medieval Europe to refer to Muslims, often depicted as enemies in literature.", "chunk_id": "bc44d364b9f11c58", "doc_id": "hp_bd117ea391b64dae"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "His cycle tells stories of fiefless lads of noble birth who went off seeking land and adventure fighting the Saracens.", "chunk_id": "bc44d364b9f11c58", "doc_id": "hp_bd117ea391b64dae"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bd117ea391b64dae"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Pollux Rock">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Pollux Rock is the southern of a pair of large off-lying rocks south of Vindication Island.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Pollux Rock ( ) is the southern of a pair of large off-lying rocks south of Vindication Island, South Sandwich Islands.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Vindication Island">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Vindication Island is an island located north of the South Sandwich Islands.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Pollux Rock ( ) is the southern of a pair of large off-lying rocks south of Vindication Island, South Sandwich Islands.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="South Sandwich Islands">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The South Sandwich Islands are a volcanic island arc in the South Atlantic Ocean.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Pollux Rock ( ) is the southern of a pair of large off-lying rocks south of Vindication Island, South Sandwich Islands.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Castor Rock">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Castor Rock is the northern of a pair of large off-lying rocks south of Vindication Island.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "This rock, with its neighbor Castor Rock, was named \"Castor and Pollux\" during the survey of these islands from \"RRS Discovery II\" in 1930.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Castor and Pollux">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Castor and Pollux was the original name given to a pair of rocks during a survey in 1930.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "This rock, with its neighbor Castor Rock, was named \"Castor and Pollux\" during the survey of these islands from \"RRS Discovery II\" in 1930.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="RRS Discovery II">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "RRS Discovery II was a ship used for surveying islands in 1930.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "This rock, with its neighbor Castor Rock, was named \"Castor and Pollux\" during the survey of these islands from \"RRS Discovery II\" in 1930.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="United Kingdom Antarctic Place-Names Committee (UK-APC)">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The UK-APC is a committee that recommends place-names in Antarctica.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In 1971 United Kingdom Antarctic Place-Names Committee (UK-APC) recommended that they be assigned unambiguous names making each individually identifiable, and this has been done by naming the southern one Pollux Rock and the northern one Castor Rock.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Association of Tennis Professionals (ATP)">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Association of Tennis Professionals (ATP) is an organization that ranks professional male tennis players.", "chunk_id": "9427c18f95847c63", "doc_id": "hp_be33f525d9693352"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Richard Gasquet (] ; born 18 June 1986) is a French professional tennis player who is currently ranked world No. 30 in men's singles by the Association of Tennis Professionals (ATP).", "chunk_id": "9427c18f95847c63", "doc_id": "hp_be33f525d9693352"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_be33f525d9693352"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Tatiana Golovin">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Tatiana Golovin is a tennis player who partnered Richard Gasquet in the 2004 French Open mixed doubles.", "chunk_id": "9427c18f95847c63", "doc_id": "hp_be33f525d9693352"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He won the mixed doubles Grand Slam title at the 2004 French Open, partnering Tatiana Golovin.", "chunk_id": "9427c18f95847c63", "doc_id": "hp_be33f525d9693352"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_be33f525d9693352"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Olympic bronze medal">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An Olympic bronze medal is an award given for third place in the Olympic Games.", "chunk_id": "9427c18f95847c63", "doc_id": "hp_be33f525d9693352"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He also won an Olympic bronze medal in 2012 with his doubles partner Julien Benneteau.", "chunk_id": "9427c18f95847c63", "doc_id": "hp_be33f525d9693352"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_be33f525d9693352"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="2012">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The year 2012, during which Richard Gasquet won an Olympic bronze medal.", "chunk_id": "9427c18f95847c63", "doc_id": "hp_be33f525d9693352"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He also won an Olympic bronze medal in 2012 with his doubles partner Julien Benneteau.", "chunk_id": "9427c18f95847c63", "doc_id": "hp_be33f525d9693352"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_be33f525d9693352"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="2015 Wimbledon Championships">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The 2015 Wimbledon Championships was a tennis tournament where Richard Gasquet reached the semifinals in singles.", "chunk_id": "9427c18f95847c63", "doc_id": "hp_be33f525d9693352"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "In singles, his best achievements in Grand Slams are reaching the semifinals of the 2007 and 2015 Wimbledon Championships and the semifinals of the 2013 US Open.", "chunk_id": "9427c18f95847c63", "doc_id": "hp_be33f525d9693352"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_be33f525d9693352"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="long-winding groundstrokes">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Long-winding groundstrokes are a characteristic playing style in tennis.", "chunk_id": "9427c18f95847c63", "doc_id": "hp_be33f525d9693352"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Gasquet is best known for his long-winding groundstrokes and his one-handed backhand.", "chunk_id": "9427c18f95847c63", "doc_id": "hp_be33f525d9693352"}]</data>
