<node id="St Cedd">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "St Cedd is one of the dedications of Chelmsford Cathedral.", "chunk_id": "a46d15f8c3fc12ac", "doc_id": "hp_c098515d47bb4e6e"}, {"text": "The founder of the Chapel of St Peter-on-the-Wall.", "chunk_id": "147b3f29c0fcd687", "doc_id": "hp_e801334348d2b1fc"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Chelmsford Cathedral in the city of Chelmsford, Essex, England, is dedicated to St Mary the Virgin, St Peter and St Cedd.", "chunk_id": "a46d15f8c3fc12ac", "doc_id": "hp_c098515d47bb4e6e"}, {"text": "The Dean of Chelmsford is also responsible for the Chapel of St Peter-on-the-Wall at Bradwell-on-Sea, founded by St Cedd, among the oldest church buildings in regular use in England.", "chunk_id": "147b3f29c0fcd687", "doc_id": "hp_e801334348d2b1fc"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c098515d47bb4e6e", "hp_e801334348d2b1fc"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Anglican Diocese of Chelmsford">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Anglican Diocese of Chelmsford is an ecclesiastical province of the Church of England.", "chunk_id": "a46d15f8c3fc12ac", "doc_id": "hp_c098515d47bb4e6e"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It became a cathedral when the Anglican Diocese of Chelmsford was created in 1914 and is the seat of the Bishop of Chelmsford.", "chunk_id": "a46d15f8c3fc12ac", "doc_id": "hp_c098515d47bb4e6e"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c098515d47bb4e6e"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Cameline">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Cameline was a fabric material used in the Middle Ages for cloth.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Cameline ( ) was a fabric material used in the Middle Ages for cloth.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="camel's hair">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Camel's hair is a material that was traditionally thought to be used in the original making of cameline.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "By tradition it is commonly thought to have been originally made of camel's hair in Asia.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Cyprus">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Cyprus is a location from which cameline was imported into Europe.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was imported from Cyprus and Syria into Europe.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Syria">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Syria is a location from which cameline was imported into Europe.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was imported from Cyprus and Syria into Europe.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Arabs">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Arabs are a group of people associated with a type of cloak made of camel's hair.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Cameline is described also as a cloak of the Arabs made of camel's hair which is oftentimes striped white and brown in color.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="French cloth">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "French cloth was a type of imitation cameline made of goat's hair.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was sometimes a lower quality French cloth imitation made of goat's hair.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="goat's hair">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Goat's hair was used to make a lower quality French cloth imitation of cameline.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was sometimes a lower quality French cloth imitation made of goat's hair.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Flanders">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Flanders is a location where cameline fibers were spun into yarn and produced in many colors in medieval times.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The fibers were spun into yarn and produced in Flanders and the Duchy of Brabant in many colors in medieval times.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Duchy of Brabant">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Duchy of Brabant is a location where cameline fibers were spun into yarn and produced in many colors in medieval times.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The fibers were spun into yarn and produced in Flanders and the Duchy of Brabant in many colors in medieval times.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="woolen textile">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A woolen textile made of camel's hair combined with wool or cotton is described as warm and light.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is also described as a warm light woolen textile of camel's hair combined with wool or cotton.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="wool">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Wool is a material that can be combined with camel's hair to create a woolen textile.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is also described as a warm light woolen textile of camel's hair combined with wool or cotton.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="camlet">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Camlet is a fabric made of camel's hair, considered of higher quality than cameline.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is considered of lesser quality than that of camlet, which is also made of camel's hair.", "chunk_id": "80b52c81ca855fef", "doc_id": "hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c12a13b85cfa0362"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Caramel (City High song)">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A song by the R&amp;B/hip hop trio City High.", "chunk_id": "4b7512b6f1c5cb80", "doc_id": "hp_c1b2bbdafbcaad90"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Caramel\" is the second single released from American R&amp;B/hip hop trio City High's self-titled debut album in 2001.", "chunk_id": "4b7512b6f1c5cb80", "doc_id": "hp_c1b2bbdafbcaad90"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c1b2bbdafbcaad90"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="City High">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An American R&amp;B/hip hop trio.", "chunk_id": "4b7512b6f1c5cb80", "doc_id": "hp_c1b2bbdafbcaad90"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "\"Caramel\" is the second single released from American R&amp;B/hip hop trio City High's self-titled debut album in 2001.", "chunk_id": "4b7512b6f1c5cb80", "doc_id": "hp_c1b2bbdafbcaad90"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c1b2bbdafbcaad90"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Brian Gough">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The person on whom the song \"Caramel\" was written.", "chunk_id": "4b7512b6f1c5cb80", "doc_id": "hp_c1b2bbdafbcaad90"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The song was actually written based on the appearance and personality of Brian Gough, though he is actually 5'6\" with brown eyes not 5'5\" with brown eyes.", "chunk_id": "4b7512b6f1c5cb80", "doc_id": "hp_c1b2bbdafbcaad90"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c1b2bbdafbcaad90"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Hot R&amp;B/Hip-Hop Singles &amp; Tracks">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A music chart that ranks the top R&amp;B/Hip-Hop songs in the U.S.", "chunk_id": "4b7512b6f1c5cb80", "doc_id": "hp_c1b2bbdafbcaad90"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It is the group's second most successful single, peaking at number 18 on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 and number nine on the Hot R&amp;B/Hip-Hop Singles &amp; Tracks in the U.S. in January 2002.", "chunk_id": "4b7512b6f1c5cb80", "doc_id": "hp_c1b2bbdafbcaad90"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c1b2bbdafbcaad90"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Seth Brooks Binzer">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An American music artist, born on August 23, 1974, also known as Shifty Shellshock.", "chunk_id": "1e82acbea30954cf", "doc_id": "hp_c1c0a020ac369351"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Seth Brooks Binzer (born August 23, 1974), better known by his stage name Shifty Shellshock, is an American music artist, best known for being a co-founder and front man of the rap rock band Crazy Town, and their hit song \"Butterfly\".", "chunk_id": "1e82acbea30954cf", "doc_id": "hp_c1c0a020ac369351"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c1c0a020ac369351"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Butterfly">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A hit song by the rap rock band Crazy Town.", "chunk_id": "1e82acbea30954cf", "doc_id": "hp_c1c0a020ac369351"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Seth Brooks Binzer (born August 23, 1974), better known by his stage name Shifty Shellshock, is an American music artist, best known for being a co-founder and front man of the rap rock band Crazy Town, and their hit song \"Butterfly\".", "chunk_id": "1e82acbea30954cf", "doc_id": "hp_c1c0a020ac369351"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_c1c0a020ac369351"]</data>
