<node id="British Columbia">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "British Columbia is a Canadian province where Langley is located.", "chunk_id": "55ab038a3c41aeea", "doc_id": "hp_d2b1b9b8bce24c9a"}, {"text": "A province in Canada, where the city of Trail is located.", "chunk_id": "8c9123487c66f805", "doc_id": "hp_f23b02c7bab7a782"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Grand'Maître is the current Canadian Women's Doubles Champion, winning her 14th doubles title in Langley, British Columbia with Jennifer Saunders in May 2013.", "chunk_id": "55ab038a3c41aeea", "doc_id": "hp_d2b1b9b8bce24c9a"}, {"text": "The Trail Smoke Eaters (previously named as the \"Trail Hockey Club\") were a senior level men's ice hockey team from Trail, British Columbia that played from 1926 to 1987.", "chunk_id": "8c9123487c66f805", "doc_id": "hp_f23b02c7bab7a782"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_d2b1b9b8bce24c9a", "hp_f23b02c7bab7a782"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Canadian Women's Champion">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Canadian Women's Champion is a singles title that Josée Grand'Maître has won three times.", "chunk_id": "55ab038a3c41aeea", "doc_id": "hp_d2b1b9b8bce24c9a"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Grand'Maître's also been the Canadian Women's Champion in singles three times, and her 18 titles overall tie her for most by a Canadian with Jennifer Saunders.", "chunk_id": "55ab038a3c41aeea", "doc_id": "hp_d2b1b9b8bce24c9a"}]</data>
