<node id="Dan">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Dan was a brother of John Vaughn Blake and played football for the Vanderbilt Commodores.", "chunk_id": "259a6531d9526bfc", "doc_id": "hp_da6328f97884070d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He played football for Dan McGugin's Vanderbilt Commodores football teams with his brothers Dan and Bob.", "chunk_id": "259a6531d9526bfc", "doc_id": "hp_da6328f97884070d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_da6328f97884070d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Bob">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Bob was a brother of John Vaughn Blake and played football for the Vanderbilt Commodores.", "chunk_id": "259a6531d9526bfc", "doc_id": "hp_da6328f97884070d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He played football for Dan McGugin's Vanderbilt Commodores football teams with his brothers Dan and Bob.", "chunk_id": "259a6531d9526bfc", "doc_id": "hp_da6328f97884070d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_da6328f97884070d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Alvin Karpis">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Alvin Karpis was captured by the FBI, an operation John Vaughn Blake was involved in.", "chunk_id": "259a6531d9526bfc", "doc_id": "hp_da6328f97884070d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He was later an FBI agent involved with the capture of Alvin Karpis.", "chunk_id": "259a6531d9526bfc", "doc_id": "hp_da6328f97884070d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_da6328f97884070d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="William Gibson">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "William Ford Gibson is an American-Canadian speculative fiction writer and essayist.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "William Ford Gibson (born March 17, 1948) is an American-Canadian speculative fiction writer and essayist widely credited with pioneering the science fiction subgenre known as cyberpunk.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="cyberpunk">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Cyberpunk is a science fiction subgenre pioneered by William Gibson.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "William Ford Gibson (born March 17, 1948) is an American-Canadian speculative fiction writer and essayist widely credited with pioneering the science fiction subgenre known as cyberpunk.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="technology">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Technology is explored in William Gibson's early works for its effects on humans.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Beginning his writing career in the late 1970s, his early works were noir, near-future stories that explored the effects of technology, cybernetics, and computer networks on humans—a \"combination of lowlife and high tech\"—and helped to create an iconography for the information age before the ubiquity of the Internet in the 1990s.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="cybernetics">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Cybernetics is explored in William Gibson's early works for its effects on humans.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Beginning his writing career in the late 1970s, his early works were noir, near-future stories that explored the effects of technology, cybernetics, and computer networks on humans—a \"combination of lowlife and high tech\"—and helped to create an iconography for the information age before the ubiquity of the Internet in the 1990s.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="computer networks">
  <data key="d0">TECHNOLOGY</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Computer networks are explored in William Gibson's early works for their effects on humans.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}, {"text": "Computer networks are systems that connect computers and other devices to share resources and information.", "chunk_id": "ef4743de89955cae", "doc_id": "hp_dc063fd42799d92d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Beginning his writing career in the late 1970s, his early works were noir, near-future stories that explored the effects of technology, cybernetics, and computer networks on humans—a \"combination of lowlife and high tech\"—and helped to create an iconography for the information age before the ubiquity of the Internet in the 1990s.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}, {"text": "The technician's responsibilities may extend to include building or configuring new hardware, installing and updating software packages, and creating and maintaining computer networks.", "chunk_id": "ef4743de89955cae", "doc_id": "hp_dc063fd42799d92d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_daedfde9b7ca2260", "hp_dc063fd42799d92d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="information age">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The information age is an era for which William Gibson's works helped create an iconography.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Beginning his writing career in the late 1970s, his early works were noir, near-future stories that explored the effects of technology, cybernetics, and computer networks on humans—a \"combination of lowlife and high tech\"—and helped to create an iconography for the information age before the ubiquity of the Internet in the 1990s.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Internet">
  <data key="d0">TECHNOLOGY</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Internet is a technology that became ubiquitous in the 1990s.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}, {"text": "A global system of interconnected computer networks that use the Internet protocol suite (TCP/IP) to link devices worldwide.", "chunk_id": "681088037d9bda6f", "doc_id": "hp_e1233259446c427d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Beginning his writing career in the late 1970s, his early works were noir, near-future stories that explored the effects of technology, cybernetics, and computer networks on humans—a \"combination of lowlife and high tech\"—and helped to create an iconography for the information age before the ubiquity of the Internet in the 1990s.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}, {"text": "Armin Meiwes ( ; born 1 December 1961) is a German computer repair technician who achieved international notoriety for killing and eating a voluntary victim whom he had found via the Internet.", "chunk_id": "681088037d9bda6f", "doc_id": "hp_e1233259446c427d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_daedfde9b7ca2260", "hp_e1233259446c427d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="cyberspace">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Cyberspace is a term coined by William Gibson.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Gibson notably coined the term \"cyberspace\" in his short story \"Burning Chrome\" (1982) and later popularized the concept in his acclaimed debut novel \"Neuromancer\" (1984).", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Burning Chrome">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Burning Chrome is a short story by William Gibson where he coined the term \"cyberspace\".", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Gibson notably coined the term \"cyberspace\" in his short story \"Burning Chrome\" (1982) and later popularized the concept in his acclaimed debut novel \"Neuromancer\" (1984).", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Neuromancer">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Neuromancer is the acclaimed debut novel by William Gibson that popularized the concept of cyberspace.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Gibson notably coined the term \"cyberspace\" in his short story \"Burning Chrome\" (1982) and later popularized the concept in his acclaimed debut novel \"Neuromancer\" (1984).", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="science fiction literature">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Science fiction literature was renovated by William Gibson's early works.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "These early works have been credited with \"renovating\" science fiction literature after it had fallen largely into insignificance in the 1970s.", "chunk_id": "4bb65110bd5235e2", "doc_id": "hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_daedfde9b7ca2260"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Ian Joyce">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Ian Joyce is an American soccer player.", "chunk_id": "43aad4e477f8ff50", "doc_id": "hp_daef9730974fe681"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Ian Francis Joyce (born July 12, 1985) is an American soccer player who most recently played for Major League Soccer club Colorado Rapids.", "chunk_id": "43aad4e477f8ff50", "doc_id": "hp_daef9730974fe681"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_daef9730974fe681"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Tedisamil">
  <data key="d0">DRUG</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Tedisamil is an experimental class III antiarrhythmic agent being investigated for atrial fibrillation.", "chunk_id": "b7d2a8a0d65a6290", "doc_id": "hp_db684e0053d7062f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Tedisamil (3,7-dicyclopropylmethyl-9,9-tetramethylene-3,7-diazabicyclo-3,3,1-nonane) is an experimental class III antiarrhythmic agent currently being investigated for the treatment of atrial fibrillation.", "chunk_id": "b7d2a8a0d65a6290", "doc_id": "hp_db684e0053d7062f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_db684e0053d7062f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="potassium channels">
  <data key="d0">BIOLOGICAL_STRUCTURE</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Potassium channels are pore-forming proteins that help establish a resting membrane potential and are crucial for the excitability of all cells.", "chunk_id": "b7d2a8a0d65a6290", "doc_id": "hp_db684e0053d7062f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Tedisamil blocks multiple types of potassium channels in the heart resulting in slowed heart rate.", "chunk_id": "b7d2a8a0d65a6290", "doc_id": "hp_db684e0053d7062f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_db684e0053d7062f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="heart">
  <data key="d0">ORGAN</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood through the body's circulatory system.", "chunk_id": "b7d2a8a0d65a6290", "doc_id": "hp_db684e0053d7062f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Tedisamil blocks multiple types of potassium channels in the heart resulting in slowed heart rate.", "chunk_id": "b7d2a8a0d65a6290", "doc_id": "hp_db684e0053d7062f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_db684e0053d7062f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="atria">
  <data key="d0">ANATOMICAL_STRUCTURE</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The atria are the two upper chambers of the heart.", "chunk_id": "b7d2a8a0d65a6290", "doc_id": "hp_db684e0053d7062f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "While the effects of tedisamil have been demonstrated in both atrial and ventricular muscle, repolarization is prolonged more efficiently in the atria.", "chunk_id": "b7d2a8a0d65a6290", "doc_id": "hp_db684e0053d7062f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_db684e0053d7062f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="ventricular muscle">
  <data key="d0">TISSUE</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Ventricular muscle refers to the muscle tissue of the ventricles of the heart.", "chunk_id": "b7d2a8a0d65a6290", "doc_id": "hp_db684e0053d7062f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "While the effects of tedisamil have been demonstrated in both atrial and ventricular muscle, repolarization is prolonged more efficiently in the atria.", "chunk_id": "b7d2a8a0d65a6290", "doc_id": "hp_db684e0053d7062f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_db684e0053d7062f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="angina">
  <data key="d0">MEDICAL_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Angina is chest pain caused by reduced blood flow to the heart muscle.", "chunk_id": "b7d2a8a0d65a6290", "doc_id": "hp_db684e0053d7062f"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Tedisamil also has significant anti-ischemic properties and was initially investigated as a potential treatment for angina until its antiarrhythmic effects were discovered.", "chunk_id": "b7d2a8a0d65a6290", "doc_id": "hp_db684e0053d7062f"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_db684e0053d7062f"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Notre Dame High School for Girls">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Notre Dame High School for Girls was a private, Roman Catholic, all-girls college prep high school in Chicago, Illinois.", "chunk_id": "e1f93f4fdb5e61f5", "doc_id": "hp_db88fb2791fae586"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Notre Dame High School for Girls was a private, Roman Catholic, all-girls college prep high school in Chicago, Illinois.", "chunk_id": "e1f93f4fdb5e61f5", "doc_id": "hp_db88fb2791fae586"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_db88fb2791fae586"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Archdiocese of Chicago">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Archdiocese of Chicago incorporated Notre Dame High School for Girls in 2009.", "chunk_id": "e1f93f4fdb5e61f5", "doc_id": "hp_db88fb2791fae586"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Notre Dame High School for Girls was founded in 1938 by the Sisters of Notre Dame de Namur and in 2009, was incorporated by the Archdiocese of Chicago, making it part of the St. Ferdinand Parish.", "chunk_id": "e1f93f4fdb5e61f5", "doc_id": "hp_db88fb2791fae586"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_db88fb2791fae586"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="St. Ferdinand Parish">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "St. Ferdinand Parish is associated with Notre Dame High School for Girls after its incorporation by the Archdiocese of Chicago.", "chunk_id": "e1f93f4fdb5e61f5", "doc_id": "hp_db88fb2791fae586"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Notre Dame High School for Girls was founded in 1938 by the Sisters of Notre Dame de Namur and in 2009, was incorporated by the Archdiocese of Chicago, making it part of the St. Ferdinand Parish.", "chunk_id": "e1f93f4fdb5e61f5", "doc_id": "hp_db88fb2791fae586"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_db88fb2791fae586"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="St. Julie Billiart">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "St. Julie Billiart was the founder of the Sisters of Notre Dame de Namur and her educational philosophy was the basis for the teachings at Notre Dame High School for Girls.", "chunk_id": "e1f93f4fdb5e61f5", "doc_id": "hp_db88fb2791fae586"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Its teachings were based on the educational philosophy of St. Julie Billiart, founder of the Sisters of Notre Dame de Namur.", "chunk_id": "e1f93f4fdb5e61f5", "doc_id": "hp_db88fb2791fae586"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_db88fb2791fae586"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Stenocereus">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A genus of columnar or tree-like cacti.", "chunk_id": "cfcc8f8ff86d83c3", "doc_id": "hp_dbf42d0cc7b618be"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Stenocereus (Gk. stenos, narrow, L. cereus, candle) is a genus of columnar or tree-like cacti from the Baja California Peninsula and other parts of Mexico, Arizona in the United States, Colombia, Costa Rica, Guatemala, Venezuela and the ABC islands of the Dutch Caribbean.", "chunk_id": "cfcc8f8ff86d83c3", "doc_id": "hp_dbf42d0cc7b618be"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_dbf42d0cc7b618be"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Baja California Peninsula">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A peninsula located in Mexico.", "chunk_id": "cfcc8f8ff86d83c3", "doc_id": "hp_dbf42d0cc7b618be"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Stenocereus (Gk. stenos, narrow, L. cereus, candle) is a genus of columnar or tree-like cacti from the Baja California Peninsula and other parts of Mexico, Arizona in the United States, Colombia, Costa Rica, Guatemala, Venezuela and the ABC islands of the Dutch Caribbean.", "chunk_id": "cfcc8f8ff86d83c3", "doc_id": "hp_dbf42d0cc7b618be"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_dbf42d0cc7b618be"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
