<node id="Remo Ruffini">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "One of the individuals who proposed the name 'ergosphere'.", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Its name was proposed by Remo Ruffini and John Archibald Wheeler during the Les Houches lectures in 1971 and is derived from the Greek word \"ergon\", which means \"work\".", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e09ae53df97c48d0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="John Archibald Wheeler">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "One of the individuals who proposed the name 'ergosphere'.", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Its name was proposed by Remo Ruffini and John Archibald Wheeler during the Les Houches lectures in 1971 and is derived from the Greek word \"ergon\", which means \"work\".", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e09ae53df97c48d0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Les Houches lectures">
  <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A series of lectures where the name 'ergosphere' was proposed.", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Its name was proposed by Remo Ruffini and John Archibald Wheeler during the Les Houches lectures in 1971 and is derived from the Greek word \"ergon\", which means \"work\".", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e09ae53df97c48d0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="ergon">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A Greek word meaning 'work'.", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Its name was proposed by Remo Ruffini and John Archibald Wheeler during the Les Houches lectures in 1971 and is derived from the Greek word \"ergon\", which means \"work\".", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e09ae53df97c48d0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Schwarzschild radius">
  <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The radius of the event horizon of a non-rotating black hole.", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The equatorial (maximum) radius of an ergosphere corresponds to the Schwarzschild radius of a non-rotating black hole; the polar (minimum) radius can be as little as half the Schwarzschild radius (the radius of a non-rotating black hole) in the case that the black hole is rotating maximally (at higher rotation rates the black hole could not have formed).", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e09ae53df97c48d0"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Armin Meiwes">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A German computer repair technician who gained notoriety for killing and eating a voluntary victim found online.", "chunk_id": "681088037d9bda6f", "doc_id": "hp_e1233259446c427d"}, {"text": "The individual whose true-crime story may have inspired the film Diary of a Cannibal.", "chunk_id": "e4fc625ee54ece8f", "doc_id": "hp_e24e3312ad888691"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Armin Meiwes ( ; born 1 December 1961) is a German computer repair technician who achieved international notoriety for killing and eating a voluntary victim whom he had found via the Internet.", "chunk_id": "681088037d9bda6f", "doc_id": "hp_e1233259446c427d"}, {"text": "It is possibly inspired by the true-crime story of Armin Meiwes, the \"Rotenburg Cannibal\" who posted an online ad searching for someone to volunteer to be mutilated and eaten.", "chunk_id": "e4fc625ee54ece8f", "doc_id": "hp_e24e3312ad888691"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e1233259446c427d", "hp_e24e3312ad888691"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Rotenburg Cannibal">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "An alias for Armin Meiwes, referring to his cannibalistic acts.", "chunk_id": "681088037d9bda6f", "doc_id": "hp_e1233259446c427d"}, {"text": "A nickname for Armin Meiwes, associated with a true-crime story that may have inspired the film Diary of a Cannibal.", "chunk_id": "e4fc625ee54ece8f", "doc_id": "hp_e24e3312ad888691"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Because of his acts, Meiwes is also known as the Rotenburg Cannibal or \"Der Metzgermeister\" (The Master Butcher).", "chunk_id": "681088037d9bda6f", "doc_id": "hp_e1233259446c427d"}, {"text": "It is possibly inspired by the true-crime story of Armin Meiwes, the \"Rotenburg Cannibal\" who posted an online ad searching for someone to volunteer to be mutilated and eaten.", "chunk_id": "e4fc625ee54ece8f", "doc_id": "hp_e24e3312ad888691"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e1233259446c427d", "hp_e24e3312ad888691"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Der Metzgermeister">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "A German phrase meaning \"The Master Butcher\", used as an alias for Armin Meiwes.", "chunk_id": "681088037d9bda6f", "doc_id": "hp_e1233259446c427d"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Because of his acts, Meiwes is also known as the Rotenburg Cannibal or \"Der Metzgermeister\" (The Master Butcher).", "chunk_id": "681088037d9bda6f", "doc_id": "hp_e1233259446c427d"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e1233259446c427d"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
