<node id="Anton Biersack">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Anton Biersack was a German composer and music educator.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Anton Biersack (30 November 1907, Greding - 18 November 1982, Frankfurt am Main) was a German composer and music educator.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e546658adba29b4c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Greding">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Greding is a location associated with Anton Biersack's birth.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "Anton Biersack (30 November 1907, Greding - 18 November 1982, Frankfurt am Main) was a German composer and music educator.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e546658adba29b4c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Eichstätt">
  <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Eichstätt is a location where Anton Biersack had initial studies in music.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "After initial studied in music in Eichstätt, he studied music composition, conducting, piano, and organ at the Hochschule für Musik Würzburg from 1928-1932.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e546658adba29b4c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Hochschule für Musik Würzburg">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Hochschule für Musik Würzburg is an institution where Anton Biersack studied music composition, conducting, piano, and organ.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "After initial studied in music in Eichstätt, he studied music composition, conducting, piano, and organ at the Hochschule für Musik Würzburg from 1928-1932.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e546658adba29b4c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Agathe Biersack">
  <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Agathe Biersack was married to Anton Biersack.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He was married to Agathe Biersack (née Laur ) (1910–1996).", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e546658adba29b4c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Frankfurt University of Music and Performing Arts">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Frankfurt University of Music and Performing Arts (FUMPA) is an institution where Anton Biersack worked as a conductor and later as a lecturer, head of orchestral studies, and full professor.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He then worked as a conductor of student choral and orchestral ensembles at the Frankfurt University of Music and Performing Arts (FUMPA) before being appointed a lecturer at that school in 1947.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e546658adba29b4c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="FUMPA">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "FUMPA is an abbreviation for Frankfurt University of Music and Performing Arts.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "He then worked as a conductor of student choral and orchestral ensembles at the Frankfurt University of Music and Performing Arts (FUMPA) before being appointed a lecturer at that school in 1947.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e546658adba29b4c"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="The Hunter (EP)">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "The Hunter is the first EP by Kele Okereke.", "chunk_id": "145e5d0c1408e198", "doc_id": "hp_e5470b4e6fa8bc35"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The Hunter is the first EP (and follow up to the 2010 solo album \"The Boxer\") by Kele Okereke (under the professional name Kele), lead singer and rhythm guitarist of the British rock band Bloc Party.", "chunk_id": "145e5d0c1408e198", "doc_id": "hp_e5470b4e6fa8bc35"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e5470b4e6fa8bc35"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Wichita Recordings">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Wichita Recordings is a record label that released The Hunter EP.", "chunk_id": "145e5d0c1408e198", "doc_id": "hp_e5470b4e6fa8bc35"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was released on 7 November 2011 by Wichita Recordings in the UK, set back a week from the original release date, and 3 days earlier on 4 November 2011 by Wichita Recordings and Liberator Music in Australia.", "chunk_id": "145e5d0c1408e198", "doc_id": "hp_e5470b4e6fa8bc35"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e5470b4e6fa8bc35"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="Liberator Music">
  <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "Liberator Music is a record label that released The Hunter EP in Australia.", "chunk_id": "145e5d0c1408e198", "doc_id": "hp_e5470b4e6fa8bc35"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "It was released on 7 November 2011 by Wichita Recordings in the UK, set back a week from the original release date, and 3 days earlier on 4 November 2011 by Wichita Recordings and Liberator Music in Australia.", "chunk_id": "145e5d0c1408e198", "doc_id": "hp_e5470b4e6fa8bc35"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e5470b4e6fa8bc35"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
<node id="What Did I Do?">
  <data key="d0">OTHER</data>
  <data key="d1">[{"text": "What Did I Do? is the first single released from The Hunter EP.", "chunk_id": "145e5d0c1408e198", "doc_id": "hp_e5470b4e6fa8bc35"}]</data>
  <data key="d2">[{"text": "The first single released from the EP was \"What Did I Do?\", which features guest vocals from Lucy Taylor.", "chunk_id": "145e5d0c1408e198", "doc_id": "hp_e5470b4e6fa8bc35"}]</data>
  <data key="d3">["hp_e5470b4e6fa8bc35"]</data>
  <data key="d4">False</data>
</node>
