  <data key="d6">Eric Yamamoto was a member of Fred Korematsu's legal team.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Flowing from the landmark Korematsu v. United States case, he is known for his work as a member of Fred Korematsu's legal team.", "chunk_id": "f107c34d10795506", "doc_id": "hp_00c8ffa1fdfa046b", "type": "MEMBER_OF_LEGAL_TEAM"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_00c8ffa1fdfa046b</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Korematsu v. United States" target="United States Supreme Court">
  <data key="d5">["DECIDED_BY", "PART_OF", "DECIDED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Korematsu v. United States was a decision made by the United States Supreme Court.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Dale Minami (born October 13, 1946) is a San Francisco-based lawyer best known for heading the legal team that overturned the conviction of Fred Korematsu, whose defiance of the World War II Japanese American internment order lead to Korematsu v. United States, one of the most controversial United States Supreme Court decisions of the 20th century.", "chunk_id": "63f34134976a8d32", "doc_id": "hp_18a6d077ab278415", "type": "DECIDED_BY"}, {"text": "Korematsu v. United States, 323 U.S. 214 (1944), was a landmark United States Supreme Court case concerning the constitutionality of Executive Order 9066, which ordered Japanese Americans into internment camps during World War II regardless of citizenship.", "chunk_id": "c923a57087201126", "doc_id": "hp_ad41e3555a82bb26", "type": "PART_OF"}, {"text": "Although the Court did not touch on the constitutionality of the exclusion of people of Japanese ancestry from the West Coast—which they had found not to violate citizen rights in their \"Korematsu v. United States\" decision on the same date—the Endo ruling nonetheless led to the reopening of the West Coast to Japanese Americans after their incarceration in camps across the U.S. interior during World War II.", "chunk_id": "615cdfa10474d8b6", "doc_id": "hp_c36e9406d9e10267", "type": "DECIDED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_18a6d077ab278415</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Korematsu v. United States" target="Fred Korematsu">
  <data key="d5">["RESULTED_FROM"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The case Korematsu v. United States resulted from Fred Korematsu's defiance.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Dale Minami (born October 13, 1946) is a San Francisco-based lawyer best known for heading the legal team that overturned the conviction of Fred Korematsu, whose defiance of the World War II Japanese American internment order lead to Korematsu v. United States, one of the most controversial United States Supreme Court decisions of the 20th century.", "chunk_id": "63f34134976a8d32", "doc_id": "hp_18a6d077ab278415", "type": "RESULTED_FROM"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_18a6d077ab278415</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Korematsu v. United States" target="Executive Order 9066">
  <data key="d5">["CONCERNING"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Korematsu v. United States case was about the constitutionality of Executive Order 9066.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Korematsu v. United States, 323 U.S. 214 (1944), was a landmark United States Supreme Court case concerning the constitutionality of Executive Order 9066, which ordered Japanese Americans into internment camps during World War II regardless of citizenship.", "chunk_id": "c923a57087201126", "doc_id": "hp_ad41e3555a82bb26", "type": "CONCERNING"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ad41e3555a82bb26</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fred Korematsu" target="Japanese American internment order">
  <data key="d5">["DEFIED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Fred Korematsu defied the Japanese American internment order.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Dale Minami (born October 13, 1946) is a San Francisco-based lawyer best known for heading the legal team that overturned the conviction of Fred Korematsu, whose defiance of the World War II Japanese American internment order lead to Korematsu v. United States, one of the most controversial United States Supreme Court decisions of the 20th century.", "chunk_id": "63f34134976a8d32", "doc_id": "hp_18a6d077ab278415", "type": "DEFIED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_18a6d077ab278415</data>
</edge>
