<edge source="Sonic Enemy" target="Golden Feelings">
  <data key="d5">["RELEASED", "RE_RELEASED", "PRESSED_ADDITIONAL_RUNS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Sonic Enemy released Beck's first full-length album, Golden Feelings.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Sonic Enemy is an independent record label, owned by Peter Hughes, best known for releasing Beck's first full-length album on cassette, \"Golden Feelings\" (1993).", "chunk_id": "57f89dc3a18cfd92", "doc_id": "hp_02b0abd7864c108e", "type": "RELEASED"}, {"text": "In 1999, they re-released \"Golden Feelings\", pressing a total of 2,000 copies, before Beck had them cease production of the CD.", "chunk_id": "57f89dc3a18cfd92", "doc_id": "hp_02b0abd7864c108e", "type": "RE_RELEASED"}, {"text": "According to Nevin Martell's Beck The Art of Mutation (page 13), the initial release was \"limited to one thousand cassette copies\" and \"Sonic Enemy pressed several additional runs until 1995.\"", "chunk_id": "57f89dc3a18cfd92", "doc_id": "hp_02b0abd7864c108e", "type": "PRESSED_ADDITIONAL_RUNS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_02b0abd7864c108e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sonic Enemy" target="Beck">
  <data key="d5">["RELEASED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Sonic Enemy released Beck's first full-length album.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Sonic Enemy is an independent record label, owned by Peter Hughes, best known for releasing Beck's first full-length album on cassette, \"Golden Feelings\" (1993).", "chunk_id": "57f89dc3a18cfd92", "doc_id": "hp_02b0abd7864c108e", "type": "RELEASED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_02b0abd7864c108e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Peter Hughes" target="Sonic Enemy">
  <data key="d5">["OWNED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Peter Hughes owns the record label Sonic Enemy.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Sonic Enemy is an independent record label, owned by Peter Hughes, best known for releasing Beck's first full-length album on cassette, \"Golden Feelings\" (1993).", "chunk_id": "57f89dc3a18cfd92", "doc_id": "hp_02b0abd7864c108e", "type": "OWNED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_02b0abd7864c108e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Beck" target="Sonic Enemy">
  <data key="d5">["CEASED_PRODUCTION"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Beck had Sonic Enemy cease production of the CD version of Golden Feelings.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In 1999, they re-released \"Golden Feelings\", pressing a total of 2,000 copies, before Beck had them cease production of the CD.", "chunk_id": "57f89dc3a18cfd92", "doc_id": "hp_02b0abd7864c108e", "type": "CEASED_PRODUCTION"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_02b0abd7864c108e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Golden Feelings" target="Beck">
  <data key="d5">["PERFORMED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Golden Feelings is an album performed by Beck.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Sonic Enemy is an independent record label, owned by Peter Hughes, best known for releasing Beck's first full-length album on cassette, \"Golden Feelings\" (1993).", "chunk_id": "57f89dc3a18cfd92", "doc_id": "hp_02b0abd7864c108e", "type": "PERFORMED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_02b0abd7864c108e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Nevin Martell" target="Beck The Art of Mutation">
  <data key="d5">["AUTHORED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Nevin Martell authored the book Beck The Art of Mutation.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "According to Nevin Martell's Beck The Art of Mutation (page 13), the initial release was \"limited to one thousand cassette copies\" and \"Sonic Enemy pressed several additional runs until 1995.\"", "chunk_id": "57f89dc3a18cfd92", "doc_id": "hp_02b0abd7864c108e", "type": "AUTHORED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_02b0abd7864c108e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Elie Wiesel" target="Moment (magazine)">
  <data key="d5">["FOUNDED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Elie Wiesel co-founded Moment magazine.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"Moment\" was founded in 1975, by Nobel Prize laureate Elie Wiesel and Jewish activist Leonard Fein, who served as the magazine's first editor from 1975 to 1987.", "chunk_id": "7156f0efb6184faa", "doc_id": "hp_02c3149273f48869", "type": "FOUNDED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_02c3149273f48869</data>
</edge>
