<edge source="Cesare Pugni" target="Genoa">
  <data key="d5">["BORN_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Cesare Pugni was born in Genoa.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Cesare Pugni (Russian: Цезарь Пуни ) (] ; 31 May 1802–26 January\r\n[O.S. 14 January]\r\n1870 ) born in Genoa, was an Italian composer of ballet music, a pianist and a violinist.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "type": "BORN_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Cesare Pugni" target="Her Majesty's Theatre">
  <data key="d5">["COMPOSED_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Cesare Pugni composed ballets for Her Majesty's Theatre.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Pugni is most noted for the ballets he composed for Her Majesty's Theatre in London (1843–1850), and for the Imperial Theatres in St. Petersburg, Russia (1850–1870).", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "type": "COMPOSED_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Cesare Pugni" target="London">
  <data key="d5">["WORKED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Cesare Pugni worked in London composing for Her Majesty's Theatre.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Pugni is most noted for the ballets he composed for Her Majesty's Theatre in London (1843–1850), and for the Imperial Theatres in St. Petersburg, Russia (1850–1870).", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "type": "WORKED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Cesare Pugni" target="Imperial Theatres">
  <data key="d5">["COMPOSED_FOR", "OFFICIAL_COMPOSER_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Cesare Pugni composed ballets for the Imperial Theatres.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Pugni is most noted for the ballets he composed for Her Majesty's Theatre in London (1843–1850), and for the Imperial Theatres in St. Petersburg, Russia (1850–1870).", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "type": "COMPOSED_FOR"}, {"text": "Pugni went on the compose for Perrot's successors Arthur Saint-Léon and Marius Petipa, serving as the Imperial Theatre's official composer of ballet music until his death in 1870.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "type": "OFFICIAL_COMPOSER_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Cesare Pugni" target="St. Petersburg">
  <data key="d5">["WORKED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Cesare Pugni worked in St. Petersburg composing for the Imperial Theatres.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Pugni is most noted for the ballets he composed for Her Majesty's Theatre in London (1843–1850), and for the Imperial Theatres in St. Petersburg, Russia (1850–1870).", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "type": "WORKED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Cesare Pugni" target="Russia">
  <data key="d5">["WORKED_IN", "MOVED_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Cesare Pugni worked in Russia.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Pugni is most noted for the ballets he composed for Her Majesty's Theatre in London (1843–1850), and for the Imperial Theatres in St. Petersburg, Russia (1850–1870).", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "type": "WORKED_IN"}, {"text": "Cesare Pugni followed Perrot and Grisi to Russia, and remained in the imperial capital even after Grisi's departure in 1853 and Perrot's departure in 1858.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "type": "MOVED_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Cesare Pugni" target="Jules Perrot">
  <data key="d5">["COLLABORATED_WITH", "FOLLOWED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Cesare Pugni composed ballet music for the works of Jules Perrot.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The majority of his ballet music was composed for the works of the ballet master Jules Perrot, who mounted nearly every one of his ballets to scores by Pugni.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "type": "COLLABORATED_WITH"}, {"text": "Cesare Pugni followed Perrot and Grisi to Russia, and remained in the imperial capital even after Grisi's departure in 1853 and Perrot's departure in 1858.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "type": "FOLLOWED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Cesare Pugni" target="Carlotta Grisi">
  <data key="d5">["FOLLOWED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Cesare Pugni followed Carlotta Grisi to Russia.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Cesare Pugni followed Perrot and Grisi to Russia, and remained in the imperial capital even after Grisi's departure in 1853 and Perrot's departure in 1858.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "type": "FOLLOWED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Cesare Pugni" target="Arthur Saint-Léon">
  <data key="d5">["COMPOSED_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Cesare Pugni composed for Arthur Saint-Léon.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Pugni went on the compose for Perrot's successors Arthur Saint-Léon and Marius Petipa, serving as the Imperial Theatre's official composer of ballet music until his death in 1870.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "type": "COMPOSED_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Cesare Pugni" target="Marius Petipa">
  <data key="d5">["COMPOSED_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Cesare Pugni composed for Marius Petipa.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Pugni went on the compose for Perrot's successors Arthur Saint-Léon and Marius Petipa, serving as the Imperial Theatre's official composer of ballet music until his death in 1870.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "type": "COMPOSED_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Jules Perrot" target="London">
  <data key="d5">["DEPARTED_FROM"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Jules Perrot departed London in 1850.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In 1850 Perrot departed London for Russia, having accepted the position of \"Premier maître de ballet\" of the St. Petersburg Imperial Theatres at the behest of Carlotta Grisi, who was engaged as \"Prima ballerina\".", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "type": "DEPARTED_FROM"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f</data>
</edge>
