<edge source="ballet music" target="Jules Perrot">
  <data key="d5">["COMPOSED_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The majority of Cesare Pugni's ballet music was composed for the works of Jules Perrot.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The majority of his ballet music was composed for the works of the ballet master Jules Perrot, who mounted nearly every one of his ballets to scores by Pugni.", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "type": "COMPOSED_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Carlotta Grisi" target="Prima ballerina">
  <data key="d5">["HAS_ROLE"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Carlotta Grisi was engaged as 'Prima ballerina'.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In 1850 Perrot departed London for Russia, having accepted the position of \"Premier maître de ballet\" of the St. Petersburg Imperial Theatres at the behest of Carlotta Grisi, who was engaged as \"Prima ballerina\".", "chunk_id": "b78dcabed6812ef8", "doc_id": "hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f", "type": "HAS_ROLE"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_031cfe5a8b4da13f</data>
</edge>
