<edge source="Florence and the Machine" target="Wish That You Were Here">
  <data key="d5">["PERFORMED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The song "Wish That You Were Here" is performed by the band Florence and the Machine.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"Wish That You Were Here\" is a song by the English indie rock band Florence and the Machine, written by Florence Welch, Andrew Wyatt, and Emilie Haynie, and was released on Island Records on 26 August 2016.", "chunk_id": "1e3c115665e783ed", "doc_id": "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8", "type": "PERFORMED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Florence and the Machine" target="Lungs">
  <data key="d5">["PRODUCED", "INTRODUCED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Florence and the Machine released the debut studio album Lungs.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Lungs is the debut studio album by English indie rock band Florence and the Machine, released on 3 July 2009 on Island Records.", "chunk_id": "2055480b7468cc45", "doc_id": "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f", "type": "PRODUCED"}, {"text": "The music on \"Lungs\" established Florence and the Machine as an internationally successful rock act, and also featured the group's successful mix of string arrangements centered around Welch's vocal prowess.", "chunk_id": "2055480b7468cc45", "doc_id": "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f", "type": "INTRODUCED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Florence and the Machine" target="London">
  <data key="d5">["FORMED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The band Florence and the Machine was formed in London.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Florence and the Machine (stylised as Florence + the Machine) are an English indie rock band that formed in London in 2007, consisting of lead singer Florence Welch, keyboardist Isabella Summers, and a collaboration of other artists.", "chunk_id": "a0e37e5744f28418", "doc_id": "hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e", "type": "FORMED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Florence and the Machine" target="BBC">
  <data key="d5">["PROMOTED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The BBC promoted Florence and the Machine.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The band's music received praise across the media, especially from the BBC, which played a large part in their rise to prominence by promoting Florence and the Machine as part of \"BBC Introducing\".", "chunk_id": "a0e37e5744f28418", "doc_id": "hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e", "type": "PROMOTED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Florence and the Machine" target="BBC Introducing">
