<edge source="Florence and the Machine" target="Ceremonials Tour">
  <data key="d5">["PERFORMED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Florence and the Machine was the band that conducted the Ceremonials Tour.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The Ceremonials Tour was the second concert tour by English indie rock band Florence and the Machine.", "chunk_id": "4a9a4f6f83f32605", "doc_id": "hp_ef31a7b23736d77e", "type": "PERFORMED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ef31a7b23736d77e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Florence and the Machine" target="Coke Live Music Festival">
  <data key="d5">["PERFORMED_AT"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Florence and the Machine was announced to play at the Coke Live Music Festival.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "On 25 February 2013 it was announced that Florence and the Machine would be playing at the Coke Live Music Festival in Poland on 10 August 2013, and on 26 March 2013 it was announced that the band would be playing at Chime for Change's \"The Sound of Change Live\" concert at London's Twickenham Stadium alongside Beyoncé, Ellie Goulding and Haim, amongst others.", "chunk_id": "4a9a4f6f83f32605", "doc_id": "hp_ef31a7b23736d77e", "type": "PERFORMED_AT"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ef31a7b23736d77e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Florence and the Machine" target="The Sound of Change Live">
  <data key="d5">["PERFORMED_AT"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Florence and the Machine was announced to play at 'The Sound of Change Live' concert.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "On 25 February 2013 it was announced that Florence and the Machine would be playing at the Coke Live Music Festival in Poland on 10 August 2013, and on 26 March 2013 it was announced that the band would be playing at Chime for Change's \"The Sound of Change Live\" concert at London's Twickenham Stadium alongside Beyoncé, Ellie Goulding and Haim, amongst others.", "chunk_id": "4a9a4f6f83f32605", "doc_id": "hp_ef31a7b23736d77e", "type": "PERFORMED_AT"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ef31a7b23736d77e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Florence Welch" target="No Light, No Light">
  <data key="d5">["WROTE"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Florence Welch co-wrote the song No Light, No Light.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The song was written by band members Florence Welch and Isabella Summers while the production was handled by Paul Epworth.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f", "type": "WROTE"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Florence Welch" target="Wish That You Were Here">
  <data key="d5">["WRITTEN_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Florence Welch co-wrote the song "Wish That You Were Here".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"Wish That You Were Here\" is a song by the English indie rock band Florence and the Machine, written by Florence Welch, Andrew Wyatt, and Emilie Haynie, and was released on Island Records on 26 August 2016.", "chunk_id": "1e3c115665e783ed", "doc_id": "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8", "type": "WRITTEN_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Florence Welch" target="Tim Burton">
  <data key="d5">["EXPRESSED_INTEREST_IN_COLLABORATING_WITH"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Florence Welch had expressed interest in collaborating with Tim Burton.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Welch — a long-time fan of Burton's work — had expressed interest in collaborating with him long before the recording of \"Wish That You Were Here\" as they shared similar artistic themes.", "chunk_id": "1e3c115665e783ed", "doc_id": "hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8", "type": "EXPRESSED_INTEREST_IN_COLLABORATING_WITH"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_0f7ce516b52f11b8</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Florence Welch" target="Sweet Nothing">
  <data key="d5">["VOCALS_ON", "ACCEPTED_INVITATION_TO_RECORD"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Florence Welch provided vocals for the song "Sweet Nothing".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It features vocals from Florence and the Machine singer Florence Welch.", "chunk_id": "95980d0e5191cb2e", "doc_id": "hp_15126f7df8c067b8", "type": "VOCALS_ON"}, {"text": "Welch accepted his invitation and the two recorded \"Sweet Nothing\".", "chunk_id": "95980d0e5191cb2e", "doc_id": "hp_15126f7df8c067b8", "type": "ACCEPTED_INVITATION_TO_RECORD"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_15126f7df8c067b8</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Florence Welch" target="Florence and the Machine">
  <data key="d5">["SINGER_IN", "VOCALIST_OF", "MEMBER_OF", "LEAD_SINGER_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Florence Welch is the singer for the band Florence and the Machine.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It features vocals from Florence and the Machine singer Florence Welch.", "chunk_id": "95980d0e5191cb2e", "doc_id": "hp_15126f7df8c067b8", "type": "SINGER_IN"}, {"text": "Florence Leontine Mary Welch (born 28 August 1986) is an English musician, singer and songwriter, best known as the vocalist of indie rock band Florence and the Machine.", "chunk_id": "0238c6f4d8a2d243", "doc_id": "hp_281a1709942e2d2a", "type": "VOCALIST_OF"}, {"text": "Florence and the Machine (stylised as Florence + the Machine) are an English indie rock band that formed in London in 2007, consisting of lead singer Florence Welch, keyboardist Isabella Summers, and a collaboration of other artists.", "chunk_id": "a0e37e5744f28418", "doc_id": "hp_6d4a91fc9052bf4e", "type": "MEMBER_OF"}, {"text": "The tour included performances at Music festivals because it is lead singer Florence Welch's favourite way to perform live.", "chunk_id": "4a9a4f6f83f32605", "doc_id": "hp_ef31a7b23736d77e", "type": "LEAD_SINGER_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_15126f7df8c067b8</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Florence Welch" target="Lungs">
  <data key="d5">["WORKED_ON"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Florence Welch experimented with and honed the album's sound.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Frontwoman Florence Welch experimented with and honed the album's sound with bandmate Isabella Summers, while also collaborating with five record producers including James Ford, Paul Epworth, Steve Mackey.", "chunk_id": "2055480b7468cc45", "doc_id": "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f", "type": "WORKED_ON"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Florence Welch" target="What the Water Gave Me (song)">
  <data key="d5">["WROTE"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Florence Welch co-wrote the song "What the Water Gave Me".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The song was written by lead singer Florence Welch and Francis \"Eg\" White, and produced by Paul Epworth.", "chunk_id": "4a33b3fb6c1ee1fa", "doc_id": "hp_7804b34667739a36", "type": "WROTE"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_7804b34667739a36</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Florence Welch" target="Frida Kahlo">
  <data key="d5">["NAMED_AFTER"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Florence Welch named the song after a painting by Frida Kahlo.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Welch decided to name the song \"What the Water Gave Me\" after seeing a Frida Kahlo painting of the same name.", "chunk_id": "4a33b3fb6c1ee1fa", "doc_id": "hp_7804b34667739a36", "type": "NAMED_AFTER"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_7804b34667739a36</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Isabella Summers" target="No Light, No Light">
  <data key="d5">["WROTE"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Isabella Summers co-wrote the song No Light, No Light.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The song was written by band members Florence Welch and Isabella Summers while the production was handled by Paul Epworth.", "chunk_id": "eacf230036b80618", "doc_id": "hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f", "type": "WROTE"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_099c2da4a99b4f6f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Isabella Summers" target="Lungs">
  <data key="d5">["WORKED_ON"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Isabella Summers helped hone the album's sound.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Frontwoman Florence Welch experimented with and honed the album's sound with bandmate Isabella Summers, while also collaborating with five record producers including James Ford, Paul Epworth, Steve Mackey.", "chunk_id": "2055480b7468cc45", "doc_id": "hp_4dcfe55bb1e0d25f", "type": "WORKED_ON"}]</data>
