<edge source="John Cage" target="Sonatas and Interludes">
  <data key="d5">["COMPOSED", "COMPOSED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">John Cage composed Sonatas and Interludes.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Sonatas and Interludes is a collection of twenty pieces for prepared piano by American avant-garde composer John Cage (1912–1992).", "chunk_id": "46e2753873dd1884", "doc_id": "hp_abe4b15111caba47", "type": "COMPOSED"}, {"text": "In the liner notes for the very first recording of his most highly acclaimed work for prepared piano, \"Sonatas and Interludes\", Cage wrote: \"Composing for the prepared piano is not a criticism of the instrument.", "chunk_id": "b7f8e7da447a5f1c", "doc_id": "hp_e9f272e0c789745f", "type": "COMPOSED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_abe4b15111caba47</data>
</edge>
<edge source="John Cage" target="Indian philosophy">
  <data key="d5">["INFLUENCED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">John Cage was influenced by Indian philosophy.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It was composed in 1946–48, shortly after Cage's introduction to Indian philosophy and the teachings of art historian Ananda K. Coomaraswamy, both of which became major influences on the composer's later work.", "chunk_id": "46e2753873dd1884", "doc_id": "hp_abe4b15111caba47", "type": "INFLUENCED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_abe4b15111caba47</data>
</edge>
<edge source="John Cage" target="Ananda K. Coomaraswamy">
  <data key="d5">["INFLUENCED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">John Cage was influenced by the teachings of Ananda K. Coomaraswamy.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It was composed in 1946–48, shortly after Cage's introduction to Indian philosophy and the teachings of art historian Ananda K. Coomaraswamy, both of which became major influences on the composer's later work.", "chunk_id": "46e2753873dd1884", "doc_id": "hp_abe4b15111caba47", "type": "INFLUENCED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_abe4b15111caba47</data>
</edge>
<edge source="John Cage" target="prepared piano">
  <data key="d5">["COMPOSED_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">John Cage composed pieces for the prepared piano.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "American avant-garde composer John Cage (1912–1992) started composing pieces for solo prepared piano around 1938–40.", "chunk_id": "b7f8e7da447a5f1c", "doc_id": "hp_e9f272e0c789745f", "type": "COMPOSED_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e9f272e0c789745f</data>
</edge>
