</edge>
<edge source="John Cage" target="Merce Cunningham">
  <data key="d5">["COLLABORATED_WITH"]</data>
  <data key="d6">John Cage created early works for prepared piano to accompany dances by Merce Cunningham.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The majority of early works for this instrument were created to accompany dances by Cage's various collaborators, most frequently Merce Cunningham.", "chunk_id": "b7f8e7da447a5f1c", "doc_id": "hp_e9f272e0c789745f", "type": "COLLABORATED_WITH"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e9f272e0c789745f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="John Cage" target="Henry Cowell">
  <data key="d5">["CITED_PREDECESSOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">John Cage cited Henry Cowell as a predecessor in response to criticisms of prepared piano.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In response to frequent criticisms of prepared piano, Cage cited numerous predecessors (such as Henry Cowell).", "chunk_id": "b7f8e7da447a5f1c", "doc_id": "hp_e9f272e0c789745f", "type": "CITED_PREDECESSOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e9f272e0c789745f</data>
</edge>
