<edge source="Raj Kapoor" target="Shree 420">
  <data key="d5">["DIRECTED", "PRODUCED", "STARRED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Raj Kapoor directed the film Shree 420.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Shree 420 (\"Hindi\" श्री ४२०, translation: \"Sir 420\", also transliterated as Shri 420) is a 1955 Hindi film, directed and produced by Raj Kapoor, written by Khwaja Ahmad Abbas, and starring Raj Kapoor and Nargis.", "chunk_id": "0a8e3d3f676d8b89", "doc_id": "hp_8c200a803fef76a7", "type": "DIRECTED"}, {"text": "Shree 420 (\"Hindi\" श्री ४२०, translation: \"Sir 420\", also transliterated as Shri 420) is a 1955 Hindi film, directed and produced by Raj Kapoor, written by Khwaja Ahmad Abbas, and starring Raj Kapoor and Nargis.", "chunk_id": "0a8e3d3f676d8b89", "doc_id": "hp_8c200a803fef76a7", "type": "PRODUCED"}, {"text": "Shree 420 (\"Hindi\" श्री ४२०, translation: \"Sir 420\", also transliterated as Shri 420) is a 1955 Hindi film, directed and produced by Raj Kapoor, written by Khwaja Ahmad Abbas, and starring Raj Kapoor and Nargis.", "chunk_id": "0a8e3d3f676d8b89", "doc_id": "hp_8c200a803fef76a7", "type": "STARRED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_8c200a803fef76a7</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Raj Kapoor" target="Bombay">
  <data key="d5">["MOVED_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Raj Kapoor's character in Shree 420 moves to Bombay with dreams of success.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The film centers on Raj, a poor but educated orphan who comes to Bombay with dreams of success.", "chunk_id": "0a8e3d3f676d8b89", "doc_id": "hp_8c200a803fef76a7", "type": "MOVED_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_8c200a803fef76a7</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Raj Kapoor" target="Awaara">
  <data key="d5">["APPEARED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Raj Kapoor's character in Shree 420 is similar to his character in the 1951 film Awaara.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Kapoor's character is influenced by Charlie Chaplin's \"little tramp\", much like Kapoor's character in his 1951 \"Awaara\".", "chunk_id": "0a8e3d3f676d8b89", "doc_id": "hp_8c200a803fef76a7", "type": "APPEARED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_8c200a803fef76a7</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Raj Kapoor" target="Kal Aaj Aur Kal">
  <data key="d5">["PRODUCED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Raj Kapoor produced the film Kal Aaj Aur Kal.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Kal Aaj Aur Kal (Yesterday, Today and Tomorrow) is a 1971 Hindi film produced by Raj Kapoor and directed by his son Randhir Kapoor.", "chunk_id": "16a91e591a40c438", "doc_id": "hp_b3f0efe2307464b8", "type": "PRODUCED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_b3f0efe2307464b8</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Raj Kapoor" target="Kapoor family">
  <data key="d5">["MEMBER_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Raj Kapoor is a member of the Kapoor family.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The film's USP is the appearance of three generations of the famous Kapoor family starring Prithviraj Kapoor, his son Raj Kapoor, Raj Kapoor's son Randhir Kapoor (in his acting debut) and Randhir's real-life wife-to-be Babita.", "chunk_id": "16a91e591a40c438", "doc_id": "hp_b3f0efe2307464b8", "type": "MEMBER_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_b3f0efe2307464b8</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Raj Kapoor" target="Aag (1948 film)">
  <data key="d5">["PRODUCED", "DIRECTED", "STARS_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Raj Kapoor produced the 1948 film Aag.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Aag (Hindi: आग ; English: \"Fire\" ) is a 1948 Bollywood film which is produced, directed by and stars Raj Kapoor.", "chunk_id": "4df4b5295e67f801", "doc_id": "hp_b8f974e5ce544d7e", "type": "PRODUCED"}, {"text": "Aag (Hindi: आग ; English: \"Fire\" ) is a 1948 Bollywood film which is produced, directed by and stars Raj Kapoor.", "chunk_id": "4df4b5295e67f801", "doc_id": "hp_b8f974e5ce544d7e", "type": "DIRECTED"}, {"text": "Aag (Hindi: आग ; English: \"Fire\" ) is a 1948 Bollywood film which is produced, directed by and stars Raj Kapoor.", "chunk_id": "4df4b5295e67f801", "doc_id": "hp_b8f974e5ce544d7e", "type": "STARS_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_b8f974e5ce544d7e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Raj Kapoor" target="Nargis">
  <data key="d5">["APPEARED_TOGETHER_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Raj Kapoor and Nargis appeared together for the first time in the film Aag.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "This was the first film in which Raj Kapoor and Nargis appeared together.", "chunk_id": "4df4b5295e67f801", "doc_id": "hp_b8f974e5ce544d7e", "type": "APPEARED_TOGETHER_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_b8f974e5ce544d7e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Rajiv Kapoor" target="Ram Teri Ganga Maili">
  <data key="d5">["ACTED_IN", "STARRED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Rajiv Kapoor co-starred with Mandakini in "Ram Teri Ganga Maili".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Then she was selected as the second lead in Raj Kapoor's \"Ram Teri Ganga Maili\" (1985) co-starring Rajiv Kapoor &amp; Mandakini.", "chunk_id": "1621f78ea00aa2b4", "doc_id": "hp_140ab3de808ede2a", "type": "ACTED_IN"}, {"text": "The movie stars Mandakini and Rajiv Kapoor, son of Raj Kapoor.", "chunk_id": "9587b01bee29deed", "doc_id": "hp_153a2c475bfeef6e", "type": "STARRED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_140ab3de808ede2a</data>
</edge>
