  <data key="d6">Fran Healy is a member of the band Travis.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Travis is an alternative rock band from Glasgow, Scotland, comprising Fran Healy (lead vocals, guitar, piano, banjo), Dougie Payne (bass guitar, backing vocals), Andy Dunlop (lead guitar, banjo, keyboards, backing vocals) and Neil Primrose (drums, percussion).", "chunk_id": "8043cae2ef7b7fae", "doc_id": "hp_5e36dcc4c1a872ca", "type": "MEMBER_OF"}, {"text": "BNQT (pronounced banquet ( ) is an indie super-group featuring Fran Healy (Travis), Alex Kapranos (Franz Ferdinand), Eric Pulido (Midlake), Ben Bridwell (Band of Horses) and Jason Lytle (Grandaddy), backed by other members of Midlake; Jesse Chandler, Joey McClellan and McKenzie Smith.", "chunk_id": "161799124afdf1e1", "doc_id": "hp_6a39ea6d8c8a05f8", "type": "ASSOCIATED_WITH"}, {"text": "Volume 1 is the debut studio album by indie super-group BNQT, lead by Eric Pulido (Midlake) with Ben Bridwell (Band of Horses), Alex Kapranos (Franz Ferdinand), Fran Healy (Travis) and Jason Lytle (Grandaddy), backed by the other members of Midlake.", "chunk_id": "f0e4892b3b37bba4", "doc_id": "hp_7cc233817d9e07c7", "type": "PART_OF"}, {"text": "He is the lead singer and main songwriter of the band Travis, having written nearly all of the songs on their first six studio albums, with the 8th being more of a co-written work.", "chunk_id": "b495da896345a856", "doc_id": "hp_8e3f3120ae8497a2", "type": "MEMBER_OF"}, {"text": "Wreckorder is the debut solo album from Travis frontman, Fran Healy.", "chunk_id": "02e94c52db8f837e", "doc_id": "hp_d73d23b34d64cf3a", "type": "MEMBER_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_5e36dcc4c1a872ca</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fran Healy" target="BNQT">
  <data key="d5">["MEMBER_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Fran Healy is a member of the indie super-group BNQT.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "BNQT (pronounced banquet ( ) is an indie super-group featuring Fran Healy (Travis), Alex Kapranos (Franz Ferdinand), Eric Pulido (Midlake), Ben Bridwell (Band of Horses) and Jason Lytle (Grandaddy), backed by other members of Midlake; Jesse Chandler, Joey McClellan and McKenzie Smith.", "chunk_id": "161799124afdf1e1", "doc_id": "hp_6a39ea6d8c8a05f8", "type": "MEMBER_OF"}]</data>
