<edge source="Dale Minami" target="Fred Korematsu">
  <data key="d5">["REPRESENTED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Dale Minami headed the legal team that overturned the conviction of Fred Korematsu.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Dale Minami (born October 13, 1946) is a San Francisco-based lawyer best known for heading the legal team that overturned the conviction of Fred Korematsu, whose defiance of the World War II Japanese American internment order lead to Korematsu v. United States, one of the most controversial United States Supreme Court decisions of the 20th century.", "chunk_id": "63f34134976a8d32", "doc_id": "hp_18a6d077ab278415", "type": "REPRESENTED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_18a6d077ab278415</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dale Minami" target="San Francisco">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Dale Minami is based in San Francisco.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Dale Minami (born October 13, 1946) is a San Francisco-based lawyer best known for heading the legal team that overturned the conviction of Fred Korematsu, whose defiance of the World War II Japanese American internment order lead to Korematsu v. United States, one of the most controversial United States Supreme Court decisions of the 20th century.", "chunk_id": "63f34134976a8d32", "doc_id": "hp_18a6d077ab278415", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_18a6d077ab278415</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dale Minami" target="UC Berkeley School of Law">
  <data key="d5">["ALUMNUS_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Dale Minami is an alumnus of UC Berkeley School of Law.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The law school has produced leaders in law, government, and society, including Chief Justice of the United States Earl Warren, Secretary of State of the United States Dean Rusk, Attorney General of the United States Edwin Meese, United States Secretary of the Treasury and Chairman of the Federal Reserve G. William Miller, Solicitor General of the United States Theodore Olson, and lead litigator of the \"Korematsu v. United States\" civil rights case, Dale Minami.", "chunk_id": "0ba5a45b986c419a", "doc_id": "hp_5dddd5f952802e7e", "type": "ALUMNUS_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_5dddd5f952802e7e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dale Minami" target="Korematsu v. United States">
  <data key="d5">["LITIGATED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Dale Minami was the lead litigator for the "Korematsu v. United States" civil rights case.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The law school has produced leaders in law, government, and society, including Chief Justice of the United States Earl Warren, Secretary of State of the United States Dean Rusk, Attorney General of the United States Edwin Meese, United States Secretary of the Treasury and Chairman of the Federal Reserve G. William Miller, Solicitor General of the United States Theodore Olson, and lead litigator of the \"Korematsu v. United States\" civil rights case, Dale Minami.", "chunk_id": "0ba5a45b986c419a", "doc_id": "hp_5dddd5f952802e7e", "type": "LITIGATED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_5dddd5f952802e7e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Japanese American internment order" target="World War II">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Japanese American internment order was related to World War II.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Dale Minami (born October 13, 1946) is a San Francisco-based lawyer best known for heading the legal team that overturned the conviction of Fred Korematsu, whose defiance of the World War II Japanese American internment order lead to Korematsu v. United States, one of the most controversial United States Supreme Court decisions of the 20th century.", "chunk_id": "63f34134976a8d32", "doc_id": "hp_18a6d077ab278415", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_18a6d077ab278415</data>
</edge>
<edge source="United States Supreme Court" target="fighting words doctrine">
  <data key="d5">["INTRODUCED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The United States Supreme Court articulated the fighting words doctrine in this case.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Chaplinsky v. New Hampshire, 315 U.S. 568 (1942) , is a United States Supreme Court case in which the Court articulated the fighting words doctrine, a limitation of the First Amendment's guarantee of freedom of speech.", "chunk_id": "e32ee493ed809ece", "doc_id": "hp_3811e4729d75dd3c", "type": "INTRODUCED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_3811e4729d75dd3c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Thomas James" target="Raymond James Financial">
  <data key="d5">["WORKS_AT"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Thomas James is the chairman of Raymond James Financial.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Thomas James (born 1942/43) is an American billionaire businessman, the chairman of Raymond James Financial, founded by his father Robert James, for 30 years.", "chunk_id": "b6874d56d2fdd648", "doc_id": "hp_18fbcd7469354b78", "type": "WORKS_AT"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_18fbcd7469354b78</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Thomas James" target="Robert James">
  <data key="d5">["FATHER_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Robert James is the father of Thomas James.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Thomas James (born 1942/43) is an American billionaire businessman, the chairman of Raymond James Financial, founded by his father Robert James, for 30 years.", "chunk_id": "b6874d56d2fdd648", "doc_id": "hp_18fbcd7469354b78", "type": "FATHER_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_18fbcd7469354b78</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Laurus novocanariensis" target="Laurus">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Laurus novocanariensis belongs to the Laurus genus.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "belonging to \"Laurus\" genus of evergreen trees belonging to the Laurel family, Lauraceae.", "chunk_id": "1680d6be464bcfe6", "doc_id": "hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Laurus novocanariensis" target="Canary islands">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Laurus novocanariensis is native to the Canary islands.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It is native of rich soils in the cloud zone of always moist spots in subtropical climate with a high air-humidity, on the Canary and Madeira islands.", "chunk_id": "1680d6be464bcfe6", "doc_id": "hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Laurus novocanariensis" target="Madeira islands">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Laurus novocanariensis is native to the Madeira islands.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It is native of rich soils in the cloud zone of always moist spots in subtropical climate with a high air-humidity, on the Canary and Madeira islands.", "chunk_id": "1680d6be464bcfe6", "doc_id": "hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_19572b7a0a3ebc1a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Michael Jackson's This Is It (album)" target="Michael Jackson's This Is It">
  <data key="d5">["COINCIDES_WITH"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The release of the album "This Is It" coincided with the theatrical release of the concert film "Michael Jackson's This Is It".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"This Is It\" was released to coincide with the theatrical release of \"Michael Jackson's This Is It\", a concert film documenting Michael Jackson's rehearsals for the This Is It concert series at London's O2 Arena.", "chunk_id": "f1142eb95496f6b8", "doc_id": "hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6", "type": "COINCIDES_WITH"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_19aa948e90d5a7f6</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Michael Jackson" target="Michael Jackson's This Is It (album)">
