  <data key="d5">["OCCURRED_ON"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Battle of Jeokjinpo occurred on 8 May 1592.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Battle of Jeokjinpo was fought on 8 May 1592.", "chunk_id": "97d42ce68ff1435a", "doc_id": "hp_1de0ceb21cf100b1", "type": "OCCURRED_ON"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_1de0ceb21cf100b1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Battle of Happo" target="Joseon naval campaigns of 1592">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Battle of Happo was one of the Joseon naval campaigns of 1592.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The Battle of Happo was a naval engagement on May 7, 1592, one of the three Joseon naval campaigns of 1592 conducted by Korean admiral Yi Sun-sin during Japanese invasions of Korea (1592-1598) against the Japanese forces of Toyotomi Hideyoshi.", "chunk_id": "bf39df43067a80b1", "doc_id": "hp_3a9829e8fd3b32c6", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_3a9829e8fd3b32c6</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Yi Sun-sin" target="Japanese ships">
  <data key="d5">["PURSUED", "DESTROYED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Yi Sun-sin and his fleet pursued the Japanese ships.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Admiral Yi once again ordered his fleet to pursue the Japanese in the direction of Jinhae.", "chunk_id": "97d42ce68ff1435a", "doc_id": "hp_1de0ceb21cf100b1", "type": "PURSUED"}, {"text": "Korean admiral Yi Sun-sin destroyed at least 47 Japanese ships, captured 12.", "chunk_id": "4d06ff352195041a", "doc_id": "hp_4e9436b9b6a97ad9", "type": "DESTROYED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_1de0ceb21cf100b1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Yi Sun-sin" target="Joseon naval campaigns of 1592">
  <data key="d5">["CONDUCTED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Yi Sun-sin conducted the Joseon naval campaigns of 1592.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The Joseon naval campaigns of 1592 was naval campaigns conducted by Korean admiral Yi Sun-sin during Japanese invasions of Korea (1592-1598) against the Japanese forces of Toyotomi Hideyoshi.", "chunk_id": "68610c0d374404f2", "doc_id": "hp_3358c15c20048369", "type": "CONDUCTED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_3358c15c20048369</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Yi Sun-sin" target="Eulji Mundeok">
  <data key="d5">["ON_PAR_WITH"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Yi Sun-sin is considered on par with, or surpassing, Eulji Mundeok in Korean History.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "These campaigns made Yi a legendary figure in Korean History on par, if not surpassing the great general Eulji Mundeok.", "chunk_id": "68610c0d374404f2", "doc_id": "hp_3358c15c20048369", "type": "ON_PAR_WITH"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_3358c15c20048369</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Yi Sun-sin" target="Korean History">
  <data key="d5">["BECAME_LEGENDARY_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Yi Sun-sin became a legendary figure in Korean History due to his campaigns.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "These campaigns made Yi a legendary figure in Korean History.", "chunk_id": "bf39df43067a80b1", "doc_id": "hp_3a9829e8fd3b32c6", "type": "BECAME_LEGENDARY_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_3a9829e8fd3b32c6</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Yi Sun-sin" target="Battle of Hansan Island">
  <data key="d5">["COMMANDED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Admiral Yi Sun-sin commanded forces in the Battle of Hansan Island.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Korean admiral Yi Sun-sin destroyed at least 47 Japanese ships, captured 12.", "chunk_id": "4d06ff352195041a", "doc_id": "hp_4e9436b9b6a97ad9", "type": "COMMANDED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_4e9436b9b6a97ad9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Yi Sun-sin" target="Jeolla Province">
  <data key="d5">["COMMANDED_FLEET_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Yi Sun-sin took command of Jeolla Province's Eastern Fleet.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "After considerable accomplishments on the northern frontier, he was promoted to admiral in 1592 and sent to the southern coast of Gyeongsang Province to command the province's Western Fleet, along with Yi Sun-sin, who became admiral before Won and took command of Jeolla Province's Eastern Fleet.", "chunk_id": "a6aad735bf59fe92", "doc_id": "hp_75d8594536b8ad92", "type": "COMMANDED_FLEET_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_75d8594536b8ad92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Yi Sun-sin" target="Joseon Dynasty">
  <data key="d5">["LIVED_DURING"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Admiral Yi Sun-sin lived during the Joseon Dynasty.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Nanjung Ilgi or War Diary of Yi Sun-sin is the personal diary of Admiral Yi Sun-sin (Hangul: 이순신, Hanja: 李舜臣), a Korean naval commander who lived during the Joseon Dynasty.", "chunk_id": "99c215cb87242ef5", "doc_id": "hp_d01934819d3bc4ad", "type": "LIVED_DURING"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_d01934819d3bc4ad</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Korean forces" target="Japanese ships">
  <data key="d5">["ENGAGED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Korean forces caught up with the Japanese ships at Jeokjinpo.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The Korean forces caught up with the Japanese ships at Jeokjinpo, but the Japanese officers and crew abandoned their ships and fled into the mountains before the Koreans could fire upon them.", "chunk_id": "97d42ce68ff1435a", "doc_id": "hp_1de0ceb21cf100b1", "type": "ENGAGED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_1de0ceb21cf100b1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Korean forces" target="Japanese warships">
  <data key="d5">["SUNK"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Koreans easily sunk the 13 abandoned Japanese warships.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The Koreans easily sunk the 13 abandoned Japanese warships.", "chunk_id": "97d42ce68ff1435a", "doc_id": "hp_1de0ceb21cf100b1", "type": "SUNK"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_1de0ceb21cf100b1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Electroconvulsive therapy" target="mental disorders">
  <data key="d5">["USED_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Electroconvulsive therapy is used to provide relief from mental disorders.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Electroconvulsive therapy (ECT), formerly known as electroshock therapy, and often referred to as shock treatment, is a psychiatric treatment in which seizures are electrically induced in patients to provide relief from mental disorders.", "chunk_id": "3217d56af62a1f79", "doc_id": "hp_1dfa7f266b4cbbfd", "type": "USED_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_1dfa7f266b4cbbfd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Electroconvulsive therapy" target="major depressive disorder">
  <data key="d5">["USED_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Electroconvulsive therapy is used as a last line of intervention for major depressive disorder.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "ECT is often used with informed consent as a last line of intervention for major depressive disorder, mania, and catatonia.", "chunk_id": "3217d56af62a1f79", "doc_id": "hp_1dfa7f266b4cbbfd", "type": "USED_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_1dfa7f266b4cbbfd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Electroconvulsive therapy" target="mania">
  <data key="d5">["USED_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Electroconvulsive therapy is used as a last line of intervention for mania.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "ECT is often used with informed consent as a last line of intervention for major depressive disorder, mania, and catatonia.", "chunk_id": "3217d56af62a1f79", "doc_id": "hp_1dfa7f266b4cbbfd", "type": "USED_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_1dfa7f266b4cbbfd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Electroconvulsive therapy" target="catatonia">
  <data key="d5">["USED_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Electroconvulsive therapy is used as a last line of intervention for catatonia.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "ECT is often used with informed consent as a last line of intervention for major depressive disorder, mania, and catatonia.", "chunk_id": "3217d56af62a1f79", "doc_id": "hp_1dfa7f266b4cbbfd", "type": "USED_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_1dfa7f266b4cbbfd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="electroshock therapy" target="Electroconvulsive therapy">
  <data key="d5">["FORMERLY_KNOWN_AS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Electroconvulsive therapy was formerly known as electroshock therapy.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Electroconvulsive therapy (ECT), formerly known as electroshock therapy, and often referred to as shock treatment, is a psychiatric treatment in which seizures are electrically induced in patients to provide relief from mental disorders.", "chunk_id": "3217d56af62a1f79", "doc_id": "hp_1dfa7f266b4cbbfd", "type": "FORMERLY_KNOWN_AS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_1dfa7f266b4cbbfd</data>
</edge>
