<edge source="Manon Lescaut" target="Mémoires et aventures d'un homme de qualité">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Manon Lescaut is the seventh and final volume of "Mémoires et aventures d'un homme de qualité".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Published in 1731, it is the seventh and final volume of \"Mémoires et aventures d'un homme de qualité\" (\"Memoirs and Adventures of a Man of Quality\").", "chunk_id": "1a052a3777da7f37", "doc_id": "hp_1e281004ae376688", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_1e281004ae376688</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Manon Lescaut" target="The Lovers of Manon Lescaut">
  <data key="d5">["BASED_ON"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The film 'The Lovers of Manon Lescaut' is based on the novel 'Manon Lescaut'.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It is based on the 1731 novel \"Manon Lescaut\" by Antoine François Prévost, which has been made into films on a number of occasions.", "chunk_id": "bef25c1257301257", "doc_id": "hp_921687d29866a375", "type": "BASED_ON"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_921687d29866a375</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Manon Lescaut" target="Boulevard Solitude">
  <data key="d5">["IS_RETOLD_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Manon Lescaut story is retold in Boulevard Solitude.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Boulevard Solitude is a \"Lyrisches Drama \" (lyric drama) or opera in one act by Hans Werner Henze to a German libretto by Grete Weil after the play by Walter Jockisch, in its turn a modern retelling of François Prévost's \"Manon Lescaut\".", "chunk_id": "8dbccb5758e54e3f", "doc_id": "hp_ce10cea1030952d1", "type": "IS_RETOLD_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ce10cea1030952d1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Abbé Prévost" target="Manon Lescaut">
  <data key="d5">["REVISED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Abbé Prévost toned down scandalous details and injected more moralizing disclaimers in a subsequent edition of Manon Lescaut.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In a subsequent 1753 edition, the Abbé Prévost toned down some scandalous details and injected more moralizing disclaimers.", "chunk_id": "1a052a3777da7f37", "doc_id": "hp_1e281004ae376688", "type": "REVISED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_1e281004ae376688</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Abbé Prévost" target="Manon Lescaut (novel)">
