<edge source="Kele Okereke" target="The Boxer">
  <data key="d5">["RELEASED", "RELEASED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Kele Okereke released his debut solo album, The Boxer.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The Boxer is the debut solo album by Kele Okereke, the lead singer of British indie rock band Bloc Party.", "chunk_id": "bb2b762aba15f55a", "doc_id": "hp_24b106283a2f2b9f", "type": "RELEASED"}, {"text": "The Hunter is the first EP (and follow up to the 2010 solo album \"The Boxer\") by Kele Okereke (under the professional name Kele), lead singer and rhythm guitarist of the British rock band Bloc Party.", "chunk_id": "145e5d0c1408e198", "doc_id": "hp_e5470b4e6fa8bc35", "type": "RELEASED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_24b106283a2f2b9f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Kele Okereke" target="Bloc Party">
  <data key="d5">["MEMBER_OF", "MEMBER_OF", "FOUNDED", "MEMBER_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Kele Okereke is the lead singer of the band Bloc Party.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The Boxer is the debut solo album by Kele Okereke, the lead singer of British indie rock band Bloc Party.", "chunk_id": "bb2b762aba15f55a", "doc_id": "hp_24b106283a2f2b9f", "type": "MEMBER_OF"}, {"text": "Bloc Party are an English indie rock band, currently composed of Kele Okereke (lead vocals, rhythm guitar, keyboards, sampler), Russell Lissack (lead guitar, keyboards), Justin Harris (bass guitar, keyboards, saxophones, backing vocals) and Louise Bartle (drums, percussion).", "chunk_id": "71ac561d76e09011", "doc_id": "hp_69c70a8b17b9692e", "type": "MEMBER_OF"}, {"text": "The band was formed at the 1999 Reading Festival by Okereke and Lissack.", "chunk_id": "71ac561d76e09011", "doc_id": "hp_69c70a8b17b9692e", "type": "FOUNDED"}, {"text": "The Hunter is the first EP (and follow up to the 2010 solo album \"The Boxer\") by Kele Okereke (under the professional name Kele), lead singer and rhythm guitarist of the British rock band Bloc Party.", "chunk_id": "145e5d0c1408e198", "doc_id": "hp_e5470b4e6fa8bc35", "type": "MEMBER_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_24b106283a2f2b9f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Kele Okereke" target="Kele">
  <data key="d5">["USES_PROFESSIONAL_NAME"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Kele Okereke released the album under the professional name of Kele.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Okereke released the album under the professional name of Kele on 21 June 2010.", "chunk_id": "bb2b762aba15f55a", "doc_id": "hp_24b106283a2f2b9f", "type": "USES_PROFESSIONAL_NAME"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_24b106283a2f2b9f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Bloc Party" target="electronica">
  <data key="d5">["INFLUENCED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Bloc Party's music retains elements of electronica.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Their brand of music, whilst rooted in rock, retains elements of other genres such as electronica and house music.", "chunk_id": "71ac561d76e09011", "doc_id": "hp_69c70a8b17b9692e", "type": "INFLUENCED_BY"}]</data>
