<edge source="Shigeko Kubota" target="New York City">
  <data key="d5">["LIVED_IN", "MOVED_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Shigeko Kubota mostly lived in New York City.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Shigeko Kubota (久保田 成子 , Kubota Shigeko ) (2 August 1937 – 23 July 2015) was a Japanese video artist, sculptor and avant-garde performance artist, who mostly lived in New York City.", "chunk_id": "bb303342f684188a", "doc_id": "hp_25e106b688a6f938", "type": "LIVED_IN"}, {"text": "She was a key member and influence on Fluxus, the international group of avant-garde artists centered on George Maciunas, having been involved with the group since witnessing John Cage perform in Tokyo in 1962 and subsequently moving to New York in 1964.", "chunk_id": "bb303342f684188a", "doc_id": "hp_25e106b688a6f938", "type": "MOVED_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_25e106b688a6f938</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shigeko Kubota" target="Sony Portapak">
  <data key="d5">["USED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Shigeko Kubota was one of the first artists to adopt the Sony Portapak.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "She was one of the first artists to adopt the portable video camera Sony Portapak in 1967.", "chunk_id": "bb303342f684188a", "doc_id": "hp_25e106b688a6f938", "type": "USED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_25e106b688a6f938</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shigeko Kubota" target="Fluxus">
  <data key="d5">["MEMBER_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Shigeko Kubota was a key member and influence on Fluxus.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "She was a key member and influence on Fluxus, the international group of avant-garde artists centered on George Maciunas, having been involved with the group since witnessing John Cage perform in Tokyo in 1962 and subsequently moving to New York in 1964.", "chunk_id": "bb303342f684188a", "doc_id": "hp_25e106b688a6f938", "type": "MEMBER_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_25e106b688a6f938</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shigeko Kubota" target="John Cage">
  <data key="d5">["WITNESSED_PERFORMANCE_OF", "ASSOCIATED_WITH"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Shigeko Kubota witnessed John Cage perform in Tokyo in 1962, which led to her involvement with Fluxus.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "She was a key member and influence on Fluxus, the international group of avant-garde artists centered on George Maciunas, having been involved with the group since witnessing John Cage perform in Tokyo in 1962 and subsequently moving to New York in 1964.", "chunk_id": "bb303342f684188a", "doc_id": "hp_25e106b688a6f938", "type": "WITNESSED_PERFORMANCE_OF"}, {"text": "She was closely associated with George Brecht, Jackson Mac Low, John Cage, Joe Jones, Nam June Paik, and Ay-O, other members of Fluxus.", "chunk_id": "bb303342f684188a", "doc_id": "hp_25e106b688a6f938", "type": "ASSOCIATED_WITH"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_25e106b688a6f938</data>
