<edge source="New York City Ballet" target="Le baiser de la fée">
  <data key="d5">["ASSOCIATED_WITH"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The New York City Ballet was associated with the revision of 'Le baiser de la fée'.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Le baiser de la fée (\"The Fairy's Kiss\") is a ballet in one act and four scenes composed by Igor Stravinsky in 1928 and revised in 1950 for George Balanchine and the New York City Ballet.", "chunk_id": "a78396980a135cb4", "doc_id": "hp_869cb734bf497707", "type": "ASSOCIATED_WITH"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_869cb734bf497707</data>
</edge>
<edge source="New York City Ballet" target="Ravel Festival">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Ravel Festival was an event for the New York City Ballet.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In G Major is a ballet made for New York City Ballet's Ravel Festival by ballet master Jerome Robbins to the composer's \"Piano Concerto in G Major\" (1928–31).", "chunk_id": "19fd24643eea1f76", "doc_id": "hp_c8a6c3f50e115d2a", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_c8a6c3f50e115d2a</data>
