<edge source="Liriodendron tulipifera" target="flowering period">
  <data key="d5">["HAS_PERIOD"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The flowering period for Liriodendron tulipifera begins in April in the southern USA and June at the northern limit of cultivation.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "April marks the start of the flowering period in the southern USA (except as noted below); trees at the northern limit of cultivation begin to flower in June.", "chunk_id": "976ede3d58522907", "doc_id": "hp_2c1beb2f73cca8d4", "type": "HAS_PERIOD"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_2c1beb2f73cca8d4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Liriodendron tulipifera" target="nectar">
  <data key="d5">["YIELDS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The flowers of the tulip tree yield large quantities of nectar.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The flowers are pale green or yellow (rarely white), with an orange band on the tepals; they yield large quantities of nectar.", "chunk_id": "976ede3d58522907", "doc_id": "hp_2c1beb2f73cca8d4", "type": "YIELDS"}]</data>
