<edge source="Gormond et Isembart" target="The Song of Roland">
  <data key="d5">["SIMILAR_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Gormond et Isembart is grouped with The Song of Roland as one of the three chansons de geste dating from before 1150.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Along with \"The Song of Roland\" and the \"Chanson de Guillaume\", it is one of the three \"chansons de geste\" whose composition incontestably dates from before 1150; it may be slightly younger than \"The Song of Roland\" and, according to one expert, may date from as early as 1068.", "chunk_id": "54cbfcfe8378cde7", "doc_id": "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75", "type": "SIMILAR_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_348f259ed8ae2d75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gormond et Isembart" target="Chanson de Guillaume">
  <data key="d5">["SIMILAR_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Gormond et Isembart is grouped with Chanson de Guillaume as one of the three chansons de geste dating from before 1150.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Along with \"The Song of Roland\" and the \"Chanson de Guillaume\", it is one of the three \"chansons de geste\" whose composition incontestably dates from before 1150; it may be slightly younger than \"The Song of Roland\" and, according to one expert, may date from as early as 1068.", "chunk_id": "54cbfcfe8378cde7", "doc_id": "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75", "type": "SIMILAR_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_348f259ed8ae2d75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gormond et Isembart" target="Geste de Doon de Mayence">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Gormond et Isembart is sometimes grouped with the Geste de Doon de Mayence.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The poem is sometimes grouped with the \"Geste de Doon de Mayence\" or \"rebellious vassal cycle\" of \"chansons de geste\".", "chunk_id": "54cbfcfe8378cde7", "doc_id": "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_348f259ed8ae2d75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Isembart" target="Gormond">
  <data key="d5">["ALLIES_WITH"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Isembart allies himself with the Saracen king Gormond.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The poem tells the story of a rebellious young French lord, Isembart, who allies himself with a Saracen king, Gormond, renounces his Christianity, and battles the French king.", "chunk_id": "54cbfcfe8378cde7", "doc_id": "hp_348f259ed8ae2d75", "type": "ALLIES_WITH"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_348f259ed8ae2d75</data>
</edge>
