  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The wild Bactrian camel has limited populations in northwest China.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The three surviving species of camel are the dromedary, or one-humped camel (\"C. dromedarius\"), which inhabits the Middle East and the Horn of Africa; the Bactrian, or two-humped camel (\"C. bactrianus\"), which inhabits Central Asia; and the critically endangered wild Bactrian camel (\"C. ferus\") that has limited populations in remote areas of northwest China and Mongolia.", "chunk_id": "0f4c26b19727d970", "doc_id": "hp_706e5d69c6cb6d2b", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
