<edge source="Duncan v. Kahanamoku" target="United States Supreme Court">
  <data key="d5">["DECIDED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Duncan v. Kahanamoku was a decision made by the United States Supreme Court.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Duncan v. Kahanamoku, 327 U.S. 304 (1946), was a decision by the United States Supreme Court.", "chunk_id": "c1e246687344e804", "doc_id": "hp_38ad5fccbbab039a", "type": "DECIDED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_38ad5fccbbab039a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Duncan v. Kahanamoku" target="Japanese exclusion cases">
  <data key="d5">["ASSOCIATED_WITH"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Duncan v. Kahanamoku is often associated with the Japanese exclusion cases.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It is often associated with the Japanese exclusion cases (\"Hirabayashi v. United States\", \"Korematsu v. United States\" and \"Ex parte Endo\") because it involved wartime curtailment of fundamental civil liberties under the aegis of military authority, though in this case neither the plaintiff nor the nominal defendant were Japanese.", "chunk_id": "c1e246687344e804", "doc_id": "hp_38ad5fccbbab039a", "type": "ASSOCIATED_WITH"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_38ad5fccbbab039a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Duncan v. Kahanamoku" target="wartime curtailment of fundamental civil liberties">
  <data key="d5">["INVOLVED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Duncan v. Kahanamoku involved the wartime curtailment of fundamental civil liberties.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It is often associated with the Japanese exclusion cases (\"Hirabayashi v. United States\", \"Korematsu v. United States\" and \"Ex parte Endo\") because it involved wartime curtailment of fundamental civil liberties under the aegis of military authority, though in this case neither the plaintiff nor the nominal defendant were Japanese.", "chunk_id": "c1e246687344e804", "doc_id": "hp_38ad5fccbbab039a", "type": "INVOLVED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_38ad5fccbbab039a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Japanese exclusion cases" target="Hirabayashi v. United States">
  <data key="d5">["INCLUDES"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Japanese exclusion cases include Hirabayashi v. United States.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It is often associated with the Japanese exclusion cases (\"Hirabayashi v. United States\", \"Korematsu v. United States\" and \"Ex parte Endo\") because it involved wartime curtailment of fundamental civil liberties under the aegis of military authority, though in this case neither the plaintiff nor the nominal defendant were Japanese.", "chunk_id": "c1e246687344e804", "doc_id": "hp_38ad5fccbbab039a", "type": "INCLUDES"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_38ad5fccbbab039a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Japanese exclusion cases" target="Korematsu v. United States">
  <data key="d5">["INCLUDES"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Japanese exclusion cases include Korematsu v. United States.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It is often associated with the Japanese exclusion cases (\"Hirabayashi v. United States\", \"Korematsu v. United States\" and \"Ex parte Endo\") because it involved wartime curtailment of fundamental civil liberties under the aegis of military authority, though in this case neither the plaintiff nor the nominal defendant were Japanese.", "chunk_id": "c1e246687344e804", "doc_id": "hp_38ad5fccbbab039a", "type": "INCLUDES"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_38ad5fccbbab039a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Japanese exclusion cases" target="Ex parte Endo">
  <data key="d5">["INCLUDES"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Japanese exclusion cases include Ex parte Endo.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It is often associated with the Japanese exclusion cases (\"Hirabayashi v. United States\", \"Korematsu v. United States\" and \"Ex parte Endo\") because it involved wartime curtailment of fundamental civil liberties under the aegis of military authority, though in this case neither the plaintiff nor the nominal defendant were Japanese.", "chunk_id": "c1e246687344e804", "doc_id": "hp_38ad5fccbbab039a", "type": "INCLUDES"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_38ad5fccbbab039a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Ex parte Endo" target="United States Supreme Court">
  <data key="d5">["DECIDED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Ex parte Endo was a decision handed down by the United States Supreme Court.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Ex parte Endo, or Ex parte Mitsuye Endo, 323 U.S. 283 (1944), was a United States Supreme Court ex parte decision handed down on December 18, 1944, in which the Justices unanimously ruled that the U.S. government could not continue to detain a citizen who was \"concededly loyal\" to the United States.", "chunk_id": "615cdfa10474d8b6", "doc_id": "hp_c36e9406d9e10267", "type": "DECIDED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_c36e9406d9e10267</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Ex parte Endo" target="U.S. government">
  <data key="d5">["CONCERNS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Ex parte Endo case ruled on the actions of the U.S. government regarding the detention of a citizen.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Ex parte Endo, or Ex parte Mitsuye Endo, 323 U.S. 283 (1944), was a United States Supreme Court ex parte decision handed down on December 18, 1944, in which the Justices unanimously ruled that the U.S. government could not continue to detain a citizen who was \"concededly loyal\" to the United States.", "chunk_id": "615cdfa10474d8b6", "doc_id": "hp_c36e9406d9e10267", "type": "CONCERNS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_c36e9406d9e10267</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Ex parte Endo" target="West Coast">
  <data key="d5">["LED_TO_REOPENING_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The ruling in Ex parte Endo led to the reopening of the West Coast to Japanese Americans.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Although the Court did not touch on the constitutionality of the exclusion of people of Japanese ancestry from the West Coast—which they had found not to violate citizen rights in their \"Korematsu v. United States\" decision on the same date—the Endo ruling nonetheless led to the reopening of the West Coast to Japanese Americans after their incarceration in camps across the U.S. interior during World War II.", "chunk_id": "615cdfa10474d8b6", "doc_id": "hp_c36e9406d9e10267", "type": "LED_TO_REOPENING_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_c36e9406d9e10267</data>
</edge>
<edge source="wartime curtailment of fundamental civil liberties" target="military authority">
  <data key="d5">["UNDER_AEGIS_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The wartime curtailment of fundamental civil liberties occurred under the aegis of military authority.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It is often associated with the Japanese exclusion cases (\"Hirabayashi v. United States\", \"Korematsu v. United States\" and \"Ex parte Endo\") because it involved wartime curtailment of fundamental civil liberties under the aegis of military authority, though in this case neither the plaintiff nor the nominal defendant were Japanese.", "chunk_id": "c1e246687344e804", "doc_id": "hp_38ad5fccbbab039a", "type": "UNDER_AEGIS_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_38ad5fccbbab039a</data>
</edge>
