<edge source="Director of Immigration v Chong Fung Yuen" target="Hong Kong">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The case took place in Hong Kong.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Director of Immigration v. Chong Fung Yuen was a 2001 case in Hong Kong's Court of Final Appeal.", "chunk_id": "e783910d896b84d9", "doc_id": "hp_3bad22e58989e25f", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_3bad22e58989e25f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Director of Immigration v Chong Fung Yuen" target="Court of Final Appeal">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The case was heard by the Court of Final Appeal.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Director of Immigration v. Chong Fung Yuen was a 2001 case in Hong Kong's Court of Final Appeal.", "chunk_id": "e783910d896b84d9", "doc_id": "hp_3bad22e58989e25f", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_3bad22e58989e25f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Director of Immigration v Chong Fung Yuen" target="Hong Kong Basic Law">
  <data key="d5">["INTERPRETED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The case involved the interpretation of the Hong Kong Basic Law.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The case touched on issues of interpretation of the Hong Kong Basic Law, both common law interpretation by courts in Hong Kong as well as interpretation by the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress (NPCSC) of the People's Republic of China.", "chunk_id": "e783910d896b84d9", "doc_id": "hp_3bad22e58989e25f", "type": "INTERPRETED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_3bad22e58989e25f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Director of Immigration v Chong Fung Yuen" target="regime of rights in the Hong Kong SAR">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The case is described as part of a period of elaboration and consolidation of the regime of rights in the Hong Kong SAR.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Professor Albert Chen of the University of Hong Kong describes the case as part of a \"period of elaboration and consolidation of the regime of rights in the Hong Kong SAR\", lasting roughly from 2000 to 2002.", "chunk_id": "e783910d896b84d9", "doc_id": "hp_3bad22e58989e25f", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_3bad22e58989e25f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Andrew Li" target="Court of Final Appeal">
  <data key="d5">["WORKS_AT"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Andrew Li was the Chief Justice of the Court of Final Appeal.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Chief Justice Andrew Li, in the Court's unanimous opinion, affirmed lower court decisions that Chinese citizens born in Hong Kong enjoyed the right of abode regardless of the Hong Kong immigration status of their parents.", "chunk_id": "e783910d896b84d9", "doc_id": "hp_3bad22e58989e25f", "type": "WORKS_AT"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_3bad22e58989e25f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Chinese citizens" target="right of abode">
  <data key="d5">["GRANTED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Chinese citizens born in Hong Kong were granted the right of abode.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Chief Justice Andrew Li, in the Court's unanimous opinion, affirmed lower court decisions that Chinese citizens born in Hong Kong enjoyed the right of abode regardless of the Hong Kong immigration status of their parents.", "chunk_id": "e783910d896b84d9", "doc_id": "hp_3bad22e58989e25f", "type": "GRANTED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_3bad22e58989e25f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Standing Committee of the National People's Congress" target="Hong Kong Basic Law">
  <data key="d5">["INTERPRETS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Standing Committee of the National People's Congress interprets the Hong Kong Basic Law.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The case touched on issues of interpretation of the Hong Kong Basic Law, both common law interpretation by courts in Hong Kong as well as interpretation by the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress (NPCSC) of the People's Republic of China.", "chunk_id": "e783910d896b84d9", "doc_id": "hp_3bad22e58989e25f", "type": "INTERPRETS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_3bad22e58989e25f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Standing Committee of the National People's Congress" target="People's Republic of China">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Standing Committee is part of the People's Republic of China.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The case touched on issues of interpretation of the Hong Kong Basic Law, both common law interpretation by courts in Hong Kong as well as interpretation by the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress (NPCSC) of the People's Republic of China.", "chunk_id": "e783910d896b84d9", "doc_id": "hp_3bad22e58989e25f", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_3bad22e58989e25f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Albert Chen" target="University of Hong Kong">
  <data key="d5">["WORKS_AT"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Albert Chen is a professor at the University of Hong Kong.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Professor Albert Chen of the University of Hong Kong describes the case as part of a \"period of elaboration and consolidation of the regime of rights in the Hong Kong SAR\", lasting roughly from 2000 to 2002.", "chunk_id": "e783910d896b84d9", "doc_id": "hp_3bad22e58989e25f", "type": "WORKS_AT"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_3bad22e58989e25f</data>
</edge>
