<edge source="Durvillaea willana" target="D. antarctica">
  <data key="d5">["SIMILAR_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Durvillaea willana is similar to D. antarctica.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It is similar to \"D. antarctica\" but is found in more sheltered coasts.", "chunk_id": "d0bb177e0eca5e20", "doc_id": "hp_445a6fbf701fbac1", "type": "SIMILAR_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_445a6fbf701fbac1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="D. antarctica" target="D. willana">
  <data key="d5">["DIFFERENT_FROM", "MORE_TOLERANT_OF", "DIFFERENT_FROM"]</data>
  <data key="d6">D. antarctica has larger blades than D. willana.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"D. willana\" has smaller blades than \"D. antarctica\" and is usually found lower on the shoreline because its tolerance of wave action is not as great as \"D. antarctica\" (Bradstock, 1989).", "chunk_id": "d0bb177e0eca5e20", "doc_id": "hp_445a6fbf701fbac1", "type": "DIFFERENT_FROM"}, {"text": "\"D. willana\" has smaller blades than \"D. antarctica\" and is usually found lower on the shoreline because its tolerance of wave action is not as great as \"D. antarctica\" (Bradstock, 1989).", "chunk_id": "d0bb177e0eca5e20", "doc_id": "hp_445a6fbf701fbac1", "type": "MORE_TOLERANT_OF"}, {"text": "The fronds are not honeycombed like \"D. antarctica\".", "chunk_id": "d0bb177e0eca5e20", "doc_id": "hp_445a6fbf701fbac1", "type": "DIFFERENT_FROM"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_445a6fbf701fbac1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="D. willana" target="D. antarctica">
  <data key="d5">["DIFFERENT_FROM", "LESS_TOLERANT_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">D. willana has smaller blades than D. antarctica.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"D. willana\" has smaller blades than \"D. antarctica\" and is usually found lower on the shoreline because its tolerance of wave action is not as great as \"D. antarctica\" (Bradstock, 1989).", "chunk_id": "d0bb177e0eca5e20", "doc_id": "hp_445a6fbf701fbac1", "type": "DIFFERENT_FROM"}, {"text": "\"D. willana\" has smaller blades than \"D. antarctica\" and is usually found lower on the shoreline because its tolerance of wave action is not as great as \"D. antarctica\" (Bradstock, 1989).", "chunk_id": "d0bb177e0eca5e20", "doc_id": "hp_445a6fbf701fbac1", "type": "LESS_TOLERANT_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_445a6fbf701fbac1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="D. willana" target="bull kelp">
  <data key="d5">["MISTAKEN_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">D. willana is usually mistaken for bull kelp.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"D. willana\" has no common name in New Zealand, however is usually mistaken for bull kelp, \"Durvillaea antarctica\".", "chunk_id": "d0bb177e0eca5e20", "doc_id": "hp_445a6fbf701fbac1", "type": "MISTAKEN_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_445a6fbf701fbac1</data>
</edge>
