<edge source="Italian Renaissance" target="Ballet">
  <data key="d5">["ORIGINATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Ballet has its origins in the Italian Renaissance courts.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Ballet is a formalized form of dance with its origins in the Italian Renaissance courts of the 15th and 16th centuries.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77", "type": "ORIGINATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_4c5083f96f89fa77</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Catherine de' Medici" target="Ballet">
  <data key="d5">["DEVELOPED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Catherine de' Medici helped spread ballet from Italy to France and further developed it.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Ballet spread from Italy to France with the help of Catherine de' Medici, where ballet developed even further under her aristocratic influence.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77", "type": "DEVELOPED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_4c5083f96f89fa77</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Catherine de' Medici" target="Le Paradis d' Amour">
  <data key="d5">["DEVELOPED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Le Paradis d' Amour is an example of Catherine de' Medici's development of ballet.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "An early example of Catherine's development of ballet is through 'Le Paradis d' Amour', a piece of work presented at her daughter's wedding, Marguerite de Valois to Henry of Navarre.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77", "type": "DEVELOPED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_4c5083f96f89fa77</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Catherine de' Medici" target="Ballet des Polonais">
  <data key="d5">["COMMISSIONED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Catherine de' Medici commissioned 'Ballet des Polonais'.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In true form of royal entertainment, 'Ballet des Polonais' was commissioned by Catherine de' Medici to honor the Polish ambassadors who were visiting Paris upon the accession of Henry of Anjou to the throne of Poland.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77", "type": "COMMISSIONED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_4c5083f96f89fa77</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Catherine de' Medici" target="Ballet Comique de la Reine">
  <data key="d5">["COMMISSIONED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Catherine de' Medici commissioned 'Ballet Comique de la Reine' in 1581.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In 1581, Catherine de' Medici commissioned another court ballet, \"Ballet Comique de la Reine\", however it was her compatriot, Balthasar de Beaujoyeulx, who organized the ballet.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77", "type": "COMMISSIONED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_4c5083f96f89fa77</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Catherine de' Medici" target="Baif's Academie">
  <data key="d5">["APPLIED_PRINCIPLES_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Catherine de' Medici was responsible for presenting the first court ballet to apply the principles of Baif's Academie.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Catherine de' Medici and Balthasar de Beaujoyeulx were responsible for presenting the first court ballet ever to apply the principles of Baif's Academie, by integrating poetry, dance, music and set design to convey a unified dramatic storyline.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77", "type": "APPLIED_PRINCIPLES_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_4c5083f96f89fa77</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Marguerite de Valois" target="Henry of Navarre">
  <data key="d5">["MARRIED_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Marguerite de Valois was married to Henry of Navarre.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "An early example of Catherine's development of ballet is through 'Le Paradis d' Amour', a piece of work presented at her daughter's wedding, Marguerite de Valois to Henry of Navarre.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77", "type": "MARRIED_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_4c5083f96f89fa77</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Balthasar de Beaujoyeulx" target="Ballet Comique de la Reine">
  <data key="d5">["ORGANIZED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Balthasar de Beaujoyeulx organized 'Ballet Comique de la Reine'.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In 1581, Catherine de' Medici commissioned another court ballet, \"Ballet Comique de la Reine\", however it was her compatriot, Balthasar de Beaujoyeulx, who organized the ballet.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77", "type": "ORGANIZED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_4c5083f96f89fa77</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Balthasar de Beaujoyeulx" target="Baif's Academie">
  <data key="d5">["APPLIED_PRINCIPLES_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Balthasar de Beaujoyeulx was responsible for presenting the first court ballet to apply the principles of Baif's Academie.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Catherine de' Medici and Balthasar de Beaujoyeulx were responsible for presenting the first court ballet ever to apply the principles of Baif's Academie, by integrating poetry, dance, music and set design to convey a unified dramatic storyline.", "chunk_id": "88dbc1f080e4265f", "doc_id": "hp_4c5083f96f89fa77", "type": "APPLIED_PRINCIPLES_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_4c5083f96f89fa77</data>
