<edge source="hatchet man" target="Watergate scandal">
  <data key="d5">["CONTEXT_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The term 'hatchet man' was used in the context of the Watergate scandal.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In the context of the Watergate scandal, the term hatchet man was used to refer to a trusted and particularly orthodox subordinate tasked by his employer with destroying a political opponent by any means necessary.", "chunk_id": "d0b1e443837cd70f", "doc_id": "hp_5042be17d44308ee", "type": "CONTEXT_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_5042be17d44308ee</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Charles Colson" target="President Richard Nixon">
  <data key="d5">["WORKS_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Charles Colson was a hatchet man for President Richard Nixon.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Charles Colson was known as a hatchet man for President Richard Nixon, as was H.R. Haldeman, who proudly described himself as \"Richard Nixon's 'son of a bitch'\".", "chunk_id": "d0b1e443837cd70f", "doc_id": "hp_5042be17d44308ee", "type": "WORKS_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_5042be17d44308ee</data>
</edge>
