<edge source="Salvia" target="Salvia divinorum">
  <data key="d5">["IS_A"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Salvia is another name for Salvia divinorum.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Salvia divinorum (also known as sage of the diviners, ska maría pastora, seer's sage, yerba de la pastora and just salvia) is a psychoactive plant which can induce visions and other spiritual experiences.", "chunk_id": "b84d18605bb81aec", "doc_id": "hp_5b549ddaeafe9045", "type": "IS_A"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_5b549ddaeafe9045</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Salvia" target="Lamiaceae">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF", "PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Salvia is a genus within the Lamiaceae family.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Salvia is the largest genus of plants in the family Lamiaceae, with the number of species estimated to range from 700 to nearly 1,000.", "chunk_id": "a02f6c09a33fee66", "doc_id": "hp_6e6c3433daecaed3", "type": "PART_OF"}, {"text": "Salvia is the largest genus of plants in the mint family, Lamiaceae, with nearly 1000 species of shrubs, herbaceous perennials, and annuals.", "chunk_id": "5634c2e12f5049d1", "doc_id": "hp_ea708a0e606fa04d", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6e6c3433daecaed3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Salvia" target="Central and South America">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Approximately 500 species of Salvia are found in Central and South America.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "There are three main regions of radiation of \"Salvia\": Central and South America, with approximately 500 species; central Asia and the Mediterranean with approx. 250 species; eastern Asia with approximately 90 species.", "chunk_id": "a02f6c09a33fee66", "doc_id": "hp_6e6c3433daecaed3", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6e6c3433daecaed3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Salvia" target="central Asia and the Mediterranean">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Approximately 250 species of Salvia are found in central Asia and the Mediterranean.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "There are three main regions of radiation of \"Salvia\": Central and South America, with approximately 500 species; central Asia and the Mediterranean with approx. 250 species; eastern Asia with approximately 90 species.", "chunk_id": "a02f6c09a33fee66", "doc_id": "hp_6e6c3433daecaed3", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6e6c3433daecaed3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Salvia" target="eastern Asia">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Approximately 90 species of Salvia are found in eastern Asia.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "There are three main regions of radiation of \"Salvia\": Central and South America, with approximately 500 species; central Asia and the Mediterranean with approx. 250 species; eastern Asia with approximately 90 species.", "chunk_id": "a02f6c09a33fee66", "doc_id": "hp_6e6c3433daecaed3", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6e6c3433daecaed3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Salvia" target="Salvia 'Jean's Purple Passion'">
  <data key="d5">["HAS_CULTIVAR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Salvia 'Jean's Purple Passion' is a cultivar of Salvia.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Salvia 'Jean's Purple Passion' is a \"Salvia\" cultivar discovered at Cabrillo College in Aptos, California.", "chunk_id": "6c8ea648c2d5ed76", "doc_id": "hp_980453e19b052243", "type": "HAS_CULTIVAR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_980453e19b052243</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Salvia" target="Mentheae">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Salvia is part of the Mentheae tribe within the Lamiaceae family.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Within the Lamiaceae, \"Salvia\" is part of the tribe Mentheae within the subfamily Nepetoideae.", "chunk_id": "5634c2e12f5049d1", "doc_id": "hp_ea708a0e606fa04d", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ea708a0e606fa04d</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Salvia" target="sage">
  <data key="d5">["SYNONYM_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Salvia is one of several genera commonly referred to as sage.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It is one of several genera commonly referred to as sage, It includes the widely produced herb used in cooking, \"Salvia officinalis\" (common sage, or just \"sage\").", "chunk_id": "5634c2e12f5049d1", "doc_id": "hp_ea708a0e606fa04d", "type": "SYNONYM_OF"}, {"text": "Salvia chamelaeagnea is a species of flowering plant in genus \"Salvia\", known as sages.", "chunk_id": "993393a5d9cfab3f", "doc_id": "hp_bae29dd7ee1c4c2e", "type": "IS_A"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ea708a0e606fa04d</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Daniel Auber" target="Manon Lescaut (Auber)">
  <data key="d5">["COMPOSED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Daniel Auber composed the opera Manon Lescaut.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Manon Lescaut is an opera or opéra comique in 3 acts by Daniel Auber to a libretto by Eugène Scribe, and, like Puccini's \"Manon Lescaut\" and Massenet's \"Manon\", is based on the Abbé Prévost's novel \"Manon Lescaut\".", "chunk_id": "62ee8e762a5f8458", "doc_id": "hp_51938f55ccd7098e", "type": "COMPOSED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_51938f55ccd7098e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Eugène Scribe" target="Manon Lescaut (Auber)">
  <data key="d5">["WROTE_LIBRETTO_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Eugène Scribe wrote the libretto for Daniel Auber's opera Manon Lescaut.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Manon Lescaut is an opera or opéra comique in 3 acts by Daniel Auber to a libretto by Eugène Scribe, and, like Puccini's \"Manon Lescaut\" and Massenet's \"Manon\", is based on the Abbé Prévost's novel \"Manon Lescaut\".", "chunk_id": "62ee8e762a5f8458", "doc_id": "hp_51938f55ccd7098e", "type": "WROTE_LIBRETTO_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_51938f55ccd7098e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Abbé Prévost's novel &quot;Manon Lescaut&quot;" target="Manon Lescaut (Auber)">
  <data key="d5">["BASED_ON"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Daniel Auber's opera Manon Lescaut is based on Abbé Prévost's novel Manon Lescaut.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Manon Lescaut is an opera or opéra comique in 3 acts by Daniel Auber to a libretto by Eugène Scribe, and, like Puccini's \"Manon Lescaut\" and Massenet's \"Manon\", is based on the Abbé Prévost's novel \"Manon Lescaut\".", "chunk_id": "62ee8e762a5f8458", "doc_id": "hp_51938f55ccd7098e", "type": "BASED_ON"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_51938f55ccd7098e</data>
</edge>
