<edge source="Hoch Conservatory" target="England">
  <data key="d5">["HAS_STUDENTS_FROM"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Conservatory had students from England.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In the 1890s about 25% of the students were from other countries: 46 were from England and 23 from America.", "chunk_id": "8866c9256d91177d", "doc_id": "hp_530d45fd86f01aa0", "type": "HAS_STUDENTS_FROM"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_530d45fd86f01aa0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hoch Conservatory" target="America">
  <data key="d5">["HAS_STUDENTS_FROM"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Conservatory had students from America.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In the 1890s about 25% of the students were from other countries: 46 were from England and 23 from America.", "chunk_id": "8866c9256d91177d", "doc_id": "hp_530d45fd86f01aa0", "type": "HAS_STUDENTS_FROM"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_530d45fd86f01aa0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hoch Conservatory" target="Frankfurt">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN", "LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Hoch Conservatory is located in Frankfurt.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "However, in 1878, Cossmann helped found the Hoch Conservatory in Frankfurt, where he occupied the post of teacher of cello.", "chunk_id": "6edb4fdb819c98a3", "doc_id": "hp_67a26b8d9bf904cd", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}, {"text": "She became a teacher at the Hoch Conservatory in Frankfurt.", "chunk_id": "5978fb5d2c7a87fb", "doc_id": "hp_ac759163e3bcf4aa", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_67a26b8d9bf904cd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hoch Conservatory" target="Frankfurt am Main">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Hoch Conservatory is located in Frankfurt am Main.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "From 1932-1936 he was a fellow at the Hoch Conservatory in Frankfurt am Main.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e546658adba29b4c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dr. Hoch’s Konservatorium - Musikakademie" target="Frankfurt am Main">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Conservatory was founded in Frankfurt am Main.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Dr. Hoch’s Konservatorium - Musikakademie was founded in Frankfurt am Main on 22 September 1878.", "chunk_id": "8866c9256d91177d", "doc_id": "hp_530d45fd86f01aa0", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_530d45fd86f01aa0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Joseph Hoch" target="Hoch Conservatory">
  <data key="d5">["FOUNDED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Joseph Hoch's generosity led to the establishment of the Conservatory.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Through the generosity of Frankfurter Joseph Hoch, who bequeathed the Conservatory one million German gold marks in his testament, a school for music and the arts was established for all age groups.", "chunk_id": "8866c9256d91177d", "doc_id": "hp_530d45fd86f01aa0", "type": "FOUNDED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_530d45fd86f01aa0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Joseph Hoch" target="Hoch Conservatory Foundation">
  <data key="d5">["FOUNDED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Joseph Hoch willed his fortune to the Hoch Conservatory Foundation.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "He willed his fortune to the Hoch Conservatory Foundation, founded in 1878 in Frankfurt.", "chunk_id": "43c8b1224e31b404", "doc_id": "hp_a82ec9e667a313c7", "type": "FOUNDED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_a82ec9e667a313c7</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Joseph Hoch" target="Frankfurt am Main">
  <data key="d5">["BORN_IN", "DIED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Joseph Hoch was born in Frankfurt am Main.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "He was born and died in Frankfurt am Main.", "chunk_id": "43c8b1224e31b404", "doc_id": "hp_a82ec9e667a313c7", "type": "BORN_IN"}, {"text": "He was born and died in Frankfurt am Main.", "chunk_id": "43c8b1224e31b404", "doc_id": "hp_a82ec9e667a313c7", "type": "DIED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_a82ec9e667a313c7</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Joachim Raff" target="Hoch Conservatory">
  <data key="d5">["DIRECTOR_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Joachim Raff was the director of the Conservatory.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Instrumental to the foundation, prosperity and success of the Conservatory was its director Joachim Raff who did most of the work including setting the entire curriculum and hiring all its faculty.", "chunk_id": "8866c9256d91177d", "doc_id": "hp_530d45fd86f01aa0", "type": "DIRECTOR_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_530d45fd86f01aa0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Clara Schumann" target="Hoch Conservatory">
  <data key="d5">["TEACHER_AT"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Clara Schumann was a teacher at the Conservatory.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Many distinguished have taught there: in the late 19th century, with such teachers as Clara Schumann on the faculty, the Conservatory achieved international renown.", "chunk_id": "8866c9256d91177d", "doc_id": "hp_530d45fd86f01aa0", "type": "TEACHER_AT"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_530d45fd86f01aa0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Clara Schumann" target="Robert Schumann">
  <data key="d5">["SPOUSE_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Robert Schumann was the husband of Clara Schumann.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Her husband was the composer Robert Schumann.", "chunk_id": "933ccb664a9a5ee9", "doc_id": "hp_82f5ebc51e47c5a7", "type": "SPOUSE_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_82f5ebc51e47c5a7</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Clara Schumann" target="Johannes Brahms">
  <data key="d5">["ENCOURAGED", "FIRST_TO_PERFORM"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Clara Schumann encouraged Johannes Brahms.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Together they encouraged Johannes Brahms.", "chunk_id": "933ccb664a9a5ee9", "doc_id": "hp_82f5ebc51e47c5a7", "type": "ENCOURAGED"}, {"text": "She was the first to perform publicly any work by Brahms.", "chunk_id": "933ccb664a9a5ee9", "doc_id": "hp_82f5ebc51e47c5a7", "type": "FIRST_TO_PERFORM"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_82f5ebc51e47c5a7</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Clara Schumann" target="Variations and Fugue on a Theme by Handel">
  <data key="d5">["PREMIERED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Clara Schumann premiered the "Variations and Fugue on a Theme by Handel".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "She later premiered some other pieces by Brahms, notably the \"Variations and Fugue on a Theme by Handel\".", "chunk_id": "933ccb664a9a5ee9", "doc_id": "hp_82f5ebc51e47c5a7", "type": "PREMIERED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_82f5ebc51e47c5a7</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Town Bloody Hall" target="Norman Mailer">
  <data key="d5">["FEATURES_PERSON", "STARS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Norman Mailer was a participant in the panel debate featured in the "Town Bloody Hall" documentary.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Town Bloody Hall is a 1971 documentary film of a panel debate between feminist advocates and activist Norman Mailer.", "chunk_id": "a75812f45ba95804", "doc_id": "hp_535589d1805f024e", "type": "FEATURES_PERSON"}, {"text": "Chris Hegedus and D. A. Pennebaker produced the film, which stars Jacqueline Ceballos, Germaine Greer, Jill Johnston, Diane Trilling, and Norman Mailer.", "chunk_id": "a75812f45ba95804", "doc_id": "hp_535589d1805f024e", "type": "STARS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_535589d1805f024e</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Town Bloody Hall" target="The Town Hall">
  <data key="d5">["FILMED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The documentary "Town Bloody Hall" was filmed in The Town Hall.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Filmed on April 30, 1971, in The Town Hall in New York City, \"Town Bloody Hall\" features a panel of feminist advocates for the women's liberation movement and Norman Mailer, the writer of \"The Prisoner of Sex\".", "chunk_id": "a75812f45ba95804", "doc_id": "hp_535589d1805f024e", "type": "FILMED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_535589d1805f024e</data>
</edge>
