<edge source="Tongyeong" target="Admiral Yi Sun-sin">
  <data key="d5">["ASSOCIATED_WITH"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The name Tongyeong is associated with Admiral Yi Sun-sin.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The name Tongyeong means \"command post\" and is itself associated with Admiral Yi, as it refers to his principal base that was located on nearby Hansan Island.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39", "type": "ASSOCIATED_WITH"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_5597a745514f1f39</data>
</edge>
<edge source="South Korea" target="Cinema of Korea">
  <data key="d5">["HAS_INDUSTRY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">South Korea has a robust film industry that has achieved wide international acclaim.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "While both countries have relatively robust film industries today, only South Korean films have achieved wide international acclaim.", "chunk_id": "ab78baf12b2f8b16", "doc_id": "hp_b840ad7146ba28d6", "type": "HAS_INDUSTRY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_b840ad7146ba28d6</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Chungmu city" target="Tongyeong City">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Chungmu city was reunited to form Tongyeong City.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Chungmu city and Tongyeong county were reunited in 1995, creating Tongyeong City as it is known today.", "chunk_id": "c3d0968c45bdecd5", "doc_id": "hp_5597a745514f1f39", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
