<edge source="Tom Petty" target="Wildflowers">
  <data key="d5">["RECORDED_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Tom Petty recorded the song "Leave Virginia Alone" for his album "Wildflowers".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"Leave Virginia Alone\" was written by Tom Petty and recorded for his album \"Wildflowers\", but was left off the finished album and given to Stewart instead.", "chunk_id": "ee3812aae430f03c", "doc_id": "hp_56786c080440345c", "type": "RECORDED_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_56786c080440345c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="George Heneage Lawrence Dundas" target="Royal Navy">
  <data key="d5">["WORKS_AT"]</data>
  <data key="d6">George Heneage Lawrence Dundas was a senior officer in the Royal Navy.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Rear Admiral George Heneage Lawrence Dundas CB (8 September 1778 – 7 October 1834) was a senior officer in the Royal Navy.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743", "type": "WORKS_AT"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_56ae2e2bc0735743</data>
</edge>
<edge source="George Heneage Lawrence Dundas" target="HMS &quot;Queen Charlotte&quot;">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">George Heneage Lawrence Dundas served on HMS "Queen Charlotte" as a junior officer.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "As a junior officer he came to prominence due to his brave conduct during a fire on the first-rate HMS \"Queen Charlotte\".", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_56ae2e2bc0735743</data>
</edge>
<edge source="George Heneage Lawrence Dundas" target="HMS &quot;Calpe&quot;">
  <data key="d5">["COMMANDED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">George Heneage Lawrence Dundas was appointed to the command of HMS "Calpe".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "As a result of this he was appointed to the command of the sixth-rate HMS \"Calpe\" in which he took part in the Battle of Algeciras Bay in July 1801 during the French Revolutionary Wars.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743", "type": "COMMANDED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_56ae2e2bc0735743</data>
</edge>
<edge source="George Heneage Lawrence Dundas" target="Richmond">
  <data key="d5">["ELECTED_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">George Heneage Lawrence Dundas served as Member of Parliament for Richmond.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "After serving for four years as Whig Member of Parliament for Richmond, he was given command of the fifth-rate HMS \"Euryalus\" and took part in the unsuccessful Walcheren Campaign in July 1809 during the Napoleonic Wars.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743", "type": "ELECTED_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_56ae2e2bc0735743</data>
</edge>
<edge source="George Heneage Lawrence Dundas" target="HMS &quot;Euryalus&quot;">
  <data key="d5">["COMMANDED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">George Heneage Lawrence Dundas was given command of HMS "Euryalus".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "After serving for four years as Whig Member of Parliament for Richmond, he was given command of the fifth-rate HMS \"Euryalus\" and took part in the unsuccessful Walcheren Campaign in July 1809 during the Napoleonic Wars.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743", "type": "COMMANDED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_56ae2e2bc0735743</data>
</edge>
<edge source="George Heneage Lawrence Dundas" target="HMS &quot;Edinburgh&quot;">
  <data key="d5">["TRANSFERRED_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">George Heneage Lawrence Dundas transferred to HMS "Edinburgh".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "He transferred to the third-rate HMS \"Edinburgh\" and landed troops at Viareggio in Italy in November 1812 later in that War.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743", "type": "TRANSFERRED_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_56ae2e2bc0735743</data>
</edge>
<edge source="George Heneage Lawrence Dundas" target="Viareggio">
  <data key="d5">["LANDED_AT"]</data>
  <data key="d6">George Heneage Lawrence Dundas landed troops at Viareggio.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "He transferred to the third-rate HMS \"Edinburgh\" and landed troops at Viareggio in Italy in November 1812 later in that War.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743", "type": "LANDED_AT"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_56ae2e2bc0735743</data>
</edge>
<edge source="George Heneage Lawrence Dundas" target="Orkney and Shetland">
  <data key="d5">["ELECTED_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">George Heneage Lawrence Dundas served as Member of Parliament for Orkney and Shetland.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "He went on to be Member of Parliament for Orkney and Shetland and became First Naval Lord in the First Melbourne ministry in August 1834 but died in office just two months later in October 1834.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743", "type": "ELECTED_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_56ae2e2bc0735743</data>
</edge>
<edge source="George Heneage Lawrence Dundas" target="First Naval Lord">
  <data key="d5">["APPOINTED_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">George Heneage Lawrence Dundas became First Naval Lord.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "He went on to be Member of Parliament for Orkney and Shetland and became First Naval Lord in the First Melbourne ministry in August 1834 but died in office just two months later in October 1834.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743", "type": "APPOINTED_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_56ae2e2bc0735743</data>
</edge>
<edge source="George Heneage Lawrence Dundas" target="First Melbourne ministry">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">George Heneage Lawrence Dundas served in the First Melbourne ministry.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "He went on to be Member of Parliament for Orkney and Shetland and became First Naval Lord in the First Melbourne ministry in August 1834 but died in office just two months later in October 1834.", "chunk_id": "d43d20bf97a0fc28", "doc_id": "hp_56ae2e2bc0735743", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_56ae2e2bc0735743</data>
</edge>
<edge source="HMS &quot;Calpe&quot;" target="Battle of Algeciras Bay">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">HMS "Calpe" took part in the Battle of Algeciras Bay.</data>
