<edge source="Tikkun Chatzot" target="Jewish ritual prayer">
  <data key="d5">["IS_A"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Tikkun Chatzot is a type of Jewish ritual prayer.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Tikkun Chatzot (Hebrew: תקון חצות‎ , lit. \"Midnight Rectification\"), also spelled Tikkun Chatzos, is a Jewish ritual prayer recited each night after midnight as an expression of mourning and lamentation over the destruction of the Temple in Jerusalem.", "chunk_id": "46b41533532c7444", "doc_id": "hp_60c26856bb2aaa62", "type": "IS_A"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_60c26856bb2aaa62</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Tikkun Chatzot" target="Temple in Jerusalem">
  <data key="d5">["EXPRESSES_MOURNING_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Tikkun Chatzot is recited as an expression of mourning for the destruction of the Temple in Jerusalem.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Tikkun Chatzot (Hebrew: תקון חצות‎ , lit. \"Midnight Rectification\"), also spelled Tikkun Chatzos, is a Jewish ritual prayer recited each night after midnight as an expression of mourning and lamentation over the destruction of the Temple in Jerusalem.", "chunk_id": "46b41533532c7444", "doc_id": "hp_60c26856bb2aaa62", "type": "EXPRESSES_MOURNING_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_60c26856bb2aaa62</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Tikkun Chatzot" target="Sephardi Jews">
  <data key="d5">["POPULAR_AMONG"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Tikkun Chatzot is popular among Sephardi Jews.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It is not universally observed, although it is popular among Sephardi and Hasidic Jews.", "chunk_id": "46b41533532c7444", "doc_id": "hp_60c26856bb2aaa62", "type": "POPULAR_AMONG"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_60c26856bb2aaa62</data>
</edge>
