<edge source="Henri Larrivée" target="basse-taille">
  <data key="d5">["HAS_VOICE_RANGE"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Henri Larrivée's voice range was basse-taille.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "His voice range was \"basse-taille\" (equivalent to baritone).", "chunk_id": "e5b8f20d23f949cd", "doc_id": "hp_6a489e030aae67cd", "type": "HAS_VOICE_RANGE"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6a489e030aae67cd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Henri Larrivée" target="Paris Opéra">
  <data key="d5">["WORKED_AT"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Henri Larrivée was hired as a chorus member by the Paris Opéra.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "According to Fétis, Larrivée was working as an apprentice to a wigmaker when the head of the Paris Opéra, Rebel, noticed his talent for singing and hired him as a chorus member.", "chunk_id": "e5b8f20d23f949cd", "doc_id": "hp_6a489e030aae67cd", "type": "WORKED_AT"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6a489e030aae67cd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Henri Larrivée" target="Castor et Pollux">
  <data key="d5">["APPEARED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Henri Larrivée made his first solo appearance in a revival of Rameau's "Castor et Pollux".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "He made his first solo appearance as a high priest in a 1755 revival of Rameau's \"Castor et Pollux\".", "chunk_id": "e5b8f20d23f949cd", "doc_id": "hp_6a489e030aae67cd", "type": "APPEARED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6a489e030aae67cd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Henri Larrivée" target="Christoph Willibald von Gluck">
  <data key="d5">["ASSOCIATED_WITH"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Henri Larrivée was particularly associated with the works of Christoph Willibald von Gluck.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "He was particularly associated with the works of Christoph Willibald von Gluck, helping Gluck establish his \"reform operas\" in France.", "chunk_id": "e5b8f20d23f949cd", "doc_id": "hp_6a489e030aae67cd", "type": "ASSOCIATED_WITH"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6a489e030aae67cd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Henri Larrivée" target="reform operas">
  <data key="d5">["HELPED_ESTABLISH"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Henri Larrivée helped Gluck establish his "reform operas" in France.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "He was particularly associated with the works of Christoph Willibald von Gluck, helping Gluck establish his \"reform operas\" in France.", "chunk_id": "e5b8f20d23f949cd", "doc_id": "hp_6a489e030aae67cd", "type": "HELPED_ESTABLISH"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6a489e030aae67cd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Henri Larrivée" target="Niccolò Piccinni">
  <data key="d5">["WORKED_WITH"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Henri Larrivée worked with Niccolò Piccinni on opera premieres.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "He found Gluck's rival, Niccolò Piccinni, less congenial but still worked with him on the premieres of operas including \"Roland\" (1778).", "chunk_id": "e5b8f20d23f949cd", "doc_id": "hp_6a489e030aae67cd", "type": "WORKED_WITH"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6a489e030aae67cd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Henri Larrivée" target="Roland">
  <data key="d5">["WORKED_ON_PREMIERE_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Henri Larrivée worked on the premiere of the opera "Roland".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "He found Gluck's rival, Niccolò Piccinni, less congenial but still worked with him on the premieres of operas including \"Roland\" (1778).", "chunk_id": "e5b8f20d23f949cd", "doc_id": "hp_6a489e030aae67cd", "type": "WORKED_ON_PREMIERE_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6a489e030aae67cd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Rebel" target="Paris Opéra">
  <data key="d5">["HEAD_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Rebel was the head of the Paris Opéra.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "According to Fétis, Larrivée was working as an apprentice to a wigmaker when the head of the Paris Opéra, Rebel, noticed his talent for singing and hired him as a chorus member.", "chunk_id": "e5b8f20d23f949cd", "doc_id": "hp_6a489e030aae67cd", "type": "HEAD_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6a489e030aae67cd</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Rameau" target="Castor et Pollux">
  <data key="d5">["COMPOSED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Rameau composed the opera 'Castor et Pollux'.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The libretto was one translated by Carlo Innocenzo Frugoni, from Pierre-Joseph-Justin Bernard's French text for Rameau's \"Castor et Pollux\".", "chunk_id": "b9a0568248760524", "doc_id": "hp_e9ebf1cff727fec5", "type": "COMPOSED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e9ebf1cff727fec5</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pinguicula orchidioides" target="Mexico">
  <data key="d5">["NATIVE_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pinguicula orchidioides is native to Mexico.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Pinguicula orchidioides is a perennial rosette-forming insectivorous herb native to Mexico and Guatemala.", "chunk_id": "1184555da09f3dbe", "doc_id": "hp_6a6940496f3fa2b9", "type": "NATIVE_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6a6940496f3fa2b9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pinguicula orchidioides" target="Guatemala">
  <data key="d5">["NATIVE_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pinguicula orchidioides is native to Guatemala.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Pinguicula orchidioides is a perennial rosette-forming insectivorous herb native to Mexico and Guatemala.", "chunk_id": "1184555da09f3dbe", "doc_id": "hp_6a6940496f3fa2b9", "type": "NATIVE_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6a6940496f3fa2b9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pinguicula orchidioides" target="butterwort">
  <data key="d5">["IS_A"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pinguicula orchidioides is a species of butterwort.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "A species of butterwort, it forms summer rosettes of flat, succulent leaves up to 5\tcentimeters (4\tin) long, which are covered in mucilagenous (sticky) glands that attract, trap, and digest arthropod prey.", "chunk_id": "1184555da09f3dbe", "doc_id": "hp_6a6940496f3fa2b9", "type": "IS_A"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6a6940496f3fa2b9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pinguicula orchidioides" target="arthropod prey">
  <data key="d5">["DIGESTS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pinguicula orchidioides digests arthropod prey using glands on its leaves.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "A species of butterwort, it forms summer rosettes of flat, succulent leaves up to 5\tcentimeters (4\tin) long, which are covered in mucilagenous (sticky) glands that attract, trap, and digest arthropod prey.", "chunk_id": "1184555da09f3dbe", "doc_id": "hp_6a6940496f3fa2b9", "type": "DIGESTS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6a6940496f3fa2b9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pinguicula orchidioides" target="Pinguicula">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pinguicula orchidioides is a species within the Pinguicula genus from the Americas.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Uniquely among \"Pinguicula\" species from the Americas, \"p. orchidioides\" produces gemma-like basal buds which elongate into stolons and serve as a means of asexual reproduction.", "chunk_id": "1184555da09f3dbe", "doc_id": "hp_6a6940496f3fa2b9", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6a6940496f3fa2b9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pinguicula orchidioides" target="gemma-like basal buds">
  <data key="d5">["PRODUCES"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pinguicula orchidioides produces gemma-like basal buds.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Uniquely among \"Pinguicula\" species from the Americas, \"p. orchidioides\" produces gemma-like basal buds which elongate into stolons and serve as a means of asexual reproduction.", "chunk_id": "1184555da09f3dbe", "doc_id": "hp_6a6940496f3fa2b9", "type": "PRODUCES"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6a6940496f3fa2b9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pinguicula orchidioides" target="purple flowers">
  <data key="d5">["PRODUCES"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pinguicula orchidioides produces single purple flowers.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Single purple flowers appear between July and September on upright stalks up to 22 centimeters long.", "chunk_id": "1184555da09f3dbe", "doc_id": "hp_6a6940496f3fa2b9", "type": "PRODUCES"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6a6940496f3fa2b9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="gemma-like basal buds" target="stolons">
