</edge>
<edge source="Ibutilide" target="sinus rhythm">
  <data key="d5">["INDICATED_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Ibutilide is indicated for the conversion of atrial fibrillation and flutter to sinus rhythm.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Ibutilide is a Class III antiarrhythmic agent that is indicated for acute cardioconversion of atrial fibrillation and atrial flutter of a recent onset to sinus rhythm.", "chunk_id": "768d5a792dd04c0c", "doc_id": "hp_6db35b9eeaff2803", "type": "INDICATED_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6db35b9eeaff2803</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Ibutilide" target="slow inward sodium current">
  <data key="d5">["INDUCES"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Ibutilide exerts its antiarrhythmic effect by inducing a slow inward sodium current.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It exerts its antiarrhythmic effect by induction of slow inward sodium current, which prolongs action potential and refractory period (physiology) of myocardial cells.", "chunk_id": "768d5a792dd04c0c", "doc_id": "hp_6db35b9eeaff2803", "type": "INDUCES"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6db35b9eeaff2803</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Ibutilide" target="Class Ia agents">
  <data key="d5">["CONTRAINDICATED_WITH"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Ibutilide should not be administered concomitantly with Class Ia agents.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Because of its Class III antiarrhythmic activity, there should not be concomitant administration of Class Ia and Class III agents.", "chunk_id": "768d5a792dd04c0c", "doc_id": "hp_6db35b9eeaff2803", "type": "CONTRAINDICATED_WITH"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6db35b9eeaff2803</data>
</edge>
