  <data key="d5">["MASS_COMPARISON"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The mass of M33 X-7 is compared to the mass of the Sun.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "M33 X-7 is the largest known stellar black hole with an estimated mass of 15.65 times that of the Sun (M ).", "chunk_id": "b630ca764564e39f", "doc_id": "hp_6ffa173614708165", "type": "MASS_COMPARISON"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6ffa173614708165</data>
</edge>
<edge source="black hole binary system" target="stellar mass black hole">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">A black hole binary system consists of a stellar mass black hole.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The system is made up of a stellar mass black hole and a companion star.", "chunk_id": "b630ca764564e39f", "doc_id": "hp_6ffa173614708165", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6ffa173614708165</data>
</edge>
<edge source="black hole binary system" target="companion star">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">A black hole binary system includes a companion star.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The system is made up of a stellar mass black hole and a companion star.", "chunk_id": "b630ca764564e39f", "doc_id": "hp_6ffa173614708165", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_6ffa173614708165</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fiddlin' Arthur Smith" target="Beautiful Brown Eyes">
  <data key="d5">["ARRANGED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Fiddlin' Arthur Smith arranged the song "Beautiful Brown Eyes".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"Beautiful Brown Eyes\" is a traditional country song arranged by Fiddlin' Arthur Smith &amp; Alton Delmore of The Delmore Brothers in 1951.", "chunk_id": "f73ede2e8ae064dc", "doc_id": "hp_7000ff84f5efb48f", "type": "ARRANGED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_7000ff84f5efb48f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Alton Delmore" target="Beautiful Brown Eyes">
  <data key="d5">["ARRANGED", "RECEIVED_AWARD_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Alton Delmore arranged the song "Beautiful Brown Eyes".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"Beautiful Brown Eyes\" is a traditional country song arranged by Fiddlin' Arthur Smith &amp; Alton Delmore of The Delmore Brothers in 1951.", "chunk_id": "f73ede2e8ae064dc", "doc_id": "hp_7000ff84f5efb48f", "type": "ARRANGED"}, {"text": "An award was presented to Alton Delmore for \"Beautiful Brown Eyes\" in 1951.", "chunk_id": "f73ede2e8ae064dc", "doc_id": "hp_7000ff84f5efb48f", "type": "RECEIVED_AWARD_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_7000ff84f5efb48f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="The Delmore Brothers" target="Beautiful Brown Eyes">
  <data key="d5">["ASSOCIATED_WITH"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Delmore Brothers are associated with the arrangement of "Beautiful Brown Eyes".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"Beautiful Brown Eyes\" is a traditional country song arranged by Fiddlin' Arthur Smith &amp; Alton Delmore of The Delmore Brothers in 1951.", "chunk_id": "f73ede2e8ae064dc", "doc_id": "hp_7000ff84f5efb48f", "type": "ASSOCIATED_WITH"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_7000ff84f5efb48f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Penrose process" target="Roger Penrose">
  <data key="d5">["THEORIZED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Penrose process was theorised by Roger Penrose.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The Penrose process (also called Penrose mechanism) is a process theorised by Roger Penrose wherein energy can be extracted from a rotating black hole.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "THEORIZED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Penrose process" target="rotating black hole">
  <data key="d5">["EXTRACTS_ENERGY_FROM"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Penrose process is a method for extracting energy from a rotating black hole.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The Penrose process (also called Penrose mechanism) is a process theorised by Roger Penrose wherein energy can be extracted from a rotating black hole.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "EXTRACTS_ENERGY_FROM"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Penrose process" target="ergosphere">
  <data key="d5">["INVOLVES"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Penrose process involves the ergosphere of a rotating black hole.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "That extraction is made possible because the rotational energy of the black hole is located not inside the event horizon of the black hole, but on the outside of it in a region of the Kerr spacetime called the ergosphere, a region in which a particle is necessarily propelled in locomotive concurrence with the rotating spacetime.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "INVOLVES"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Penrose process" target="energy">
  <data key="d5">["RESULTS_IN_EXTRACTION_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Penrose process results in the extraction of energy.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Although momentum is conserved the effect is that more energy can be extracted than was originally provided, the difference being provided by the black hole itself.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "RESULTS_IN_EXTRACTION_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Penrose process" target="angular momentum">
  <data key="d5">["RESULTS_IN_DECREASE_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Penrose process results in a slight decrease in the angular momentum of the black hole.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In summary, the process results in a slight decrease in the angular momentum of the black hole, which corresponds to a transference of energy to the matter.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "RESULTS_IN_DECREASE_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Penrose mechanism" target="Roger Penrose">
  <data key="d5">["THEORIZED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Penrose mechanism was theorised by Roger Penrose.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The Penrose process (also called Penrose mechanism) is a process theorised by Roger Penrose wherein energy can be extracted from a rotating black hole.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "THEORIZED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ergosphere" target="Kerr spacetime">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The ergosphere is a region within the Kerr spacetime.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "That extraction is made possible because the rotational energy of the black hole is located not inside the event horizon of the black hole, but on the outside of it in a region of the Kerr spacetime called the ergosphere, a region in which a particle is necessarily propelled in locomotive concurrence with the rotating spacetime.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ergosphere" target="event horizon">
  <data key="d5">["OUTSIDE_OF", "TOUCHES"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The ergosphere is located outside the event horizon of a rotating black hole.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "That extraction is made possible because the rotational energy of the black hole is located not inside the event horizon of the black hole, but on the outside of it in a region of the Kerr spacetime called the ergosphere, a region in which a particle is necessarily propelled in locomotive concurrence with the rotating spacetime.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "OUTSIDE_OF"}, {"text": "The ergosphere touches the event horizon at the poles of a rotating black hole and extends to a greater radius at the equator.", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0", "type": "TOUCHES"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ergosphere" target="rotating spacetime">
  <data key="d5">["DRAGGED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Objects in the ergosphere are dragged by the rotating spacetime.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "All objects in the ergosphere become dragged by a rotating spacetime.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "DRAGGED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ergosphere" target="black hole">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The ergosphere is a region located outside a rotating black hole's outer event horizon.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The ergosphere is a region located outside a rotating black hole's outer event horizon.", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e09ae53df97c48d0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ergosphere" target="Remo Ruffini">
  <data key="d5">["PROPOSED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Remo Ruffini proposed the name 'ergosphere'.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Its name was proposed by Remo Ruffini and John Archibald Wheeler during the Les Houches lectures in 1971 and is derived from the Greek word \"ergon\", which means \"work\".", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0", "type": "PROPOSED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e09ae53df97c48d0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ergosphere" target="John Archibald Wheeler">
  <data key="d5">["PROPOSED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">John Archibald Wheeler proposed the name 'ergosphere'.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Its name was proposed by Remo Ruffini and John Archibald Wheeler during the Les Houches lectures in 1971 and is derived from the Greek word \"ergon\", which means \"work\".", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0", "type": "PROPOSED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e09ae53df97c48d0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ergosphere" target="Les Houches lectures">
  <data key="d5">["INTRODUCED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The name 'ergosphere' was proposed during the Les Houches lectures.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Its name was proposed by Remo Ruffini and John Archibald Wheeler during the Les Houches lectures in 1971 and is derived from the Greek word \"ergon\", which means \"work\".", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0", "type": "INTRODUCED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e09ae53df97c48d0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ergosphere" target="ergon">
  <data key="d5">["DERIVED_FROM"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The name 'ergosphere' is derived from the Greek word 'ergon'.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Its name was proposed by Remo Ruffini and John Archibald Wheeler during the Les Houches lectures in 1971 and is derived from the Greek word \"ergon\", which means \"work\".", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0", "type": "DERIVED_FROM"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e09ae53df97c48d0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ergosphere" target="Schwarzschild radius">
  <data key="d5">["CORRESPONDS_TO", "RELATED_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The equatorial radius of an ergosphere corresponds to the Schwarzschild radius of a non-rotating black hole.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The equatorial (maximum) radius of an ergosphere corresponds to the Schwarzschild radius of a non-rotating black hole; the polar (minimum) radius can be as little as half the Schwarzschild radius (the radius of a non-rotating black hole) in the case that the black hole is rotating maximally (at higher rotation rates the black hole could not have formed).", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0", "type": "CORRESPONDS_TO"}, {"text": "The equatorial (maximum) radius of an ergosphere corresponds to the Schwarzschild radius of a non-rotating black hole; the polar (minimum) radius can be as little as half the Schwarzschild radius (the radius of a non-rotating black hole) in the case that the black hole is rotating maximally (at higher rotation rates the black hole could not have formed).", "chunk_id": "e1493fe4a7e31d6c", "doc_id": "hp_e09ae53df97c48d0", "type": "RELATED_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e09ae53df97c48d0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="lump of matter" target="ergosphere">
  <data key="d5">["ENTERS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">A lump of matter enters the ergosphere of a black hole.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In the process, a lump of matter enters into the ergosphere of the black hole, and once it enters the ergosphere, it is forcibly split into two parts.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "ENTERS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="lump of matter" target="two parts">
  <data key="d5">["SPLIT_INTO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The lump of matter is forcibly split into two parts once it enters the ergosphere.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In the process, a lump of matter enters into the ergosphere of the black hole, and once it enters the ergosphere, it is forcibly split into two parts.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "SPLIT_INTO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="two parts" target="explosive or rocket">
  <data key="d5">["SEPARATED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The two parts of the matter can be separated by firing an explosive or rocket.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "For example, the matter might be made of two parts that separate by firing an explosive or rocket which pushes its halves apart.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "SEPARATED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="momentum" target="energy">
  <data key="d5">["CONVERTED_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The momentum lost in the Penrose process is converted to energy extracted.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The momentum lost is converted to energy extracted.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "CONVERTED_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="escaping piece of matter" target="original piece of matter">
  <data key="d5">["GREATER_MASS_ENERGY_THAN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The escaping piece of matter can be made to have greater mass-energy than the original piece of matter.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "With careful arrangement, the escaping piece of matter can be made to have greater mass-energy than the original piece of matter, and the infalling piece has negative mass-energy.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "GREATER_MASS_ENERGY_THAN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="infalling piece" target="original piece of matter">
  <data key="d5">["HAS_NEGATIVE_MASS_ENERGY_COMPARED_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The infalling piece has negative mass-energy, in contrast to the original piece of matter.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "With careful arrangement, the escaping piece of matter can be made to have greater mass-energy than the original piece of matter, and the infalling piece has negative mass-energy.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "HAS_NEGATIVE_MASS_ENERGY_COMPARED_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="infalling piece" target="negative mass-energy">
  <data key="d5">["HAS_PROPERTY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The infalling piece has negative mass-energy.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "With careful arrangement, the escaping piece of matter can be made to have greater mass-energy than the original piece of matter, and the infalling piece has negative mass-energy.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "HAS_PROPERTY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="angular momentum" target="energy">
  <data key="d5">["CORRESPONDS_TO_TRANSFERENCE_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The decrease in angular momentum corresponds to a transference of energy to the matter.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In summary, the process results in a slight decrease in the angular momentum of the black hole, which corresponds to a transference of energy to the matter.", "chunk_id": "23b2ee36b2a2b6a0", "doc_id": "hp_704af24e111af685", "type": "CORRESPONDS_TO_TRANSFERENCE_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_704af24e111af685</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Camel" target="Camelus">
  <data key="d5">["BELONGS_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">A camel belongs to the genus Camelus.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "A camel is an even-toed ungulate in the genus Camelus, bearing distinctive fatty deposits known as \"humps\" on its back.", "chunk_id": "0f4c26b19727d970", "doc_id": "hp_706e5d69c6cb6d2b", "type": "BELONGS_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_706e5d69c6cb6d2b</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dromedary" target="C. dromedarius">
  <data key="d5">["IS_A"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The dromedary is also known as C. dromedarius.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The three surviving species of camel are the dromedary, or one-humped camel (\"C. dromedarius\"), which inhabits the Middle East and the Horn of Africa; the Bactrian, or two-humped camel (\"C. bactrianus\"), which inhabits Central Asia; and the critically endangered wild Bactrian camel (\"C. ferus\") that has limited populations in remote areas of northwest China and Mongolia.", "chunk_id": "0f4c26b19727d970", "doc_id": "hp_706e5d69c6cb6d2b", "type": "IS_A"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_706e5d69c6cb6d2b</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dromedary" target="Middle East">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The dromedary inhabits the Middle East.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The three surviving species of camel are the dromedary, or one-humped camel (\"C. dromedarius\"), which inhabits the Middle East and the Horn of Africa; the Bactrian, or two-humped camel (\"C. bactrianus\"), which inhabits Central Asia; and the critically endangered wild Bactrian camel (\"C. ferus\") that has limited populations in remote areas of northwest China and Mongolia.", "chunk_id": "0f4c26b19727d970", "doc_id": "hp_706e5d69c6cb6d2b", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_706e5d69c6cb6d2b</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dromedary" target="Horn of Africa">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The dromedary inhabits the Horn of Africa.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The three surviving species of camel are the dromedary, or one-humped camel (\"C. dromedarius\"), which inhabits the Middle East and the Horn of Africa; the Bactrian, or two-humped camel (\"C. bactrianus\"), which inhabits Central Asia; and the critically endangered wild Bactrian camel (\"C. ferus\") that has limited populations in remote areas of northwest China and Mongolia.", "chunk_id": "0f4c26b19727d970", "doc_id": "hp_706e5d69c6cb6d2b", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_706e5d69c6cb6d2b</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Bactrian" target="C. bactrianus">
  <data key="d5">["IS_A"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Bactrian camel is also known as C. bactrianus.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The three surviving species of camel are the dromedary, or one-humped camel (\"C. dromedarius\"), which inhabits the Middle East and the Horn of Africa; the Bactrian, or two-humped camel (\"C. bactrianus\"), which inhabits Central Asia; and the critically endangered wild Bactrian camel (\"C. ferus\") that has limited populations in remote areas of northwest China and Mongolia.", "chunk_id": "0f4c26b19727d970", "doc_id": "hp_706e5d69c6cb6d2b", "type": "IS_A"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_706e5d69c6cb6d2b</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Bactrian" target="Central Asia">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Bactrian camel inhabits Central Asia.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The three surviving species of camel are the dromedary, or one-humped camel (\"C. dromedarius\"), which inhabits the Middle East and the Horn of Africa; the Bactrian, or two-humped camel (\"C. bactrianus\"), which inhabits Central Asia; and the critically endangered wild Bactrian camel (\"C. ferus\") that has limited populations in remote areas of northwest China and Mongolia.", "chunk_id": "0f4c26b19727d970", "doc_id": "hp_706e5d69c6cb6d2b", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_706e5d69c6cb6d2b</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Library technician" target="Librarians">
  <data key="d5">["ASSISTS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Library technicians assist librarians in the acquisition, preparation, and organization of information.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "A library technician or library assistant is a skilled library and information professional trained to perform the day-to-day functions of a library, and assists librarians in the acquisition, preparation, and organization of information.", "chunk_id": "2f47939c7061409f", "doc_id": "hp_708a5f62a130daf5", "type": "ASSISTS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_708a5f62a130daf5</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Library technician" target="Library patrons">
  <data key="d5">["ASSISTS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Library technicians assist library patrons in finding information.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "They also assist library patrons in finding information.", "chunk_id": "2f47939c7061409f", "doc_id": "hp_708a5f62a130daf5", "type": "ASSISTS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_708a5f62a130daf5</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Library technician" target="Technical services">
  <data key="d5">["HANDLES"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Library technicians assist in the handling of technical services.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The widespread use of computerized information storage and retrieval systems has resulted in library technicians assisting in the handling of technical services (such as cataloguing) that were once performed exclusively by librarians.", "chunk_id": "2f47939c7061409f", "doc_id": "hp_708a5f62a130daf5", "type": "HANDLES"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_708a5f62a130daf5</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Library technician" target="Small village libraries">
  <data key="d5">["STAFFS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">A library technician may be the only person staffing a small village library.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Especially in small village libraries, a library technician may be the only person (or one of only a few) staffing the library.", "chunk_id": "2f47939c7061409f", "doc_id": "hp_708a5f62a130daf5", "type": "STAFFS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_708a5f62a130daf5</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Library technician" target="Larger libraries">
  <data key="d5">["WORKS_AT"]</data>
  <data key="d6">In larger libraries, library technicians may help run departments.</data>
