  <data key="d5">["PRODUCED_AS_ALTERNATIVE_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">National Geographic Explorer was produced as a less costly and intensive alternative to PBS's "National Geographic Specials".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "National Geographic Explorer (or simply Explorer) is an American documentary television series that originally premiered on Nickelodeon on April 7, 1985, after having been produced as a less costly and intensive alternative to PBS's \"National Geographic Specials\" by Pittsburgh station WQED.", "chunk_id": "f810a5fb38ef5d82", "doc_id": "hp_7baec64414b3f113", "type": "PRODUCED_AS_ALTERNATIVE_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_7baec64414b3f113</data>
</edge>
<edge source="National Geographic Explorer" target="WQED">
  <data key="d5">["PRODUCED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">National Geographic Explorer was produced by Pittsburgh station WQED.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "National Geographic Explorer (or simply Explorer) is an American documentary television series that originally premiered on Nickelodeon on April 7, 1985, after having been produced as a less costly and intensive alternative to PBS's \"National Geographic Specials\" by Pittsburgh station WQED.", "chunk_id": "f810a5fb38ef5d82", "doc_id": "hp_7baec64414b3f113", "type": "PRODUCED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_7baec64414b3f113</data>
</edge>
<edge source="National Geographic Explorer" target="National Geographic Society">
  <data key="d5">["PRODUCED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The premiere of National Geographic Explorer required an increase in production from the National Geographic Society.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Although the National Geographic Society had been producing specials for television for 20 years prior to \"Explorer\", the premiere of the series required an increase in production from 4 hours of programming a year to 156 hours.", "chunk_id": "f810a5fb38ef5d82", "doc_id": "hp_7baec64414b3f113", "type": "PRODUCED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_7baec64414b3f113</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Herculaneum: Voices from the Past" target="WQED">
  <data key="d5">["PRODUCED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The first episode, "Herculaneum: Voices from the Past", was produced by WQED.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The first episode (\"Herculaneum: Voices from the Past\") was produced by WQED and featured long-time \"Explorer\" camerman Mark Knobil, who is the few staff members with the franchise during all 24 seasons.", "chunk_id": "f810a5fb38ef5d82", "doc_id": "hp_7baec64414b3f113", "type": "PRODUCED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_7baec64414b3f113</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Herculaneum: Voices from the Past" target="Mark Knobil">
