<edge source="Rose Mary Woods" target="Richard Nixon">
  <data key="d5">["WORKS_AT", "GATEKEEPER_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Rose Mary Woods was Richard Nixon's secretary.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Rose Mary Woods (December 26, 1917 – January 22, 2005) was Richard Nixon's secretary from his days in Congress in 1951, through the end of his political career.", "chunk_id": "7a98a826c469ba66", "doc_id": "hp_866e1a0ee1799d1f", "type": "WORKS_AT"}, {"text": "Before H. R. Haldeman and John Ehrlichman became the operators of Nixon's presidential campaign, Woods was Nixon's gatekeeper.", "chunk_id": "7a98a826c469ba66", "doc_id": "hp_866e1a0ee1799d1f", "type": "GATEKEEPER_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_866e1a0ee1799d1f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="John Ehrlichman" target="Richard Nixon">
  <data key="d5">["OPERATED_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">John Ehrlichman was an operator of Nixon's presidential campaign.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Before H. R. Haldeman and John Ehrlichman became the operators of Nixon's presidential campaign, Woods was Nixon's gatekeeper.", "chunk_id": "7a98a826c469ba66", "doc_id": "hp_866e1a0ee1799d1f", "type": "OPERATED_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_866e1a0ee1799d1f</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Le baiser de la fée" target="Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky">
  <data key="d5">["HOMAGE_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">'Le baiser de la fée' is an homage to Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Based on Hans Christian Andersen's short story \"Isjomfruen\" (English: The Ice-Maiden), the work is an homage to Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky, for the 35th anniversary of the composer's death.", "chunk_id": "a78396980a135cb4", "doc_id": "hp_869cb734bf497707", "type": "HOMAGE_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_869cb734bf497707</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Le baiser de la fée" target="Paris">
  <data key="d5">["PREMIERED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">'Le baiser de la fée' premiered in Paris.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "A commission by Ida Rubinstein from 1927, the ballet was choreographed by Bronislava Nijinska and premiered in Paris on 27 November 1928.", "chunk_id": "a78396980a135cb4", "doc_id": "hp_869cb734bf497707", "type": "PREMIERED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_869cb734bf497707</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Igor Stravinsky" target="Le baiser de la fée">
  <data key="d5">["COMPOSED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Igor Stravinsky composed 'Le baiser de la fée'.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Le baiser de la fée (\"The Fairy's Kiss\") is a ballet in one act and four scenes composed by Igor Stravinsky in 1928 and revised in 1950 for George Balanchine and the New York City Ballet.", "chunk_id": "a78396980a135cb4", "doc_id": "hp_869cb734bf497707", "type": "COMPOSED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_869cb734bf497707</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Igor Stravinsky" target="Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky">
  <data key="d5">["USED_MELODIES_FROM"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Igor Stravinsky used melodies from Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky's early piano pieces and songs in his score.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Stravinsky elaborated several melodies from early piano pieces and songs by Tchaikovsky in his score.", "chunk_id": "a78396980a135cb4", "doc_id": "hp_869cb734bf497707", "type": "USED_MELODIES_FROM"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_869cb734bf497707</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Igor Stravinsky" target="Apollo">
  <data key="d5">["COMPOSED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Igor Stravinsky composed the ballet Apollo.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Apollo (originally Apollon musagète and variously known as \"Apollo musagetes\", \"Apolo Musageta\", and \"Apollo, Leader of the Muses\") is a ballet in two tableaux composed between 1927 and 1928 by Igor Stravinsky.", "chunk_id": "7d4e3a512ec3ac2c", "doc_id": "hp_9db3a175e11b24ac", "type": "COMPOSED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_9db3a175e11b24ac</data>
</edge>
