<edge source="Pam Teeguarden" target="Chris Evert">
  <data key="d5">["RECORD_HELD_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pam Teeguarden held the record for consecutive US Opens until Chris Evert surpassed it.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Teeguarden played in 19 consecutive US Opens, holding the record until Chris Evert played in 20.", "chunk_id": "b07f6a48318ea8c0", "doc_id": "hp_8e9d4247e8ae3a7a", "type": "RECORD_HELD_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_8e9d4247e8ae3a7a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pam Teeguarden" target="Nike">
  <data key="d5">["SIGNED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pam Teeguarden was the first woman tennis player signed by Nike.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Teeguarden was the first woman tennis player signed by Nike.", "chunk_id": "b07f6a48318ea8c0", "doc_id": "hp_8e9d4247e8ae3a7a", "type": "SIGNED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_8e9d4247e8ae3a7a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pam Teeguarden" target="Los Angeles Strings Team Tennis team">
  <data key="d5">["MEMBER_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pam Teeguarden was a member of the victorious Los Angeles Strings Team Tennis team in 1981.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "She played on the victorious Los Angeles Strings Team Tennis team in 1981 and won the Team Tennis Mixed Doubles Division with Tom Gullikson in 1977; they were also runners-up in the league that year.", "chunk_id": "b07f6a48318ea8c0", "doc_id": "hp_8e9d4247e8ae3a7a", "type": "MEMBER_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_8e9d4247e8ae3a7a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pam Teeguarden" target="Tom Gullikson">
  <data key="d5">["PARTNERED_WITH"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pam Teeguarden won the Team Tennis Mixed Doubles Division with Tom Gullikson in 1977.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "She played on the victorious Los Angeles Strings Team Tennis team in 1981 and won the Team Tennis Mixed Doubles Division with Tom Gullikson in 1977; they were also runners-up in the league that year.", "chunk_id": "b07f6a48318ea8c0", "doc_id": "hp_8e9d4247e8ae3a7a", "type": "PARTNERED_WITH"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_8e9d4247e8ae3a7a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pam Teeguarden" target="The French Open">
  <data key="d5">["PARTICIPATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pam Teeguarden was a quarter finalist in singles at The French Open.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "She won two Grand Slam Doubles Titles and was a quarter finalist in singles at the U.S. Open and The French Open.", "chunk_id": "b07f6a48318ea8c0", "doc_id": "hp_8e9d4247e8ae3a7a", "type": "PARTICIPATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_8e9d4247e8ae3a7a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pam Teeguarden" target="The Bridgestone Doubles Championships">
  <data key="d5">["PARTICIPATED_IN"]</data>
