<edge source="Extreme mass ratio inspiral" target="gravitational waves">
  <data key="d5">["CAUSES"]</data>
  <data key="d6">An extreme mass ratio inspiral decays due the emission of gravitational waves.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In astrophysics, an extreme mass ratio inspiral (EMRI) is the orbit of a relatively light object around a much heavier (by a factor 10,000 or more) object, that gradually decays due the emission of gravitational waves.", "chunk_id": "85874c3e24dbd553", "doc_id": "hp_9ef7f82d0f1702ec", "type": "CAUSES"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_9ef7f82d0f1702ec</data>
</edge>
<edge source="stellar mass compact objects" target="centers of galaxies">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Stellar mass compact objects are likely to be found in the centers of galaxies.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Such systems are likely to be found in the centers of galaxies, where stellar mass compact objects, such as stellar black holes and neutron stars, may be found orbiting a supermassive black hole.", "chunk_id": "85874c3e24dbd553", "doc_id": "hp_9ef7f82d0f1702ec", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_9ef7f82d0f1702ec</data>
</edge>
<edge source="stellar black holes" target="supermassive black hole">
  <data key="d5">["ORBITS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Stellar black holes may be found orbiting a supermassive black hole.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Such systems are likely to be found in the centers of galaxies, where stellar mass compact objects, such as stellar black holes and neutron stars, may be found orbiting a supermassive black hole.", "chunk_id": "85874c3e24dbd553", "doc_id": "hp_9ef7f82d0f1702ec", "type": "ORBITS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_9ef7f82d0f1702ec</data>
</edge>
<edge source="neutron stars" target="supermassive black hole">
  <data key="d5">["ORBITS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Neutron stars may be found orbiting a supermassive black hole.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Such systems are likely to be found in the centers of galaxies, where stellar mass compact objects, such as stellar black holes and neutron stars, may be found orbiting a supermassive black hole.", "chunk_id": "85874c3e24dbd553", "doc_id": "hp_9ef7f82d0f1702ec", "type": "ORBITS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_9ef7f82d0f1702ec</data>
</edge>
<edge source="EMRI" target="gravitational waveform">
  <data key="d5">["SHORTHAND_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The term EMRI is sometimes used as a shorthand to denote the emitted gravitational waveform.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The term EMRI is sometimes used as a shorthand to denote the emitted gravitational waveform as well as the orbit itself.", "chunk_id": "85874c3e24dbd553", "doc_id": "hp_9ef7f82d0f1702ec", "type": "SHORTHAND_FOR"}]</data>
