<edge source="Pterostyrax" target="Styracaceae">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pterostyrax is a genus within the Styracaceae family.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Pterostyrax, the epaulette tree, is a small genus of four species of deciduous large shrubs or small trees in the family Styracaceae, native to eastern Asia in China and Japan.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_a0fb254153ed3917</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pterostyrax" target="China">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pterostyrax is native to China.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Pterostyrax, the epaulette tree, is a small genus of four species of deciduous large shrubs or small trees in the family Styracaceae, native to eastern Asia in China and Japan.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_a0fb254153ed3917</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pterostyrax" target="Japan">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pterostyrax is native to Japan.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Pterostyrax, the epaulette tree, is a small genus of four species of deciduous large shrubs or small trees in the family Styracaceae, native to eastern Asia in China and Japan.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_a0fb254153ed3917</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pterostyrax" target="leaves">
  <data key="d5">["HAS_PART"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pterostyrax has leaves.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "They grow 4 - tall, with alternate, simple ovate leaves 6 - long and 4 - broad.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917", "type": "HAS_PART"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_a0fb254153ed3917</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pterostyrax" target="fruit">
  <data key="d5">["HAS_PART"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pterostyrax has fruit.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The fruit is an oblong dry drupe, with longitudinal ribs or narrow wings (the wings are absent in the related genus \"Styrax\", whence the name \"Pterostyrax\", \"winged styrax\").", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917", "type": "HAS_PART"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_a0fb254153ed3917</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pterostyrax" target="Styrax">
  <data key="d5">["RELATED_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pterostyrax is related to the genus Styrax.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The fruit is an oblong dry drupe, with longitudinal ribs or narrow wings (the wings are absent in the related genus \"Styrax\", whence the name \"Pterostyrax\", \"winged styrax\").", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917", "type": "RELATED_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_a0fb254153ed3917</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pterostyrax" target="flower">
  <data key="d5">["HAS_PART"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pterostyrax has flowers.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The flowers are white, produced in dense panicles 8 - long.", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917", "type": "HAS_PART"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_a0fb254153ed3917</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Styrax" target="fruit">
  <data key="d5">["HAS_PART"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Styrax has fruit, which lacks wings.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The fruit is an oblong dry drupe, with longitudinal ribs or narrow wings (the wings are absent in the related genus \"Styrax\", whence the name \"Pterostyrax\", \"winged styrax\").", "chunk_id": "0ae20fe970e7c14c", "doc_id": "hp_a0fb254153ed3917", "type": "HAS_PART"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_a0fb254153ed3917</data>
</edge>
