<edge source="Gibraltar Nature Reserve" target="British Overseas Territory of Gibraltar">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Gibraltar Nature Reserve is located within the British Overseas Territory of Gibraltar.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The Gibraltar Nature Reserve (formerly the Upper Rock Nature Reserve) is a protected nature reserve in the British Overseas Territory of Gibraltar that covers over 40% of the country's land area.", "chunk_id": "b2cecb19f962314a", "doc_id": "hp_a2873cfc53097a81", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_a2873cfc53097a81</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Gibraltar Nature Reserve" target="Barbary macaques">
  <data key="d5">["HAS_POPULATION"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Gibraltar Nature Reserve is known for its population of Barbary macaques.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It is known for its semi-wild population of Barbary macaques, and is an important resting point for migrating birds.", "chunk_id": "b2cecb19f962314a", "doc_id": "hp_a2873cfc53097a81", "type": "HAS_POPULATION"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_a2873cfc53097a81</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Upper Rock Nature Reserve" target="International Union for Conservation of Nature">
  <data key="d5">["ESTABLISHED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Upper Rock Nature Reserve was established by the International Union for Conservation of Nature.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It was established as the Upper Rock Nature Reserve in 1993 under the International Union for Conservation of Nature's category Ia (strict nature reserve) and was last extended in 2013.", "chunk_id": "b2cecb19f962314a", "doc_id": "hp_a2873cfc53097a81", "type": "ESTABLISHED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_a2873cfc53097a81</data>
</edge>
