<edge source="Ulf Merbold" target="Sigmund Jähn">
  <data key="d5">["PRECEDED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Sigmund Jähn was the first German native to fly in space, and Ulf Merbold was the second.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Dr. Ulf Dietrich Merbold (born June 20, 1941) is the first West German citizen and second German native (after Sigmund Jähn) to have flown in space.", "chunk_id": "1dda59241bb9cd52", "doc_id": "hp_cc1f6a95f8e649b8", "type": "PRECEDED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_cc1f6a95f8e649b8</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Ulf Merbold" target="European Space Agency Astronaut Corps">
  <data key="d5">["MEMBER_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Ulf Merbold is a member of the European Space Agency Astronaut Corps.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "He is also the first member of the European Space Agency Astronaut Corps to participate in a spaceflight mission and the first non-US citizen to reach orbit in a US spacecraft.", "chunk_id": "1dda59241bb9cd52", "doc_id": "hp_cc1f6a95f8e649b8", "type": "MEMBER_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_cc1f6a95f8e649b8</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Ulf Merbold" target="Byron Lichtenberg">
  <data key="d5">["PARTNERED_WITH"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Ulf Merbold and Byron Lichtenberg flew together as Payload Specialists in 1983.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In 1983, he and Byron Lichtenberg became the first Payload Specialists to fly on the shuttle.", "chunk_id": "1dda59241bb9cd52", "doc_id": "hp_cc1f6a95f8e649b8", "type": "PARTNERED_WITH"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_cc1f6a95f8e649b8</data>
</edge>
