<edge source="Paul Anka" target="This Is It (Michael Jackson song)">
  <data key="d5">["CO_WROTE"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Paul Anka co-wrote the song "This Is It".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"This Is It\" is a song co-written by American pop star and musician Michael Jackson and Canadian singer-songwriter Paul Anka.", "chunk_id": "8fc2541873625ab9", "doc_id": "hp_aba1d192473010be", "type": "CO_WROTE"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_aba1d192473010be</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Paul Anka" target="Walk a Fine Line (album)">
  <data key="d5">["RECORDED_ON"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Paul Anka intended to record a duet with Michael Jackson on his album "Walk a Fine Line".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "According to Anka, the song was recorded in 1983 and intended to be a duet between him and Jackson on Anka's \"Walk a Fine Line\" album under the title \"I Never Heard\", but these plans fell through.", "chunk_id": "8fc2541873625ab9", "doc_id": "hp_aba1d192473010be", "type": "RECORDED_ON"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_aba1d192473010be</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Paul Anka" target="Duets (album)">
  <data key="d5">["RELEASED_ON"]</data>
  <data key="d6">A duet version of the song "This Is It" was featured on Paul Anka's "Duets" album.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The duet version of the song was featured in Anka's 2013 \"Duets\" album.", "chunk_id": "8fc2541873625ab9", "doc_id": "hp_aba1d192473010be", "type": "RELEASED_ON"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_aba1d192473010be</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Paul Anka" target="Jackson's estate">
  <data key="d5">["THREATENED_LEGAL_ACTION_AGAINST"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Paul Anka threatened legal action against Jackson's estate immediately after the song's release.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Immediately after its release, Anka threatened legal action against Jackson's estate.", "chunk_id": "8fc2541873625ab9", "doc_id": "hp_aba1d192473010be", "type": "THREATENED_LEGAL_ACTION_AGAINST"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_aba1d192473010be</data>
</edge>
<edge source="This Is It (album)" target="Michael Jackson's This Is It">
  <data key="d5">["ACCOMPANIES"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The album "This Is It" accompanies the concert documentary "Michael Jackson's This Is It".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The song was recorded by the former and featured as a track on the album, \"This Is It\" (2009), which accompanies the 2009 concert documentary \"Michael Jackson's This Is It\".", "chunk_id": "8fc2541873625ab9", "doc_id": "hp_aba1d192473010be", "type": "ACCOMPANIES"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_aba1d192473010be</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sa-Fire" target="I Wasn't Born Yesterday (album)">
  <data key="d5">["RECORDED_ON"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Sa-Fire recorded the track "This Is It" on her album "I Wasn't Born Yesterday".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Thereafter, Sa-Fire recorded the track for her album, \"I Wasn't Born Yesterday\" (1991).", "chunk_id": "8fc2541873625ab9", "doc_id": "hp_aba1d192473010be", "type": "RECORDED_ON"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_aba1d192473010be</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Jackson's estate" target="Paul Anka">
  <data key="d5">["AGREED_TO_GIVE_PUBLISHING_RIGHTS_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Jackson's estate agreed to give Paul Anka 50% of the song's publishing rights.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The estate then agreed to give Anka 50% of the song's publishing rights.", "chunk_id": "8fc2541873625ab9", "doc_id": "hp_aba1d192473010be", "type": "AGREED_TO_GIVE_PUBLISHING_RIGHTS_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_aba1d192473010be</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sonatas and Interludes" target="prepared piano">
  <data key="d5">["FOR", "IS_A_WORK_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Sonatas and Interludes is a collection of pieces for prepared piano.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Sonatas and Interludes is a collection of twenty pieces for prepared piano by American avant-garde composer John Cage (1912–1992).", "chunk_id": "46e2753873dd1884", "doc_id": "hp_abe4b15111caba47", "type": "FOR"}, {"text": "In the liner notes for the very first recording of his most highly acclaimed work for prepared piano, \"Sonatas and Interludes\", Cage wrote: \"Composing for the prepared piano is not a criticism of the instrument.", "chunk_id": "b7f8e7da447a5f1c", "doc_id": "hp_e9f272e0c789745f", "type": "IS_A_WORK_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_abe4b15111caba47</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Sonatas and Interludes" target="John Cage">
  <data key="d5">["ACHIEVEMENT_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Sonatas and Interludes is recognized as one of John Cage's finest achievements.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"Sonatas and Interludes\" is generally recognized as one of Cage's finest achievements.", "chunk_id": "46e2753873dd1884", "doc_id": "hp_abe4b15111caba47", "type": "ACHIEVEMENT_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_abe4b15111caba47</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Indian philosophy" target="John Cage">
  <data key="d5">["MAJOR_INFLUENCE_ON"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Indian philosophy became a major influence on John Cage's later work.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It was composed in 1946–48, shortly after Cage's introduction to Indian philosophy and the teachings of art historian Ananda K. Coomaraswamy, both of which became major influences on the composer's later work.", "chunk_id": "46e2753873dd1884", "doc_id": "hp_abe4b15111caba47", "type": "MAJOR_INFLUENCE_ON"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_abe4b15111caba47</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Ananda K. Coomaraswamy" target="John Cage">
  <data key="d5">["MAJOR_INFLUENCE_ON"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The teachings of Ananda K. Coomaraswamy became a major influence on John Cage's later work.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It was composed in 1946–48, shortly after Cage's introduction to Indian philosophy and the teachings of art historian Ananda K. Coomaraswamy, both of which became major influences on the composer's later work.", "chunk_id": "46e2753873dd1884", "doc_id": "hp_abe4b15111caba47", "type": "MAJOR_INFLUENCE_ON"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_abe4b15111caba47</data>
</edge>
