<edge source="Chinese" target="Sino-Tibetan languages">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Chinese is a variety of Sino-Tibetan languages.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The Sino-Tibetan languages with the most native speakers are the varieties of Chinese (1.3 billion speakers, the most of any language on Earth if counted as a single language), Burmese (33 million), and the Tibetic languages (8 million); but many Sino-Tibetan languages are spoken by small communities in remote mountain areas and as such are poorly documented.", "chunk_id": "8d2f0f99801ebf15", "doc_id": "hp_b4175e524ae4a823", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_b4175e524ae4a823</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Burmese" target="Sino-Tibetan languages">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Burmese is a Sino-Tibetan language.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The Sino-Tibetan languages with the most native speakers are the varieties of Chinese (1.3 billion speakers, the most of any language on Earth if counted as a single language), Burmese (33 million), and the Tibetic languages (8 million); but many Sino-Tibetan languages are spoken by small communities in remote mountain areas and as such are poorly documented.", "chunk_id": "8d2f0f99801ebf15", "doc_id": "hp_b4175e524ae4a823", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_b4175e524ae4a823</data>
</edge>
