<edge source="Nixon v. General Services Administration" target="presidential privilege">
  <data key="d5">["CONCERNS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The court case concerns the principle of presidential privilege.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Nixon v. General Services Administration, 433 U.S 425 (1977), is a landmark court case concerning the principle of presidential privilege and whether the public is allowed to view a President’s “confidential documents”.", "chunk_id": "011991db30ac2dac", "doc_id": "hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2", "type": "CONCERNS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Nixon v. General Services Administration" target="confidential documents">
  <data key="d5">["CONCERNS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The court case concerns whether the public is allowed to view a President’s confidential documents.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Nixon v. General Services Administration, 433 U.S 425 (1977), is a landmark court case concerning the principle of presidential privilege and whether the public is allowed to view a President’s “confidential documents”.", "chunk_id": "011991db30ac2dac", "doc_id": "hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2", "type": "CONCERNS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Presidential Recordings and Materials Preservation Act" target="President Gerald Ford">
  <data key="d5">["SIGNED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">President Gerald Ford signed the Presidential Recordings and Materials Preservation Act into law.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The Presidential Recordings and Materials Preservation Act, signed into law by President Gerald Ford in 1974, ordered that the Administrator of General Services obtain President Richard Nixon’s presidential papers and tape recordings.", "chunk_id": "011991db30ac2dac", "doc_id": "hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2", "type": "SIGNED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Presidential Recordings and Materials Preservation Act" target="Administrator of General Services">
  <data key="d5">["ORDERED_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Act ordered the Administrator of General Services to obtain President Richard Nixon’s presidential papers and tape recordings.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The Presidential Recordings and Materials Preservation Act, signed into law by President Gerald Ford in 1974, ordered that the Administrator of General Services obtain President Richard Nixon’s presidential papers and tape recordings.", "chunk_id": "011991db30ac2dac", "doc_id": "hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2", "type": "ORDERED_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Presidential Recordings and Materials Preservation Act" target="government archivists">
  <data key="d5">["ORDERED_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Act ordered government archivists to seize President Nixon's materials.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In addition, the Act further ordered that government archivists seize these materials.", "chunk_id": "011991db30ac2dac", "doc_id": "hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2", "type": "ORDERED_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Presidential Recordings and Materials Preservation Act" target="judicial hearings and proceedings">
  <data key="d5">["MATERIAL_COULD_BE_USED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Act stated that preserved material could be used in judicial hearings and proceedings.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Furthermore, this Act stated that material that was preserved could be used in judicial hearings and proceedings.", "chunk_id": "011991db30ac2dac", "doc_id": "hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2", "type": "MATERIAL_COULD_BE_USED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Administrator of General Services" target="President Richard Nixon">
  <data key="d5">["OBTAIN_MATERIALS_FROM"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Administrator of General Services was ordered to obtain President Richard Nixon’s presidential papers and tape recordings.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The Presidential Recordings and Materials Preservation Act, signed into law by President Gerald Ford in 1974, ordered that the Administrator of General Services obtain President Richard Nixon’s presidential papers and tape recordings.", "chunk_id": "011991db30ac2dac", "doc_id": "hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2", "type": "OBTAIN_MATERIALS_FROM"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="government archivists" target="historic">
  <data key="d5">["PRESERVE_MATERIAL_DEEMED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Government archivists would preserve the material deemed historic.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "These archivists would preserve the material deemed historic and return to former President Nixon the materials deemed as private.", "chunk_id": "011991db30ac2dac", "doc_id": "hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2", "type": "PRESERVE_MATERIAL_DEEMED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="government archivists" target="former President Nixon">
  <data key="d5">["RETURN_MATERIALS_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Government archivists would return materials deemed private to former President Nixon.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "These archivists would preserve the material deemed historic and return to former President Nixon the materials deemed as private.", "chunk_id": "011991db30ac2dac", "doc_id": "hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2", "type": "RETURN_MATERIALS_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_ba0b2efa73fa43d2</data>
</edge>
