<edge source="film art" target="North Korean cinema">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Film art is a component or aspect of North Korean cinema.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In recent years our film art has created an unprecedented sensation in the world's filmdom...", "chunk_id": "7cd59a2829630305", "doc_id": "hp_bb98f886833576c8", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_bb98f886833576c8</data>
</edge>
<edge source="feature film" target="film art">
  <data key="d5">["OTHER"]</data>
  <data key="d6">A feature film is a specific type of work within the broader category of film art.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The revolutionary people of the world are unstinting in their praise of this feature film and other monumental works, calling them 'the first-class films by international standards', 'the most wonderful movies ever produced' and 'immortal revolutionary and popular films'.", "chunk_id": "7cd59a2829630305", "doc_id": "hp_bb98f886833576c8", "type": "OTHER"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_bb98f886833576c8</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Garin de Monglane" target="Conrad von Stöffler">
  <data key="d5">["CREATED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Garin de Monglane was created by Conrad von Stöffler.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Garin de Monglane, or Montglane, is a fictional character created by Conrad von Stöffler in 1280.", "chunk_id": "bc44d364b9f11c58", "doc_id": "hp_bd117ea391b64dae", "type": "CREATED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_bd117ea391b64dae</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Garin de Monglane" target="Saracens">
  <data key="d5">["FOUGHT"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The character Garin de Monglane fought against the Saracens.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "His cycle tells stories of fiefless lads of noble birth who went off seeking land and adventure fighting the Saracens.", "chunk_id": "bc44d364b9f11c58", "doc_id": "hp_bd117ea391b64dae", "type": "FOUGHT"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_bd117ea391b64dae</data>
</edge>
<edge source="La Geste de Garin de Monglane" target="Garin de Monglane">
  <data key="d5">["NAMED_AFTER"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The cycle "La Geste de Garin de Monglane" is named after the character Garin de Monglane.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The character gives his name to the second cycle of Old French \"chansons de geste\", \"La Geste de Garin de Monglane\".", "chunk_id": "bc44d364b9f11c58", "doc_id": "hp_bd117ea391b64dae", "type": "NAMED_AFTER"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_bd117ea391b64dae</data>
</edge>
<edge source="La Geste de Garin de Monglane" target="chansons de geste">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The cycle "La Geste de Garin de Monglane" is part of the genre "chansons de geste".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The character gives his name to the second cycle of Old French \"chansons de geste\", \"La Geste de Garin de Monglane\".", "chunk_id": "bc44d364b9f11c58", "doc_id": "hp_bd117ea391b64dae", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_bd117ea391b64dae</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pollux Rock" target="Vindication Island">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pollux Rock is located south of Vindication Island.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Pollux Rock ( ) is the southern of a pair of large off-lying rocks south of Vindication Island, South Sandwich Islands.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pollux Rock" target="South Sandwich Islands">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pollux Rock is part of the South Sandwich Islands.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Pollux Rock ( ) is the southern of a pair of large off-lying rocks south of Vindication Island, South Sandwich Islands.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Pollux Rock" target="Castor and Pollux">
  <data key="d5">["PART_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Pollux Rock was one of the rocks named "Castor and Pollux".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "This rock, with its neighbor Castor Rock, was named \"Castor and Pollux\" during the survey of these islands from \"RRS Discovery II\" in 1930.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc", "type": "PART_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc</data>
</edge>
