<edge source="United Kingdom Antarctic Place-Names Committee (UK-APC)" target="Pollux Rock">
  <data key="d5">["RECOMMENDED_NAME_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The UK-APC recommended the name Pollux Rock for the southern rock.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In 1971 United Kingdom Antarctic Place-Names Committee (UK-APC) recommended that they be assigned unambiguous names making each individually identifiable, and this has been done by naming the southern one Pollux Rock and the northern one Castor Rock.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc", "type": "RECOMMENDED_NAME_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc</data>
</edge>
<edge source="United Kingdom Antarctic Place-Names Committee (UK-APC)" target="Castor Rock">
  <data key="d5">["RECOMMENDED_NAME_FOR"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The UK-APC recommended the name Castor Rock for the northern rock.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In 1971 United Kingdom Antarctic Place-Names Committee (UK-APC) recommended that they be assigned unambiguous names making each individually identifiable, and this has been done by naming the southern one Pollux Rock and the northern one Castor Rock.", "chunk_id": "5492b7c1b1697966", "doc_id": "hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc", "type": "RECOMMENDED_NAME_FOR"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_bd3863e9ad3c06bc</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Takanori Arisawa" target="Sailor Moon">
  <data key="d5">["COMPOSED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Takanori Arisawa composed the music for the "Sailor Moon" anime series.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Takanori Arisawa (有澤 孝紀 , Arisawa Takanori , April 2, 1951 – November 26, 2005) was a Japanese composer and arranger best known for composing the \"Sailor Moon\" anime series and \"Digimon\" series (Seasons 1-4).", "chunk_id": "a288b38bfb013c0a", "doc_id": "hp_be8748f7d316f7c3", "type": "COMPOSED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_be8748f7d316f7c3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Takanori Arisawa" target="Digimon">
  <data key="d5">["COMPOSED", "COMPOSED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Takanori Arisawa composed the music for the "Digimon" series (Seasons 1-4).</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Takanori Arisawa (有澤 孝紀 , Arisawa Takanori , April 2, 1951 – November 26, 2005) was a Japanese composer and arranger best known for composing the \"Sailor Moon\" anime series and \"Digimon\" series (Seasons 1-4).", "chunk_id": "a288b38bfb013c0a", "doc_id": "hp_be8748f7d316f7c3", "type": "COMPOSED"}, {"text": "After \"Sailor Moon\", Arisawa composed music for several shows, including the \"Digimon\" series, until his death from bladder cancer in 2005.", "chunk_id": "a288b38bfb013c0a", "doc_id": "hp_be8748f7d316f7c3", "type": "COMPOSED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_be8748f7d316f7c3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Takanori Arisawa" target="Tokyo">
  <data key="d5">["BORN_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Takanori Arisawa was born in Tokyo.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Born in Tokyo, Arisawa began to learn piano at the age of 20.", "chunk_id": "a288b38bfb013c0a", "doc_id": "hp_be8748f7d316f7c3", "type": "BORN_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_be8748f7d316f7c3</data>
