<edge source="Catan: Cities &amp; Knights" target="The Settlers of Catan">
  <data key="d5">["EXPANSION_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Catan: Cities &amp; Knights is an expansion to the board game The Settlers of Catan.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Catan: Cities &amp; Knights (German: \"Städte und Ritter\" ), formerly \"The Cities and Knights of Catan\" is an expansion to the board game \"The Settlers of Catan\" for three to four players (five to six player play is also possible with the \"Settlers\" and \"Cities &amp; Knights\" five to six player extensions; two-player play is possible with the \"\" expansion).", "chunk_id": "42769d289195cfc3", "doc_id": "hp_c20f6b270e53f1ff", "type": "EXPANSION_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_c20f6b270e53f1ff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Catan: Cities &amp; Knights" target="city development">
  <data key="d5">["EMPHASIS_ON"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Catan: Cities &amp; Knights places emphasis on city development.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It contains features taken from \"The Settlers of Catan\", with emphasis on city development and the use of knights, which are used as a method of attacking other players as well as helping opponents defend Catan against a common foe.", "chunk_id": "42769d289195cfc3", "doc_id": "hp_c20f6b270e53f1ff", "type": "EMPHASIS_ON"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_c20f6b270e53f1ff</data>
</edge>
