<edge source="Emerald ash borer" target="northeastern Asia">
  <data key="d5">["NATIVE_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The emerald ash borer is native to northeastern Asia.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Agrilus planipennis, commonly known as the emerald ash borer, is a green buprestid or jewel beetle native to northeastern Asia that feeds on ash species.", "chunk_id": "18ee4a00e65dd0d7", "doc_id": "hp_cc129f1449a3ee73", "type": "NATIVE_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_cc129f1449a3ee73</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Emerald ash borer" target="ash species">
  <data key="d5">["FEEDS_ON"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The emerald ash borer feeds on ash species.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Agrilus planipennis, commonly known as the emerald ash borer, is a green buprestid or jewel beetle native to northeastern Asia that feeds on ash species.", "chunk_id": "18ee4a00e65dd0d7", "doc_id": "hp_cc129f1449a3ee73", "type": "FEEDS_ON"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_cc129f1449a3ee73</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Emerald ash borer" target="ash trees">
  <data key="d5">["AFFECTS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Emerald ash borers lay eggs in and feed on ash trees.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Females lay eggs in bark crevices on ash trees, and larvae feed underneath the bark of ash trees to emerge as adults in one to two years.", "chunk_id": "18ee4a00e65dd0d7", "doc_id": "hp_cc129f1449a3ee73", "type": "AFFECTS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_cc129f1449a3ee73</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Emerald ash borer" target="northwest Europe">
  <data key="d5">["INVASIVE_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The emerald ash borer is an invasive species in northwest Europe.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Outside its native range, it is an invasive species and is highly destructive to ash trees native to northwest Europe and North America.", "chunk_id": "18ee4a00e65dd0d7", "doc_id": "hp_cc129f1449a3ee73", "type": "INVASIVE_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_cc129f1449a3ee73</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Emerald ash borer" target="North America">
  <data key="d5">["INVASIVE_IN", "RESEARCH_FOCUSED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The emerald ash borer is an invasive species in North America.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Outside its native range, it is an invasive species and is highly destructive to ash trees native to northwest Europe and North America.", "chunk_id": "18ee4a00e65dd0d7", "doc_id": "hp_cc129f1449a3ee73", "type": "INVASIVE_IN"}, {"text": "Prior to being found in North America, very little was known about emerald ash borer in its native range; this has resulted in much of the research on its biology being focused in North America.", "chunk_id": "18ee4a00e65dd0d7", "doc_id": "hp_cc129f1449a3ee73", "type": "RESEARCH_FOCUSED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_cc129f1449a3ee73</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Agrilus planipennis" target="Emerald ash borer">
  <data key="d5">["SYNONYM_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Agrilus planipennis is commonly known as the emerald ash borer.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Agrilus planipennis, commonly known as the emerald ash borer, is a green buprestid or jewel beetle native to northeastern Asia that feeds on ash species.", "chunk_id": "18ee4a00e65dd0d7", "doc_id": "hp_cc129f1449a3ee73", "type": "SYNONYM_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_cc129f1449a3ee73</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Local governments in North America" target="Emerald ash borer">
  <data key="d5">["ATTEMPTS_TO_CONTROL"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Local governments in North America are attempting to control the emerald ash borer.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Local governments in North America are attempting to control it by monitoring its spread, diversifying tree species, insecticides, and biological control.", "chunk_id": "18ee4a00e65dd0d7", "doc_id": "hp_cc129f1449a3ee73", "type": "ATTEMPTS_TO_CONTROL"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_cc129f1449a3ee73</data>
</edge>
<edge source="River Farset" target="River Lagan">
  <data key="d5">["TRIBUTARY_OF", "JOINS", "ENTERS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The River Farset is a tributary of the River Lagan.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The River Farset (\"An Fhearsaid\" or \"Abhainn na Feirste\" in Irish) is a river in Belfast, Northern Ireland, a tributary of the River Lagan.", "chunk_id": "ffad64e807ea3b1b", "doc_id": "hp_cc911f866aa0efaa", "type": "TRIBUTARY_OF"}, {"text": "The River Farset is on the County Antrim side of the Lagan and joins the Lagan close to its outflow into Belfast Lough.", "chunk_id": "ffad64e807ea3b1b", "doc_id": "hp_cc911f866aa0efaa", "type": "JOINS"}, {"text": "The Farset rises above Legoniel, flowed past the medieval parish church at Shankill, through Millfield and under High Street, giving that street a curving appearance, entering the Lagan to the east of the Albert Clock and High Street.", "chunk_id": "ffad64e807ea3b1b", "doc_id": "hp_cc911f866aa0efaa", "type": "ENTERS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_cc911f866aa0efaa</data>
</edge>
<edge source="River Farset" target="Belfast">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The River Farset is a river in Belfast.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The River Farset (\"An Fhearsaid\" or \"Abhainn na Feirste\" in Irish) is a river in Belfast, Northern Ireland, a tributary of the River Lagan.", "chunk_id": "ffad64e807ea3b1b", "doc_id": "hp_cc911f866aa0efaa", "type": "LOCATED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_cc911f866aa0efaa</data>
</edge>
