  <data key="d6">The River Farset flows into Belfast Lough via the River Lagan.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The River Farset is on the County Antrim side of the Lagan and joins the Lagan close to its outflow into Belfast Lough.", "chunk_id": "ffad64e807ea3b1b", "doc_id": "hp_cc911f866aa0efaa", "type": "FLOWS_INTO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_cc911f866aa0efaa</data>
</edge>
<edge source="River Farset" target="High Street">
  <data key="d5">["LOCATED_UNDER", "FLOWED_UNDER", "LOCATED_EAST_OF"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The River Farset is now contained within a tunnel under Belfast's High Street.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "The River Farset is now contained within a tunnel under Belfast's High Street; a tunnel supposedly big enough to take a bus.", "chunk_id": "ffad64e807ea3b1b", "doc_id": "hp_cc911f866aa0efaa", "type": "LOCATED_UNDER"}, {"text": "The Farset rises above Legoniel, flowed past the medieval parish church at Shankill, through Millfield and under High Street, giving that street a curving appearance, entering the Lagan to the east of the Albert Clock and High Street.", "chunk_id": "ffad64e807ea3b1b", "doc_id": "hp_cc911f866aa0efaa", "type": "FLOWED_UNDER"}, {"text": "The Farset rises above Legoniel, flowed past the medieval parish church at Shankill, through Millfield and under High Street, giving that street a curving appearance, entering the Lagan to the east of the Albert Clock and High Street.", "chunk_id": "ffad64e807ea3b1b", "doc_id": "hp_cc911f866aa0efaa", "type": "LOCATED_EAST_OF"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_cc911f866aa0efaa</data>
</edge>
