<edge source="Anton Biersack" target="Greding">
  <data key="d5">["BORN_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Anton Biersack was born in Greding.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Anton Biersack (30 November 1907, Greding - 18 November 1982, Frankfurt am Main) was a German composer and music educator.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c", "type": "BORN_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e546658adba29b4c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Anton Biersack" target="Frankfurt am Main">
  <data key="d5">["DIED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Anton Biersack died in Frankfurt am Main.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Anton Biersack (30 November 1907, Greding - 18 November 1982, Frankfurt am Main) was a German composer and music educator.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c", "type": "DIED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e546658adba29b4c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Anton Biersack" target="Eichstätt">
  <data key="d5">["STUDIED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Anton Biersack had initial studies in music in Eichstätt.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "After initial studied in music in Eichstätt, he studied music composition, conducting, piano, and organ at the Hochschule für Musik Würzburg from 1928-1932.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c", "type": "STUDIED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e546658adba29b4c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Anton Biersack" target="Hochschule für Musik Würzburg">
  <data key="d5">["STUDIED_AT"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Anton Biersack studied music composition, conducting, piano, and organ at the Hochschule für Musik Würzburg.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "After initial studied in music in Eichstätt, he studied music composition, conducting, piano, and organ at the Hochschule für Musik Würzburg from 1928-1932.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c", "type": "STUDIED_AT"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e546658adba29b4c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Anton Biersack" target="Hoch Conservatory">
  <data key="d5">["FELLOW_AT", "STAFF_AT"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Anton Biersack was a fellow at the Hoch Conservatory.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "From 1932-1936 he was a fellow at the Hoch Conservatory in Frankfurt am Main.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c", "type": "FELLOW_AT"}, {"text": "He joined the staff of that conservatory in 1936 where he spent the next 4 years teaching music theory and directing the youth orchestra.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c", "type": "STAFF_AT"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e546658adba29b4c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Anton Biersack" target="Frankfurt University of Music and Performing Arts">
  <data key="d5">["WORKED_AT", "LECTURER_AT", "HEAD_OF_STUDIES_AT", "PROFESSOR_AT"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Anton Biersack worked as a conductor of student choral and orchestral ensembles at the Frankfurt University of Music and Performing Arts.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "He then worked as a conductor of student choral and orchestral ensembles at the Frankfurt University of Music and Performing Arts (FUMPA) before being appointed a lecturer at that school in 1947.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c", "type": "WORKED_AT"}, {"text": "He then worked as a conductor of student choral and orchestral ensembles at the Frankfurt University of Music and Performing Arts (FUMPA) before being appointed a lecturer at that school in 1947.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c", "type": "LECTURER_AT"}, {"text": "He was made head of orchestral studies at the FUMPA in 1957 and was appointed full professor at the school in 1960.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c", "type": "HEAD_OF_STUDIES_AT"}, {"text": "He was made head of orchestral studies at the FUMPA in 1957 and was appointed full professor at the school in 1960.", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c", "type": "PROFESSOR_AT"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e546658adba29b4c</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Anton Biersack" target="Agathe Biersack">
  <data key="d5">["MARRIED_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Anton Biersack was married to Agathe Biersack.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "He was married to Agathe Biersack (née Laur ) (1910–1996).", "chunk_id": "35f0b94190768e0c", "doc_id": "hp_e546658adba29b4c", "type": "MARRIED_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_e546658adba29b4c</data>
</edge>
