<edge source="Madonna" target="True Blue">
  <data key="d5">["RELEASED_ALBUM"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Madonna released her third studio album, "True Blue".</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "With the title track from her third studio album \"True Blue\" (1986), Madonna's impact on MTV and popular music was established when a contest entitled \"Making My Video\", was held to create a music video for the song.", "chunk_id": "ead4118602be8d9d", "doc_id": "hp_f2eafe05aec63f00", "type": "RELEASED_ALBUM"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f2eafe05aec63f00</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Madonna" target="La Isla Bonita">
  <data key="d5">["RELEASED_VIDEO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Madonna released the music video "La Isla Bonita" in 1987.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"La Isla Bonita\" and \"Who's That Girl\", both released in 1987, showed Madonna's fascination with Hispanic culture and religious symbolism.", "chunk_id": "ead4118602be8d9d", "doc_id": "hp_f2eafe05aec63f00", "type": "RELEASED_VIDEO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f2eafe05aec63f00</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Madonna" target="Who's That Girl">
  <data key="d5">["RELEASED_VIDEO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Madonna released the music video "Who's That Girl" in 1987.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"La Isla Bonita\" and \"Who's That Girl\", both released in 1987, showed Madonna's fascination with Hispanic culture and religious symbolism.", "chunk_id": "ead4118602be8d9d", "doc_id": "hp_f2eafe05aec63f00", "type": "RELEASED_VIDEO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f2eafe05aec63f00</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Madonna" target="Like a Prayer">
  <data key="d5">["RELEASED_VIDEO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Madonna released the controversial music video "Like a Prayer" in 1989.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "In 1989, the video of \"Like a Prayer\" portrayed her dancing in front of burning crosses, receiving stigmata, kissing a black saint and having sex with him in a church altar.", "chunk_id": "ead4118602be8d9d", "doc_id": "hp_f2eafe05aec63f00", "type": "RELEASED_VIDEO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f2eafe05aec63f00</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Madonna" target="Express Yourself">
  <data key="d5">["RELEASED_VIDEO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Madonna released the music video "Express Yourself" in 1989.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"Express Yourself\" released the same year was critically appreciated for its positive feminist themes.", "chunk_id": "ead4118602be8d9d", "doc_id": "hp_f2eafe05aec63f00", "type": "RELEASED_VIDEO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f2eafe05aec63f00</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Madonna" target="MTV">
  <data key="d5">["IMPACTED"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Madonna's impact on MTV and popular music was established with her third studio album.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "With the title track from her third studio album \"True Blue\" (1986), Madonna's impact on MTV and popular music was established when a contest entitled \"Making My Video\", was held to create a music video for the song.", "chunk_id": "ead4118602be8d9d", "doc_id": "hp_f2eafe05aec63f00", "type": "IMPACTED"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f2eafe05aec63f00</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Borderline" target="MTV">
  <data key="d5">["RECEIVED_ATTENTION_ON"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The music video "Borderline" received attention on MTV.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Her first video to receive attention on MTV was \"Borderline\", followed by \"Lucky Star\" and \"Like a Virgin\", which popularized Madonna's image and fashion among younger generation.", "chunk_id": "ead4118602be8d9d", "doc_id": "hp_f2eafe05aec63f00", "type": "RECEIVED_ATTENTION_ON"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f2eafe05aec63f00</data>
</edge>
