<edge source="Fuscospora gunnii" target="Tasmania">
  <data key="d5">["ENDEMIC_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Fuscospora gunnii is endemic to the highlands of Tasmania.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Fuscospora gunnii, the tanglefoot- or deciduous beech, or fagus, is a deciduous shrub endemic to the highlands of Tasmania, Australia.", "chunk_id": "cc7d1eb73c73bea4", "doc_id": "hp_f4fcfac633a5b005", "type": "ENDEMIC_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f4fcfac633a5b005</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fuscospora gunnii" target="Australia">
  <data key="d5">["ENDEMIC_TO"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Fuscospora gunnii is endemic to Australia (specifically Tasmania).</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Fuscospora gunnii, the tanglefoot- or deciduous beech, or fagus, is a deciduous shrub endemic to the highlands of Tasmania, Australia.", "chunk_id": "cc7d1eb73c73bea4", "doc_id": "hp_f4fcfac633a5b005", "type": "ENDEMIC_TO"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f4fcfac633a5b005</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fuscospora gunnii" target="R.C Gunn">
  <data key="d5">["DISCOVERED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">R.C Gunn discovered Fuscospora gunnii in 1847.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It was discovered in 1847 by R.C Gunn and evidence exists that it once lived in Antarctica.", "chunk_id": "cc7d1eb73c73bea4", "doc_id": "hp_f4fcfac633a5b005", "type": "DISCOVERED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f4fcfac633a5b005</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fuscospora gunnii" target="Antarctica">
  <data key="d5">["PREVIOUSLY_LIVED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Evidence suggests Fuscospora gunnii once lived in Antarctica.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It was discovered in 1847 by R.C Gunn and evidence exists that it once lived in Antarctica.", "chunk_id": "cc7d1eb73c73bea4", "doc_id": "hp_f4fcfac633a5b005", "type": "PREVIOUSLY_LIVED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f4fcfac633a5b005</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fuscospora gunnii" target="Tasmanian maritime climate">
  <data key="d5">["LIMITED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">The Tasmanian maritime climate limits Fuscospora gunnii to mountain habitats.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It lives only on mountains due to temperature limitations within the Tasmanian maritime climate and can survive up to heights of 1400 m .", "chunk_id": "cc7d1eb73c73bea4", "doc_id": "hp_f4fcfac633a5b005", "type": "LIMITED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f4fcfac633a5b005</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fuscospora gunnii" target="alpine and sub-alpine regions">
  <data key="d5">["GROWS_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Fuscospora gunnii grows in alpine and sub-alpine regions in Tasmania.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "It grows in alpine and sub-alpine regions in the west to central portions of the state but is absent from the mountains of the northeast.", "chunk_id": "cc7d1eb73c73bea4", "doc_id": "hp_f4fcfac633a5b005", "type": "GROWS_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f4fcfac633a5b005</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fuscospora gunnii" target="woody ground cover">
  <data key="d5">["GROWS_AS"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Fuscospora gunnii can grow as a woody ground cover.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Though capable of reaching the size of a small tree, it rarely exceeds 2 m in height, instead growing as a thick shrub or as a woody ground cover hence its common name of \"tanglefoot\".", "chunk_id": "cc7d1eb73c73bea4", "doc_id": "hp_f4fcfac633a5b005", "type": "GROWS_AS"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f4fcfac633a5b005</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Fuscospora gunnii" target="tanglefoot">
  <data key="d5">["HAS_COMMON_NAME"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Fuscospora gunnii has the common name 'tanglefoot'.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "Though capable of reaching the size of a small tree, it rarely exceeds 2 m in height, instead growing as a thick shrub or as a woody ground cover hence its common name of \"tanglefoot\".", "chunk_id": "cc7d1eb73c73bea4", "doc_id": "hp_f4fcfac633a5b005", "type": "HAS_COMMON_NAME"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f4fcfac633a5b005</data>
</edge>
<edge source="F. Gunnii" target="Nothofagus">
  <data key="d5">["PREVIOUSLY_INCLUDED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">F. Gunnii was previously included in the genus Nothofagus.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"F. Gunnii\" was previously included in the genus \"Nothofagus\", although recent DNA analysis has placed it in the genus \"Fuscospora\".", "chunk_id": "cc7d1eb73c73bea4", "doc_id": "hp_f4fcfac633a5b005", "type": "PREVIOUSLY_INCLUDED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f4fcfac633a5b005</data>
</edge>
<edge source="F. Gunnii" target="Fuscospora">
  <data key="d5">["PLACED_IN"]</data>
  <data key="d6">Recent DNA analysis has placed F. Gunnii in the genus Fuscospora.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"F. Gunnii\" was previously included in the genus \"Nothofagus\", although recent DNA analysis has placed it in the genus \"Fuscospora\".", "chunk_id": "cc7d1eb73c73bea4", "doc_id": "hp_f4fcfac633a5b005", "type": "PLACED_IN"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f4fcfac633a5b005</data>
</edge>
<edge source="F. Gunnii" target="DNA analysis">
  <data key="d5">["ANALYZED_BY"]</data>
  <data key="d6">DNA analysis was used to determine the genus placement of F. Gunnii.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"F. Gunnii\" was previously included in the genus \"Nothofagus\", although recent DNA analysis has placed it in the genus \"Fuscospora\".", "chunk_id": "cc7d1eb73c73bea4", "doc_id": "hp_f4fcfac633a5b005", "type": "ANALYZED_BY"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f4fcfac633a5b005</data>
</edge>
<edge source="F. Gunnii" target="woody tree">
  <data key="d5">["IS_A"]</data>
  <data key="d6">F. Gunnii is described as a small woody tree with a shrubby appearance.</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"text": "\"F. Gunnii\" is a small woody tree with a shrubby appearance known to grow up to 3 m .", "chunk_id": "cc7d1eb73c73bea4", "doc_id": "hp_f4fcfac633a5b005", "type": "IS_A"}]</data>
  <data key="d8">hp_f4fcfac633a5b005</data>
</edge>
